  (`question_id`, `audio_url`, `transcript`, `duration_seconds`, `audio_total_seconds`, `audio_start_seconds`, `audio_end_seconds`, `question_start_seconds`, `question_end_seconds`, `answer_start_seconds`, `answer_end_seconds`, `group_key`, `listening_type`, `lrc_content`, `created_at`, `updated_at`)
SELECT
  @a_cet4_2023_12_1_05, '/audio/exams/listening-cet4-2023-12-1.mp3', 'News Report Three\n新闻三\n\nAmid all the election drama, air pollution problems and disease outbreaks, five tourists'' good work is being spread online.\n在选举闹剧、空气污染问题和疾病爆发的背景下，五名游客的善举正在网上传播。\n\nYesterday, two male and three female tourists were spotted walking the kilometer-long beach, picking up trash.\n昨天，有人看到两名男游客和三名女游客在长达一公里的海滩上捡垃圾。\n\nOne of the male tourists from Australia commented that although there was a lot of trash, nobody was doing anything.\n一位来自澳大利亚的男性游客评论说，虽然海滩上有很多垃圾，但没有人做任何事情。\n\nThe beach was not as nice or beautiful as it should be.\n海滩没有它本来的那么漂亮。\n\nHe felt so sad to see such a gorgeous place littered with so much trash.\n看到这么美丽的地方到处都是垃圾，他感到很难过。\n\nThus, he and his friends decided to grab a few trash bags and clean it all up.\n因此，他和他的朋友们决定拿几个垃圾袋，把垃圾都清理干净。\n\nA man passing by decided to video their good deed and put it on the Internet.\n一名路过的男子决定将这一善举拍摄下来并上传到互联网上。\n\nIt was unclear where the rest of the group was from, but they were most likely traveling together.\n目前还不清楚这一组人中的其他人来自哪里，但他们很可能是一起旅行的。\n\nOne local woman commented on being embarrassed that tourists were cleaning up their beach.\n一位当地的女士评论说，游客们正在清理他们的海滩，她感到很尴尬。\n\nAnother mentioned that it was actually the natives who brought food and drinks, then left trash all along the island.\n另一位提到，实际上是当地人带来了食物和饮料，然后在岛上到处扔垃圾。\n\nQuestions 5 to 7 are based on the news report you have just heard.\n请根据你刚听到的新闻报道回答第5至7题。\n\n5. Why did one of the male tourists feel sad?\n5.为什么其中一名男性游客感到难过？\n\n6. Who put the good deed video on the Internet?\n6.是谁把这段善举视频放到网上的？\n\n7. Why did one local woman say she was embarrassed?\n7.为什么一位当地的女士说她感到尴尬？', 67, 1413.12, 276.41, 342.92, 348.16, 366.85, 296.35, 307.21, 'cet4-2023-12-1-g03', 'NEWS', '[04:36.41]News Report Three｜新闻三\n[04:39.25]Amid all the election drama, air pollution problems and disease outbreaks, five tourists'' good work is being spread online.｜在选举闹剧、空气污染问题和疾病爆发的背景下，五名游客的善举正在网上传播。\n[04:48.15]Yesterday, two male and three female tourists were spotted walking the kilometer-long beach, picking up trash.｜昨天，有人看到两名男游客和三名女游客在长达一公里的海滩上捡垃圾。\n[04:56.35]One of the male tourists from Australia commented that although there was a lot of trash, nobody was doing anything.｜一位来自澳大利亚的男性游客评论说，虽然海滩上有很多垃圾，但没有人做任何事情。\n[05:03.62]The beach was not as nice or beautiful as it should be.｜海滩没有它本来的那么漂亮。\n[05:07.51]He felt so sad to see such a gorgeous place littered with so much trash.｜看到这么美丽的地方到处都是垃圾，他感到很难过。\n[05:12.17]Thus, he and his friends decided to grab a few trash bags and clean it all up.｜因此，他和他的朋友们决定拿几个垃圾袋，把垃圾都清理干净。\n[05:18.37]A man passing by decided to video their good deed and put it on the Internet.｜一名路过的男子决定将这一善举拍摄下来并上传到互联网上。\n[05:23.69]It was unclear where the rest of the group was from, but they were most likely traveling together.｜目前还不清楚这一组人中的其他人来自哪里，但他们很可能是一起旅行的。\n[05:29.85]One local woman commented on being embarrassed that tourists were cleaning up their beach.｜一位当地的女士评论说，游客们正在清理他们的海滩，她感到很尴尬。\n[05:35.69]Another mentioned that it was actually the natives who brought food and drinks, then left trash all along the island.｜另一位提到，实际上是当地人带来了食物和饮料，然后在岛上到处扔垃圾。\n[05:42.92]Questions 5 to 7 are based on the news report you have just heard.｜请根据你刚听到的新闻报道回答第5至7题。\n[05:48.16]5. Why did one of the male tourists feel sad?｜5.为什么其中一名男性游客感到难过？\n[06:07.15]6. Who put the good deed video on the Internet?｜6.是谁把这段善举视频放到网上的？\n[06:26.69]7. Why did one local woman say she was embarrassed?｜7.为什么一位当地的女士说她感到尴尬？', NOW(), NOW()
WHERE @a_cet4_2023_12_1_05 IS NOT NULL
