  (`question_id`, `audio_url`, `transcript`, `duration_seconds`, `audio_total_seconds`, `audio_start_seconds`, `audio_end_seconds`, `question_start_seconds`, `question_end_seconds`, `answer_start_seconds`, `answer_end_seconds`, `group_key`, `listening_type`, `lrc_content`, `created_at`, `updated_at`)
SELECT
  @a_cet4_2023_12_1_08, '/audio/exams/listening-cet4-2023-12-1.mp3', 'Conversation One\n对话一\n\nW: Hello, Benjamin. Dan and I will be going for a run along the canal Saturday morning. Would you like to join us?\n女：你好，本杰明。星期六早上，丹和我要沿着运河去跑步，你愿意加入我们吗？\n\nM: I''d love to, but I hurt my ankle last weekend playing football with work colleagues.\n男：我很想去，但上周末我和同事们踢足球时脚踝受伤了。\n\nW: Oh dear, is it serious?\n女：天哪，严重吗？\n\nM: No, not at all. I landed badly during a fall and twisted it a little, but it''s no big deal.\n男：不，不严重。我落地时不稳，扭伤了脚，但没什么大不了的。\n\nIt''s just a little swollen and I should be fine for next Saturday if you still want to go for a jog then.\n只是有点肿，如果你还想慢跑的话，下周六我应该会没事的。\n\nW: I won''t be here next Saturday. I''m going to the zoo.\n女：下周六我不在这里。我要去动物园。\n\nM: The zoo?\n男：动物园？\n\nW: Yeah. My little nephew turns six. And he loves the zoo. So the whole family is going.\n女：是的。我的小侄子六岁了。而且他喜欢动物园，所以全家都去。\n\nM: Oh, okay then. I haven''t been to a zoo since I was a kid.\n男：哦，好吧。我长大后就没去过动物园。\n\nW: They are nowhere near as popular as they used to be when we were children.\n女：动物园远没有我们小时候那么受欢迎。\n\nI personally feel sorry for the poor animals stuck in cages.\n我个人为那些被关在笼子里的可怜的动物感到难过。\n\nBut there''s no denying they are fun and educational for children.\n但不可否认，它们对孩子们来说既有趣又有教育意义。\n\nM: Do you know if Dan will be around next Saturday?\n男：你知道丹下周六是否会来吗？\n\nW: Yeah, I think he will. Just send him a text message. He''s always keen on physical activities.\n女：是的，我想他会的。给他发短信。他总是热衷于运动。\n\nM: That''s true. Dan is extremely fit and healthy. He goes to the gym most days, plus tennis two or three times a week.\n这是真的。丹非常健康。他大部分时间都去健身房，而且每周打两到三次网球。\n\nW: So what have you been doing to stay busy while you''ve had that swollen ankle?\n女：所以你脚踝肿胀的时候，你一直在做什么呢？\n\nM: I''ve been catching up on some reading.\n男：我一直在赶进度阅读。\n\nI was given three books over Christmas, and I''m only now getting around to reading them.\n圣诞节期间我收到了三本书，现在我才抽出时间来读它们。\n\nQuestions 8 to 11 are based on the conversation you have just heard.\n请根据你刚听到的对话回答第8至11题。\n\n8. Why can''t the man go for a run Saturday morning?\n8.男士周六早上为什么不能去跑步？\n\n9. Why is the woman''s whole family going to the zoo next Saturday?\n9.女士全家下周六为什么要去动物园？\n\n10. What do we learn about Dan from the man''s description?\n10.关于丹，我们从男士的描述中知道什么？\n\n11. What has the man been doing since last weekend?\n11.男士上周末以来一直在做什么？', 86, 1413.12, 440.92, 527.15, 532.21, 551.43, NULL, NULL, 'cet4-2023-12-1-g04', 'LONG_DIALOGUE', '[07:20.92]Conversation One｜对话一\n[07:22.43]W: Hello, Benjamin. Dan and I will be going for a run along the canal Saturday morning. Would you like to join us?｜女：你好，本杰明。星期六早上，丹和我要沿着运河去跑步，你愿意加入我们吗？\n[07:29.97]M: I''d love to, but I hurt my ankle last weekend playing football with work colleagues.｜男：我很想去，但上周末我和同事们踢足球时脚踝受伤了。\n[07:35.32]W: Oh dear, is it serious?｜女：天哪，严重吗？\n[07:37.65]M: No, not at all. I landed badly during a fall and twisted it a little, but it''s no big deal.｜男：不，不严重。我落地时不稳，扭伤了脚，但没什么大不了的。\n[07:43.92]It''s just a little swollen and I should be fine for next Saturday if you still want to go for a jog then.｜只是有点肿，如果你还想慢跑的话，下周六我应该会没事的。\n[07:49.61]W: I won''t be here next Saturday. I''m going to the zoo.｜女：下周六我不在这里。我要去动物园。\n[07:52.95]M: The zoo?｜男：动物园？\n[07:53.84]W: Yeah. My little nephew turns six. And he loves the zoo. So the whole family is going.｜女：是的。我的小侄子六岁了。而且他喜欢动物园，所以全家都去。\n[07:59.93]M: Oh, okay then. I haven''t been to a zoo since I was a kid.｜男：哦，好吧。我长大后就没去过动物园。\n[08:03.94]W: They are nowhere near as popular as they used to be when we were children.｜女：动物园远没有我们小时候那么受欢迎。\n[08:08.42]I personally feel sorry for the poor animals stuck in cages.｜我个人为那些被关在笼子里的可怜的动物感到难过。\n[08:13.00]But there''s no denying they are fun and educational for children.｜但不可否认，它们对孩子们来说既有趣又有教育意义。\n[08:17.70]M: Do you know if Dan will be around next Saturday?｜男：你知道丹下周六是否会来吗？\n[08:20.61]W: Yeah, I think he will. Just send him a text message. He''s always keen on physical activities.｜女：是的，我想他会的。给他发短信。他总是热衷于运动。\n[08:26.89]M: That''s true. Dan is extremely fit and healthy. He goes to the gym most days, plus tennis two or three times a week.｜这是真的。丹非常健康。他大部分时间都去健身房，而且每周打两到三次网球。\n[08:34.93]W: So what have you been doing to stay busy while you''ve had that swollen ankle?｜女：所以你脚踝肿胀的时候，你一直在做什么呢？\n[08:40.30]M: I''ve been catching up on some reading.｜男：我一直在赶进度阅读。\n[08:42.25]I was given three books over Christmas, and I''m only now getting around to reading them.｜圣诞节期间我收到了三本书，现在我才抽出时间来读它们。\n[08:47.15]Questions 8 to 11 are based on the conversation you have just heard.｜请根据你刚听到的对话回答第8至11题。\n[08:52.21]8. Why can''t the man go for a run Saturday morning?｜8.男士周六早上为什么不能去跑步？\n[09:11.73]9. Why is the woman''s whole family going to the zoo next Saturday?｜9.女士全家下周六为什么要去动物园？\n[09:30.96]10. What do we learn about Dan from the man''s description?｜10.关于丹，我们从男士的描述中知道什么？\n[09:52.82]11. What has the man been doing since last weekend?｜11.男士上周末以来一直在做什么？', NOW(), NOW()
WHERE @a_cet4_2023_12_1_08 IS NOT NULL
