SELECT
  @a_cet4_2023_12_1_16, '/audio/exams/listening-cet4-2023-12-1.mp3', 'Passage One\n短文一\n\nNew research from America studies the role that the presence of individuals from different social or racial groups has in influencing consumers'' food choices.\n美国的一个新项目研究了来自不同社会或种族群体的人在影响消费者食物选择方面的作用。\n\nThis research found college students were more likely to choose healthy food in the presence of an observer of a different race, as opposed to an observer from their own race.\n这项研究发现，大学生在有不同种族的观察者在场的情况下，比有自己种族的观察者在场的情况下，更有可能选择健康食品。\n\nThe same was true when they were with someone from a different university compared to someone from their own.\n与和自己同一所大学的人在一起时相比，他们与来自不同大学的人在一起时也是如此。\n\nResearchers say this was because participants anticipated more negative judgment from an outsider group.\n研究人员表示，这是因为参与者预计外部群体会做出更负面的判断。\n\nIn contrast, they felt less judged by members of their own group.\n相比之下，他们觉得自己的团队成员对他们的评判更少。\n\nIn one experiment, participants were offered the choice between candy and fruit as a snack.\n在一项实验中，参与者可以选择糖果和水果作为零食。\n\nWhen in the presence of an unknown student from their own university, only 12% of students selected the healthier option.\n在自己大学的陌生同学面前，只有12%的学生选择了更健康的选择。\n\nHowever, this number was 31% when in the presence of an unknown student from another university.\n然而，在另一所大学的一名陌生同学在场的情况下，这一数字为31%。\n\nOther experiments showed similar results based on racial group.\n其他基于种族群体的实验显示了类似的结果。\n\nWhat''s the reason for this pattern?\n出现这种情况的原因是什么？\n\nThe study found that people feel judged to a larger extent by members of other groups.\n研究发现，人们在很大程度上感觉受到其他群体成员的评判。\n\nBecause of this, they strategically use healthy food choices to make a positive impression.\n正因为如此，他们战略性地选择健康的食物来给人留下积极的印象。\n\nThere have been many attempts to help consumers make healthier choices, but consumers often struggle to maintain a healthy diet.\n有很多人试图帮助消费者做出更健康的选择，但消费者往往难以保持健康的饮食。\n\nThis research finds that one way to promote a healthy diet could be to advertise the social benefits of healthy choices.\n这项研究发现，宣传健康选择的社会效益可能是促进健康饮食的一种方法。\n\nQuestions 16 to 18 are based on the passage you have just heard.\n请根据你刚听到的短文回答第16至18题。\n\n16. What was the finding of the new research from America about consumers'' food choices?\n16.美国一项关于消费者食物选择的新研究发现了什么？\n\n17. When did 31% of students in the experiment select the healthier option?\n17.实验中31%的学生何时选择了更健康的选项？\n\n18. How could a healthy diet be promoted according to the findings of the new research?\n18. 根据这项新研究的发现，如何促进健康饮食？', 106, 1413.12, 847.38, 953.09, 958.98, 978.98, 849.43, 860.61, 'cet4-2023-12-1-g06', 'PASSAGE', '[14:07.38]Passage One｜短文一\n[14:09.43]New research from America studies the role that the presence of individuals from different social or racial groups has in influencing consumers'' food choices.｜美国的一个新项目研究了来自不同社会或种族群体的人在影响消费者食物选择方面的作用。\n[14:20.91]This research found college students were more likely to choose healthy food in the presence of an observer of a different race, as opposed to an observer from their own race.｜这项研究发现，大学生在有不同种族的观察者在场的情况下，比有自己种族的观察者在场的情况下，更有可能选择健康食品。\n[14:33.16]The same was true when they were with someone from a different university compared to someone from their own.｜与和自己同一所大学的人在一起时相比，他们与来自不同大学的人在一起时也是如此。\n[14:39.34]Researchers say this was because participants anticipated more negative judgment from an outsider group.｜研究人员表示，这是因为参与者预计外部群体会做出更负面的判断。\n[14:46.97]In contrast, they felt less judged by members of their own group.｜相比之下，他们觉得自己的团队成员对他们的评判更少。\n[14:51.80]In one experiment, participants were offered the choice between candy and fruit as a snack.｜在一项实验中，参与者可以选择糖果和水果作为零食。\n[14:58.43]When in the presence of an unknown student from their own university, only 12% of students selected the healthier option.｜在自己大学的陌生同学面前，只有12%的学生选择了更健康的选择。\n[15:07.17]However, this number was 31% when in the presence of an unknown student from another university.｜然而，在另一所大学的一名陌生同学在场的情况下，这一数字为31%。\n[15:14.24]Other experiments showed similar results based on racial group.｜其他基于种族群体的实验显示了类似的结果。\n[15:18.96]What''s the reason for this pattern?｜出现这种情况的原因是什么？\n[15:21.25]The study found that people feel judged to a larger extent by members of other groups.｜研究发现，人们在很大程度上感觉受到其他群体成员的评判。\n[15:27.76]Because of this, they strategically use healthy food choices to make a positive impression.｜正因为如此，他们战略性地选择健康的食物来给人留下积极的印象。\n[15:34.07]There have been many attempts to help consumers make healthier choices, but consumers often struggle to maintain a healthy diet.｜有很多人试图帮助消费者做出更健康的选择，但消费者往往难以保持健康的饮食。\n[15:43.73]This research finds that one way to promote a healthy diet could be to advertise the social benefits of healthy choices.｜这项研究发现，宣传健康选择的社会效益可能是促进健康饮食的一种方法。\n[15:53.09]Questions 16 to 18 are based on the passage you have just heard.｜请根据你刚听到的短文回答第16至18题。\n[15:58.98]16. What was the finding of the new research from America about consumers'' food choices?｜16.美国一项关于消费者食物选择的新研究发现了什么？\n[16:21.83]17. When did 31% of students in the experiment select the healthier option?｜17.实验中31%的学生何时选择了更健康的选项？\n[16:41.88]18. How could a healthy diet be promoted according to the findings of the new research?｜18. 根据这项新研究的发现，如何促进健康饮食？', NOW(), NOW()
WHERE @a_cet4_2023_12_1_16 IS NOT NULL
