  @a_cet4_2023_12_1_24, '/audio/exams/listening-cet4-2023-12-1.mp3', 'Passage Three\n短文三\n\nTaking risks in business does not mean going into business blindly and then expecting great results.\n商业冒险并不意味着盲目地经商，然后期待丰硕的成果。\n\nOn the contrary, taking risks in entrepreneurship involves careful planning and hard work.\n相反，商业冒险需要精心规划和努力工作。\n\nNobody can really be sure if risks will be met with success, no matter how calculated they may be.\n无论如何计算，没有人能真正确定冒险是否会成功。\n\nBut this should not stop you from taking risks, as risks are necessary if you want your business to succeed.\n但这不应该阻止你冒险，因为如果你想让你的企业成功，冒险是必要的。\n\nSome risks may not work out, but an optimistic risk-taker will always look at failure as an opportunity to learn.\n有些风险可能无法解决，但一个乐观的冒险者总是会把失败视为一个学习的机会。\n\nThe willingness to experiment with new ideas is key to business growth.\n愿意尝试新想法是业务增长的关键。\n\nAs the old saying goes, “nothing ventured, nothing gained.”\n俗话说，“不入虎穴，焉得虎子。”\n\nFailure will teach you how to think and plan strategically.\n失败会教会你如何进行战略性思考和计划。\n\nBut just remember that not all risks are good ones, and when you fail, learn from it and move forward.\n但请记住，并非所有冒险都是好的。当你失败时，要从中吸取教训，继续前进。\n\nSince most people tend to avoid risk, businesses that are brave enough to take risks already have a competitive advantage.\n由于大多数人倾向于避免风险，勇于冒险的企业已经具有竞争优势。\n\nThey are the ones setting the standard with new ideas, fresh offers and bold inventions.\n他们用新的想法、新的提议和大胆的发明来树立标准。\n\nRisk-takers are best at adapting in difficult times.\n冒险者最擅长适应困难。\n\nSimply put, when most individuals stay away from risk, it means less competition for risk-takers.\n简单地说，当大多数人远离风险时，这意味着冒险者的竞争减少。\n\nWe don''t know if you''ll achieve what these risk-takers have achieved, but for as long as you want to stay safe and for as long as you''re content with where your business is right now, you will never find out.\n我们不知道你是否会实现这些冒险者所取得的成就，但只要你想保持安全，只要你满足于你的业务现状，你将永远不会知道。\n\nQuestions 22 to 25 are based on the passage you have just heard.\n请根据你刚听到的短文回答第22至25