t times.｜冒险者最擅长适应困难。\n[21:36.81]Simply put, when most individuals stay away from risk, it means less competition for risk-takers.｜简单地说，当大多数人远离风险时，这意味着冒险者的竞争减少。\n[21:44.98]We don''t know if you''ll achieve what these risk-takers have achieved, but for as long as you want to stay safe and for as long as you''re content with where your business is right now, you will never find out.｜我们不知道你是否会实现这些冒险者所取得的成就，但只要你想保持安全，只要你满足于你的业务现状，你将永远不会知道。\n[21:58.37]Questions 22 to 25 are based on the passage you have just heard.｜请根据你刚听到的短文回答第22至25题。\n[22:03.89]22. What do entrepreneurs have to do when taking risks according to the passage?｜22. 按照短文所说，企业家在冒险时要做什么？\n[22:25.37]23. What does the passage say is key to business growth?｜23. 按照短文所说，企业成长的关键是什么？\n[22:45.76]24. What are we advised to do when we fail?｜24. 当我们失败时，我们被建议做什么？\n[23:04.60]25. What does it mean to risk-taking businesses when most people tend to avoid risk?｜25. 当大多数人倾向于规避风险时，这对冒险企业意味着什么？', NOW(), NOW()
