  @a_cet4_2023_12_2_01, '/audio/exams/listening-cet4-2023-12-2.mp3', 'News Report One\n新闻一\n\nA police officer in the U.S. stopped a large SUV car that was going very slowly and drifting across lanes on a highway.\n一名警察在高速公路上拦下了一辆行驶非常缓慢、在车道上漂移的大型SUV。\n\nHe expected to find the driver who was either very drunk or having a medical emergency. Instead, the officer discovered a five-year-old boy sat on the edge of the driver''s seat.\n他以为会发现那个司机不是喝得烂醉就是有急症。相反，警察发现一个五岁的男孩坐在驾驶座的边缘。\n\nHis feet could barely reach the brake, and his head was only just high enough to see out of the windows.\n他的脚几乎够不到刹车，而且他的头刚好可以看到窗外。\n\nThe child had taken the keys to the family car, while his teenage sister was napping.\n他十几岁的妹妹正在打盹时，他拿走了家里汽车的钥匙。\n\nHe then drove three kilometers across town before getting on the highway.\n然后，他驱车三公里穿过小镇，然后上了高速公路。\n\nThe boy later told confused officers that he was planning to travel to California and buy a Lamborghini sports car. Although he only had $3 in his wallet, at least he was driving in the right direction.\n这名男孩后来告诉困惑的警察，他计划去加利福尼亚州买一辆兰博基尼跑车。尽管他钱包里只有3美元，但至少他开的方向是正确的。\n\nQuestions 1 and 2 are based on the news report you have just heard.\n请根据你刚听到的新闻报道回答第1题和第2题。\n\n1. Why did the police officer stop the SUV car?\n1. 为什么警察拦下了那辆越野车？\n\n2. What did the boy tell the police officers he was planning to do?\n2. 男孩告诉警察他打算做什么？', 56, 1415.93, 40.85, 96.61, 102.11, 121.80, NULL, NULL, 'cet4-2023-12-2-g01', 'NEWS', '[00:40.85]News Report One｜新闻一\n[00:43.39]A police officer in the U.S. stopped a large SUV car that was going very slowly and drifting across lanes on a highway.｜一名警察在高速公路上拦下了一辆行驶非常缓慢、在车道上漂移的大型SUV。\n[00:52.22]He expected to find the driver who was either very drunk or having a medical emergency. Instead, the officer discovered a five-year-old boy sat on the edge of the driver''s seat.｜他以为会发现那个司机不是喝得烂醉就是有急症。相反，警察发现一个五岁的男孩坐在驾驶座的边缘。\n[01:04.69]His feet could barely reach the brake, and his head was only just high enough to see out of the windows.｜他的脚几乎够不到刹车，而且他的头刚好可以看到窗外。\n[01:11.19]The child had taken the keys to the family car, while his teenage sister was napping.｜他十几岁的妹妹正在打盹时，他拿走了家里汽车的钥匙。\n[01:17.01]He then drove three kilometers across town before getting on the highway.｜然后，他驱车三公里穿过小镇，然后上了高速公路。\n[01:22.17]The boy later told confused officers that he was planning to travel to California and buy a Lamborghini sports car. Although he only had $3 in his wallet, at least he was driving in the right direction.｜这名男孩后来告诉困惑的警察，他计划去加利福尼亚州买一辆兰博基尼跑车。尽管他钱包里只有3美元，但至少他开的方向是正确的。\n[01:36.61]Questions 1 and 2 are based on the news report you have just heard.｜请根据你刚听到的新闻报道回答第1题和第2题。\n[01:42.11]1. Why did the police officer stop the SUV car?｜1. 为什么警察拦下了那辆越野车？\n[02:02.10]2. What did the boy tell the police officers he was planning to do?｜2. 男孩告诉警察他打算做什么？', NOW(), NOW()
