SELECT
  @a_cet4_2023_12_2_03, '/audio/exams/listening-cet4-2023-12-2.mp3', 'News Report Two\n新闻二\n\nMobile phones have changed the way we live—how we read, work, communicate and shop.\n手机改变了我们的生活方式，比如我们如何阅读、工作、交流和购物等。\n\nBut we already know this.\n但我们已经知道这些了。\n\nWhat we have not yet understood is the way the tiny machines in front of us are changing our skeletons, possibly altering not just the way we behave, but even the very shape of our bodies.\n我们还不了解的是，我们面前的微小机器（手机）正在改变我们的骨骼，可能不仅改变我们的行为方式，甚至改变我们的身体形状。\n\nNew scientific research at the University of the Sunshine Coast in Queensland, Australia, suggests that young people are developing extra pieces of bone at the backs of their heads.\n澳大利亚昆士兰阳光海岸大学的一项新科学研究表明，年轻人的后脑勺正在长出多余的骨头。\n\nThese pieces of bone are caused by the way people bend their heads when they use the phone.\n这些骨头碎片是由人们使用手机时低头的方式引起的。\n\nThis shifts weight onto the muscles at the back of the head and causes the bone to grow in a way that is not normal.\n这会将头部的重量转移到头部后面的肌肉上，导致骨骼以不正常的方式生长。\n\nThis process can be compared to the way the skin hardens in response to constant rubbing or pressure.\n这个过程就像皮肤在持续摩擦或压力下变硬一样。\n\nThe result is a piece of bone like a horn that sticks out from the head by the neck.\n结果是一块像角一样的骨头从头伸到脖子上。\n\nQuestions 3 and 4 are based on the news report you have just heard.\n请根据你刚听到的新闻报道回答第3题和第4题。\n\n3. What does the report say we have not yet understood about mobile phones?\n3. 报道说，我们对手机还不了解什么？\n\n4. What happens to the skin when rubbed or pressed constantly?\n4. 不断摩擦或按压皮肤会发生什么？', 71, 1415.93, 140.89, 212.01, 218.03, 239.58, 155.80, 169.82, 'cet4-2023-12-2-g02', 'NEWS', '[02:20.89]News Report Two｜新闻二\n[02:25.50]Mobile phones have changed the way we live—how we read, work, communicate and shop.｜手机改变了我们的生活方式，比如我们如何阅读、工作、交流和购物等。\n[02:33.73]But we already know this.｜但我们已经知道这些了。\n[02:35.80]What we have not yet understood is the way the tiny machines in front of us are changing our skeletons, possibly altering not just the way we behave, but even the very shape of our bodies.｜我们还不了解的是，我们面前的微小机器（手机）正在改变我们的骨骼，可能不仅改变我们的行为方式，甚至改变我们的身体形状。\n[02:50.12]New scientific research at the University of the Sunshine Coast in Queensland, Australia, suggests that young people are developing extra pieces of bone at the backs of their heads.｜澳大利亚昆士兰阳光海岸大学的一项新科学研究表明，年轻人的后脑勺正在长出多余的骨头。\n[03:03.42]These pieces of bone are caused by the way people bend their heads when they use the phone.｜这些骨头碎片是由人们使用手机时低头的方式引起的。\n[03:09.46]This shifts weight onto the muscles at the back of the head and causes the bone to grow in a way that is not normal.｜这会将头部的重量转移到头部后面的肌肉上，导致骨骼以不正常的方式生长。\n[03:18.01]This process can be compared to the way the skin hardens in response to constant rubbing or pressure.｜这个过程就像皮肤在持续摩擦或压力下变硬一样。\n[03:25.09]The result is a piece of bone like a horn that sticks out from the head by the neck.｜结果是一块像角一样的骨头从头伸到脖子上。\n[03:32.01]Questions 3 and 4 are based on the news report you have just heard.｜请根据你刚听到的新闻报道回答第3题和第4题。\n[03:38.03]3. What does the report say we have not yet understood about mobile phones?｜3. 报道说，我们对手机还不了解什么？\n[03:59.88]4. What happens to the skin when rubbed or pressed constantly?｜4. 不断摩擦或按压皮肤会发生什么？', NOW(), NOW()
WHERE @a_cet4_2023_12_2_03 IS NOT NULL
