  @a_cet4_2023_12_2_08, '/audio/exams/listening-cet4-2023-12-2.mp3', 'Conversation One\n对话一\n\nM: So where do you want to go for lunch?\n男：那么你想去哪里吃午饭？\n\nW: I don''t know. Do you have anything in mind?\n女：我不知道。你有什么想法吗？\n\nM: What about the sandwich place on Camden Street?\n男：去卡姆登街上的三明治店吃饭怎么样？\n\nW: Um, no, sorry. I don''t feel like sandwiches today.\n女：嗯，不，对不起。我今天不想吃三明治。\n\nIt''s a great place, but I think we go there too often.\n这个地方很不错，但我觉得我们去那里太频繁了。\n\nM: That''s true. Remember, that''s where we saw Brigette Clark, the famous movie star.\n男：的确。记得那是我们看到著名影星布丽奇特·克拉克的地方。\n\nW: Of course. How could I ever forget?\n女：当然。我怎么会忘记？\n\nThere were crowds of people around her, asking for a photo with her.\n她周围挤满了人，要求和她合影。\n\nM: What about hamburgers, then? There''s that American style diner on the way to the mall.\n男：那汉堡怎么样？在去商场的路上有一家美式餐馆。\n\nW: I like that place. Their chips are great, but their service takes a long time.\n女：我喜欢那个地方。他们的薯条很好，但需要等很长时间。\n\nAnd I need to get back by 2:30 for a conference call.\n我需要在2:30前回来参加电话会议。\n\nHow about trying something new? We could try Mario''s, the new Italian restaurant on the corner.\n吃点新的怎么样？我们可以试试拐角处的新意式餐厅马里奥。\n\nIt looks all right. Have you been there?\n看起来很好。你去过那里吗？\n\nM: No, I haven''t. But I''ve noticed that it has great reviews on the Internet.\n男：不，我没有。但我注意到它在互联网上有很好的评价。\n\nIt''s supposed to be one of the best Italians in town.\n它应该是城里最好的意式餐厅之一。\n\nI think Jeremy has been there and said it was amazing. I''m up for that.\n我想杰里米去过那里，说这太棒了。我准备好了。\n\nW: Cool. Have you asked Jeremy if he would like to come with us?\n女：太好了。你问过杰里米是否愿意和我们一起去吗？\n\nM: I already have. He says he can''t.\n男：我已经问了。他说不来。\n\nHe has brought his own lunch today.\n他今天自带午餐。\n\nSo he will stay in. I think his wife made him soup.\n所以他不出来。我想他妻子给他做了汤。\n\nW: Poor Jeremy. His wife is a terrible cook.\n女：可怜的杰里米。他的妻子是个糟糕的厨师。\n\nHe should throw that soup in the bin and join us.\n他应该把妻子做的汤扔进垃圾桶，和我们一起出去吃饭。\n\nQuestions 8 to 11 are based on the conversation you have just heard.\n请根据你刚听到的对话回答第8至11题。\n\n8. What are the speakers talking about in this conversation?\n8. 说话者在此对话中谈论的是什么？\n\n9. Where did the speakers see Brigette Clark the famous movie star?\n9. 说话者是在哪里看到著名影星布丽奇特·克拉克的？\n\n10. Why does the woman say she needs to get back by 2:30?\n10. 为什么女士说她需要在2:30之前回来？\n\n11. Why does the woman say Jeremy should throw his soup in the bin?\n11. 为什么女士说杰里米应该把他的汤扔进垃圾桶？', 85, 1415.93, 441.11, 526.13, 531.41, 549.58, NULL, NULL, 'cet4-2023-12-2-g04', 'LONG_DIALOGUE', '[07:21.11]Conversation One｜对话一\n[07:23.11]M: So where do you want to go for lunch?｜男：那么你想去哪里吃午饭？\n[07:26.59]W: I don''t know. Do you have anything in mind?｜女：我不知道。你有什么想法吗？\n[07:29.09]M: What about the sandwich place on Camden Street?｜男：去卡姆登街上的三明治店吃饭怎么样？\n[07:32.77]W: Um, no, sorry. I don''t feel like sandwiches today.｜女：嗯，不，对不起。我今天不想吃三明治。\n[07:37.22]It''s a great place, but I think we go there too often.｜这个地方很不错，但我觉得我们去那里太频繁了。\n[07:40.52]M: That''s true. Remember, that''s where we saw Brigette Clark, the famous movie star.｜男：的确。记得那是我们看到著名影星布丽奇特·克拉克的地方。\n[07:45.96]W: Of course. How could I ever forget?｜女：当然。我怎么会忘记？\n[07:48.38]There were crowds of people around her, asking for a photo with her.｜她周围挤满了人，要求和她合影。\n[07:52.42]M: What about hamburgers, then? There''s that American style diner on the way to the mall.｜男：那汉堡怎么样？在去商场的路上有一家美式餐馆。\n[07:57.93]W: I like that place. Their chips are great, but their service takes a long time.｜女：我喜欢那个地方。他们的薯条很好，但需要等很长时间。\n[08:03.04]And I need to get back by 2:30 for a conference call.｜我需要在2:30前回来参加电话会议。\n[08:06.59]How about trying something new? We could try Mario''s, the new Italian restaurant on the corner.｜吃点新的怎么样？我们可以试试拐角处的新意式餐厅马里奥。\n[08:13.33]It looks all right. Have you been there?｜看起来很好。你去过那里吗？\n[08:15.80]M: No, I haven''t. But I''ve noticed that it has great reviews on the Internet.｜男：不，我没有。但我注意到它在互联网上有很好的评价。\n[08:20.38]It''s supposed to be one of the best Italians in town.｜它应该是城里最好的意式餐厅之一。\n[08:23.27]I think Jeremy has been there and said it was amazing. I''m up for that.｜我想杰里米去过那里，说这太棒了。我准备好了。\n[08:27.60]W: Cool. Have you asked Jeremy if he would like to come with us?｜女：太好了。你问过杰里米是否愿意和我们一起去吗？\n[08:31.23]M: I already have. He says he can''t.｜男：我已经问了。他说不来。\n[08:33.63]He has brought his own lunch today.｜他今天自带午餐。\n[08:35.83]So he will stay in. I think his wife made him soup.｜所以他不出来。我想他妻子给他做了汤。\n[08:38.98]W: Poor Jeremy. His wife is a terrible cook.｜女：可怜的杰里米。他的妻子是个糟糕的厨师。\n[08:42.47]He should throw that soup in the bin and join us.｜他应该把妻子做的汤扔进垃圾桶，和我们一起出去吃饭。\n[08:46.13]Questions 8 to 11 are based on the conversation you have just heard.｜请根据你刚听到的对话回答第8至11题。\n[08:51.41]8. What are the speakers talking about in this conversation?｜8. 说话者在此对话中谈论的是什么？\n[09:09.88]9. Where did the speakers see Brigette Clark the famous movie star?｜9. 说话者是在哪里看到著名影星布丽奇特·克拉克的？\n[09:32.24]10. Why does the woman say she needs to get back by 2:30?｜10. 为什么女士说她需要在2:30之前回来？\n[09:52.65]11. Why does the woman say Jeremy should throw his soup in the bin?｜11. 为什么女士说杰里米应该把他的汤扔进垃圾桶？', NOW(), NOW()
