  @a_cet4_2023_12_2_14, '/audio/exams/listening-cet4-2023-12-2.mp3', 'Conversation Two\n对话二\n\nW: Hi there. How are you today? Do you have a reservation with us already?\n女：您好。今天好吗？您有预订吗？\n\nM: Good afternoon. Yes, we reserved our rooms yesterday morning on your website for three nights. The name''s Patterson.\n男：下午好。是的，我们昨天上午在您的网站上预订了三晚的房间。我叫帕特森。\n\nW: Okay, let me have a look. Yes, we have it here. You brought the whole family with you, I see.\n女：好的，让我看看。是的，我们这里有。我明白了，你把全家都带来了。\n\nM: Yes, the two kids, my wife and I, and her parents too.\n男：是的，两个孩子，我和妻子，还有她的父母。\n\nW: Great. So we have a family room for you and your wife and the kids, and another double room for your parents-in-law.\n女：太好了。所以我们有一个家庭房间给你、你的妻子和孩子，还有一个双人房间给你的岳父母。\n\nThey are right next to each other on the ground floor, since you mentioned in your message that they have trouble with stairs.\n它们在一楼紧挨着，因为您在留言中提到他们上下楼梯不方便。\n\nM: That''s wonderful. My father-in-law has had terrible problems getting up and down stairs since his knee operation last April.\n男：太棒了。自从我岳父去年4月做了膝盖手术，上下楼梯都很困难。\n\nW: I''m sorry to hear that. And if you need any help to find transportation for the whole family, we can definitely recommend someone for you.\n女：听到这个消息我很抱歉。如果您需要帮助来为家人寻找交通工具的话，我们可以为你推荐一个人。\n\nM: We were thinking of renting a car, but we will explore all the options available for sure.\n男：我们曾考虑租车，但我们肯定会考虑所有可用的选择。\n\nSo yes, that would be very helpful in comparing prices. We''re also wondering what tours and day trips are available.\n是的，这对比较价格很有帮助。我们还想知道有哪些旅游团和一日游。\n\nW: We have bunches of brochures here.\n女：我们这里有一捆小册子。\n\nI would recommend getting out on a boat trip.\n我建议出去坐船旅行。\n\nThe kids will love it, and there are so many islands nearby to explore.\n孩子们会喜欢的，附近有很多岛屿可以玩耍。\n\nThere''s also a great night market further into town that has all kinds of food and cool little shops selling souvenirs and local jewelry and clothing made by hand.\n镇上还有一个很棒的夜市，里面有各种各样的食物和很酷的小商店，出售手工制作的纪念品、珠宝和服装。\n\nM: That all sounds marvelous.\n男：这一切听起来太棒了。\n\nW: Now, all I need is to photocopy your passports, and then I can get you all checked in and show you to your rooms.\n女：现在，我需要复印你们的护照，然后我就可以办理入住手续，带你们去房间。\n\nQuestions 12 to 15 are based on the conversation you have just heard.\n请根据你刚听到的对话回答第12至15题。\n\n12. Who is the man talking to in the conversation?\n12. 对话中的男士在和谁说话？\n\n13. What do we learn about the man''s father-in-law from the conversation?\n13. 从对话中，我们知道男子岳父的什么情况？\n\n14. Why does the man say they will explore all the options available?\n14. 为什么男士说他们会考虑所有可用的选择？\n\n15. What does the woman suggest the man and his family do close to the end of the conversation?\n15. 在对话末尾，女士建议男士及其家人做什么？', 99, 1415.93, 613.15, 712.60, 759.27, 778.86, NULL, NULL, 'cet4-2023-12-2-g05', 'LONG_DIALOGUE', '[10:13.15]Conversation Two｜对话二\n[10:16.25]W: Hi there. How are you today? Do you have a reservation with us already?｜女：您好。今天好吗？您有预订吗？\n[10:21.05]M: Good afternoon. Yes, we reserved our rooms yesterday morning on your website for three nights. The name''s Patterson.｜男：下午好。是的，我们昨天上午在您的网站上预订了三晚的房间。我叫帕特森。\n[10:28.58]W: Okay, let me have a look. Yes, we have it here. You brought the whole family with you, I see.｜女：好的，让我看看。是的，我们这里有。我明白了，你把全家都带来了。\n[10:34.16]M: Yes, the two kids, my wife and I, and her parents too.｜男：是的，两个孩子，我和妻子，还有她的父母。\n[10:38.29]W: Great. So we have a family room for you and your wife and the kids, and another double room for your parents-in-law.｜女：太好了。所以我们有一个家庭房间给你、你的妻子和孩子，还有一个双人房间给你的岳父母。\n[10:46.65]They are right next to each other on the ground floor, since you mentioned in your message that they have trouble with stairs.｜它们在一楼紧挨着，因为您在留言中提到他们上下楼梯不方便。\n[10:53.44]M: That''s wonderful. My father-in-law has had terrible problems getting up and down stairs since his knee operation last April.｜男：太棒了。自从我岳父去年4月做了膝盖手术，上下楼梯都很困难。\n[11:00.71]W: I''m sorry to hear that. And if you need any help to find transportation for the whole family, we can definitely recommend someone for you.｜女：听到这个消息我很抱歉。如果您需要帮助来为家人寻找交通工具的话，我们可以为你推荐一个人。\n[11:08.69]M: We were thinking of renting a car, but we will explore all the options available for sure.｜男：我们曾考虑租车，但我们肯定会考虑所有可用的选择。\n[11:14.00]So yes, that would be very helpful in comparing prices. We''re also wondering what tours and day trips are available.｜是的，这对比较价格很有帮助。我们还想知道有哪些旅游团和一日游。\n[11:21.45]W: We have bunches of brochures here.｜女：我们这里有一捆小册子。\n[11:23.89]I would recommend getting out on a boat trip.｜我建议出去坐船旅行。\n[11:26.64]The kids will love it, and there are so many islands nearby to explore.｜孩子们会喜欢的，附近有很多岛屿可以玩耍。\n[11:31.25]There''s also a great night market further into town that has all kinds of food and cool little shops selling souvenirs and local jewelry and clothing made by hand.｜镇上还有一个很棒的夜市，里面有各种各样的食物和很酷的小商店，出售手工制作的纪念品、珠宝和服装。\n[11:42.06]M: That all sounds marvelous.｜男：这一切听起来太棒了。\n[11:44.78]W: Now, all I need is to photocopy your passports, and then I can get you all checked in and show you to your rooms.｜女：现在，我需要复印你们的护照，然后我就可以办理入住手续，带你们去房间。\n[11:52.60]Questions 12 to 15 are based on the conversation you have just heard.｜请根据你刚听到的对话回答第12至15题。\n[11:58.38]12. Who is the man talking to in the conversation?｜12. 对话中的男士在和谁说话？\n[12:18.15]13. What do we learn about the man''s father-in-law from the conversation?｜13. 从对话中，我们知道男子岳父的什么情况？\n[12:39.27]14. Why does the man say they will explore all the options available?｜14. 为什么男士说他们会考虑所有可用的选择？\n[12:59.16]15. What does the woman suggest the man and his family do close to the end of the conversation?｜15. 在对话末尾，女士建议男士及其家人做什么？', NOW(), NOW()
