ploy deceptive strategies when assigned an agent to negotiate on their behalf.\n当参与者被指派人工智能代理人代表他们进行谈判时，他们更愿意采用欺骗性策略。\n\nQuestions 16 to 18 are based on the passage you have just heard.\n请根据你刚听到的短文回答第16至18题。\n\n16. What does the passage say about artificial intelligence agents?\n16. 关于人工智能代理，短文说了什么？\n\n17. What does the new study want to find out about using an artificial intelligence agent?\n17. 关于使用人工智能代理，这项新研究想了解什么？\n\n18. What did participants tend to do when assigned an AI agent to negotiate on their behalf?\n18. 当参与者被指派人工智能代理代表他们进行谈判时，他们倾向于做什么？', 109, 1415.93, 833.80, 942.71, 990.10, 1010.10, 931.47, 934.78, 'cet4-2023-12-2-g06', 'PASSAGE', '[13:53.80]Passage One｜短文一\n[13:55.69]Artificial intelligence agents play ever more influential roles in our lives.｜人工智能代理在我们的生活中扮演着越来越有影响力的角色。\n[14:02.16]They do everything from suggesting new friends to recommending purchases.｜他们可以做任何事情，从推荐新朋友到推荐购买。\n[14:07.42]They are even beginning to drive our cars.｜他们甚至开始开我们的车。\n[14:10.55]Another role that they are expected to take over is negotiating on our behalf in commercial transactions or legal disputes.｜他们预计将接管的另一个角色是代表我们在商业交易或法律纠纷中进行谈判。\n[14:19.85]So, it''s important to know whether using an artificial intelligence agent might affect how we negotiate.｜因此，了解使用人工智能代理是否会影响我们的谈判方式是很重要的。\n[14:27.53]Research indicates that it does.｜研究也表明确实如此。\n[14:30.24]In a new study, participants were told to imagine that they were negotiating for something important to them, like a house.｜在一项新的研究中，参与者被要求想象他们正在为一些对自己重要的事情进行谈判，比如房子。\n[14:38.39]Next, they were told either that they would negotiate for themselves, or they would program an artificial intelligence agent to negotiate for them.｜接下来，他们被告知要么自己谈判，要么编程一个人工智能代理为他们谈判。\n[14:48.64]Participants then completed a survey, indicating how tough, deceptive and pleasant or otherwise they wanted to be or wanted their agent to be in the negotiations.｜然后，参与者完成了一项调查，表明他们希望自己或代理人在谈判中表现得多么强硬、欺骗性和愉快。\n[15:00.88]For example, participants could choose to be tough by making an opening demand far greater than what they''d be willing to accept.｜例如，参与者可以选择强硬，提出远大于他们愿意接受的开放要求。\n[15:09.37]They could also choose to express sympathy with their opponent to appear pleasant.｜他们也可以选择表达对对手的同情，以表现得愉快。\n[15:14.86]But they could also indicate that they, or their agent, would strategically express anger toward the opponent to gain advantage.｜但他们也可以表示自己或代理人会战略性地向对手表达愤怒，以获得优势。\n[15:23.27]Or they could opt to convey dissatisfaction with the encounter so that the other party would think they were losing interest.｜或者，他们可以选择表达对这次遭遇的不满，这样对方就会认为他们正在失去兴趣。\n[15:31.47]These are both examples of deceptive strategies.｜这些都是欺骗性策略的例子。\n[15:35.08]Participants were more willing to employ deceptive strategies when assigned an agent to negotiate on their behalf.｜当参与者被指派人工智能代理人代表他们进行谈判时，他们更愿意采用欺骗性策略。\n[15:42.71]Questions 16 to 18 are based on the passage you have just heard.｜请根据你刚听到的短文回答第16至18题。\n[15:48.72]16. What does the passage say about artificial intelligence agents?｜16. 关于人工智能代理，短文说了什么？\n[16:09.68]17. What does the new study want to find out about using an artificial intelligence agent?｜17. 关于使用人工智能代理，这项新研究想了解什么？\n[16:30.10]18. What did participants tend to do when assigned an AI agent to negotiate on their behalf?｜18. 当参与者被指派人工智能代理代表他们进行谈判时，他们倾向于做什么？', NOW(), NOW()
