SELECT
  @a_cet4_2024_06_1_03, '/audio/exams/listening-cet4-2024-06-1.mp3', 'News Report Two\n新闻二\n\nA new study has cast doubt on historic research suggesting that the season or month of someone''s birth is associated with an increased risk of certain mental health conditions.\n一项新的研究对历史研究提出了质疑，历史研究表明，一个人出生的季节或月份与某些心理健康状况的风险增加有关。\n\nThe study looks at symptoms of anxiety and depression among more than 70,000 older adults in Europe.\n这项新研究调查了欧洲7万多名老年人的焦虑和抑郁症状。\n\nA number of past studies have found the link between season of birth and mental health diagnoses.\n过去的一些研究发现了出生季节与心理健康诊断结果之间存在联系。\n\nResearchers have suggested that such links could arise from various things.\n研究人员认为，这种联系可能源于多种因素。\n\nThese include nutrient intake, sun exposure, climate, and disease exposure varying across the course of the year.\n这些因素包括一年中营养摄入、日晒、气候和疾病暴露的变化情况。\n\nHowever, evidence has been mixed.\n然而，这方面的证据并不一致。\n\nMore recent studies have suggested that factors such as social class or economic background have more to do with these diagnoses than month of birth.\n更多最近的研究表明，与出生月份相比，社会阶层或经济背景等因素与这些诊断结果更有关系。\n\nOverall, the new study found no significant relationship between participants'' month of birth and symptoms of depression or anxiety.\n总体而言，这项新研究发现，研究对象的出生月份与抑郁或焦虑症状之间没有显著关系。\n\nThere was some variability in some countries.\n但在一些国家存在一些差异。\n\nIn Poland, depressive symptoms fluctuated a little depending on birth month.\n在波兰，抑郁症状随出生月份的不同而略有波动。\n\nIn the Czech Republic, the same was true of anxiety symptoms.\n在捷克共和国，焦虑症状也是如此。\n\nBut on the whole, there was no systematic pattern.\n但总的来说，没有发现系统性的规律。\n\nQuestions 3 and 4 are based on the news report you have just heard.\n请根据你刚听到的新闻报道回答第3题和第4题。\n\n3. What have a number of past studies found about season of birth?\n3. 关于出生季节，过去的一些研究有什么发现？\n\n4. What did the new study find about the relationship between participants'' month of birth and symptoms of depression?\n4. 关于研究对象的出生月份与抑郁症状之间的关系，这项新研究发现了什么？', 85, 1409.83, 157.82, 242.97, 248.30, 269.48, 159.82, 172.70, 'cet4-2024-06-1-g02', 'NEWS', '[02:37.82]News Report Two｜新闻二\n[02:39.82]A new study has cast doubt on historic research suggesting that the season or month of someone''s birth is associated with an increased risk of certain mental health conditions.｜一项新的研究对历史研究提出了质疑，历史研究表明，一个人出生的季节或月份与某些心理健康状况的风险增加有关。\n[02:53.00]The study looks at symptoms of anxiety and depression among more than 70,000 older adults in Europe.｜这项新研究调查了欧洲7万多名老年人的焦虑和抑郁症状。\n[03:00.96]A number of past studies have found the link between season of birth and mental health diagnoses.｜过去的一些研究发现了出生季节与心理健康诊断结果之间存在联系。\n[03:08.35]Researchers have suggested that such links could arise from various things.｜研究人员认为，这种联系可能源于多种因素。\n[03:13.22]These include nutrient intake, sun exposure, climate, and disease exposure varying across the course of the year.｜这些因素包括一年中营养摄入、日晒、气候和疾病暴露的变化情况。\n[03:22.47]However, evidence has been mixed.｜然而，这方面的证据并不一致。\n[03:25.53]More recent studies have suggested that factors such as social class or economic background have more to do with these diagnoses than month of birth.｜更多最近的研究表明，与出生月份相比，社会阶层或经济背景等因素与这些诊断结果更有关系。\n[03:35.92]Overall, the new study found no significant relationship between participants'' month of birth and symptoms of depression or anxiety.｜总体而言，这项新研究发现，研究对象的出生月份与抑郁或焦虑症状之间没有显著关系。\n[03:45.94]There was some variability in some countries.｜但在一些国家存在一些差异。\n[03:49.15]In Poland, depressive symptoms fluctuated a little depending on birth month.｜在波兰，抑郁症状随出生月份的不同而略有波动。\n[03:55.06]In the Czech Republic, the same was true of anxiety symptoms.｜在捷克共和国，焦虑症状也是如此。\n[03:59.68]But on the whole, there was no systematic pattern.｜但总的来说，没有发现系统性的规律。\n[04:02.97]Questions 3 and 4 are based on the news report you have just heard.｜请根据你刚听到的新闻报道回答第3题和第4题。\n[04:08.30]3. What have a number of past studies found about season of birth?｜3. 关于出生季节，过去的一些研究有什么发现？\n[04:29.78]4. What did the new study find about the relationship between participants'' month of birth and symptoms of depression?｜4. 关于研究对象的出生月份与抑郁症状之间的关系，这项新研究发现了什么？', NOW(), NOW()
