  (`question_id`, `audio_url`, `transcript`, `duration_seconds`, `audio_total_seconds`, `audio_start_seconds`, `audio_end_seconds`, `question_start_seconds`, `question_end_seconds`, `answer_start_seconds`, `answer_end_seconds`, `group_key`, `listening_type`, `lrc_content`, `created_at`, `updated_at`)
SELECT
  @a_cet4_2024_06_1_08, '/audio/exams/listening-cet4-2024-06-1.mp3', 'Conversation One\n对话一\n\nW: Tom, did you see the article online about the new TV series based on the book The Three-Body Problem?\n女：汤姆，你看到网上那篇关于改编自《三体》一书的新电视剧的文章了吗？\n\nM: A colleague mentioned the book, but I''ve been so busy writing my thesis that I haven''t been able to read for pleasure in months.\n男：有位同事提到过这本书，但我一直忙着写论文，已经好几个月都没能读书消遣了。\n\nW: Well, sounds like if you''re going to read anything for fun, this is the book.\n女：好吧，听起来如果你想读什么书来消遣的话，这本书正合适。\n\nIt''s written by a Chinese science fiction writer.\n这本书是一位中国科幻作家写的。\n\nI can''t remember his name, but he''s written three books in all, and The Three-Body Problem is the first in the series.\n我不记得他的名字了，但他总共写了三本书，《三体》是这个系列的第一本。\n\nI don''t want to say too much and spoil it for you.\n我不想说太多，以免破坏了你的阅读体验。\n\nBut it''s definitely got some amazing technological and sociological concepts in it.\n但书中确实包含了一些令人惊叹的科技和社会学概念。\n\nM: It does sound like it would suit my taste.\n男：听起来确实很符合我的口味。\n\nBut if they are making a TV series based on it now, I don''t know if I should read the book or watch the show first.\n但如果他们现在要把它改编成电视剧，我不知道我是应该先看书，还是先看剧。\n\nW: I think it''s better to read the book first.\n女：我认为最好先看书。\n\nIt''s rare for the show or movie to be better than the book.\n很少有电视剧或电影比书更好。\n\nAnd then, you just end up ruining the book for yourself, if the show isn''t very good.\n而且，如果电视剧不好看，你就会毁了自己对这本书的印象。\n\nM: When is the show supposed to start?\n男：电视剧什么时候开播？\n\nI''m a bit overwhelmed with the amount of data I still need to collect to finish my thesis.\n我还需要收集大量的数据来完成我的论文，有点忙不过来。\n\nBut I still need to relax sometimes.\n但我偶尔也需要放松一下。\n\nW: I can''t remember exactly.\n女：我记不清了。\n\nIt''s pretty soon, and it''s going to be quite long. There are 24 episodes.\n应该很快就会开播，而且剧集很长，总共有24集。\n\nWell, maybe you could download an electronic copy of the book and try to read it before the show starts.\n嗯，也许你可以下载这本书的电子版，试着在电视剧开播前读一读。\n\nM: That''s a good idea.\n男：这是个好主意。\n\nAnd then, maybe we can watch the series together.\n然后，也许我们可以一起看这部电视剧。\n\nThanks for the tip, Alice.\n谢谢你的建议，艾丽斯。\n\nW: No problem.\n女：不客气。\n\nQuestions 8 to 11 are based on the conversation you have just heard.\n请根据你刚听到的对话回答第8至11题。\n\n8. How did the man get to know about the book The Three-Body Problem?\n8. 男士是如何知道《三体》这本书的？\n\n9. What does the woman say she can''t remember about the book''s author?\n9. 女士说关于这本书的作者，她不记得的是什么？\n\n10. What does the man have to do to finish his thesis?\n10. 男士必须做些什么才能完成他的论文？\n\n11. What will the man most probably do first after the conversation?\n11. 对话结束后，男士最有可能先做什么？', 95, 1409.83, 462.06, 557.34, 562.80, 583.85, NULL, NULL, 'cet4-2024-06-1-g04', 'LONG_DIALOGUE', '[07:42.06]Conversation One｜对话一\n[07:44.01]W: Tom, did you see the article online about the new TV series based on the book The Three-Body Problem?｜女：汤姆，你看到网上那篇关于改编自《三体》一书的新电视剧的文章了吗？\n[07:51.53]M: A colleague mentioned the book, but I''ve been so busy writing my thesis that I haven''t been able to read for pleasure in months.｜男：有位同事提到过这本书，但我一直忙着写论文，已经好几个月都没能读书消遣了。\n[07:59.00]W: Well, sounds like if you''re going to read anything for fun, this is the book.｜女：好吧，听起来如果你想读什么书来消遣的话，这本书正合适。\n[08:03.57]It''s written by a Chinese science fiction writer.｜这本书是一位中国科幻作家写的。\n[08:06.52]I can''t remember his name, but he''s written three books in all, and The Three-Body Problem is the first in the series.｜我不记得他的名字了，但他总共写了三本书，《三体》是这个系列的第一本。\n[08:14.06]I don''t want to say too much and spoil it for you.｜我不想说太多，以免破坏了你的阅读体验。\n[08:17.28]But it''s definitely got some amazing technological and sociological concepts in it.｜但书中确实包含了一些令人惊叹的科技和社会学概念。\n[08:23.28]M: It does sound like it would suit my taste.｜男：听起来确实很符合我的口味。\n[08:26.56]But if they are making a TV series based on it now, I don''t know if I should read the book or watch the show first.｜但如果他们现在要把它改编成电视剧，我不知道我是应该先看书，还是先看剧。\n[08:33.99]W: I think it''s better to read the book first.｜女：我认为最好先看书。\n[08:36.55]It''s rare for the show or movie to be better than the book.｜很少有电视剧或电影比书更好。\n[08:39.90]And then, you just end up ruining the book for yourself, if the show isn''t very good.｜而且，如果电视剧不好看，你就会毁了自己对这本书的印象。\n[08:44.87]M: When is the show supposed to start?｜男：电视剧什么时候开播？\n[08:47.23]I''m a bit overwhelmed with the amount of data I still need to collect to finish my thesis.｜我还需要收集大量的数据来完成我的论文，有点忙不过来。\n[08:52.40]But I still need to relax sometimes.｜但我偶尔也需要放松一下。\n[08:55.40]W: I can''t remember exactly.｜女：我记不清了。\n[08:57.23]It''s pretty soon, and it''s going to be quite long. There are 24 episodes.｜应该很快就会开播，而且剧集很长，总共有24集。\n[09:02.82]Well, maybe you could download an electronic copy of the book and try to read it before the show starts.｜嗯，也许你可以下载这本书的电子版，试着在电视剧开播前读一读。\n[09:09.12]M: That''s a good idea.｜男：这是个好主意。\n[09:10.60]And then, maybe we can watch the series together.｜然后，也许我们可以一起看这部电视剧。\n[09:13.76]Thanks for the tip, Alice.｜谢谢你的建议，艾丽斯。\n[09:15.84]W: No problem.｜女：不客气。\n[09:17.34]Questions 8 to 11 are based on the conversation you have just heard.｜请根据你刚听到的对话回答第8至11题。\n[09:22.80]8. How did the man get to know about the book The Three-Body Problem?｜8. 男士是如何知道《三体》这本书的？\n[09:44.15]9. What does the woman say she can''t remember about the book''s author?｜9. 女士说关于这本书的作者，她不记得的是什么？\n[10:04.66]10. What does the man have to do to finish his thesis?｜10. 男士必须做些什么才能完成他的论文？\n[10:22.64]11. What will the man most probably do first after the conversation?｜11. 对话结束后，男士最有可能先做什么？', NOW(), NOW()
