SELECT
  @a_cet4_2024_06_1_17, '/audio/exams/listening-cet4-2024-06-1.mp3', 'Passage One\n短文一\n\nSupporters call it wild camping.\n支持者称之为野外露营。\n\nOpponents call it illegal camping.\n而反对者称之为非法露营。\n\nWhat both sides accept is that there has been a boom in the past few months, with increasing numbers of visitors pitching their tents on any bit of land they fancy in the UK.\n双方都承认，在过去几个月里，随着越来越多的游客在英国任何一块他们喜欢的土地上搭起帐篷，露营热逐渐兴起。\n\nIn part, this reflects the fact that official campsites have been wholly or partially closed, or are overflowing in a summer when fewer people are going abroad.\n这在一定程度上反映了一个事实：官方露营地要不被全部或部分关闭，要不就是在出国人数减少的夏天人满为患。\n\nIt is also cheap, at a time when many are worried about what the economic future holds.\n在许多人担心经济前景的时候，露营也是一种经济实惠的选择。\n\nBut it may also be an expression of a desire for going outdoors, a response to the months of lockdown.\n但这也可能表达了人们对户外活动的渴望，是人们对数月封锁的回应。\n\nMost of the coverage of the boom in wild camping has been negative.\n大多数关于野外露营热潮的报道都是负面的。\n\nCamping in public parks has now been banned for August and the early part of September, because campers dump litter, human waste, and even their tents on the grassland.8\n月和9月初禁止在公园露营，因为露营者将垃圾、人类排泄物甚至他们的帐篷丢弃在草地上。\n\nSimilar action has been taken even in Scotland, where camping is usually permitted on most of its open land.\n就连大部分空地通常都允许露营的苏格兰也采取了类似的行动。\n\nClearly, there have to be rules.\n显然，露营必须有规则。\n\nIt would make sense that wild campers need to ask for permission to camp from landowners, especially outside Scotland, where the law is far more restrictive.\n露营者需要向土地所有者申请露营许可，这是有道理的，尤其是在苏格兰以外的地区，那里的法律限制要严格得多。\n\nIt would be common sense for people to use small tents and leave no trace of their visit.\n人们要使用小帐篷，并且不留下他们到访的痕迹，这将成为常识。\n\nThey''ve been attracted by a patch of land that is close to wilderness, and it is their responsibility to keep it that way.\n他们被一片接近荒野的土地所吸引，那他们就有责任维持这片土地的原貌。\n\nQuestions 16 to 18 are based on the passage you have just heard.\n请根据你刚听到的短文回答第16至18题。\n\n16. Why has wild camping become popular in the UK?\n16. 为什么野外露营在英国变得流行？\n\n17. Why is camping banned for part of the summer in public parks?\n17. 为什么夏天的部分时间禁止在公园露营？\n\n18. What does the speaker suggest campers do?\n18. 讲话者建议露营者做什么？', 98, 1409.83, 854.01, 952.19, 976.97, 997.83, NULL, NULL, 'cet4-2024-06-1-g06', 'PASSAGE', '[14:14.01]Passage One｜短文一\n[14:16.54]Supporters call it wild camping.｜支持者称之为野外露营。\n[14:19.81]Opponents call it illegal camping.｜而反对者称之为非法露营。\n[14:22.71]What both sides accept is that there has been a boom in the past few months, with increasing numbers of visitors pitching their tents on any bit of land they fancy in the UK.｜双方都承认，在过去几个月里，随着越来越多的游客在英国任何一块他们喜欢的土地上搭起帐篷，露营热逐渐兴起。\n[14:34.35]In part, this reflects the fact that official campsites have been wholly or partially closed, or are overflowing in a summer when fewer people are going abroad.｜这在一定程度上反映了一个事实：官方露营地要不被全部或部分关闭，要不就是在出国人数减少的夏天人满为患。\n[14:45.39]It is also cheap, at a time when many are worried about what the economic future holds.｜在许多人担心经济前景的时候，露营也是一种经济实惠的选择。\n[14:52.25]But it may also be an expression of a desire for going outdoors, a response to the months of lockdown.｜但这也可能表达了人们对户外活动的渴望，是人们对数月封锁的回应。\n[15:00.09]Most of the coverage of the boom in wild camping has been negative.｜大多数关于野外露营热潮的报道都是负面的。\n[15:05.14]Camping in public parks has now been banned for August and the early part of September, because campers dump litter, human waste, and even their tents on the grassland.8｜月和9月初禁止在公园露营，因为露营者将垃圾、人类排泄物甚至他们的帐篷丢弃在草地上。\n[15:17.46]Similar action has been taken even in Scotland, where camping is usually permitted on most of its open land.｜就连大部分空地通常都允许露营的苏格兰也采取了类似的行动。\n[15:24.64]Clearly, there have to be rules.｜显然，露营必须有规则。\n[15:27.59]It would make sense that wild campers need to ask for permission to camp from landowners, especially outside Scotland, where the law is far more restrictive.｜露营者需要向土地所有者申请露营许可，这是有道理的，尤其是在苏格兰以外的地区，那里的法律限制要严格得多。\n[15:38.86]It would be common sense for people to use small tents and leave no trace of their visit.｜人们要使用小帐篷，并且不留下他们到访的痕迹，这将成为常识。\n[15:44.43]They''ve been attracted by a patch of land that is close to wilderness, and it is their responsibility to keep it that way.｜他们被一片接近荒野的土地所吸引，那他们就有责任维持这片土地的原貌。\n[15:52.19]Questions 16 to 18 are based on the passage you have just heard.｜请根据你刚听到的短文回答第16至18题。\n[15:57.43]16. Why has wild camping become popular in the UK?｜16. 为什么野外露营在英国变得流行？\n[16:16.97]17. Why is camping banned for part of the summer in public parks?｜17. 为什么夏天的部分时间禁止在公园露营？\n[16:38.13]18. What does the speaker suggest campers do?｜18. 讲话者建议露营者做什么？', NOW(), NOW()
