INSERT INTO `listening_audio`
  (`question_id`, `audio_url`, `transcript`, `duration_seconds`, `audio_total_seconds`, `audio_start_seconds`, `audio_end_seconds`, `question_start_seconds`, `question_end_seconds`, `answer_start_seconds`, `answer_end_seconds`, `group_key`, `listening_type`, `lrc_content`, `created_at`, `updated_at`)
SELECT
  @a_cet4_2024_06_1_19, '/audio/exams/listening-cet4-2024-06-1.mp3', 'Passage Two\n短文二\n\nImagine boating down the Amazon River, minding your own business—calmly keeping an eye out for alarmingly large snakes—and a curious pink dolphin appears to swim alongside.\n想象一下，你正沿着亚马孙河划船，想着自己的事，冷静地盯着大得惊人的蛇，一只好奇的粉红河豚出现在旁边游来游去。\n\nWhile this may seem like a mythical creature, pink dolphins do exist in the Amazon region.\n虽然粉红河豚看起来像是一种神话里的生物，但它确实存在于亚马孙地区。\n\nThe Amazon river dolphin is a giant among its species.\n亚马孙河豚是同类物种中的庞然大物。\n\nIt can measure up to two metres long and weigh around 204 kilograms.\n它的体长可达两米，重约204千克。\n\nSize isn''t the only thing that sets the Amazon river dolphin apart.\n体形并不是亚马孙河豚与众不同的唯一原因。\n\nThriving in South American rivers and temporary lakes caused by seasonal flooding, this freshwater dolphin is sometimes shockingly pink.\n这种淡水豚生长在南美洲的河流和季节性洪水形成的临时湖泊中，有时会呈现出令人震惊的粉红色。\n\nAlthough born gray, males of the species are easily identified as they enter adulthood by a decisive pink shade.\n虽然雄性亚马孙河豚出生时是灰色的，但在进入成年期后，它们的体表会呈现出明显的粉红色，从而很容易被识别。\n\nTheir unusual coloring is believed to be the result of scar tissue from dolphin fights, whether playfighting or a serious bid for a mate.\n它们不同寻常的颜色被认为是源自它们打斗时留下的疤痕组织，无论这种打斗是嬉戏还是为争夺配偶而进行的激烈斗争。\n\nThe deeper the pink, the more attractive the males are believed to be, and the older the male, the more pink he will have.\n粉红色越深，雄性河豚就越有吸引力。而且年龄越大，它们身上的粉红色就越多。\n\nThere''s also a theory that this color helps the dolphins more readily blend in with their surroundings.\n还有一种理论认为，这种颜色有助于河豚更容易融入周围环境。\n\nDuring heavy rains, rivers along the Amazon rainforest turn a pink shade, and with their pink coloring, male dolphins are harder to detect.\n在暴雨期间，亚马孙雨林沿岸的河流会变成粉红色，这样雄性河豚就更难被发现了。\n\nThe Amazon wetland system, fed by the Amazon River, is a crucial place for pink dolphins to breed, and since 2018 has been granted internationally protected status.\n亚马孙湿地以亚马孙河为水源，是粉红河豚繁殖的重要区域，自2018年以来，该地已被授予国际保护地位。\n\nQuestions 19 to 21 are based on the passage you have just heard.\n请根据你刚听到的短文回答第19至21题。\n\n19. What does the passage say about pink dolphins?\n19. 关于粉红河豚，短文说了什么？\n\n20. What is the unusual coloring of pink dolphins believed to originate in?\n20. 粉红河豚不同寻常的颜色被认为源于什么？\n\n21. What has become of the Amazon wetland system since 2018?\n21. 自2018年以来，亚马孙湿地系统的情况如何？', 105, 1409.83, 1017.79, 1123.18, 1128.85, 1148.53, 1033.77, 1039.94, 'cet4-2024-06-1-g07', 'PASSAGE', '[16:57.79]Passage Two｜短文二\n[16:59.86]Imagine boating down the Amazon River, minding your own business—calmly keeping an eye out for alarmingly large snakes—and a curious pink dolphin appears to swim alongside.｜想象一下，你正沿着亚马孙河划船，想着自己的事，冷静地盯着大得惊人的蛇，一只好奇的粉红河豚出现在旁边游来游去。\n[17:13.77]While this may seem like a mythical creature, pink dolphins do exist in the Amazon region.｜虽然粉红河豚看起来像是一种神话里的生物，但它确实存在于亚马孙地区。\n[17:20.24]The Amazon river dolphin is a giant among its species.｜亚马孙河豚是同类物种中的庞然大物。\n[17:24.57]It can measure up to two metres long and weigh around 204 kilograms.｜它的体长可达两米，重约204千克。\n[17:30.54]Size isn''t the only thing that sets the Amazon river dolphin apart.｜体形并不是亚马孙河豚与众不同的唯一原因。\n[17:36.04]Thriving in South American rivers and temporary lakes caused by seasonal flooding, this freshwater dolphin is sometimes shockingly pink.｜这种淡水豚生长在南美洲的河流和季节性洪水形成的临时湖泊中，有时会呈现出令人震惊的粉红色。\n[17:46.31]Although born gray, males of the species are easily identified as they enter adulthood by a decisive pink shade.｜虽然雄性亚马孙河豚出生时是灰色的，但在进入成年期后，它们的体表会呈现出明显的粉红色，从而很容易被识别。\n[17:54.85]Their unusual coloring is believed to be the result of scar tissue from dolphin fights, whether playfighting or a serious bid for a mate.｜它们不同寻常的颜色被认为是源自它们打斗时留下的疤痕组织，无论这种打斗是嬉戏还是为争夺配偶而进行的激烈斗争。\n[18:05.09]The deeper the pink, the more attractive the males are believed to be, and the older the male, the more pink he will have.｜粉红色越深，雄性河豚就越有吸引力。而且年龄越大，它们身上的粉红色就越多。\n[18:12.59]There''s also a theory that this color helps the dolphins more readily blend in with their surroundings.｜还有一种理论认为，这种颜色有助于河豚更容易融入周围环境。\n[18:19.50]During heavy rains, rivers along the Amazon rainforest turn a pink shade, and with their pink coloring, male dolphins are harder to detect.｜在暴雨期间，亚马孙雨林沿岸的河流会变成粉红色，这样雄性河豚就更难被发现了。\n[18:29.81]The Amazon wetland system, fed by the Amazon River, is a crucial place for pink dolphins to breed, and since 2018 has been granted internationally protected status.｜亚马孙湿地以亚马孙河为水源，是粉红河豚繁殖的重要区域，自2018年以来，该地已被授予国际保护地位。\n[18:43.18]Questions 19 to 21 are based on the passage you have just heard.｜请根据你刚听到的短文回答第19至21题。\n[18:48.85]19. What does the passage say about pink dolphins?｜19. 关于粉红河豚，短文说了什么？\n[19:08.83]20. What is the unusual coloring of pink dolphins believed to originate in?｜20. 粉红河豚不同寻常的颜色被认为源于什么？\n[19:31.86]21. What has become of the Amazon wetland system since 2018?｜21. 自2018年以来，亚马孙湿地系统的情况如何？', NOW(), NOW()
