  @a_cet4_2024_06_2_02, '/audio/exams/listening-cet4-2024-06-2.mp3', 'News Report One\n新闻一\n\nA JetBlue Airlines flight from West Palm Beach to New York City was forced to turn around and land Sunday morning after the plane struck a bird.\n周日上午，捷蓝航空公司一架从西棕榈滩飞往纽约市的飞机在撞上一只鸟后被迫掉头降落。\n\nThe flight from Palm Beach International Airport to LaGuardia Airport turned around just minutes after takeoff following the strike.\n从棕榈滩国际机场飞往拉瓜迪亚机场的航班在起飞几分钟后就因撞鸟而掉头折返。\n\nNo injuries were reported on the plane, and the flight took off once again seven and a half hours after the first attempt.\n据报道，飞机上没有人员受伤，在首次尝试起飞的七个半小时后，飞机再次起飞。\n\n“It was like a split second of panic that resulted in this nervous reaction on the plane,” said passenger Brian Healy.\n乘客布雷恩·希利说：“这就像一瞬间的恐慌，导致了飞机上的紧张反应。”\n\n“There was total quiet, and then there was relief when the plane came to a stop.” “\n当时一片寂静，飞机停下来时，人们才如释重负。”\n\nAn email from JetBlue read, “Our team is working to accommodate customers on later flights.”\n捷蓝航空的一封电子邮件写道：“我们的团队正在努力安排乘客乘坐后续的航班。”\n\nQuestions 1 and 2 are based on the news report you have just heard.\n请根据你刚听到的新闻报道回答第1题和第2题。\n\n1. What do we learn about the JetBlue Airlines flight from the news report?\n1. 从新闻报道中我们对捷蓝航空的航班情况有何了解？\n\n2. How did the passengers feel when the plane came to a stop, according to Brian Healy?\n2. 据布雷恩·希利所说，飞机停下来时乘客们的感受如何？', 59, 1398.46, 37.41, 96.20, 125.75, 145.75, NULL, NULL, 'cet4-2024-06-2-g01', 'NEWS', '[00:37.41]News Report One｜新闻一\n[00:39.64]A JetBlue Airlines flight from West Palm Beach to New York City was forced to turn around and land Sunday morning after the plane struck a bird.｜周日上午，捷蓝航空公司一架从西棕榈滩飞往纽约市的飞机在撞上一只鸟后被迫掉头降落。\n[00:52.26]The flight from Palm Beach International Airport to LaGuardia Airport turned around just minutes after takeoff following the strike.｜从棕榈滩国际机场飞往拉瓜迪亚机场的航班在起飞几分钟后就因撞鸟而掉头折返。\n[01:02.09]No injuries were reported on the plane, and the flight took off once again seven and a half hours after the first attempt.｜据报道，飞机上没有人员受伤，在首次尝试起飞的七个半小时后，飞机再次起飞。\n[01:11.59]“It was like a split second of panic that resulted in this nervous reaction on the plane,” said passenger Brian Healy.｜乘客布雷恩·希利说：“这就像一瞬间的恐慌，导致了飞机上的紧张反应。”\n[01:20.90]“There was total quiet, and then there was relief when the plane came to a stop.” “｜当时一片寂静，飞机停下来时，人们才如释重负。”\n[01:27.80]An email from JetBlue read, “Our team is working to accommodate customers on later flights.”｜捷蓝航空的一封电子邮件写道：“我们的团队正在努力安排乘客乘坐后续的航班。”\n[01:36.20]Questions 1 and 2 are based on the news report you have just heard.｜请根据你刚听到的新闻报道回答第1题和第2题。\n[01:43.51]1. What do we learn about the JetBlue Airlines flight from the news report?｜1. 从新闻报道中我们对捷蓝航空的航班情况有何了解？\n[02:05.75]2. How did the passengers feel when the plane came to a stop, according to Brian Healy?｜2. 据布雷恩·希利所说，飞机停下来时乘客们的感受如何？', NOW(), NOW()
