SELECT
  @a_cet4_2024_06_2_03, '/audio/exams/listening-cet4-2024-06-2.mp3', 'News Report Two\n新闻二\n\nA deadly snake which had finally been tracked down after escaping a zoo has slipped away for the second time.\n一条致命毒蛇在逃离动物园后终于被找到了，但它又第二次溜走了。\n\nThe poisonous snake forced the closure of the attraction last week when staff noticed the disappearance.\n上周，当工作人员注意到这条毒蛇失踪时，动物园被迫关门。\n\nAfter six days of desperate searching, he was eventually found and placed in a supposedly secure area.\n经过六天的全力搜寻，这条毒蛇最终被找到，并被安置在一个据称安全的区域。\n\nBut it seems the animal is no fan of the zoo, because yet again he is out on the loose.\n但这条蛇似乎并不喜欢动物园，因为它又一次逃脱了。\n\nThe snake is a relative newcomer to the zoo but has already been frustrating its staff.\n这条蛇虽是动物园的新成员，但它已经让工作人员感到沮丧。\n\nThe staff believe he squeezed himself out of a gap located around new energy-saving bulbs installed inside the snake house.\n工作人员认为，它是从蛇屋里新安装的节能灯泡周围的缝隙中挤出来的。\n\nHe was only found the first time around because staff brought in a special machine to trace him inside a wall opening.\n它第一次被找回是因为工作人员带来了一台特殊的机器，在一个墙洞里追踪到它的位置。\n\nThis kind of snake is one of the most deadly and poisonous in the wild, and they can range from three to five metres in length.\n这种蛇是野外最致命、毒性最强的蛇之一，体长可达三至五米。\n\nQuestions 3 and 4 are based on the news report you have just heard.\n请根据你刚听到的新闻报道回答第3题和第4题。\n\n3. What do we learn about the deadly snake from the news report?\n3. 从新闻报道中我们对这条致命的蛇有何了解？\n\n4. How have the zoo staff been feeling about the snake?\n4. 动物园工作人员对这条蛇有什么样的感受？', 68, 1398.46, 148.30, 216.52, 222.14, 240.43, 150.21, 157.68, 'cet4-2024-06-2-g02', 'NEWS', '[02:28.30]News Report Two｜新闻二\n[02:30.21]A deadly snake which had finally been tracked down after escaping a zoo has slipped away for the second time.｜一条致命毒蛇在逃离动物园后终于被找到了，但它又第二次溜走了。\n[02:37.98]The poisonous snake forced the closure of the attraction last week when staff noticed the disappearance.｜上周，当工作人员注意到这条毒蛇失踪时，动物园被迫关门。\n[02:46.30]After six days of desperate searching, he was eventually found and placed in a supposedly secure area.｜经过六天的全力搜寻，这条毒蛇最终被找到，并被安置在一个据称安全的区域。\n[02:54.03]But it seems the animal is no fan of the zoo, because yet again he is out on the loose.｜但这条蛇似乎并不喜欢动物园，因为它又一次逃脱了。\n[03:01.56]The snake is a relative newcomer to the zoo but has already been frustrating its staff.｜这条蛇虽是动物园的新成员，但它已经让工作人员感到沮丧。\n[03:08.26]The staff believe he squeezed himself out of a gap located around new energy-saving bulbs installed inside the snake house.｜工作人员认为，它是从蛇屋里新安装的节能灯泡周围的缝隙中挤出来的。\n[03:18.10]He was only found the first time around because staff brought in a special machine to trace him inside a wall opening.｜它第一次被找回是因为工作人员带来了一台特殊的机器，在一个墙洞里追踪到它的位置。\n[03:27.20]This kind of snake is one of the most deadly and poisonous in the wild, and they can range from three to five metres in length.｜这种蛇是野外最致命、毒性最强的蛇之一，体长可达三至五米。\n[03:36.52]Questions 3 and 4 are based on the news report you have just heard.｜请根据你刚听到的新闻报道回答第3题和第4题。\n[03:42.14]3. What do we learn about the deadly snake from the news report?｜3. 从新闻报道中我们对这条致命的蛇有何了解？\n[04:00.73]4. How have the zoo staff been feeling about the snake?｜4. 动物园工作人员对这条蛇有什么样的感受？', NOW(), NOW()
WHERE @a_cet4_2024_06_2_03 IS NOT NULL
