  (`question_id`, `audio_url`, `transcript`, `duration_seconds`, `audio_total_seconds`, `audio_start_seconds`, `audio_end_seconds`, `question_start_seconds`, `question_end_seconds`, `answer_start_seconds`, `answer_end_seconds`, `group_key`, `listening_type`, `lrc_content`, `created_at`, `updated_at`)
SELECT
  @a_cet4_2024_06_2_09, '/audio/exams/listening-cet4-2024-06-2.mp3', 'Conversation One\n对话一\n\nM: What''s the best way to teach children how to save and spend their money?\n男：教孩子们如何存钱和花钱的最好方法是什么？\n\nW: You should make money a regular topic of discussion.\n女：你应该让钱成为经常讨论的话题。\n\nIt''s best to start young. So it''s instinctive rather than a scary subject.\n最好从孩子小时候就开始，这样它就会成为一种本能，而不是一个可怕的话题。\n\nM: In our family, we talk openly about things like the budget for holidays, how taxes reduce your income, and how to shop around for the best deals.\n男：在我们家，我们公开谈论假期预算，税收是如何减少收入的以及如何货比三家买到最优惠的物品等问题。\n\nW: Indeed. It''s also essential to make money real for children through practical examples.\n女：的确如此。通过实际例子让孩子们真正了解金钱也很重要。\n\nWorking out how much we save using discount pizza coupons, for example, is much more relevant than abstract sums.\n例如，计算出使用比萨折扣券能节省多少钱，这比抽象的金额更有意义。\n\nM: We also give our kids pocket money, and the amount they get is linked to chores, such as putting the bins out and emptying the dishwasher.\n男：我们还会给孩子们零花钱，而且零花钱的数额与家务劳动挂钩，比如倒垃圾和清空洗碗机。\n\nW: We do that, too.\n女：我们也这样做。\n\nAnd it''s paid according to their age, ￡2 for each year.\n零花钱是根据他们的年龄来给的，每年涨2英镑。\n\nSo they can see some progression.\n这样他们就能看到奖励的增长。\n\nM: Teaching them to save is important.\n男：教他们储蓄很重要。\n\nWe opened the savings account when they were young.\n我们在他们小的时候就开设了储蓄账户。\n\nAfter birthdays and Christmas, they would go to the branch and deposit their gift money.\n过完生日和圣诞节后，他们就会去分行存入礼金。\n\nW: Oh, I hadn''t considered doing that.\n女：哦，我还没考虑过这样做。\n\nIn our house, we have transparent money boxes for them to put small change in.\n在我们家，我们有透明的存钱罐，他们可以把零钱放进去。\n\nSo they can see their savings grow.\n这样他们就能看到自己的存款在增加。\n\nM: When the time is right, I''ll start talking to our children about investing and show them how the money saved for their further education has grown.\n男：等时机成熟了，我会开始和孩子们讨论投资，让他们看看为升学存下的钱是如何增加的。\n\nW: I am always talking to my elder daughter about the importance of saving into a pension. She''s just started a part-time job and was thinking of not contributing to her pension.\n女：我总是和我的大女儿谈论储蓄养老金的重要性。她刚开始做兼职工作，正考虑不缴纳养老金。\n\nLuckily, I managed to persuade her otherwise.\n幸运的是，我说服了她。\n\nM: Yes, it''s such an important lesson to learn.\n男：是的，这是非常重要的一课。\n\nQuestions 8 to 11 are based on the conversation you have just heard.\n请根据你刚听到的对话回答第8至11题。\n\n8. What should we do with the topic of money according to the woman?\n8. 根据女士的说法，我们应该如何处理金钱这个话题？\n\n9. How does the woman say money can be made real for children?\n9. 女士说怎样才能让孩子们真正了解钱？\n\n10. What is the common practice between the man and the woman?\n10. 男士和女士共同的做法是什么？\n\n11. What is the woman always talking about to her elder daughter?\n11. 女士总是对她的大女儿说什么？', 105, 1398.46, 442.97, 548.00, 574.17, 593.67, NULL, NULL, 'cet4-2024-06-2-g04', 'LONG_DIALOGUE', '[07:22.97]Conversation One｜对话一\n[07:25.11]M: What''s the best way to teach children how to save and spend their money?｜男：教孩子们如何存钱和花钱的最好方法是什么？\n[07:30.73]W: You should make money a regular topic of discussion.｜女：你应该让钱成为经常讨论的话题。\n[07:34.44]It''s best to start young. So it''s instinctive rather than a scary subject.｜最好从孩子小时候就开始，这样它就会成为一种本能，而不是一个可怕的话题。\n[07:40.76]M: In our family, we talk openly about things like the budget for holidays, how taxes reduce your income, and how to shop around for the best deals.｜男：在我们家，我们公开谈论假期预算，税收是如何减少收入的以及如何货比三家买到最优惠的物品等问题。\n[07:50.25]W: Indeed. It''s also essential to make money real for children through practical examples.｜女：的确如此。通过实际例子让孩子们真正了解金钱也很重要。\n[07:56.82]Working out how much we save using discount pizza coupons, for example, is much more relevant than abstract sums.｜例如，计算出使用比萨折扣券能节省多少钱，这比抽象的金额更有意义。\n[08:05.83]M: We also give our kids pocket money, and the amount they get is linked to chores, such as putting the bins out and emptying the dishwasher.｜男：我们还会给孩子们零花钱，而且零花钱的数额与家务劳动挂钩，比如倒垃圾和清空洗碗机。\n[08:13.99]W: We do that, too.｜女：我们也这样做。\n[08:15.17]And it''s paid according to their age, ￡2 for each year.｜零花钱是根据他们的年龄来给的，每年涨2英镑。\n[08:19.18]So they can see some progression.｜这样他们就能看到奖励的增长。\n[08:21.56]M: Teaching them to save is important.｜男：教他们储蓄很重要。\n[08:23.56]We opened the savings account when they were young.｜我们在他们小的时候就开设了储蓄账户。\n[08:26.25]After birthdays and Christmas, they would go to the branch and deposit their gift money.｜过完生日和圣诞节后，他们就会去分行存入礼金。\n[08:31.53]W: Oh, I hadn''t considered doing that.｜女：哦，我还没考虑过这样做。\n[08:34.01]In our house, we have transparent money boxes for them to put small change in.｜在我们家，我们有透明的存钱罐，他们可以把零钱放进去。\n[08:39.20]So they can see their savings grow.｜这样他们就能看到自己的存款在增加。\n[08:41.16]M: When the time is right, I''ll start talking to our children about investing and show them how the money saved for their further education has grown.｜男：等时机成熟了，我会开始和孩子们讨论投资，让他们看看为升学存下的钱是如何增加的。\n[08:50.34]W: I am always talking to my elder daughter about the importance of saving into a pension. She''s just started a part-time job and was thinking of not contributing to her pension.｜女：我总是和我的大女儿谈论储蓄养老金的重要性。她刚开始做兼职工作，正考虑不缴纳养老金。\n[09:01.27]Luckily, I managed to persuade her otherwise.｜幸运的是，我说服了她。\n[09:04.33]M: Yes, it''s such an important lesson to learn.｜男：是的，这是非常重要的一课。\n[09:08.00]Questions 8 to 11 are based on the conversation you have just heard.｜请根据你刚听到的对话回答第8至11题。\n[09:13.57]8. What should we do with the topic of money according to the woman?｜8. 根据女士的说法，我们应该如何处理金钱这个话题？\n[09:34.17]9. How does the woman say money can be made real for children?｜9. 女士说怎样才能让孩子们真正了解钱？\n[09:53.97]10. What is the common practice between the man and the woman?｜10. 男士和女士共同的做法是什么？\n[10:14.54]11. What is the woman always talking about to her elder daughter?｜11. 女士总是对她的大女儿说什么？', NOW(), NOW()
