SELECT
  @a_cet4_2024_06_2_17, '/audio/exams/listening-cet4-2024-06-2.mp3', 'Passage One\n短文一\n\nI met three different people today, and each time, when I asked, “How are you?”, the reply was exactly the same “I''m busy.”\n今天我遇到了三个不同的人，每次当我问“你好吗？”，得到的回答都是一样的“我很忙”。\n\nHonestly, I hear the same answer from the vast majority of people I meet.\n老实说，我从我遇到的绝大多数人那里都听到了同样的回答。\n\nSo I started to think. Guess what? Everybody''s busy!\n所以我开始思考。你猜怎么着？每个人都很忙！\n\nI''m busy. You''re busy. Everybody''s busy.\n我很忙，你很忙，每个人都很忙。\n\nSo you being busy doesn''t make me sympathetic at all.\n所以我一点也不同情你的忙碌。\n\nBecause “busy” is the state of the world.\n因为“忙碌”是世界的状态。\n\nSo I''m launching a campaign to stop people complaining about being “busy”.\n因此，我发起了一场活动，让人们停止抱怨“忙碌”。\n\nIt may sound harsh, but the truth is, nobody cares.\n这听起来可能很苛刻，但事实是，没人在乎。\n\nIn a busy world, “being busy” doesn''t stand out, nor does it mean productive, creative, accomplished, or professional.\n在繁忙的世界里，“忙碌”并不突出，也不意味着高效、有创造力、有成就或专业。\n\nSteve Maraboli once said, “When someone tells you they are too ‘busy’, it''s not a reflection of their schedule; it''s a reflection of your spot on their schedule.”\n史蒂夫·马拉博利曾经说过：“当有人告诉你他们太‘忙’了，这并不能反映他们的日程安排很忙，而是反映了你在他们日程安排中的位置。”\n\nDonna Lynn Hope has also remarked, “Busy doesn''t mean better. I''ve never envied a busy person—the one who likes to point out their busy lives to others.”\n唐娜·林恩·霍普也说过：“忙碌并不意味着更好。我从来不羡慕忙碌的人——那种喜欢向别人说自己生活很忙碌的人。”\n\nThe reality is, nobody''s too busy.\n事实是，没有人太忙。\n\nIt''s just about priorities.\n这只是轻重缓急的问题。\n\nSo the next time someone asks you how you are, maybe respond differently.\n所以，下次有人问你过得怎么样时，你可以给出不同的回答。\n\nIn my experience, the “I''m busy” response is really covering up the fact that they''re not actually accomplishing their real purpose.\n根据我的经验，“我很忙”这个回答实际上掩盖了他们没有真正达到目的的事实。\n\nAnd “being busy” is the lie they tell themselves about why they can''t achieve it.\n而“忙碌”是他们对自己为什么不能实现这一目标所说的谎言。\n\nQuestions 16 to 18 are based on the passage you have just heard.\n请根据你刚听到的短文回答第16至18题。\n\n16. Why is the speaker launching a campaign?\n16. 讲话者为什么要发起一场活动？\n\n17. What does the speaker advise us to do next time someone asks us how we are?\n17. 下次有人问我们过得怎么样时，讲话者建议我们怎么做？\n\n18. Why do many people make the “I''m busy” response, according to the speaker?\n18. 在讲话者看来，为什么很多人会回答“我很忙”？', 96, 1398.46, 866.69, 962.84, 989.80, 1010.67, NULL, NULL, 'cet4-2024-06-2-g06', 'PASSAGE', '[14:26.69]Passage One｜短文一\n[14:28.66]I met three different people today, and each time, when I asked, “How are you?”, the reply was exactly the same “I''m busy.”｜今天我遇到了三个不同的人，每次当我问“你好吗？”，得到的回答都是一样的“我很忙”。\n[14:37.70]Honestly, I hear the same answer from the vast majority of people I meet.｜老实说，我从我遇到的绝大多数人那里都听到了同样的回答。\n[14:42.75]So I started to think. Guess what? Everybody''s busy!｜所以我开始思考。你猜怎么着？每个人都很忙！\n[14:47.03]I''m busy. You''re busy. Everybody''s busy.｜我很忙，你很忙，每个人都很忙。\n[14:50.87]So you being busy doesn''t make me sympathetic at all.｜所以我一点也不同情你的忙碌。\n[14:55.21]Because “busy” is the state of the world.｜因为“忙碌”是世界的状态。\n[14:57.87]So I''m launching a campaign to stop people complaining about being “busy”.｜因此，我发起了一场活动，让人们停止抱怨“忙碌”。\n[15:03.44]It may sound harsh, but the truth is, nobody cares.｜这听起来可能很苛刻，但事实是，没人在乎。\n[15:07.53]In a busy world, “being busy” doesn''t stand out, nor does it mean productive, creative, accomplished, or professional.｜在繁忙的世界里，“忙碌”并不突出，也不意味着高效、有创造力、有成就或专业。\n[15:16.07]Steve Maraboli once said, “When someone tells you they are too ‘busy’, it''s not a reflection of their schedule; it''s a reflection of your spot on their schedule.”｜史蒂夫·马拉博利曾经说过：“当有人告诉你他们太‘忙’了，这并不能反映他们的日程安排很忙，而是反映了你在他们日程安排中的位置。”\n[15:27.03]Donna Lynn Hope has also remarked, “Busy doesn''t mean better. I''ve never envied a busy person—the one who likes to point out their busy lives to others.”｜唐娜·林恩·霍普也说过：“忙碌并不意味着更好。我从来不羡慕忙碌的人——那种喜欢向别人说自己生活很忙碌的人。”\n[15:38.16]The reality is, nobody''s too busy.｜事实是，没有人太忙。\n[15:41.42]It''s just about priorities.｜这只是轻重缓急的问题。\n[15:43.46]So the next time someone asks you how you are, maybe respond differently.｜所以，下次有人问你过得怎么样时，你可以给出不同的回答。\n[15:48.73]In my experience, the “I''m busy” response is really covering up the fact that they''re not actually accomplishing their real purpose.｜根据我的经验，“我很忙”这个回答实际上掩盖了他们没有真正达到目的的事实。\n[15:57.19]And “being busy” is the lie they tell themselves about why they can''t achieve it.｜而“忙碌”是他们对自己为什么不能实现这一目标所说的谎言。\n[16:02.84]Questions 16 to 18 are based on the passage you have just heard.｜请根据你刚听到的短文回答第16至18题。\n[16:09.02]16. Why is the speaker launching a campaign?｜16. 讲话者为什么要发起一场活动？\n[16:29.80]17. What does the speaker advise us to do next time someone asks us how we are?｜17. 下次有人问我们过得怎么样时，讲话者建议我们怎么做？\n[16:50.97]18. Why do many people make the “I''m busy” response, according to the speaker?｜18. 在讲话者看来，为什么很多人会回答“我很忙”？', NOW(), NOW()
