SELECT
  @a_cet4_2024_06_2_19, '/audio/exams/listening-cet4-2024-06-2.mp3', 'Passage Two\n短文二\n\nMore and more people are taking up extreme sports like snowboarding, skateboarding, mountain biking, and many more.\n越来越多的人开始从事极限运动，如单板滑雪、滑板、山地自行车等等。\n\nWhy are these sports becoming so popular?\n为什么这些运动变得如此受欢迎？\n\nOne thing that extreme sports do better than perhaps anything else is to help you stop being afraid.\n极限运动比其他任何运动做得更好的一件事就是帮助你停止恐惧。\n\nIt may sound strange to say that their main function is to induce fear, but after a time, your fear response to other things in life will be dramatically reduced.\n说起这件事情可能听起来有些奇怪：极限运动的主要功能是诱发恐惧，但一段时间后，你对生活中其他事情的恐惧反应会大大减少。\n\nAfter all, if you can jump out of a plane or off a bridge, then you can face anything else easily.\n毕竟，如果你能从飞机上或从桥上跳下来，那么你就可以轻松面对其他任何事情。\n\nWhen doing extreme sports, you have to become more focused.\n在进行极限运动时，你必须更加专注。\n\nYou''ll be pushed to your limits.\n你会被逼到极限。\n\nAnd if you aren''t focused, you''ll make dangerous mistakes.\n如果注意力不集中，你就会犯危险的错误。\n\nLearning to be this focused when enjoying extreme sports will help you to be focused at work, keeping you more productive and ultimately more successful.\n在享受极限运动时学会这种专注，将有助于你在工作中保持专注，从而提高工作效率，最终取得更大的成功。\n\nIt''s great to stay fit and healthy, but standard exercise routines and sports only work the same muscles repeatedly.\n保持健康是件好事，但常规的锻炼方式和运动只会反复锻炼相同的肌肉。\n\nWith extreme sports, you''ll be working entirely different muscles, and that means you get an all-over workout.\n通过极限运动，你将锻炼完全不同的肌肉，这意味着你会得到全面的锻炼。\n\nExtreme sports also burn a lot more calories than other sports.\n极限运动消耗的卡路里也比其他运动多得多。\n\nSkateboarding, for example, can burn as many as 500 calories per hour.\n例如，滑板运动每小时可以燃烧多达500卡路里的热量。\n\nBasketball burns around 300 in the same time.\n而篮球运动在相同时间内燃烧约300卡路里。\n\nWhen you find that you can overcome the physical or mental challenges involved in extreme sports, you''ll feel superhuman and your self-confidence will be at an all-time high.\n当你发现自己能够克服极限运动带来的身体或心理挑战时，你会感到自己无所不能，自信心也会空前高涨。\n\nQuestions 19 to 21 are based on the passage you have just heard.\n请根据你刚听到的短文回答第19至21题。\n\n19. What may sound strange to say about extreme sports?\n19. 关于极限运动，什么说法听起来奇怪？\n\n20. Why should one be highly focused when doing extreme sports?\n20. 为什么在进行极限运动时要高度集中注意力？\n\n21. How can extreme sports benefit us more than standard exercise routines and sports?\n21. 极限运动如何比常规的锻炼方式和运动更能让我们受益？', 106, 1398.46, 1032.25, 1138.06, 1144.53, 1164.94, 1046.51, 1064.95, 'cet4-2024-06-2-g07', 'PASSAGE', '[17:12.25]Passage Two｜短文二\n[17:14.45]More and more people are taking up extreme sports like snowboarding, skateboarding, mountain biking, and many more.｜越来越多的人开始从事极限运动，如单板滑雪、滑板、山地自行车等等。\n[17:23.28]Why are these sports becoming so popular?｜为什么这些运动变得如此受欢迎？\n[17:26.51]One thing that extreme sports do better than perhaps anything else is to help you stop being afraid.｜极限运动比其他任何运动做得更好的一件事就是帮助你停止恐惧。\n[17:33.89]It may sound strange to say that their main function is to induce fear, but after a time, your fear response to other things in life will be dramatically reduced.｜说起这件事情可能听起来有些奇怪：极限运动的主要功能是诱发恐惧，但一段时间后，你对生活中其他事情的恐惧反应会大大减少。\n[17:45.25]After all, if you can jump out of a plane or off a bridge, then you can face anything else easily.｜毕竟，如果你能从飞机上或从桥上跳下来，那么你就可以轻松面对其他任何事情。\n[17:52.29]When doing extreme sports, you have to become more focused.｜在进行极限运动时，你必须更加专注。\n[17:57.23]You''ll be pushed to your limits.｜你会被逼到极限。\n[17:59.16]And if you aren''t focused, you''ll make dangerous mistakes.｜如果注意力不集中，你就会犯危险的错误。\n[18:02.53]Learning to be this focused when enjoying extreme sports will help you to be focused at work, keeping you more productive and ultimately more successful.｜在享受极限运动时学会这种专注，将有助于你在工作中保持专注，从而提高工作效率，最终取得更大的成功。\n[18:12.79]It''s great to stay fit and healthy, but standard exercise routines and sports only work the same muscles repeatedly.｜保持健康是件好事，但常规的锻炼方式和运动只会反复锻炼相同的肌肉。\n[18:21.88]With extreme sports, you''ll be working entirely different muscles, and that means you get an all-over workout.｜通过极限运动，你将锻炼完全不同的肌肉，这意味着你会得到全面的锻炼。\n[18:29.50]Extreme sports also burn a lot more calories than other sports.｜极限运动消耗的卡路里也比其他运动多得多。\n[18:34.88]Skateboarding, for example, can burn as many as 500 calories per hour.｜例如，滑板运动每小时可以燃烧多达500卡路里的热量。\n[18:40.62]Basketball burns around 300 in the same time.｜而篮球运动在相同时间内燃烧约300卡路里。\n[18:44.73]When you find that you can overcome the physical or mental challenges involved in extreme sports, you''ll feel superhuman and your self-confidence will be at an all-time high.｜当你发现自己能够克服极限运动带来的身体或心理挑战时，你会感到自己无所不能，自信心也会空前高涨。\n[18:58.06]Questions 19 to 21 are based on the passage you have just heard.｜请根据你刚听到的短文回答第19至21题。\n[19:04.53]19. What may sound strange to say about extreme sports?｜19. 关于极限运动，什么说法听起来奇怪？\n[19:25.24]20. Why should one be highly focused when doing extreme sports?｜20. 为什么在进行极限运动时要高度集中注意力？\n[19:46.98]21. How can extreme sports benefit us more than standard exercise routines and sports?｜21. 极限运动如何比常规的锻炼方式和运动更能让我们受益？', NOW(), NOW()
