  @a_cet4_2024_06_2_23, '/audio/exams/listening-cet4-2024-06-2.mp3', 'Passage Three\n短文三\n\nMost of us have been in teams or organizations where we''ve had conflict with the people that we''re working with around the ideas or decisions that we''re discussing.\n我们中的大多数人都曾在团队或组织中与同事就我们正在讨论的想法或决策发生过冲突。\n\nConflict is natural.\n冲突是自然的。\n\nWe all bring different life and work experiences to the table.\n我们都有不同的生活和工作经历。\n\nWe all have different personality preferences and tendencies.\n我们都有不同的性格偏好和倾向。\n\nWe''re not all going to have the same ideas on how to approach policies, programs, or problems.\n在如何处理政策、计划或问题方面，我们并非都有相同的想法。\n\nBut too often, we get caught in this place where conflict is perceived to be negative—something we want to avoid so that we can maintain the harmony of our workplace.\n但很多时候，我们会陷入这样一种境地：冲突被认为是消极的，我们想要避免冲突，以保持工作场所的和谐。\n\nThis could be because some people want to avoid conflict at all costs.\n这可能是因为有些人想不惜一切代价避免冲突。\n\nAfter all, they still have to work together.\n毕竟他们还要一起工作。\n\nBut this kind of artificial harmony isn''t the answer.\n但这种人为的和谐并不能解决问题。\n\nProductive conflict is a vital part of teams and organizations that want to push forward and do more.\n团队和组织想要向前推进、取得更多成果，有成效的冲突是必不可少的。\n\nWithout conflict, we''re often stuck in this artificial harmony where people don''t express potentially innovative ideas for fear that they may start conflict with others.\n如果没有冲突，我们往往会陷入这种人为的和谐，人们因为害怕与他人发生冲突而不敢表达潜在的有创意的想法。\n\nBut if you''re in a place where you have a basis of trust, conflict can be extremely productive.\n但是如果你处于一个有信任基础的地方，冲突就会富有成效。\n\nIt can lead to increased innovation and greater trust on teams.\n它可以激发创新，并增强团队间的信任。\n\nIt may be an uncomfortable process, but good leaders and healthy teams recognize that productive and healthy conflict is an important part of how they function.\n这个过程可能令人不太舒服，但优秀的领导者和健康的团队都认识到，有成效的、健康的冲突是他们运作的重要组成部分。\n\nQuestions 22 to 25 are based on the passage you have just heard.\n请根据你刚听到的短文回答第22至25题。\n\n22. What does the passage say about conflict in organizations?\n22. 关于组织中的冲突，短文说了什么？\n\n23. Why do some people want to avoid conflict at all costs?\n23. 为什么有些人想不惜一切代价避免冲突？\n\n24. Why is productive conflict important for teams and organizations?\n24. 为什么有成效的冲突对团队和组织很重要？\n\n25. What does productive conflict need as a basis?\n25. 有成效的冲突需要什么作为基础？', 96, 1398.46, 1209.86, 1305.97, 1332.43, 1352.21, 1239.48, 1250.61, 'cet4-2024-06-2-g08', 'PASSAGE', '[20:09.86]Passage Three｜短文三\n[20:11.36]Most of us have been in teams or organizations where we''ve had conflict with the people that we''re working with around the ideas or decisions that we''re discussing.｜我们中的大多数人都曾在团队或组织中与同事就我们正在讨论的想法或决策发生过冲突。\n[20:21.89]Conflict is natural.｜冲突是自然的。\n[20:24.13]We all bring different life and work experiences to the table.｜我们都有不同的生活和工作经历。\n[20:28.29]We all have different personality preferences and tendencies.｜我们都有不同的性格偏好和倾向。\n[20:32.82]We''re not all going to have the same ideas on how to approach policies, programs, or problems.｜在如何处理政策、计划或问题方面，我们并非都有相同的想法。\n[20:39.48]But too often, we get caught in this place where conflict is perceived to be negative—something we want to avoid so that we can maintain the harmony of our workplace.｜但很多时候，我们会陷入这样一种境地：冲突被认为是消极的，我们想要避免冲突，以保持工作场所的和谐。\n[20:50.91]This could be because some people want to avoid conflict at all costs.｜这可能是因为有些人想不惜一切代价避免冲突。\n[20:55.38]After all, they still have to work together.｜毕竟他们还要一起工作。\n[20:57.90]But this kind of artificial harmony isn''t the answer.｜但这种人为的和谐并不能解决问题。\n[21:02.00]Productive conflict is a vital part of teams and organizations that want to push forward and do more.｜团队和组织想要向前推进、取得更多成果，有成效的冲突是必不可少的。\n[21:09.57]Without conflict, we''re often stuck in this artificial harmony where people don''t express potentially innovative ideas for fear that they may start conflict with others.｜如果没有冲突，我们往往会陷入这种人为的和谐，人们因为害怕与他人发生冲突而不敢表达潜在的有创意的想法。\n[21:21.48]But if you''re in a place where you have a basis of trust, conflict can be extremely productive.｜但是如果你处于一个有信任基础的地方，冲突就会富有成效。\n[21:27.88]It can lead to increased innovation and greater trust on teams.｜它可以激发创新，并增强团队间的信任。\n[21:33.40]It may be an uncomfortable process, but good leaders and healthy teams recognize that productive and healthy conflict is an important part of how they function.｜这个过程可能令人不太舒服，但优秀的领导者和健康的团队都认识到，有成效的、健康的冲突是他们运作的重要组成部分。\n[21:45.97]Questions 22 to 25 are based on the passage you have just heard.｜请根据你刚听到的短文回答第22至25题。\n[21:50.93]22. What does the passage say about conflict in organizations?｜22. 关于组织中的冲突，短文说了什么？\n[22:12.43]23. Why do some people want to avoid conflict at all costs?｜23. 为什么有些人想不惜一切代价避免冲突？\n[22:32.51]24. Why is productive conflict important for teams and organizations?｜24. 为什么有成效的冲突对团队和组织很重要？\n[22:53.82]25. What does productive conflict need as a basis?｜25. 有成效的冲突需要什么作为基础？', NOW(), NOW()
