SELECT
  @a_cet4_2024_12_1_04, '/audio/exams/listening-cet4-2024-12-1.mp3', 'News Report Two\n新闻二\n\nThe Wilton School Board has proposed a 5.99 percent spending increase.\n威尔顿学校董事会已提议增加5.99%的支出。\n\nIf approved, it would be the largest jump in at least 8 budget cycles.\n如果获得批准，这将是至少8个预算周期内增幅最大的一次。\n\nThe 5.99 percent request more than doubles the highest previous year-over-year increase in the last 8 years, which was 2.99 percent for the 2021-2022 school year. 2021-2022\n学年的增幅为2.99%，是过去8年来最高的同比增幅，而5.99%的增幅是其两倍多。\n\nThe biggest driver of the $91.8 million proposed budget remains teachers’ salaries.\n在预算提案的9,180万美元中，份额最大的仍然是教师工资。\n\nThese account for 64 percent of the total request at $59 million.\n教师工资占预算总数的64%，共计5,900万美元。\n\nThe $59 million is up from the $56.7 million budgeted for the current school year.\n这5,900万美元高于本学年预算的5,670万美元。\n\nThere are some factors that could affect the budget moving forward.\n有一些因素可能会影响预算工作的推进。\n\nOne of those is total enrollment.\n其中一个因素就是总入学人数。\n\nThe district will have a total enrollment of 3,742 students.\n该学区将招收3,742名学生。\n\nAlmost all of these students will be in kindergarten through high school, but 66 will be in pre-kindergarten and other programs.\n这些学生基本都将是幼儿园至高中阶段的学生，但其中有66名将就读于学前班或其他课程。\n\nThis represents 47 fewer students than the current year.\n这说明，相比今年，总入学人数将减少47名学生。\n\nFewer students mean less federal and state funding.\n学生人数减少意味着联邦和州政府的资金减少。\n\nQuestions 3 and 4 are based on the news report you have just heard.\n请根据你刚听到的新闻报道回答第3题和第4题。\n\n3. What does the news report say the Wilton School Board has done?\n3. 新闻报道说威尔顿学校董事会做了什么？\n\n4. What will a decline in the total enrollment lead to?\n4. 总入学人数的减少会导致什么？', 84, 1426.14, 144.57, 228.72, 253.33, 273.32, 224.11, 228.42, 'cet4-2024-12-1-g02', 'NEWS', '[02:24.57]News Report Two｜新闻二\n[02:26.08]The Wilton School Board has proposed a 5.99 percent spending increase.｜威尔顿学校董事会已提议增加5.99%的支出。\n[02:32.98]If approved, it would be the largest jump in at least 8 budget cycles.｜如果获得批准，这将是至少8个预算周期内增幅最大的一次。\n[02:38.24]The 5.99 percent request more than doubles the highest previous year-over-year increase in the last 8 years, which was 2.99 percent for the 2021-2022 school year. 2021-2022｜学年的增幅为2.99%，是过去8年来最高的同比增幅，而5.99%的增幅是其两倍多。\n[02:55.38]The biggest driver of the $91.8 million proposed budget remains teachers’ salaries.｜在预算提案的9,180万美元中，份额最大的仍然是教师工资。\n[03:02.73]These account for 64 percent of the total request at $59 million.｜教师工资占预算总数的64%，共计5,900万美元。\n[03:08.84]The $59 million is up from the $56.7 million budgeted for the current school year.｜这5,900万美元高于本学年预算的5,670万美元。\n[03:16.42]There are some factors that could affect the budget moving forward.｜有一些因素可能会影响预算工作的推进。\n[03:20.65]One of those is total enrollment.｜其中一个因素就是总入学人数。\n[03:23.48]The district will have a total enrollment of 3,742 students.｜该学区将招收3,742名学生。\n[03:29.52]Almost all of these students will be in kindergarten through high school, but 66 will be in pre-kindergarten and other programs.｜这些学生基本都将是幼儿园至高中阶段的学生，但其中有66名将就读于学前班或其他课程。\n[03:38.79]This represents 47 fewer students than the current year.｜这说明，相比今年，总入学人数将减少47名学生。\n[03:44.11]Fewer students mean less federal and state funding.｜学生人数减少意味着联邦和州政府的资金减少。\n[03:48.72]Questions 3 and 4 are based on the news report you have just heard.｜请根据你刚听到的新闻报道回答第3题和第4题。\n[03:53.86]3. What does the news report say the Wilton School Board has done?｜3. 新闻报道说威尔顿学校董事会做了什么？\n[04:13.33]4. What will a decline in the total enrollment lead to?｜4. 总入学人数的减少会导致什么？', NOW(), NOW()
