 special offer, where I don’t pay any interest for six months.｜但是我的信用卡有一个很好的特别优惠，可以在6个月内不用支付任何利息。\n[08:33.66]I’ll be able to pay for the phone well before that period is over.｜在优惠时间结束之前，我就能偿还手机的费用。\n[08:38.34]W: I still think it’s a bad idea to use a credit card for something you don’t need.｜女：我仍然认为用信用卡购买你不需要的东西是个坏主意。\n[08:43.11]One of my colleagues bought a lot of things on credit during her first year of work, and it became a bad habit, and she accumulated a lot of debt.｜我的一位同事在她工作的第一年就用信用卡买了很多东西，这让她养成了一个坏习惯，而她也因此积累了很多债务。\n[08:52.18]M: Well, I can see how that might happen to someone.｜男：好吧，我能理解这种情况可能会发生在某些人身上。\n[08:56.01]I’m sure she regrets it.｜我觉得她肯定很后悔。\n[08:58.14]But I know it won’t happen to me.｜但我认为这种事不会发生在我身上。\n[09:00.62]Questions 8 to 11 are based on the conversation you have just heard.｜请根据你刚听到的对话回答第8至11题。\n[09:05.62]8. What does the woman say she was actually wondering about?｜8. 女士说她实际上想知道什么？\n[09:26.01]9. Why is the man a little embarrassed by the phone he’s using now?｜9. 为什么男士现在使用的手机会让他感到有点难为情？\n[09:46.48]10. What does the man say about the credit card he just got?｜10. 关于男士刚办理的信用卡，他怎么说？\n[10:05.56]11. What do we learn about one of the woman’s colleagues?｜11. 关于女士的一位同事，我们了解了什么？', NOW(), NOW()
