SELECT
  @a_cet4_2024_12_1_10, '/audio/exams/listening-cet4-2024-12-1.mp3', 'Conversation One\n对话一\n\nM: I’m going to the city center to buy a new phone today.\n男：我今天要去市中心买一部新手机。\n\nW: Didn’t you buy a new phone just two months ago?\n女：你不是两个月前刚买了一部新手机吗？\n\nM: It was three months ago, and I already know what you’re going to say.\n男：那是三个月前的事了，而且我已经知道你要说什么了。\n\nYou’re thinking I shouldn’t replace my phone this soon.\n你在想我不应该这么快就换手机。\n\nW: No, actually, I was wondering how you could possibly afford a new phone.\n女：不是，我实际上想知道你怎么可能买得起一部新手机。\n\nBut now that you mention it, I do think getting another phone so soon is wasteful, regardless of the cost.\n但既然你提到了，我的确认为无论价格如何，这么快就换另一部手机还是太浪费了。\n\nM: Maybe you’re right.\n男：也许你是对的。\n\nBut the thing is, everyone at the office has a nice, expensive phone, and I’m a little embarrassed by mine.\n但问题是，办公室里的每个人都有一部漂亮而昂贵的手机，而我自己的手机让我感到有点难为情。\n\nI just got a credit card, so I thought I might as well buy a new phone.\n我刚办了一张信用卡，所以我想着不如再买一部新手机。\n\nW: I don’t think buying a phone on credit is a good idea.\n女：我认为贷款买手机不是个好主意。\n\nLook, you’ve only been working for five months now.\n你看，你现在只工作了5个月。\n\nPeople understand that you are a recent graduate.\n人们都知道你是刚毕业的。\n\nAnd I doubt anyone cares about your phone other than yourself.\n我怀疑除了你自己，没有人会在意你用什么手机。\n\nM: Maybe you’re right.\n男：也许你是对的。\n\nBut the credit card has a very good special offer, where I don’t pay any interest for six months.\n但是我的信用卡有一个很好的特别优惠，可以在6个月内不用支付任何利息。\n\nI’ll be able to pay for the phone well before that period is over.\n在优惠时间结束之前，我就能偿还手机的费用。\n\nW: I still think it’s a bad idea to use a credit card for something you don’t need.\n女：我仍然认为用信用卡购买你不需要的东西是个坏主意。\n\nOne of my colleagues bought a lot of things on credit during her first year of work, and it became a bad habit, and she accumulated a lot of debt.\n我的一位同事在她工作的第一年就用信用卡买了很多东西，这让她养成了一个坏习惯，而她也因此积累了很多债务。\n\nM: Well, I can see how that might happen to someone.\n男：好吧，我能理解这种情况可能会发生在某些人身上。\n\nI’m sure she regrets it.\n我觉得她肯定很后悔。\n\nBut I know it won’t happen to me.\n但我认为这种事不会发生在我身上。\n\nQuestions 8 to 11 are based on the conversation you have just heard.\n请根据你刚听到的对话回答第8至11题。\n\n8. What does the woman say she was actually wondering about?\n8. 女士说她实际上想知道什么？\n\n9. Why is the man a little embarrassed by the phone he’s using now?\n9. 为什么男士现在使用的手机会让他感到有点难为情？\n\n10. What does the man say about the credit card he just got?\n10. 关于男士刚办理的信用卡，他怎么说？\n\n11. What do we learn about one of the woman’s colleagues?\n11. 关于女士的一位同事，我们了解了什么？', 90, 1426.14, 450.89, 540.62, 586.48, 605.26, NULL, NULL, 'cet4-2024-12-1-g04', 'LONG_DIALOGUE', '[07:30.89]Conversation One｜对话一\n[07:33.21]M: I’m going to the city center to buy a new phone today.｜男：我今天要去市中心买一部新手机。\n[07:36.77]W: Didn’t you buy a new phone just two months ago?｜女：你不是两个月前刚买了一部新手机吗？\n[07:40.02]M: It was three months ago, and I already know what you’re going to say.｜男：那是三个月前的事了，而且我已经知道你要说什么了。\n[07:44.14]You’re thinking I shouldn’t replace my phone this soon.｜你在想我不应该这么快就换手机。\n[07:47.15]W: No, actually, I was wondering how you could possibly afford a new phone.｜女：不是，我实际上想知道你怎么可能买得起一部新手机。\n[07:51.86]But now that you mention it, I do think getting another phone so soon is wasteful, regardless of the cost.｜但既然你提到了，我的确认为无论价格如何，这么快就换另一部手机还是太浪费了。\n[07:59.07]M: Maybe you’re right.｜男：也许你是对的。\n[08:00.34]But the thing is, everyone at the office has a nice, expensive phone, and I’m a little embarrassed by mine.｜但问题是，办公室里的每个人都有一部漂亮而昂贵的手机，而我自己的手机让我感到有点难为情。\n[08:07.20]I just got a credit card, so I thought I might as well buy a new phone.｜我刚办了一张信用卡，所以我想着不如再买一部新手机。\n[08:11.89]W: I don’t think buying a phone on credit is a good idea.｜女：我认为贷款买手机不是个好主意。\n[08:15.71]Look, you’ve only been working for five months now.｜你看，你现在只工作了5个月。\n[08:18.86]People understand that you are a recent graduate.｜人们都知道你是刚毕业的。\n[08:21.50]And I doubt anyone cares about your phone other than yourself.｜我怀疑除了你自己，没有人会在意你用什么手机。\n[08:25.51]M: Maybe you’re right.｜男：也许你是对的。\n[08:27.14]But the credit card has a very good special offer, where I don’t pay any interest for six months.｜但是我的信用卡有一个很好的特别优惠，可以在6个月内不用支付任何利息。\n[08:33.66]I’ll be able to pay for the phone well before that period is over.｜在优惠时间结束之前，我就能偿还手机的费用。\n[08:38.34]W: I still think it’s a bad idea to use a credit card for something you don’t need.｜女：我仍然认为用信用卡购买你不需要的东西是个坏主意。\n[08:43.11]One of my colleagues bought a lot of things on credit during her first year of work, and it became a bad habit, and she accumulated a lot of debt.｜我的一位同事在她工作的第一年就用信用卡买了很多东西，这让她养成了一个坏习惯，而她也因此积累了很多债务。\n[08:52.18]M: Well, I can see how that might happen to someone.｜男：好吧，我能理解这种情况可能会发生在某些人身上。\n[08:56.01]I’m sure she regrets it.｜我觉得她肯定很后悔。\n[08:58.14]But I know it won’t happen to me.｜但我认为这种事不会发生在我身上。\n[09:00.62]Questions 8 to 11 are based on the conversation you have just heard.｜请根据你刚听到的对话回答第8至11题。\n[09:05.62]8. What does the woman say she was actually wondering about?｜8. 女士说她实际上想知道什么？\n[09:26.01]9. Why is the man a little embarrassed by the phone he’s using now?｜9. 为什么男士现在使用的手机会让他感到有点难为情？\n[09:46.48]10. What does the man say about the credit card he just got?｜10. 关于男士刚办理的信用卡，他怎么说？\n[10:05.56]11. What do we learn about one of the woman’s colleagues?｜11. 关于女士的一位同事，我们了解了什么？', NOW(), NOW()
