  @a_cet4_2024_12_1_14, '/audio/exams/listening-cet4-2024-12-1.mp3', 'Conversation Two\n对话二\n\nW: Welcome to The Morning Show.\n女：欢迎收听《早间秀》节目。\n\nOur guest today is a popular blog writer and a major figure in the Tiny Home Community.\n我们今天的嘉宾是一位受欢迎的博客作者，也是微型住宅社区的重要人物。\n\nWelcome, Bob Jones.\n欢迎，鲍勃·琼斯。\n\nM: Hi, Mary.\n男：你好，玛丽。\n\nW: Hi, Bob.\n女：你好，鲍勃。\n\nYou’re an advocate of the Tiny Home Movement.\n你是微型住宅运动的倡导者。\n\nA lot of people don’t know about this movement.\n很多人都不知道这场运动。\n\nCan you tell our audience what it’s about?\n你能告诉我们的听众这是关于什么的吗？\n\nM: Well, it’s mainly about increasing home ownership and protecting the environment.\n男：嗯，这主要是关于增加住房拥有率和保护环境的。\n\nW: Of course, those are great goals.\n女：当然，这些都是伟大的目标。\n\nBut I’ve seen your blog, and you write about houses that are as small as 20 square meters.\n但我看过你的博客，其中提到了小到20平方米的房子。\n\nThat’s not a realistic size for families.\n对于家庭来说，这个住房面积不太现实。\n\nM: I do talk about very small homes.\n男：我确实提到过面积很小的房子。\n\nBut there’s no set definition of a tiny home, and other people include homes that are much larger, say, 60 square meters.\n但是，微型住宅没有固定的定义，也有人将面积更大的房子包括在内，比如60平方米的房子。\n\nAnd you’d be surprised.\n而且你会感到很惊讶。\n\nMany families of four are happy living in houses that are under 30 square meters.\n许多四口之家都很乐意住在不到30平方米的房子里。\n\nW: But I think most of us want spacious homes.\n女：但我认为我们大多数人都想要宽敞的房子。\n\nThe average new house in this area is 150 square meters.\n这个地区的平均新房面积是150平方米。\n\nAnd that’s what people dream of owning.\n这也是人们梦想拥有的。\n\nM: Yes. But I think that dream needs to change, considering the cost of housing.\n男：是的。但我觉得考虑到住房成本，这个梦想需要改变。\n\nW: Housing costs are high.\n女：住房成本很高。\n\nBut do people really save that much by having a smaller home?\n但是，人们真的会因为买了面积更小的房子而省下那么多钱吗？\n\nM: Absolutely. Many people who can only afford to rent a larger home are able to buy a tiny home.\n男：当然。许多人要是想拥有面积更大的房子只能靠租，但他们能够买得起微型住宅。\n\nIn this city, the average home costs $200,000, and a tiny home costs just $50,000.\n在这个城市，普通住宅的均价为20万美元，而一套微型住宅仅需5万美元。\n\nW: Those are huge savings.\n女：这能省下一大笔钱。\n\nM: So tiny homes might not be for everyone, but they are a good option for many.\n男：所以微型住宅可能不适合每个人，但对许多人来说，这是一个不错的选择。\n\nW: You mentioned the environment earlier.\n女：你之前还提到了环境。\n\nHow does this benefit the planet?\n这对地球有什么好处？\n\nM: Well, if people have smaller homes, they use less land and fewer resources to build them.\n男：嗯，如果人们住的房子面积更小，那么建造房子所用的土地和资源就会更少。\n\nQuestions 12 to 15 are based on the conversation you have just heard.\n请根据你刚听到的对话回答第12至15题。\n\n12. What does the Tiny Home Movement mainly advocate?\n12. 微型住宅运动主要倡导什么？\n\n13. What does the woman say about houses as small as 20 square meters?\n13. 对于小到20平方米的房子，女士怎么说？\n\n14. What does the man think about the dream of owning a 150-square-meter house?\n14. 对于拥有150平米房子的梦想，男士有什么看法？\n\n15. What does the man say about tiny homes?\n15. 对于微型住宅，男士怎么说？\n\nSection\nCC节', 122, 1426.14, 625.50, 747.52, 793.87, 813.87, NULL, NULL, 'cet4-2024-12-1-g05', 'LONG_DIALOGUE', '[10:25.50]Conversation Two｜对话二\n[10:28.27]W: Welcome to The Morning Show.｜女：欢迎收听《早间秀》节目。\n[10:30.54]Our guest today is a popular blog writer and a major figure in the Tiny Home Community.｜我们今天的嘉宾是一位受欢迎的博客作者，也是微型住宅社区的重要人物。\n[10:36.72]Welcome, Bob Jones.｜欢迎，鲍勃·琼斯。\n[10:38.70]M: Hi, Mary.｜男：你好，玛丽。\n[10:39.84]W: Hi, Bob.｜女：你好，鲍勃。\n[10:40.87]You’re an advocate of the Tiny Home Movement.｜你是微型住宅运动的倡导者。\n[10:43.91]A lot of people don’t know about this movement.｜很多人都不知道这场运动。\n[10:46.94]Can you tell our audience what it’s about?｜你能告诉我们的听众这是关于什么的吗？\n[10:49.81]M: Well, it’s mainly about increasing home ownership and protecting the environment.｜男：嗯，这主要是关于增加住房拥有率和保护环境的。\n[10:55.76]W: Of course, those are great goals.｜女：当然，这些都是伟大的目标。\n[10:58.16]But I’ve seen your blog, and you write about houses that are as small as 20 square meters.｜但我看过你的博客，其中提到了小到20平方米的房子。\n[11:04.32]That’s not a realistic size for families.｜对于家庭来说，这个住房面积不太现实。\n[11:07.66]M: I do talk about very small homes.｜男：我确实提到过面积很小的房子。\n[11:10.89]But there’s no set definition of a tiny home, and other people include homes that are much larger, say, 60 square meters.｜但是，微型住宅没有固定的定义，也有人将面积更大的房子包括在内，比如60平方米的房子。\n[11:19.75]And you’d be surprised.｜而且你会感到很惊讶。\n[11:21.49]Many families of four are happy living in houses that are under 30 square meters.｜许多四口之家都很乐意住在不到30平方米的房子里。\n[11:27.60]W: But I think most of us want spacious homes.｜女：但我认为我们大多数人都想要宽敞的房子。\n[11:31.47]The average new house in this area is 150 square meters.｜这个地区的平均新房面积是150平方米。\n[11:36.11]And that’s what people dream of owning.｜这也是人们梦想拥有的。\n[11:38.29]M: Yes. But I think that dream needs to change, considering the cost of housing.｜男：是的。但我觉得考虑到住房成本，这个梦想需要改变。\n[11:44.45]W: Housing costs are high.｜女：住房成本很高。\n[11:46.78]But do people really save that much by having a smaller home?｜但是，人们真的会因为买了面积更小的房子而省下那么多钱吗？\n[11:50.34]M: Absolutely. Many people who can only afford to rent a larger home are able to buy a tiny home.｜男：当然。许多人要是想拥有面积更大的房子只能靠租，但他们能够买得起微型住宅。\n[11:58.21]In this city, the average home costs $200,000, and a tiny home costs just $50,000.｜在这个城市，普通住宅的均价为20万美元，而一套微型住宅仅需5万美元。\n[12:07.57]W: Those are huge savings.｜女：这能省下一大笔钱。\n[12:09.60]M: So tiny homes might not be for everyone, but they are a good option for many.｜男：所以微型住宅可能不适合每个人，但对许多人来说，这是一个不错的选择。\n[12:15.82]W: You mentioned the environment earlier.｜女：你之前还提到了环境。\n[12:18.62]How does this benefit the planet?｜这对地球有什么好处？\n[12:21.04]M: Well, if people have smaller homes, they use less land and fewer resources to build them.｜男：嗯，如果人们住的房子面积更小，那么建造房子所用的土地和资源就会更少。\n[12:27.52]Questions 12 to 15 are based on the conversation you have just heard.｜请根据你刚听到的对话回答第12至15题。\n[12:33.01]12. What does the Tiny Home Movement mainly advocate?｜12. 微型住宅运动主要倡导什么？\n[12:53.01]13. What does the woman say about houses as small as 20 square meters?｜13. 对于小到20平方米的房子，女士怎么说？\n[13:13.87]14. What does the man think about the dream of owning a 150-square-meter house?｜14. 对于拥有150平米房子的梦想，男士有什么看法？\n[13:36.45]15. What does the man say about tiny homes?｜15. 对于微型住宅，男士怎么说？\n[13:55.54]Section｜CC节', NOW(), NOW()
