SELECT
  @a_cet4_2024_12_1_18, '/audio/exams/listening-cet4-2024-12-1.mp3', 'Passage One\n短文一\n\nKids need time every day to run, jump, stretch and play.\n孩子们每天都要花点时间来进行跑步、跳跃、伸展运动，以及玩耍。\n\nThese experiences have been shown to build children’s confidence and pleasure in physical activities, develop their motor skills, and even improve emotional well-being.\n这些活动已被证明可以建立孩子们对体育活动的信心并让他们从中获得乐趣，还能增强他们的运动能力，甚至有益于情绪健康。\n\nTo begin with, children seem to have a natural desire to overcome challenges and take risks.\n首先，孩子们似乎天生就有克服挑战和追求冒险的欲望。\n\nTaking healthy risks through physical movement builds children’s confidence and ability to solve problems and persist through frustration.\n通过体育活动进行安全的冒险，可以建立孩子们的信心，培养他们解决问题的能力以及面对挫折坚持不懈的精神。\n\nSecondly, movement activities build children’s big body skills such as coordination and balance, as well as the fine motor skills they need for tasks like writing, tying their shoes, or throwing and catching a ball.\n其次，体育活动可以提高孩子们重要的肢体技能，如协调性和平衡感，同时也能提升他们完成书写、系鞋带或投球和接球等任务所需的精细运动技能。\n\nThirdly, according to the American Psychological Association, regular physical activity, and especially outdoor activity, reduces children’s stress and depression and improves their ability to focus and learn.\n第三，根据美国心理学会的说法，定期进行体育活动，尤其是户外活动，可以缓解孩子们的压力和抑郁情绪，提高他们的专注力和学习能力。\n\nRegular exercise can significantly improve self-regulation and decrease disciplinary consequences for negative behavior.\n定期锻炼可以显著提高自我调节能力，并减少因不良行为而受到的纪律处分。\n\nPhysical activity provides a positive outlet for frustration, anxiety, or anger and can become a healthy coping skill throughout life.\n体育活动为沮丧、焦虑或愤怒情绪提供了一个积极的发泄途径，可以作为一种健康的应对技能贯穿人的一生。\n\nFinally, we know that physical activity is important for our physical and mental health, and cultivating the habit of physical activity starts early.\n最后，我们知道体育活动对身心健康很重要，培养体育活动的习惯要从早期开始。\n\nChildren are more likely to develop a lifelong love of physical activity from frequent positive early experiences.\n孩子们如果能在早期频繁获得积极的运动体验，就更有可能培养出对体育活动的终身热爱。\n\nNot every child enjoys competitive sports or playing with balls, and that’s OK.\n不是每个孩子都喜欢竞技运动或球类运动，这都没关系。\n\nThere are plenty of other options such as imaginative play, noncompetitive games, and gardening or nature experiences.\n还有很多其他选择，比如想象游戏、非竞技类游戏、园艺或自然体验。\n\nQuestions 16 to 18 are based on the passage you have just heard.\n请根据你刚听到的短文回答第16至18题。\n\n16. What do children seem to have a natural desire to do?\n16. 孩子们似乎天生就渴望做什么？\n\n17. According to the American Psychological Association, what does regular physical activity do to children?\n17. 根据美国心理学会的说法，定期进行体育活动对孩子们有什么作用？\n\n18. What does the passage say about cultivating the habit of physical activity?\n18. 关于培养体育活动的习惯，短文说了什么？', 123, 1426.14, 863.80, 986.55, 1036.41, 1057.16, NULL, NULL, 'cet4-2024-12-1-g06', 'PASSAGE', '[14:23.80]Passage One｜短文一\n[14:26.02]Kids need time every day to run, jump, stretch and play.｜孩子们每天都要花点时间来进行跑步、跳跃、伸展运动，以及玩耍。\n[14:30.94]These experiences have been shown to build children’s confidence and pleasure in physical activities, develop their motor skills, and even improve emotional well-being.｜这些活动已被证明可以建立孩子们对体育活动的信心并让他们从中获得乐趣，还能增强他们的运动能力，甚至有益于情绪健康。\n[14:42.11]To begin with, children seem to have a natural desire to overcome challenges and take risks.｜首先，孩子们似乎天生就有克服挑战和追求冒险的欲望。\n[14:48.92]Taking healthy risks through physical movement builds children’s confidence and ability to solve problems and persist through frustration.｜通过体育活动进行安全的冒险，可以建立孩子们的信心，培养他们解决问题的能力以及面对挫折坚持不懈的精神。\n[14:58.90]Secondly, movement activities build children’s big body skills such as coordination and balance, as well as the fine motor skills they need for tasks like writing, tying their shoes, or throwing and catching a ball.｜其次，体育活动可以提高孩子们重要的肢体技能，如协调性和平衡感，同时也能提升他们完成书写、系鞋带或投球和接球等任务所需的精细运动技能。\n[15:15.84]Thirdly, according to the American Psychological Association, regular physical activity, and especially outdoor activity, reduces children’s stress and depression and improves their ability to focus and learn.｜第三，根据美国心理学会的说法，定期进行体育活动，尤其是户外活动，可以缓解孩子们的压力和抑郁情绪，提高他们的专注力和学习能力。\n[15:30.48]Regular exercise can significantly improve self-regulation and decrease disciplinary consequences for negative behavior.｜定期锻炼可以显著提高自我调节能力，并减少因不良行为而受到的纪律处分。\n[15:40.65]Physical activity provides a positive outlet for frustration, anxiety, or anger and can become a healthy coping skill throughout life.｜体育活动为沮丧、焦虑或愤怒情绪提供了一个积极的发泄途径，可以作为一种健康的应对技能贯穿人的一生。\n[15:51.08]Finally, we know that physical activity is important for our physical and mental health, and cultivating the habit of physical activity starts early.｜最后，我们知道体育活动对身心健康很重要，培养体育活动的习惯要从早期开始。\n[16:01.56]Children are more likely to develop a lifelong love of physical activity from frequent positive early experiences.｜孩子们如果能在早期频繁获得积极的运动体验，就更有可能培养出对体育活动的终身热爱。\n[16:10.36]Not every child enjoys competitive sports or playing with balls, and that’s OK.｜不是每个孩子都喜欢竞技运动或球类运动，这都没关系。\n[16:16.60]There are plenty of other options such as imaginative play, noncompetitive games, and gardening or nature experiences.｜还有很多其他选择，比如想象游戏、非竞技类游戏、园艺或自然体验。\n[16:26.55]Questions 16 to 18 are based on the passage you have just heard.｜请根据你刚听到的短文回答第16至18题。\n[16:32.06]16. What do children seem to have a natural desire to do?｜16. 孩子们似乎天生就渴望做什么？\n[16:52.57]17. According to the American Psychological Association, what does regular physical activity do to children?｜17. 根据美国心理学会的说法，定期进行体育活动对孩子们有什么作用？\n[17:16.41]18. What does the passage say about cultivating the habit of physical activity?｜18. 关于培养体育活动的习惯，短文说了什么？', NOW(), NOW()
