SELECT
  @a_cet4_2024_12_1_19, '/audio/exams/listening-cet4-2024-12-1.mp3', 'Passage Two\n短文二\n\nA new study finds that job seekers are even willing to explore jobs with lower salaries when companies are more diverse.\n一项新的研究发现，当公司更加多元化时，求职者甚至愿意尝试薪资较低的工作。\n\nIt finds that sharing information about diversity makes job postings more attractive to job seekers, even when pay is lower.\n研究发现，对求职者来说，分享有关多元化的信息会使招聘信息更具吸引力，即使薪资较低也是如此。\n\nTo conduct the study, the team partnered with an online job listings platform which emails postings relevant to individuals and their job search criteria.\n为了进行这项研究，该团队与一家在线招聘平台合作，该平台会以电子邮件的方式发送与个人及其求职标准相关的招聘信息。\n\nFor the course of the 11-week study, the platform emailed job listings to some 180,000 users placed in one of two conditions.\n在为期11周的研究过程中，该平台向18万名用户发送了职位招聘信息，这些用户作为参与者被分别置于两种不同的条件下。\n\nIn the baseline condition, participants saw emails in the normal format, with no information on diversity;\n在基准条件下，参与者看到的是常规格式的电子邮件，其中没有关于多元化的信息；\n\nin the diversity condition, participants saw a diversity score for each listing:\n在多元化条件下，参与者会看到每条招聘信息的多元化评分：\n\ninformation about the race, gender, education, and language skills of a company’s workforce compared to others in the same sector and location.\n招聘公司与同一行业、同一地点的其他公司相比，其员工的种族、性别、教育背景和语言技能等方面的信息。\n\nInformation was then gathered on whether the email was opened and which job listings were clicked on by each user.\n随后，收集信息以统计每封邮件是否被点开查看以及每个用户点击了哪些招聘信息。\n\nParticipants in the diversity condition tended to click on job listings from companies with slightly higher diversity scores than those in the baseline condition.\n与基准条件下的参与者相比，多元化条件下的参与者更倾向于点击多元化评分略高的公司的招聘信息。\n\nThat is, participants seemed to be paying attention to information about diversity and using this when deciding whether to click on the listing.\n也就是说，参与者似乎在关注多元化信息，并根据这些信息决定是否点击招聘信息。\n\nAnd the team also found that participants were willing to look at listings with lower salaries if they came from companies with a higher diversity score.\n该团队还发现，如果招聘信息来自多元化评分较高的公司，即使薪资较低，参与者也愿意查看。\n\nQuestions 19 to 21 are based on the passage you have just heard.\n请根据你刚听到的短文回答第19至21题。\n\n19. When are job seekers willing to explore jobs with lower salaries, according to a new study?\n19. 根据一项新的研究，求职者什么时候愿意尝试薪资较低的工作？\n\n20. What did participants see in the baseline condition of the study?\n20. 在这项研究的基准条件下，参与者看到了什么？\n\n21. What does the passage say participants seem to be paying attention to?\n21. 短文指出参与者似乎在关注什么？', 104, 1426.14, 1057.46, 1161.80, 1168.10, 1188.10, 1131.59, 1142.17, 'cet4-2024-12-1-g07', 'PASSAGE', '[17:37.46]Passage Two｜短文二\n[17:39.57]A new study finds that job seekers are even willing to explore jobs with lower salaries when companies are more diverse.｜一项新的研究发现，当公司更加多元化时，求职者甚至愿意尝试薪资较低的工作。\n[17:49.21]It finds that sharing information about diversity makes job postings more attractive to job seekers, even when pay is lower.｜研究发现，对求职者来说，分享有关多元化的信息会使招聘信息更具吸引力，即使薪资较低也是如此。\n[17:58.01]To conduct the study, the team partnered with an online job listings platform which emails postings relevant to individuals and their job search criteria.｜为了进行这项研究，该团队与一家在线招聘平台合作，该平台会以电子邮件的方式发送与个人及其求职标准相关的招聘信息。\n[18:08.83]For the course of the 11-week study, the platform emailed job listings to some 180,000 users placed in one of two conditions.｜在为期11周的研究过程中，该平台向18万名用户发送了职位招聘信息，这些用户作为参与者被分别置于两种不同的条件下。\n[18:19.64]In the baseline condition, participants saw emails in the normal format, with no information on diversity;｜在基准条件下，参与者看到的是常规格式的电子邮件，其中没有关于多元化的信息；\n[18:27.34]in the diversity condition, participants saw a diversity score for each listing:｜在多元化条件下，参与者会看到每条招聘信息的多元化评分：\n[18:33.29]information about the race, gender, education, and language skills of a company’s workforce compared to others in the same sector and location.｜招聘公司与同一行业、同一地点的其他公司相比，其员工的种族、性别、教育背景和语言技能等方面的信息。\n[18:43.70]Information was then gathered on whether the email was opened and which job listings were clicked on by each user.｜随后，收集信息以统计每封邮件是否被点开查看以及每个用户点击了哪些招聘信息。\n[18:51.59]Participants in the diversity condition tended to click on job listings from companies with slightly higher diversity scores than those in the baseline condition.｜与基准条件下的参与者相比，多元化条件下的参与者更倾向于点击多元化评分略高的公司的招聘信息。\n[19:02.47]That is, participants seemed to be paying attention to information about diversity and using this when deciding whether to click on the listing.｜也就是说，参与者似乎在关注多元化信息，并根据这些信息决定是否点击招聘信息。\n[19:12.17]And the team also found that participants were willing to look at listings with lower salaries if they came from companies with a higher diversity score.｜该团队还发现，如果招聘信息来自多元化评分较高的公司，即使薪资较低，参与者也愿意查看。\n[19:21.80]Questions 19 to 21 are based on the passage you have just heard.｜请根据你刚听到的短文回答第19至21题。\n[19:28.10]19. When are job seekers willing to explore jobs with lower salaries, according to a new study?｜19. 根据一项新的研究，求职者什么时候愿意尝试薪资较低的工作？\n[19:50.48]20. What did participants see in the baseline condition of the study?｜20. 在这项研究的基准条件下，参与者看到了什么？\n[20:11.73]21. What does the passage say participants seem to be paying attention to?｜21. 短文指出参与者似乎在关注什么？', NOW(), NOW()
WHERE @a_cet4_2024_12_1_19 IS NOT NULL
