  (`question_id`, `audio_url`, `transcript`, `duration_seconds`, `audio_total_seconds`, `audio_start_seconds`, `audio_end_seconds`, `question_start_seconds`, `question_end_seconds`, `answer_start_seconds`, `answer_end_seconds`, `group_key`, `listening_type`, `lrc_content`, `created_at`, `updated_at`)
SELECT
  @a_cet4_2024_12_1_22, '/audio/exams/listening-cet4-2024-12-1.mp3', 'Passage Three\n短文三\n\nA new study from Oregon State University found that dogs tend to match their behavior with the children in their family.\n俄勒冈州立大学的一项新研究发现，狗在行为上倾向于配合家里的孩子。\n\nThe findings are important, because there is a growing body of evidence that dogs can help children in many ways.\n这些发现很重要，因为越来越多的证据表明，狗可以在很多方面帮助孩子们。\n\nThese include helping with social development, increasing physical activity, managing anxiety or serving as a source of attachment in the face of changing family structures.\n这些方面包括促进孩子的社交发展、增加孩子的体育活动、缓解孩子的焦虑情绪，或是在家庭结构发生变化时成为孩子的依恋来源。\n\nYet, very little research has focused on how dogs perceive and socially engage with children.\n然而，很少有研究关注狗是如何感知孩子并与其进行社交互动的。\n\n“The great news is that this study suggests dogs are paying a lot of attention to the kids that they live with,” said Monique Udell, the lead author of the study.\n该研究的主要作者莫妮克·尤德尔说：“好消息是，这项研究表明狗非常关注与它们生活在一起的孩子。”\n\n“One interesting thing we have observed is that dogs are matching children’s behavior, but less frequently than what we have seen between dogs and adults. “\n我们观察到的一个有趣的现象是，狗会配合孩子的行为，但其频率比我们在狗和成人之间所观察到的更低。\n\nThis suggests that while dogs may view children as social companions, there are also some differences that we need to understand better.”\n这表明，虽然狗可能将孩子视为社交伙伴，但其中也存在一些差异需要我们去进一步了解。”\n\nWhile research has found dogs can have a lot of positive impacts on a child’s life, there are also risks associated with the dog-child relationship.\n虽然研究发现狗可以对孩子的生活产生很多积极影响，但两者的关系也存在风险。\n\nFor example, other studies have found dogs are more likely to bite children versus adults.\n例如，其他研究发现，与成年人相比，狗更有可能去咬孩子。\n\n“We still have a lot to learn about the dog-child relationship,” Udell said.\n尤德尔说：“关于狗和儿童的关系，我们还有很多要了解的地方。”\n\nBut research does show that kids are very capable of training dogs.\n但研究确实表明，孩子们在训练狗这方面非常有能力。\n\nQuestions 22 to 25 are based on the passage you have just heard.\n请根据你刚听到的短文回答第22至25题。\n\n22. What does the passage say about the findings of a new study from Oregon State University?\n22. 关于俄勒冈州立大学一项新研究的发现，短文说了什么？\n\n23. What does a growing body of evidence show, according to the passage?\n23. 根据短文，越来越多的证据表明了什么？\n\n24. What did Monique Udell say their study suggests?\n24. 莫妮克·尤德尔说他们的研究表明了什么？\n\n25. What does research show kids are very capable of doing?\n25. 研究表明，孩子们非常有能力做什么？', 99, 1426.14, 1233.46, 1332.69, 1338.26, 1360.17, NULL, NULL, 'cet4-2024-12-1-g08', 'PASSAGE', '[20:33.46]Passage Three｜短文三\n[20:35.37]A new study from Oregon State University found that dogs tend to match their behavior with the children in their family.｜俄勒冈州立大学的一项新研究发现，狗在行为上倾向于配合家里的孩子。\n[20:43.53]The findings are important, because there is a growing body of evidence that dogs can help children in many ways.｜这些发现很重要，因为越来越多的证据表明，狗可以在很多方面帮助孩子们。\n[20:51.43]These include helping with social development, increasing physical activity, managing anxiety or serving as a source of attachment in the face of changing family structures.｜这些方面包括促进孩子的社交发展、增加孩子的体育活动、缓解孩子的焦虑情绪，或是在家庭结构发生变化时成为孩子的依恋来源。\n[21:04.80]Yet, very little research has focused on how dogs perceive and socially engage with children.｜然而，很少有研究关注狗是如何感知孩子并与其进行社交互动的。\n[21:11.73]“The great news is that this study suggests dogs are paying a lot of attention to the kids that they live with,” said Monique Udell, the lead author of the study.｜该研究的主要作者莫妮克·尤德尔说：“好消息是，这项研究表明狗非常关注与它们生活在一起的孩子。”\n[21:23.19]“One interesting thing we have observed is that dogs are matching children’s behavior, but less frequently than what we have seen between dogs and adults. “｜我们观察到的一个有趣的现象是，狗会配合孩子的行为，但其频率比我们在狗和成人之间所观察到的更低。\n[21:34.43]This suggests that while dogs may view children as social companions, there are also some differences that we need to understand better.”｜这表明，虽然狗可能将孩子视为社交伙伴，但其中也存在一些差异需要我们去进一步了解。”\n[21:44.07]While research has found dogs can have a lot of positive impacts on a child’s life, there are also risks associated with the dog-child relationship.｜虽然研究发现狗可以对孩子的生活产生很多积极影响，但两者的关系也存在风险。\n[21:54.14]For example, other studies have found dogs are more likely to bite children versus adults.｜例如，其他研究发现，与成年人相比，狗更有可能去咬孩子。\n[22:01.11]“We still have a lot to learn about the dog-child relationship,” Udell said.｜尤德尔说：“关于狗和儿童的关系，我们还有很多要了解的地方。”\n[22:07.18]But research does show that kids are very capable of training dogs.｜但研究确实表明，孩子们在训练狗这方面非常有能力。\n[22:12.69]Questions 22 to 25 are based on the passage you have just heard.｜请根据你刚听到的短文回答第22至25题。\n[22:18.26]22. What does the passage say about the findings of a new study from Oregon State University?｜22. 关于俄勒冈州立大学一项新研究的发现，短文说了什么？\n[22:40.47]23. What does a growing body of evidence show, according to the passage?｜23. 根据短文，越来越多的证据表明了什么？\n[23:01.39]24. What did Monique Udell say their study suggests?｜24. 莫妮克·尤德尔说他们的研究表明了什么？\n[23:22.40]25. What does research show kids are very capable of doing?｜25. 研究表明，孩子们非常有能力做什么？', NOW(), NOW()
