SELECT
  @a_cet4_2024_12_2_06, '/audio/exams/listening-cet4-2024-12-2.mp3', 'News Report Three\n新闻三\n\nIt was a heartwarming moment that dozens of Indian rescuers rallied together to use a crane in order to save an elephant trapped at the bottom of a 20-foot well.\n这是一个温暖人心的时刻，一头大象被困在20英尺深的井底，数十名印度救援人员聚集在一起，使用起重机将其救出。\n\nThe massive rescue effort took place last week close to an army camp.\n上周，这场大规模的救援行动在军营附近展开。\n\nThe elephant wandered out of the jungle and fell into the well.\n大象走出丛林后，掉进了井里。\n\nThe army officers heard a noise coming from the well and realized an elephant was trapped deep inside.\n军官们听到了井里的杂音，意识到一头大象被困在井的深处。\n\nThe officers then threw in some food for the creature and called the local forest department for help.\n之后，军官们给井里的这头大象扔了些食物，并打电话向当地的林业部门寻求帮助。\n\nVideo of the rescue operation shows how the team used a crane to lift up the huge animal out of the well and onto the back of a truck.\n救援行动的视频展示了救援小组是如何使用起重机将这头庞然大物从井中吊起并放到卡车后面的。\n\nIt was then taken to an examining room for evaluation of any injuries.\n随后，它被送往检查室接受伤情鉴定。\n\nThe elephant was kept under close supervision for a few days before it was successfully released back into the wild.\n在被密切照看了几天后，这头大象被成功放归野外。\n\nQuestions 5 to 7 are based on the news report you have just heard.\n请根据你刚听到的新闻报道回答第5至7题。\n\n5. What does the report say dozens of Indians did last week?\n5. 报道称数十名印度人上周做了什么？\n\n6. Why did the army officers call the local forest department?\n6. 军官们为什么给当地的林业部门打电话？\n\n7. What does the news report say happened finally?\n7. 新闻报道称最后发生了什么？', 62, 1422.79, 285.40, 347.27, 374.16, 394.82, NULL, NULL, 'cet4-2024-12-2-g03', 'NEWS', '[04:45.40]News Report Three｜新闻三\n[04:47.60]It was a heartwarming moment that dozens of Indian rescuers rallied together to use a crane in order to save an elephant trapped at the bottom of a 20-foot well.｜这是一个温暖人心的时刻，一头大象被困在20英尺深的井底，数十名印度救援人员聚集在一起，使用起重机将其救出。\n[04:59.52]The massive rescue effort took place last week close to an army camp.｜上周，这场大规模的救援行动在军营附近展开。\n[05:04.80]The elephant wandered out of the jungle and fell into the well.｜大象走出丛林后，掉进了井里。\n[05:09.17]The army officers heard a noise coming from the well and realized an elephant was trapped deep inside.｜军官们听到了井里的杂音，意识到一头大象被困在井的深处。\n[05:16.31]The officers then threw in some food for the creature and called the local forest department for help.｜之后，军官们给井里的这头大象扔了些食物，并打电话向当地的林业部门寻求帮助。\n[05:23.22]Video of the rescue operation shows how the team used a crane to lift up the huge animal out of the well and onto the back of a truck.｜救援行动的视频展示了救援小组是如何使用起重机将这头庞然大物从井中吊起并放到卡车后面的。\n[05:33.18]It was then taken to an examining room for evaluation of any injuries.｜随后，它被送往检查室接受伤情鉴定。\n[05:38.89]The elephant was kept under close supervision for a few days before it was successfully released back into the wild.｜在被密切照看了几天后，这头大象被成功放归野外。\n[05:47.27]Questions 5 to 7 are based on the news report you have just heard.｜请根据你刚听到的新闻报道回答第5至7题。\n[05:52.98]5. What does the report say dozens of Indians did last week?｜5. 报道称数十名印度人上周做了什么？\n[06:14.16]6. Why did the army officers call the local forest department?｜6. 军官们为什么给当地的林业部门打电话？\n[06:35.12]7. What does the news report say happened finally?｜7. 新闻报道称最后发生了什么？', NOW(), NOW()
WHERE @a_cet4_2024_12_2_06 IS NOT NULL
