nd more than what I had budgeted.\n在那之后，我就拒绝花超过预算的钱。\n\nAnd by now, it’s just a habit.\n现在这已经成为一种习惯。\n\nQuestions 8 to 11 are based on the conversation you have just heard.\n请根据你刚听到的对话回答第8至11题。\n\n8. Why has the man stopped paying online for the last three months?\n8. 为什么男士在过去3个月不再使用在线支付了？\n\n9. What problem does the woman say she may also have?\n9. 女士说她可能也有什么问题？\n\n10. What does the man say he could do at the canteen?\n10. 男士说他在食堂能做什么？\n\n11. What is now just a habit for the man?\n11. 现在对男士来说，什么只是他的一种习惯？', 98, 1422.79, 443.58, 541.09, 587.45, 608.21, 495.53, 506.00, 'cet4-2024-12-2-g04', 'LONG_DIALOGUE', '[07:23.58]Conversation One｜对话一\n[07:26.16]M: I need to stop at the bank to withdraw some cash.｜男：我需要去银行取些现金。\n[07:29.91]W: Why not just pay with your phone?｜女：为什么不直接用手机支付呢？\n[07:32.24]M: Well, actually, I’ve stopped using online payments for the past three months now.｜男：嗯，事实上，在过去的3个月里，我已经停止使用在线支付了。\n[07:36.98]W: Stopped paying online?｜女：停止使用在线支付？\n[07:39.17]Oh, you must be worried that online payments aren’t secure.｜哦，你一定是担心在线支付不安全。\n[07:43.28]M: No, they are safe.｜男：不，在线支付很安全。\n[07:45.52]But paying online is too convenient.｜但在线支付太方便了。\n[07:47.82]I spent too much money on things I didn’t need.｜我在不需要的东西上花了太多钱。\n[07:51.14]W: Oh, impulse purchases can be an issue for me, too.｜女：哦，冲动购物对我来说也是个问题。\n[07:55.56]I’ve definitely bought clothes and shoes I didn’t need because they were on sale, and paying with my phone was so easy.｜我肯定买过一些不需要的衣服和鞋子，只是因为它们在打折，而且手机支付实在是太容易了。\n[08:03.47]But I’ve found that if I review my spending every night, that keeps me from spending too much.｜但我发现，如果每天晚上都复盘一下开支，我就不会花太多钱。\n[08:09.60]M: I tried that strategy, but it just didn’t work, because I’d be busy studying all day.｜男：我试过这个方法，但效果不佳，因为我整天都忙着学习。\n[08:15.53]Then when I was tired and hungry, I’d use my phone to order food, like burgers and other junk, instead of going to the canteen where I could get a healthier meal for half the price.｜当我又累又饿的时候，就会用手机订餐，如汉堡和其他垃圾食品，而不是去食堂吃价格便宜一半且更健康的饭菜。\n[08:26.30]W: Well, what do you do now then?｜女：那么，你现在是怎么做的呢？\n[08:28.67]It seems like you’d have the same problems with cash.｜你用现金似乎也会遇到同样的问题。\n[08:31.53]M: I go to the bank once a week, and the rest of the time I keep my bank card at home, so I can’t get more cash out.｜男：我每周去一次银行，其余时间我把银行卡放在家里，这样我就取不了更多的现金。\n[08:38.86]And I also have a notebook where I record my expenses.｜而且我还有一个记录开支的笔记本。\n[08:43.25]W: But what prevents you from just going to the bank and getting more money if you want to buy something?｜女：但是如果你想买东西，是什么阻止你去银行取更多的钱呢？\n[08:48.89]M: The first month I did withdraw extra cash twice, but I felt guilty about it.｜男：我第一个月确实多取了两次钱，但我对此感到内疚。\n[08:54.31]And after that, I refused to spend more than what I had budgeted.｜在那之后，我就拒绝花超过预算的钱。\n[08:58.63]And by now, it’s just a habit.｜现在这已经成为一种习惯。\n[09:01.09]Questions 8 to 11 are based on the conversation you have just heard.｜请根据你刚听到的对话回答第8至11题。\n[09:06.36]8. Why has the man stopped paying online for the last three months?｜8. 为什么男士在过去3个月不再使用在线支付了？\n[09:27.51]9. What problem does the woman say she may also have?｜9. 女士说她可能也有什么问题？\n[09:47.45]10. What does the man say he could do at the canteen?｜10. 男士说他在食堂能做什么？\n[10:08.51]11. What is now just a habit for the man?｜11. 现在对男士来说，什么只是他的一种习惯？', NOW(), NOW()
