SELECT
  @a_cet4_2024_12_2_15, '/audio/exams/listening-cet4-2024-12-2.mp3', 'Conversation Two\n对话二\n\nM: Please hear me out.\n男：请听我说完。\n\nI don’t want our son to spend his afternoons doing something he hates, even if it might prepare him for the future.\n我不想让我们的儿子把下午的时间都浪费在做他讨厌的事情上，即使这可能会为他的未来做准备。\n\nWhat about getting him to join a sport like soccer?\n让他参加足球这样的运动怎么样？\n\nFrom all the running and training, he could become quite athletic, not to mention the great physical benefits from exercising outside every day.\n通过跑步和训练，他会变得很健壮，更不用说每天在户外锻炼对身体大有裨益。\n\nW: Um, I don’t think he should be doing something so challenging with all his breathing issues.\n女：呃，儿子有呼吸方面的问题，我认为他不应该做这么有挑战性的事。\n\nWhat about playing an indoor sport like badminton?\n羽毛球这样的室内运动怎么样？\n\nThe environment is easier to control, and he can still get a good workout in addition to improving his hand-eye coordination.\n环境更容易控制，而且他仍然可以得到良好的锻炼，还能提高手眼协调能力。\n\nBesides, I could teach him some of the basics from my time as a badminton player.\n另外，我可以教他一些我当羽毛球运动员时学到的基本技能。\n\nM: Um, I’m thinking team sports should be the way to go.\n男：我觉得团队运动应该也是不错的选择。\n\nThere’s nothing like playing as part of a unit to accomplish a goal like winning a game or even a championship.\n没有什么比得上作为团队的一员去实现目标，比如赢得一场比赛，甚至是拿到冠军。\n\nHe could try basketball since many of the courts are indoors now, and it’s a sport that could help him understand team spirit while cooperating with others.\n他可以尝试打篮球，因为现在许多球场都在室内，而且这项运动可以帮助他在与他人合作的过程中理解团队精神。\n\nMaybe he could even join the school basketball team when he’s ready.\n也许等他准备好了，他甚至还可以加入学校的篮球队。\n\nW: Oh, oh, what about volleyball?\n女：哦，哦，排球怎么样？\n\nIt’s a team sport, and they often have mixed-gender teams, so he could socialize with both girls and boys.\n这是一项团队运动，经常会有男女混合的队伍，所以他跟女孩和男孩都有相处的机会。\n\nIt’s not as popular as some sports, which means he has better odds of possibly getting an athletic scholarship in the future.\n它不像某些运动那样受欢迎，这意味着他将来获得体育奖学金的可能性更大。\n\nI also believe you were a beach volleyball athlete yourself not so long ago.\n而且我知道你不久前还是一名沙滩排球运动员。\n\nM: As I’ve said many times before, beach volleyball and indoor volleyball are completely different.\n男：正如我之前多次说过的那样，沙滩排球和室内排球是完全不同的。\n\nQuestions 12 to 15 are based on the conversation you have just heard.\n请根据你刚听到的对话回答第12至15题。\n\n12. Why is the woman opposed to their son joining a sport like soccer?\n12. 为什么女士反对他们的儿子参加足球这样的运动？\n\n13. What does the man suggest their son try in order to understand team spirit?\n13. 男士建议他们的儿子尝试什么运动来理解团队精神？\n\n14. What is one of the woman’s considerations in choosing a sport for her son?\n14. 女士在为她儿子选择运动项目方面考虑的因素之一是什么？\n\n15. What does the man say about beach volleyball?\n15. 对于沙滩排球，男士的看法是什么？\n\nSection\nCC节', 104, 1422.79, 626.80, 730.79, 801.51, 821.51, 722.59, 730.49, 'cet4-2024-12-2-g05', 'LONG_DIALOGUE', '[10:26.80]Conversation Two｜对话二\n[10:29.71]M: Please hear me out.｜男：请听我说完。\n[10:31.85]I don’t want our son to spend his afternoons doing something he hates, even if it might prepare him for the future.｜我不想让我们的儿子把下午的时间都浪费在做他讨厌的事情上，即使这可能会为他的未来做准备。\n[10:39.22]What about getting him to join a sport like soccer?｜让他参加足球这样的运动怎么样？\n[10:42.73]From all the running and training, he could become quite athletic, not to mention the great physical benefits from exercising outside every day.｜通过跑步和训练，他会变得很健壮，更不用说每天在户外锻炼对身体大有裨益。\n[10:51.62]W: Um, I don’t think he should be doing something so challenging with all his breathing issues.｜女：呃，儿子有呼吸方面的问题，我认为他不应该做这么有挑战性的事。\n[10:57.91]What about playing an indoor sport like badminton?｜羽毛球这样的室内运动怎么样？\n[11:01.63]The environment is easier to control, and he can still get a good workout in addition to improving his hand-eye coordination.｜环境更容易控制，而且他仍然可以得到良好的锻炼，还能提高手眼协调能力。\n[11:09.43]Besides, I could teach him some of the basics from my time as a badminton player.｜另外，我可以教他一些我当羽毛球运动员时学到的基本技能。\n[11:14.85]M: Um, I’m thinking team sports should be the way to go.｜男：我觉得团队运动应该也是不错的选择。\n[11:19.36]There’s nothing like playing as part of a unit to accomplish a goal like winning a game or even a championship.｜没有什么比得上作为团队的一员去实现目标，比如赢得一场比赛，甚至是拿到冠军。\n[11:25.97]He could try basketball since many of the courts are indoors now, and it’s a sport that could help him understand team spirit while cooperating with others.｜他可以尝试打篮球，因为现在许多球场都在室内，而且这项运动可以帮助他在与他人合作的过程中理解团队精神。\n[11:35.79]Maybe he could even join the school basketball team when he’s ready.｜也许等他准备好了，他甚至还可以加入学校的篮球队。\n[11:39.95]W: Oh, oh, what about volleyball?｜女：哦，哦，排球怎么样？\n[11:42.85]It’s a team sport, and they often have mixed-gender teams, so he could socialize with both girls and boys.｜这是一项团队运动，经常会有男女混合的队伍，所以他跟女孩和男孩都有相处的机会。\n[11:49.76]It’s not as popular as some sports, which means he has better odds of possibly getting an athletic scholarship in the future.｜它不像某些运动那样受欢迎，这意味着他将来获得体育奖学金的可能性更大。\n[11:57.60]I also believe you were a beach volleyball athlete yourself not so long ago.｜而且我知道你不久前还是一名沙滩排球运动员。\n[12:02.59]M: As I’ve said many times before, beach volleyball and indoor volleyball are completely different.｜男：正如我之前多次说过的那样，沙滩排球和室内排球是完全不同的。\n[12:10.79]Questions 12 to 15 are based on the conversation you have just heard.｜请根据你刚听到的对话回答第12至15题。\n[12:15.99]12. Why is the woman opposed to their son joining a sport like soccer?｜12. 为什么女士反对他们的儿子参加足球这样的运动？\n[12:37.36]13. What does the man suggest their son try in order to understand team spirit?｜13. 男士建议他们的儿子尝试什么运动来理解团队精神？\n[12:59.84]14. What is one of the woman’s considerations in choosing a sport for her son?｜14. 女士在为她儿子选择运动项目方面考虑的因素之一是什么？\n[13:21.51]15. What does the man say about beach volleyball?｜15. 对于沙滩排球，男士的看法是什么？\n[13:41.34]Section｜CC节', NOW(), NOW()
WHERE @a_cet4_2024_12_2_15 IS NOT NULL
