SELECT
  @a_cet4_2024_12_2_17, '/audio/exams/listening-cet4-2024-12-2.mp3', 'Passage One\n短文一\n\nLift-off is usually the most environmentally harmful stage of any space mission, with vast quantities of fuel burnt up in a matter of minutes.\n在所有的太空任务中，发射阶段通常都是对环境危害最大的阶段，大量燃料会在短短几分钟内就燃烧殆尽。\n\nFor instance, SpaceX’s Falcon 9 gets through 112 tonnes of refined fuel, emitting about 336 tonnes of CO2.\n例如，美国太空探索技术公司的猎鹰9号火箭要消耗112吨精炼燃料，排放约336吨二氧化碳。\n\nThis is the equivalent produced by your average car driving almost 70 times around the world.\n这相当于一辆普通汽车绕地球行驶近70圈所产生的排放量。\n\nAs well as greenhouse gases, rocket engines emit particles that destroy ozone.\n除了排放温室气体，火箭发动机还会排放破坏臭氧的颗粒物。\n\nThese issues are growing more pressing with the emergence of commercial spaceflight.\n随着商业太空飞行的出现，这些问题变得越来越紧迫。\n\nThere were 114 space launches in 2020, but there may be up to 1,000 per year in future. 2020\n年共有114次太空发射，但未来每年可能会有多达1,000次。\n\nSustainable fuels are the top priority to enable greener space travel.\n可持续燃料是实现绿色太空旅行的首选。\n\nCurrent spacecraft use a variety of fuels, but most are based on fossil fuels.\n目前的航天器可以使用各种燃料，但大多数用的还是化石燃料。\n\nOne potentially greener option is liquid hydrogen and oxygen.\n一种可能更环保的选择是液态氢和液态氧。\n\nHydrogen can be obtained sustainably by using solar power to break water down into oxygen and hydrogen.\n通过利用太阳能将水分解为氧气和氢气，可以可持续地获得氢气。\n\nReusable rockets can cut down on some of the waste associated with spaceflight.\n可重复使用的火箭能够减少一些与太空飞行相关的废弃物。\n\nTraditionally, boosters, fuel tanks and other components are treated as expendable.\n传统上，助推器、燃料箱和其他部件被视为消耗品。\n\nBut guiding them back to Earth in a controlled manner opens new possibilities—most components from the Falcon 9 can be reused up to 100 times.\n但以可控的方式将它们引导回地球开辟了新的可能性——猎鹰9号的大多数组件都可以重复使用100多次。\n\nTruly environmentally friendly space travel is still some way off.\n实现真正环保的太空旅行尚需时日。\n\nBut we already have many of the technologies needed to start limiting its impact on our planet.\n但我们已经拥有了许多必要的技术，可以开始减少太空旅行对地球的影响。\n\nQuestions 16 to 18 are based on the passage you have just heard.\n请根据你刚听到的短文回答第16至18题。\n\n16. What do we learn from the passage about the lift-off of spacecraft?\n16. 关于航天器的发射，我们从短文中了解到了什么？\n\n17. What happens traditionally to boosters, fuel tanks and other components in spaceflight?\n17. 传统上，航天飞行中的助推器、燃料箱和其他部件会如何处理？\n\n18. What does the passage say we already have regarding spaceflight?\n18. 关于航天飞行，短文说我们已经拥有了什么？', 114, 1422.79, 850.01, 964.36, 991.23, 1011.23, 933.62, 939.39, 'cet4-2024-12-2-g06', 'PASSAGE', '[14:10.01]Passage One｜短文一\n[14:12.30]Lift-off is usually the most environmentally harmful stage of any space mission, with vast quantities of fuel burnt up in a matter of minutes.｜在所有的太空任务中，发射阶段通常都是对环境危害最大的阶段，大量燃料会在短短几分钟内就燃烧殆尽。\n[14:23.54]For instance, SpaceX’s Falcon 9 gets through 112 tonnes of refined fuel, emitting about 336 tonnes of CO2.｜例如，美国太空探索技术公司的猎鹰9号火箭要消耗112吨精炼燃料，排放约336吨二氧化碳。\n[14:34.44]This is the equivalent produced by your average car driving almost 70 times around the world.｜这相当于一辆普通汽车绕地球行驶近70圈所产生的排放量。\n[14:41.39]As well as greenhouse gases, rocket engines emit particles that destroy ozone.｜除了排放温室气体，火箭发动机还会排放破坏臭氧的颗粒物。\n[14:47.56]These issues are growing more pressing with the emergence of commercial spaceflight.｜随着商业太空飞行的出现，这些问题变得越来越紧迫。\n[14:52.80]There were 114 space launches in 2020, but there may be up to 1,000 per year in future. 2020｜年共有114次太空发射，但未来每年可能会有多达1,000次。\n[15:01.34]Sustainable fuels are the top priority to enable greener space travel.｜可持续燃料是实现绿色太空旅行的首选。\n[15:07.74]Current spacecraft use a variety of fuels, but most are based on fossil fuels.｜目前的航天器可以使用各种燃料，但大多数用的还是化石燃料。\n[15:14.17]One potentially greener option is liquid hydrogen and oxygen.｜一种可能更环保的选择是液态氢和液态氧。\n[15:19.04]Hydrogen can be obtained sustainably by using solar power to break water down into oxygen and hydrogen.｜通过利用太阳能将水分解为氧气和氢气，可以可持续地获得氢气。\n[15:27.27]Reusable rockets can cut down on some of the waste associated with spaceflight.｜可重复使用的火箭能够减少一些与太空飞行相关的废弃物。\n[15:33.62]Traditionally, boosters, fuel tanks and other components are treated as expendable.｜传统上，助推器、燃料箱和其他部件被视为消耗品。\n[15:39.69]But guiding them back to Earth in a controlled manner opens new possibilities—most components from the Falcon 9 can be reused up to 100 times.｜但以可控的方式将它们引导回地球开辟了新的可能性——猎鹰9号的大多数组件都可以重复使用100多次。\n[15:51.35]Truly environmentally friendly space travel is still some way off.｜实现真正环保的太空旅行尚需时日。\n[15:57.28]But we already have many of the technologies needed to start limiting its impact on our planet.｜但我们已经拥有了许多必要的技术，可以开始减少太空旅行对地球的影响。\n[16:04.36]Questions 16 to 18 are based on the passage you have just heard.｜请根据你刚听到的短文回答第16至18题。\n[16:09.88]16. What do we learn from the passage about the lift-off of spacecraft?｜16. 关于航天器的发射，我们从短文中了解到了什么？\n[16:31.23]17. What happens traditionally to boosters, fuel tanks and other components in spaceflight?｜17. 传统上，航天飞行中的助推器、燃料箱和其他部件会如何处理？\n[16:55.43]18. What does the passage say we already have regarding spaceflight?｜18. 关于航天飞行，短文说我们已经拥有了什么？', NOW(), NOW()
