  @a_cet4_2024_12_2_21, '/audio/exams/listening-cet4-2024-12-2.mp3', 'Passage Two\n短文二\n\nHelping to look after a pet can facilitate numerous aspects of a child’s emotional development.\n让孩子帮助照顾宠物可以在多个方面促进孩子的情感发展。\n\nResearch shows that reading to a loyal and non-judgmental companion, such as a dog or cat, can encourage reluctant readers to read aloud, which will in turn boost their self-confidence.\n研究表明，给忠实且不妄加评判的同伴（如狗或猫）读书，可以鼓励那些不愿意朗读的读者大声朗读，还能增强他们的自信心。\n\nHaving a companion to talk to about their feelings can also help children feel secure and develop communication skills.\n有一个可以倾诉感受的同伴也能让孩子感到安心，并提高其沟通技巧。\n\nA household pet can also cultivate a child’s sense of responsibility as their parent explains the necessary processes of keeping their pet happy and healthy.\n家养宠物还可以培养孩子的责任感，因为父母会告诉他们让宠物保持快乐和健康所必需的过程。\n\nAs a child matures, they can then take on more of the daily responsibilities, boosting their sense of independence.\n随着孩子长大，他们可以承担更多日常责任，从而增强独立意识。\n\nPets also provide a fantastic subject for research and learning.\n宠物也是研究和学习的绝佳主题。\n\nParents can encourage their child to research their favourite pets at the library or during a supervised internet search.\n父母可以鼓励孩子去图书馆或在监督下进行网络搜索，以研究他们最喜欢的宠物。\n\nTaking children along to the pet shop to buy food and supplies will support their cognitive development as their passion for learning flourishes.\n随着孩子们的学习热情高涨，带他们去宠物店购买宠物食品和用品将有助于其认知发展。\n\nA child’s physical development can benefit greatly from taking pets for walks in the fresh air.\n让孩子带宠物出门，呼吸外面的新鲜空气，这对其身体发育大有裨益。\n\nEven their fine motor skills can be utilised in taking care of a beloved animal.\n甚至他们的精细运动技能也能在照顾宠物的过程中得以运用。\n\nWhen responsibilities are well paced and communicated, a child can benefit greatly from involvement in bringing up a happy and healthy pet.\n当责任得到妥善安排和充分沟通时，孩子在养宠物使其健康快乐地长大这一过程中能够受益匪浅。\n\nAnd of course, if a child doesn’t have a pet in their own household, they can still benefit from all of the above when visiting a friend who does.\n当然，如果孩