SELECT
  @a_cet4_2024_12_2_23, '/audio/exams/listening-cet4-2024-12-2.mp3', 'Passage Three\n短文三\n\nA new bill in the Ohio legislature would require state public colleges and universities to send prospective students a packet of information.\n俄亥俄州立法机构的一项新法案将要求州立公立学院和大学向有意愿的学生发送一份资料。\n\nThis would include costs of college, grants and scholarships.\n资料里的信息包括大学学费、助学金和奖学金。\n\nIt would also include expected monthly loan payments and projected salary after college.\n还包括预计的每月贷款还款额和大学毕业后的预期工资。\n\nState Representative Adam Mathews is one of the two legislators who proposed the bill.\n州议员亚当·马修斯是提出该法案的两名立法者之一。\n\nHe said it would give prospective students more information about what to expect once they graduate.\n他表示，该法案将为有意愿的学生提供更多信息，让他们知道自己毕业后会面临什么。\n\n“Putting that information in front of them will give them the best opportunity to match their skills and their dreams to what our schools can provide,” said Mathews.\n马修斯说：“把这些信息摆在他们面前，将为他们提供最好的机会，让他们能够根据拥有的技能和梦想选择可以为其提供相应资源的学校。”\n\nHe notes that the state can only regulate public institutions in this way, but he hopes private institutions in Ohio follow the lead of the state and post similar information.\n他指出，该州用这种方式只能对公立大学进行监管，但他希望俄亥俄州的私立大学能够效仿该做法，发送类似的信息。\n\nHe believes giving out this information will help Ohio’s colleges and universities to be more competitive.\n他认为，发送这些信息可以让俄亥俄州的学院和大学更具竞争力。\n\nThe information will highlight what a great value they have for their very reasonable cost.\n这些信息会突出强调，它们拥有巨大的价值，只需要通过非常合理的花费就能获得。\n\nOhio’s schools are already competitive.\n俄亥俄州的学校已经很有竞争力了。\n\nThe state attracts more undergraduate students than it sends to colleges out of state.\n该州吸引的本科生人数超过了其送往州外上大学的本科生人数。\n\nMany colleges and universities currently provide similar information on their websites.\n许多学院和大学目前在其网站上提供了类似的信息。\n\nThis includes tuition, fees, graduation rates and more.\n包括学费、杂费、毕业率等。\n\nBut students need to search for the information.\n但学生需要自己去搜索这些信息。\n\nThis bill would require the universities and colleges to send a packet directly to students.\n该法案将要求大学和学院把资料直接发送给学生。\n\nQuestions 22 to 25 are based on the passage you have just heard.\n请根据你刚听到的短文回答第22至25题。\n\n22. What would the new bill in the Ohio legislature require public colleges and universities to do?\n22. 俄亥俄州立法机构的新法案要求公立学院和大学做什么？\n\n23. What can the state only do according to Adam Mathews?\n23. 根据亚当·马修斯的说法，该州只能做什么？\n\n24. What do we learn about Ohio’s schools from the passage?\n24. 关于俄亥俄州的学校，我们从短文中了解到了什么？\n\n25. What is the problem with schools providing information on their websites?\n25.在其网站上提供信息的学校有什么问题？', 109, 1422.79, 1216.53, 1325.24, 1354.56, 1374.96, 1265.47, 1278.71, 'cet4-2024-12-2-g08', 'PASSAGE', '[20:16.53]Passage Three｜短文三\n[20:18.47]A new bill in the Ohio legislature would require state public colleges and universities to send prospective students a packet of information.｜俄亥俄州立法机构的一项新法案将要求州立公立学院和大学向有意愿的学生发送一份资料。\n[20:28.26]This would include costs of college, grants and scholarships.｜资料里的信息包括大学学费、助学金和奖学金。\n[20:33.57]It would also include expected monthly loan payments and projected salary after college.｜还包括预计的每月贷款还款额和大学毕业后的预期工资。\n[20:40.60]State Representative Adam Mathews is one of the two legislators who proposed the bill.｜州议员亚当·马修斯是提出该法案的两名立法者之一。\n[20:47.14]He said it would give prospective students more information about what to expect once they graduate.｜他表示，该法案将为有意愿的学生提供更多信息，让他们知道自己毕业后会面临什么。\n[20:54.58]“Putting that information in front of them will give them the best opportunity to match their skills and their dreams to what our schools can provide,” said Mathews.｜马修斯说：“把这些信息摆在他们面前，将为他们提供最好的机会，让他们能够根据拥有的技能和梦想选择可以为其提供相应资源的学校。”\n[21:05.47]He notes that the state can only regulate public institutions in this way, but he hopes private institutions in Ohio follow the lead of the state and post similar information.｜他指出，该州用这种方式只能对公立大学进行监管，但他希望俄亥俄州的私立大学能够效仿该做法，发送类似的信息。\n[21:19.01]He believes giving out this information will help Ohio’s colleges and universities to be more competitive.｜他认为，发送这些信息可以让俄亥俄州的学院和大学更具竞争力。\n[21:26.72]The information will highlight what a great value they have for their very reasonable cost.｜这些信息会突出强调，它们拥有巨大的价值，只需要通过非常合理的花费就能获得。\n[21:32.81]Ohio’s schools are already competitive.｜俄亥俄州的学校已经很有竞争力了。\n[21:36.52]The state attracts more undergraduate students than it sends to colleges out of state.｜该州吸引的本科生人数超过了其送往州外上大学的本科生人数。\n[21:42.83]Many colleges and universities currently provide similar information on their websites.｜许多学院和大学目前在其网站上提供了类似的信息。\n[21:49.26]This includes tuition, fees, graduation rates and more.｜包括学费、杂费、毕业率等。\n[21:55.04]But students need to search for the information.｜但学生需要自己去搜索这些信息。\n[21:58.58]This bill would require the universities and colleges to send a packet directly to students.｜该法案将要求大学和学院把资料直接发送给学生。\n[22:05.24]Questions 22 to 25 are based on the passage you have just heard.｜请根据你刚听到的短文回答第22至25题。\n[22:10.95]22. What would the new bill in the Ohio legislature require public colleges and universities to do?｜22. 俄亥俄州立法机构的新法案要求公立学院和大学做什么？\n[22:34.56]23. What can the state only do according to Adam Mathews?｜23. 根据亚当·马修斯的说法，该州只能做什么？\n[22:55.26]24. What do we learn about Ohio’s schools from the passage?｜24. 关于俄亥俄州的学校，我们从短文中了解到了什么？\n[23:17.23]25. What is the problem with schools providing information on their websites?｜25.在其网站上提供信息的学校有什么问题？', NOW(), NOW()
WHERE @a_cet4_2024_12_2_23 IS NOT NULL
