  (`question_id`, `audio_url`, `transcript`, `duration_seconds`, `audio_total_seconds`, `audio_start_seconds`, `audio_end_seconds`, `question_start_seconds`, `question_end_seconds`, `answer_start_seconds`, `answer_end_seconds`, `group_key`, `listening_type`, `lrc_content`, `created_at`, `updated_at`)
SELECT
  @a_cet4_2025_06_1_05, '/audio/exams/listening-cet4-2025-06-1.mp3', 'News Report Three\n新闻三\n\nCan fast-fashion be sustainable?\n快时尚能否实现可持续发展？\n\nResearchers think yes.\n研究人员认为答案是肯定的。\n\nIdentifying why the fast-fashion business model creates waste and determining whether regulators can establish incentives for consumers and manufacturers are steps to reduce waste.\n找出快时尚商业模式造成浪费的原因，并确定监管机构是否能够为消费者和制造商建立激励机制，是减少浪费的办法。\n\nRecently, the clothing industry has come under attack for creating a waste problem with serious environmental consequences.\n最近，服装行业因其造成的浪费引发了严重的环境问题而受到抨击。\n\nIn the absence of environmentally and economically feasible recycling options, fast-fashion manufacturers pump out low-quality clothes produced in high volumes that are worn only a few times and then discarded.\n由于缺乏在环境和经济上均可行的回收方案，快时尚制造商大量生产低质量衣服，这些衣服往往只穿几次就被丢弃。\n\nThe researchers put forth policy contributions, ranging from sustainable disposal of leftover stock to production tax, to incentivize both manufacturers and consumers to be more waste conscious.\n研究人员提出了一系列政策建议，包括采用可持续的方式处理剩余库存、征收生产税等，旨在激励制造商和消费者增强减少浪费的意识。\n\nIn order to devise effective policies to curb the environmental impact of the clothing industry, it is important to identify the source of the problem in the supply chain.\n为了制定有效的政策来遏制服装行业对环境的影响，找出供应链中的问题根源至关重要。\n\nManufacturers, consumers, and regulatory bodies can then take an informed approach to recognize the environmental impact of fast-fashion and to design an ecosystem to reduce waste, incentivize innovation, and create new business models to manage waste.\n然后，制造商、消费者和监管机构可以采取明智的方法，认识到快时尚对环境的影响，并设计一个生态系统来减少浪费、激励创新，以及创建新的商业模式来治理浪费。\n\nQuestions 5 to 7 are based on the news report you have just heard.\n请根据你刚听到的新闻报道回答第5至7题。\n\n5. Why has the clothing industry come under attack?\n5. 为什么服装行业受到了抨击？\n\n6. Why do the researchers put forth such policies as production tax?\n6. 为什么研究人员提出了生产税这样的政策？\n\n7. What should be done first to eliminate the harm caused by the clothing industry?\n7. 为了消除服装行业造成的危害，首先应该做什么？', 96, 1415.84, 269.73, 365.73, 371.17, 389.85, NULL, NULL, 'cet4-2025-06-1-g03', 'NEWS', '[04:29.73]News Report Three｜新闻三\n[04:32.00]Can fast-fashion be sustainable?｜快时尚能否实现可持续发展？\n[04:35.09]Researchers think yes.｜研究人员认为答案是肯定的。\n[04:37.87]Identifying why the fast-fashion business model creates waste and determining whether regulators can establish incentives for consumers and manufacturers are steps to reduce waste.｜找出快时尚商业模式造成浪费的原因，并确定监管机构是否能够为消费者和制造商建立激励机制，是减少浪费的办法。\n[04:51.84]Recently, the clothing industry has come under attack for creating a waste problem with serious environmental consequences.｜最近，服装行业因其造成的浪费引发了严重的环境问题而受到抨击。\n[05:01.17]In the absence of environmentally and economically feasible recycling options, fast-fashion manufacturers pump out low-quality clothes produced in high volumes that are worn only a few times and then discarded.｜由于缺乏在环境和经济上均可行的回收方案，快时尚制造商大量生产低质量衣服，这些衣服往往只穿几次就被丢弃。\n[05:17.08]The researchers put forth policy contributions, ranging from sustainable disposal of leftover stock to production tax, to incentivize both manufacturers and consumers to be more waste conscious.｜研究人员提出了一系列政策建议，包括采用可持续的方式处理剩余库存、征收生产税等，旨在激励制造商和消费者增强减少浪费的意识。\n[05:32.41]In order to devise effective policies to curb the environmental impact of the clothing industry, it is important to identify the source of the problem in the supply chain.｜为了制定有效的政策来遏制服装行业对环境的影响，找出供应链中的问题根源至关重要。\n[05:44.26]Manufacturers, consumers, and regulatory bodies can then take an informed approach to recognize the environmental impact of fast-fashion and to design an ecosystem to reduce waste, incentivize innovation, and create new business models to manage waste.｜然后，制造商、消费者和监管机构可以采取明智的方法，认识到快时尚对环境的影响，并设计一个生态系统来减少浪费、激励创新，以及创建新的商业模式来治理浪费。\n[06:05.73]Questions 5 to 7 are based on the news report you have just heard.｜请根据你刚听到的新闻报道回答第5至7题。\n[06:11.17]5. Why has the clothing industry come under attack?｜5. 为什么服装行业受到了抨击？\n[06:30.15]6. Why do the researchers put forth such policies as production tax?｜6. 为什么研究人员提出了生产税这样的政策？\n[06:50.35]7. What should be done first to eliminate the harm caused by the clothing industry?｜7. 为了消除服装行业造成的危害，首先应该做什么？', NOW(), NOW()
WHERE @a_cet4_2025_06_1_05 IS NOT NULL
