SELECT
  @a_cet4_2025_06_1_12, '/audio/exams/listening-cet4-2025-06-1.mp3', 'Conversation Two\n对话二\n\nM: Did you hear about Johnny?\n男：你听说约翰尼的事了吗？\n\nW: No, why? Is he okay?\n女：没有，怎么了？他还好吗？\n\nM: He had some plastic surgery done.\n男：他做了些整形手术。\n\nW: What? Why?\n女：什么？为什么？\n\nM: Do you remember he had a scar on his face?\n男：你还记得他脸上有道疤吗？\n\nW: Yes, of course. He always had that.\n女：是的，当然记得。他一直都有那道疤。\n\nI’ve known him since primary school, and I always remember him having that on his cheek.\n我从小学就认识他了，我一直记得他脸颊上有那道疤。\n\nM: Well, he had it fixed.\n男：嗯，他把那道疤修好了。\n\nW: Fixed? What do you mean?\n女：修好？你是什么意思？\n\nYou can’t fix a scar.\n疤痕是无法修好的。\n\nM: You know what I mean.\n男：你知道我的意思。\n\nHe had an operation done on it, plastic surgery, in order to cover it and make it less noticeable.\n他做了个手术，就是整形手术，为了遮住那道疤，让它不那么明显。\n\nW: Oh, well, that’s ridiculous, isn’t it?\n女：哦，好吧，那太荒谬了，不是吗？\n\nIt was noticeable, sure, but it wasn’t an ugly scar.\n那道疤确实很明显，但并不丑啊。\n\nIt never occurred to me that he should have it taken care of like that.\n我从来没想过他会用那种方式去处理它。\n\nM: I agree. I can understand some scars and physical defects can be ugly and distracting, but not Johnny’s.\n男：我同意。我能理解有些疤痕和身体缺陷确实影响美观，让人分心，但约翰尼的可不是。\n\nIn fact, I thought it added character, like it gave him a certain uniqueness.\n事实上，我认为那道疤为约翰尼增添了个性，就像赋予了他某种独特性。\n\nW: He must have felt differently, though.\n女：不过，他自己可能不这样想。\n\nHe must have felt self-conscious and insecure, perhaps.\n他可能觉得不自在，没有自信。\n\nM: No, no, that’s not the reason.\n男：不，不，那不是原因。\n\nHe was totally fine with his scar.\n他对那道疤完全不在意。\n\nAs you said, he had had it for most of his life.\n就像你说的，他大半辈子都有那道疤。\n\nW: Then why did he have the operation?\n女：那他为什么还要做手术呢？\n\nM: Because his girlfriend wanted him to.\n男：因为他的女朋友想让他这么做。\n\nW: What? That’s so superficial and selfish of her.\n什么？她真是太肤浅、太自私了。\n\nIf Johnny’s girlfriend doesn’t like him for who he is, then she does not deserve to be his girlfriend.\n如果约翰尼的女朋友不能接受他原本的样子，那她就不配做他的女朋友。\n\nM: You’re right.\n男：你说得对。\n\nSo he is insane to give in to her like that.\n所以他那么轻易就向她妥协，真是太疯狂了。\n\nBut when I told him, he said he loves her and would just do what she wants him to.\n但当我告诉他时，他说他爱她，所以会照她说的做。\n\nW: What a fool he is!\n女：他真是个傻瓜！\n\nQuestions 12 to 15 are based on the conversation you have just heard.\n请根据你刚听到的对话回答第12至15题。\n\n12. What does the man say about Johnny?\n12. 关于约翰尼，男士说了什么?\n\n13. What does the woman find puzzling?\n13. 女士觉得什么令人困惑?\n\n14. What did the man think of Johnny’s scar?\n14. 男士对约翰尼的伤疤有什么看法?\n\n15. How could we describe the speakers’ attitude towards Johnny’s girlfriend?\n15. 我们该如何描述说话者对约翰尼的女朋友的态度?', 103, 1415.84, 649.59, 752.43, 757.21, 774.73, 655.82, 657.68, 'cet4-2025-06-1-g05', 'LONG_DIALOGUE', '[10:49.59]Conversation Two｜对话二\n[10:51.75]M: Did you hear about Johnny?｜男：你听说约翰尼的事了吗？\n[10:53.50]W: No, why? Is he okay?｜女：没有，怎么了？他还好吗？\n[10:55.82]M: He had some plastic surgery done.｜男：他做了些整形手术。\n[10:57.98]W: What? Why?｜女：什么？为什么？\n[10:59.49]M: Do you remember he had a scar on his face?｜男：你还记得他脸上有道疤吗？\n[11:02.49]W: Yes, of course. He always had that.｜女：是的，当然记得。他一直都有那道疤。\n[11:05.21]I’ve known him since primary school, and I always remember him having that on his cheek.｜我从小学就认识他了，我一直记得他脸颊上有那道疤。\n[11:10.60]M: Well, he had it fixed.｜男：嗯，他把那道疤修好了。\n[11:13.09]W: Fixed? What do you mean?｜女：修好？你是什么意思？\n[11:15.01]You can’t fix a scar.｜疤痕是无法修好的。\n[11:17.41]M: You know what I mean.｜男：你知道我的意思。\n[11:18.89]He had an operation done on it, plastic surgery, in order to cover it and make it less noticeable.｜他做了个手术，就是整形手术，为了遮住那道疤，让它不那么明显。\n[11:25.76]W: Oh, well, that’s ridiculous, isn’t it?｜女：哦，好吧，那太荒谬了，不是吗？\n[11:28.79]It was noticeable, sure, but it wasn’t an ugly scar.｜那道疤确实很明显，但并不丑啊。\n[11:32.96]It never occurred to me that he should have it taken care of like that.｜我从来没想过他会用那种方式去处理它。\n[11:36.95]M: I agree. I can understand some scars and physical defects can be ugly and distracting, but not Johnny’s.｜男：我同意。我能理解有些疤痕和身体缺陷确实影响美观，让人分心，但约翰尼的可不是。\n[11:44.60]In fact, I thought it added character, like it gave him a certain uniqueness.｜事实上，我认为那道疤为约翰尼增添了个性，就像赋予了他某种独特性。\n[11:50.44]W: He must have felt differently, though.｜女：不过，他自己可能不这样想。\n[11:52.70]He must have felt self-conscious and insecure, perhaps.｜他可能觉得不自在，没有自信。\n[11:57.16]M: No, no, that’s not the reason.｜男：不，不，那不是原因。\n[11:59.50]He was totally fine with his scar.｜他对那道疤完全不在意。\n[12:01.72]As you said, he had had it for most of his life.｜就像你说的，他大半辈子都有那道疤。\n[12:05.11]W: Then why did he have the operation?｜女：那他为什么还要做手术呢？\n[12:07.66]M: Because his girlfriend wanted him to.｜男：因为他的女朋友想让他这么做。\n[12:10.06]W: What? That’s so superficial and selfish of her.｜什么？她真是太肤浅、太自私了。\n[12:14.10]If Johnny’s girlfriend doesn’t like him for who he is, then she does not deserve to be his girlfriend.｜如果约翰尼的女朋友不能接受他原本的样子，那她就不配做他的女朋友。\n[12:20.68]M: You’re right.｜男：你说得对。\n[12:21.62]So he is insane to give in to her like that.｜所以他那么轻易就向她妥协，真是太疯狂了。\n[12:24.64]But when I told him, he said he loves her and would just do what she wants him to.｜但当我告诉他时，他说他爱她，所以会照她说的做。\n[12:30.18]W: What a fool he is!｜女：他真是个傻瓜！\n[12:32.43]Questions 12 to 15 are based on the conversation you have just heard.｜请根据你刚听到的对话回答第12至15题。\n[12:37.21]12. What does the man say about Johnny?｜12. 关于约翰尼，男士说了什么?\n[12:55.03]13. What does the woman find puzzling?｜13. 女士觉得什么令人困惑?\n[13:13.16]14. What did the man think of Johnny’s scar?｜14. 男士对约翰尼的伤疤有什么看法?\n[13:31.54]15. How could we describe the speakers’ attitude towards Johnny’s girlfriend?｜15. 我们该如何描述说话者对约翰尼的女朋友的态度?', NOW(), NOW()
WHERE @a_cet4_2025_06_1_12 IS NOT NULL
