SELECT
  @a_cet4_2025_06_1_16, '/audio/exams/listening-cet4-2025-06-1.mp3', 'Passage One\n短文一\n\nTalking is unique to humans.\n说话是人类独有的能力。\n\nAn animal might make ten different sounds, but an adult human knows more than 20,000 words.\n动物可能会发出十种不同的声音，但一个成年人类却知道超过两万个词语。\n\nAdditionally, we’re the only animal that expresses thoughts in full sentences.\n此外，我们是唯一能用完整句子表达思想的动物。\n\nResearchers don’t think language was invented.\n研究人员认为语言不是发明出来的。\n\nInstead, they think it evolved.\n相反，他们认为语言是进化而来的。\n\nHow did talking evolve?\n说话是如何进化的呢？\n\nThere are two main theories.\n主要有两种理论。\n\nThe first theory is that language started with people making different sounds, mostly imitating the things around them, like animal calls, nature sounds and the sounds of tools.\n第一种理论认为，语言起源于人们发出的不同声音，这些声音大多是对周围事物的模仿，比如动物的叫声、大自然的声响以及工具发出的声音。\n\nPerhaps they made the sound of wind to comment on the weather or imitated the sound of a bird to tell a friend that there was a bird nearby.\n也许他们会模仿风声来评论天气，或者模仿鸟叫声来告诉朋友附近有只鸟。\n\nThen over hundreds of thousands of years, those sounds turned into words that people began to learn as part of their language.\n然后，在数十万年的时间里，这些声音逐渐演变为词语，成为人们语言学习的一部分。\n\nAt some point, people started stringing the words together to form sentences.\n在某个时刻，人们开始将这些词语串连起来形成句子。\n\nThe other main theory, which is more recent, is that people started off by gesturing-pointing at things with their hands and imitating actions using their bodies.\n另一种更新的主要理论认为，人们最初是通过手势来交流的，也就是用手指着东西，用身体模仿动作。\n\nEventually, these gestures turned into full sign language.\n最终，这些手势演变成了完整的手语。\n\nThis theory guesses that after developing sign languages, people eventually started making sounds along with their gestures.\n这种理论推测，在发展出手语之后，人们最终开始配合手势发出声音。\n\nAt some point, they switched to mostly making sounds that became words instead of just using their bodies.\n在某个时刻，他们转而主要使用声音，而不仅仅依靠身体动作，这些声音逐渐变成了词语。\n\nThe reason they switched to making sounds, the theory goes, is that talking out loud lets you communicate with someone even when you can’t see them.\n这个理论认为，人们转而使用声音交流的原因是，大声说话可以让你在看不见对方的情况下也能与他们交流。\n\nQuestions 16 to 18 are based on the passage you have just heard.\n请根据你刚听到的短文回答第16至18题。\n\n16. How did language come into being according to researchers?\n16. 根据研究人员的说法，语言是如何形成的?\n\n17. How did language start according to the first theory?\n17. 根据第一种理论，语言是如何起源的?\n\n18. Why did people switch from gesturing to making sounds according to the more recent theory?\n18. 根据更新的理论，为什么人们会从使用手势转向使用声音?', 105, 1415.84, 864.10, 969.03, 974.31, 994.93, NULL, NULL, 'cet4-2025-06-1-g06', 'PASSAGE', '[14:24.10]Passage One｜短文一\n[14:25.68]Talking is unique to humans.｜说话是人类独有的能力。\n[14:28.18]An animal might make ten different sounds, but an adult human knows more than 20,000 words.｜动物可能会发出十种不同的声音，但一个成年人类却知道超过两万个词语。\n[14:34.73]Additionally, we’re the only animal that expresses thoughts in full sentences.｜此外，我们是唯一能用完整句子表达思想的动物。\n[14:39.89]Researchers don’t think language was invented.｜研究人员认为语言不是发明出来的。\n[14:42.98]Instead, they think it evolved.｜相反，他们认为语言是进化而来的。\n[14:45.60]How did talking evolve?｜说话是如何进化的呢？\n[14:47.53]There are two main theories.｜主要有两种理论。\n[14:49.96]The first theory is that language started with people making different sounds, mostly imitating the things around them, like animal calls, nature sounds and the sounds of tools.｜第一种理论认为，语言起源于人们发出的不同声音，这些声音大多是对周围事物的模仿，比如动物的叫声、大自然的声响以及工具发出的声音。\n[15:02.26]Perhaps they made the sound of wind to comment on the weather or imitated the sound of a bird to tell a friend that there was a bird nearby.｜也许他们会模仿风声来评论天气，或者模仿鸟叫声来告诉朋友附近有只鸟。\n[15:11.12]Then over hundreds of thousands of years, those sounds turned into words that people began to learn as part of their language.｜然后，在数十万年的时间里，这些声音逐渐演变为词语，成为人们语言学习的一部分。\n[15:19.79]At some point, people started stringing the words together to form sentences.｜在某个时刻，人们开始将这些词语串连起来形成句子。\n[15:25.79]The other main theory, which is more recent, is that people started off by gesturing-pointing at things with their hands and imitating actions using their bodies.｜另一种更新的主要理论认为，人们最初是通过手势来交流的，也就是用手指着东西，用身体模仿动作。\n[15:37.49]Eventually, these gestures turned into full sign language.｜最终，这些手势演变成了完整的手语。\n[15:42.22]This theory guesses that after developing sign languages, people eventually started making sounds along with their gestures.｜这种理论推测，在发展出手语之后，人们最终开始配合手势发出声音。\n[15:51.33]At some point, they switched to mostly making sounds that became words instead of just using their bodies.｜在某个时刻，他们转而主要使用声音，而不仅仅依靠身体动作，这些声音逐渐变成了词语。\n[15:59.03]The reason they switched to making sounds, the theory goes, is that talking out loud lets you communicate with someone even when you can’t see them.｜这个理论认为，人们转而使用声音交流的原因是，大声说话可以让你在看不见对方的情况下也能与他们交流。\n[16:09.03]Questions 16 to 18 are based on the passage you have just heard.｜请根据你刚听到的短文回答第16至18题。\n[16:14.31]16. How did language come into being according to researchers?｜16. 根据研究人员的说法，语言是如何形成的?\n[16:35.23]17. How did language start according to the first theory?｜17. 根据第一种理论，语言是如何起源的?\n[16:55.37]18. Why did people switch from gesturing to making sounds according to the more recent theory?｜18. 根据更新的理论，为什么人们会从使用手势转向使用声音?', NOW(), NOW()
