SELECT
  @a_cet4_2025_06_2_04, '/audio/exams/listening-cet4-2025-06-2.mp3', 'News Report Two\n新闻二\n\nBritish astronaut Tim Peake is stepping down permanently from his role as a European astronaut.\n英国宇航员蒂姆·皮克将永久卸任欧洲宇航员一职。\n\nHe’s going to take up a full-time position as ambassador for science and space instead—work he has been doing since 2019.\n他将转而全职担任科学和太空大使，这是他自2019年以来一直在做的工作。\n\nThe former British Army Air Corps helicopter pilot was selected as a European Space Agency astronaut in 2009.\n这位英国陆军航空队前直升机飞行员于2009年被选为欧洲航天局宇航员。\n\nHe flew to the space station for a 6-month tour in 2015. 2015\n年，他前往空间站进行了为期 6 个月的太空任务。\n\nThe tour saw him control a robot on Earth remotely from orbit.\n在这次任务中，他从轨道上远程操控了地球上的一个机器人。\n\nHe also helped dock two spacecraft.\n他还协助了两艘航天器的对接工作。\n\nTim said, “Being an astronaut has been the most extraordinary experience.\n蒂姆表示：“成为一名宇航员是一次非凡的经历。\n\nI’ve had the privilege of working with an exceptional team of individuals during the past 13 years with the agency.\n在过去的 13 年里，我有幸与欧洲航天局一支杰出的团队共事。\n\nIt has been incredibly exciting and rewarding.\n这段经历无比令人兴奋且富有意义。\n\nBy assuming the role of an ambassador for human flights to space, I’ll continue to support the European and the UK Space Agencies.”\n通过担任人类太空飞行大使这一角色，我将继续支持欧洲航天局和英国航天局。”\n\nQuestions 3 and 4 are based on the news report you have just heard.\n请根据你刚听到的新闻报道回答第3题和第4题。\n\n3. What do we learn from the news report about Tim Peake?\n3. 关于蒂姆·皮克，我们从新闻报道中了解到什么?\n\n4. What did Tim Peake say about his work with the European Space Agency?\n4. 蒂姆·皮克如何评价他在欧洲航天局的工作?', 70, 1425.61, 167.41, 237.14, 262.17, 282.89, 223.50, 226.77, 'cet4-2025-06-2-g02', 'NEWS', '[02:47.41]News Report Two｜新闻二\n[02:49.68]British astronaut Tim Peake is stepping down permanently from his role as a European astronaut.｜英国宇航员蒂姆·皮克将永久卸任欧洲宇航员一职。\n[02:57.43]He’s going to take up a full-time position as ambassador for science and space instead—work he has been doing since 2019.｜他将转而全职担任科学和太空大使，这是他自2019年以来一直在做的工作。\n[03:07.07]The former British Army Air Corps helicopter pilot was selected as a European Space Agency astronaut in 2009.｜这位英国陆军航空队前直升机飞行员于2009年被选为欧洲航天局宇航员。\n[03:16.43]He flew to the space station for a 6-month tour in 2015. 2015｜年，他前往空间站进行了为期 6 个月的太空任务。\n[03:21.75]The tour saw him control a robot on Earth remotely from orbit.｜在这次任务中，他从轨道上远程操控了地球上的一个机器人。\n[03:27.41]He also helped dock two spacecraft.｜他还协助了两艘航天器的对接工作。\n[03:30.60]Tim said, “Being an astronaut has been the most extraordinary experience.｜蒂姆表示：“成为一名宇航员是一次非凡的经历。\n[03:35.78]I’ve had the privilege of working with an exceptional team of individuals during the past 13 years with the agency.｜在过去的 13 年里，我有幸与欧洲航天局一支杰出的团队共事。\n[03:43.50]It has been incredibly exciting and rewarding.｜这段经历无比令人兴奋且富有意义。\n[03:47.07]By assuming the role of an ambassador for human flights to space, I’ll continue to support the European and the UK Space Agencies.”｜通过担任人类太空飞行大使这一角色，我将继续支持欧洲航天局和英国航天局。”\n[03:57.14]Questions 3 and 4 are based on the news report you have just heard.｜请根据你刚听到的新闻报道回答第3题和第4题。\n[04:02.68]3. What do we learn from the news report about Tim Peake?｜3. 关于蒂姆·皮克，我们从新闻报道中了解到什么?\n[04:22.17]4. What did Tim Peake say about his work with the European Space Agency?｜4. 蒂姆·皮克如何评价他在欧洲航天局的工作?', NOW(), NOW()
WHERE @a_cet4_2025_06_2_04 IS NOT NULL
