INSERT INTO `listening_audio`
  (`question_id`, `audio_url`, `transcript`, `duration_seconds`, `audio_total_seconds`, `audio_start_seconds`, `audio_end_seconds`, `question_start_seconds`, `question_end_seconds`, `answer_start_seconds`, `answer_end_seconds`, `group_key`, `listening_type`, `lrc_content`, `created_at`, `updated_at`)
SELECT
  @a_cet4_2025_06_2_07, '/audio/exams/listening-cet4-2025-06-2.mp3', 'News Report Three\n新闻三\n\nAn Asda store in Wales is now home to five cats after they wandered in and made themselves comfortable.\n威尔士的一家阿斯达超市现在是5只猫的家，它们先前溜达进来，然后就舒舒服服地安顿下来了。\n\nThe supermarket is known for its loyal customers but now has a different kind of visitor that has appeared over the last year.\n这家超市向来以忠实的顾客群体而闻名，但过去一年里，超市里出现了一种与众不同的访客。\n\nRegular shoppers at the supermarket are familiar with the sight of several cats settling down in the shop aisles.\n常来这家超市购物的顾客对几只猫在超市过道里安家落户的景象已经习以为常。\n\nThe unusual situation started about 12 months ago, when one cat routinely started visiting the store.\n这种不同寻常的情况大约始于12个月前，当时有一只猫开始经常光顾这家超市。\n\nLocal newspapers reported that puzzled customers posted on Facebook groups to try to find out if the cat was lost.\n当地报纸报道称，困惑的顾客们在脸书群组里发帖，试图弄清楚这只猫是不是走丢了。\n\nBut its owner assured the concerned customers it was very much loved and fed at home.\n但猫主人向那些担忧的顾客保证，这只猫在家里备受宠爱，也不缺食物。\n\nIt just enjoyed visiting the shop.\n它只是喜欢来超市逛逛。\n\nStaff did their best to discourage the pet from hanging around.\n店员们也尽力劝阻这只宠物在超市附近逗留。\n\nBut instead of leaving and never coming back, it invited its friends round.\n然而，它不仅没有离开且再也不回来，反而还叫来了它的朋友们。\n\nThere are now at least five different cats who come almost on a daily basis.\n现在至少有5只不同的猫几乎每天都会来超市。\n\nThey visit the store so much that staff have been forced to put up signs asking their customers not to feed them.\n这5只猫频繁光顾超市，以至于店员们不得不张贴告示，提醒顾客们不要给它们喂食。\n\nQuestions 5 to 7 are based on the news report you have just heard.\n请根据你刚听到的新闻报道回答第5至7题。\n\n5. What do we learn about the five cats seen in the Asda store?\n5. 关于在阿斯达超市里看到的5只猫，我们了解到了什么?\n\n6. What did some customers think when they saw the first cat routinely appear in the store?\n6. 当一些顾客看到第一只猫经常在超市里出现时，他们是怎么想的?\n\n7. What are customers asked not to do?\n7. 顾客被要求不要做什么?\n\nSection\nBB节', 80, 1425.61, 283.19, 363.43, 412.45, 432.45, 348.30, 363.13, 'cet4-2025-06-2-g03', 'NEWS', '[04:43.19]News Report Three｜新闻三\n[04:45.70]An Asda store in Wales is now home to five cats after they wandered in and made themselves comfortable.｜威尔士的一家阿斯达超市现在是5只猫的家，它们先前溜达进来，然后就舒舒服服地安顿下来了。\n[04:54.29]The supermarket is known for its loyal customers but now has a different kind of visitor that has appeared over the last year.｜这家超市向来以忠实的顾客群体而闻名，但过去一年里，超市里出现了一种与众不同的访客。\n[05:03.01]Regular shoppers at the supermarket are familiar with the sight of several cats settling down in the shop aisles.｜常来这家超市购物的顾客对几只猫在超市过道里安家落户的景象已经习以为常。\n[05:11.47]The unusual situation started about 12 months ago, when one cat routinely started visiting the store.｜这种不同寻常的情况大约始于12个月前，当时有一只猫开始经常光顾这家超市。\n[05:19.83]Local newspapers reported that puzzled customers posted on Facebook groups to try to find out if the cat was lost.｜当地报纸报道称，困惑的顾客们在脸书群组里发帖，试图弄清楚这只猫是不是走丢了。\n[05:28.79]But its owner assured the concerned customers it was very much loved and fed at home.｜但猫主人向那些担忧的顾客保证，这只猫在家里备受宠爱，也不缺食物。\n[05:35.11]It just enjoyed visiting the shop.｜它只是喜欢来超市逛逛。\n[05:38.02]Staff did their best to discourage the pet from hanging around.｜店员们也尽力劝阻这只宠物在超市附近逗留。\n[05:42.87]But instead of leaving and never coming back, it invited its friends round.｜然而，它不仅没有离开且再也不回来，反而还叫来了它的朋友们。\n[05:48.30]There are now at least five different cats who come almost on a daily basis.｜现在至少有5只不同的猫几乎每天都会来超市。\n[05:54.41]They visit the store so much that staff have been forced to put up signs asking their customers not to feed them.｜这5只猫频繁光顾超市，以至于店员们不得不张贴告示，提醒顾客们不要给它们喂食。\n[06:03.43]Questions 5 to 7 are based on the news report you have just heard.｜请根据你刚听到的新闻报道回答第5至7题。\n[06:09.46]5. What do we learn about the five cats seen in the Asda store?｜5. 关于在阿斯达超市里看到的5只猫，我们了解到了什么?\n[06:29.61]6. What did some customers think when they saw the first cat routinely appear in the store?｜6. 当一些顾客看到第一只猫经常在超市里出现时，他们是怎么想的?\n[06:52.45]7. What are customers asked not to do?｜7. 顾客被要求不要做什么?\n[07:11.23]Section｜BB节', NOW(), NOW()
