SELECT
  @a_cet4_2025_06_2_08, '/audio/exams/listening-cet4-2025-06-2.mp3', 'Conversation One\n对话一\n\nW: I’ve been thinking about moving off campus next semester.\n女：我一直在考虑下学期搬到校外住。\n\nM: Hmm, I don’t know if that’s a good idea as your mother and I would worry about you living all by yourself in an apartment so far from home.\n男：嗯，我不确定这是不是一个好主意，因为你妈妈和我会担心你一个人住在离家那么远的公寓里。\n\nAnd then there’s the expense too.\n而且，还有费用问题。\n\nI’m not sure we can afford it.\n我不确定我们是否能负担得起。\n\nW: Well, I wouldn’t be alone, actually.\n女：好吧，实际上我不会一个人住。\n\nThree of my friends from the dormitory would share the place with me.\n我的三个室友会和我合租这个公寓。\n\nAnd with four of us, it wouldn’t cost any more than living in the dorm.\n而且我们四个人一起住，费用不会比住在宿舍高。\n\nM: Are you sure about that?\n男：你确定吗？\n\nRents in big cities are high, and then there’s the cost of electricity and gas.\n大城市的房租很高，而且还有电费和煤气费。\n\nHave you factored those in?\n你把这些因素考虑在内了吗？\n\nW: We’ve budgeted for those and for Internet and transportation.\n女：我们已经把这些费用以及网络费和交通费都纳入预算了。\n\nAnd if we move far enough from the city center, the rent is low enough for us to afford all of it.\n如果我们搬到离市中心足够远的地方，租金就足够低，我们可以负担得起所有的费用。\n\nM: What about the commute to and from campus?\n男：那每天往返学校的通勤时间呢？\n\nIt sounds like you’ll be wasting several hours every day on the road instead of studying.\n听起来你每天都会在路上浪费几个小时，而不是用来学习。\n\nW: It’s about an hour to campus.\n女：到学校大约需要一个小时。\n\nBut there’s no reason I can’t study on the bus.\n但是我完全可以在公交车上学习。\n\nAfter all, I did that during high school, and my commute was even longer then.\n毕竟我在高中时就这样做，而且那时的通勤时间更长。\n\nM: That’s true.\n男：这倒是真的。\n\nBut I’m not sure why you want to leave campus and go through all that trouble when the cost is the same.\n但我不明白，既然费用一样，你为什么要离开学校，去受这份罪。\n\nW: For a lot of reasons.\n女：有很多原因。\n\nWe’d have a kitchen, so we could cook ourselves.\n我们会有厨房，这样我们就可以自己做饭了。\n\nAnd we’d each have our own bedroom where we could study, instead of going to the library.\n我们每个人都会有自己的卧室，可以在里面学习，而不用去图书馆。\n\nWe’d just have more space and privacy.\n我们会有更多的空间和隐私。\n\nM: I’m not convinced that the benefits are greater than the disadvantages, but I’ll discuss this with your mother.\n男：我不确定好处是否大于坏处，但我会和你妈妈商量一下这件事。\n\nQuestions 8 to 11 are based on the conversation you have just heard.\n请根据你刚听到的对话回答第8至11题。\n\n8. What has the woman been thinking of doing next semester?\n8. 女士一直在考虑下学期做什么?\n\n9. What does the man suggest the woman take into consideration?\n9. 男士建议女士考虑什么?\n\n10. What does the woman say she did during high school?\n10. 女士说她在高中时做了什么?\n\n11. What does the man say he’ll do at the end of the conversation?\n11. 男士在对话结束时说他要做什么?', 99, 1425.61, 463.08, 562.07, 567.52, 587.02, 465.13, 478.39, 'cet4-2025-06-2-g04', 'LONG_DIALOGUE', '[07:43.08]Conversation One｜对话一\n[07:45.13]W: I’ve been thinking about moving off campus next semester.｜女：我一直在考虑下学期搬到校外住。\n[07:49.18]M: Hmm, I don’t know if that’s a good idea as your mother and I would worry about you living all by yourself in an apartment so far from home.｜男：嗯，我不确定这是不是一个好主意，因为你妈妈和我会担心你一个人住在离家那么远的公寓里。\n[07:58.69]And then there’s the expense too.｜而且，还有费用问题。\n[08:00.74]I’m not sure we can afford it.｜我不确定我们是否能负担得起。\n[08:02.86]W: Well, I wouldn’t be alone, actually.｜女：好吧，实际上我不会一个人住。\n[08:05.81]Three of my friends from the dormitory would share the place with me.｜我的三个室友会和我合租这个公寓。\n[08:09.84]And with four of us, it wouldn’t cost any more than living in the dorm.｜而且我们四个人一起住，费用不会比住在宿舍高。\n[08:14.65]M: Are you sure about that?｜男：你确定吗？\n[08:16.36]Rents in big cities are high, and then there’s the cost of electricity and gas.｜大城市的房租很高，而且还有电费和煤气费。\n[08:21.12]Have you factored those in?｜你把这些因素考虑在内了吗？\n[08:22.82]W: We’ve budgeted for those and for Internet and transportation.｜女：我们已经把这些费用以及网络费和交通费都纳入预算了。\n[08:27.55]And if we move far enough from the city center, the rent is low enough for us to afford all of it.｜如果我们搬到离市中心足够远的地方，租金就足够低，我们可以负担得起所有的费用。\n[08:34.93]M: What about the commute to and from campus?｜男：那每天往返学校的通勤时间呢？\n[08:37.66]It sounds like you’ll be wasting several hours every day on the road instead of studying.｜听起来你每天都会在路上浪费几个小时，而不是用来学习。\n[08:42.85]W: It’s about an hour to campus.｜女：到学校大约需要一个小时。\n[08:45.06]But there’s no reason I can’t study on the bus.｜但是我完全可以在公交车上学习。\n[08:48.20]After all, I did that during high school, and my commute was even longer then.｜毕竟我在高中时就这样做，而且那时的通勤时间更长。\n[08:53.56]M: That’s true.｜男：这倒是真的。\n[08:54.76]But I’m not sure why you want to leave campus and go through all that trouble when the cost is the same.｜但我不明白，既然费用一样，你为什么要离开学校，去受这份罪。\n[09:00.72]W: For a lot of reasons.｜女：有很多原因。\n[09:02.39]We’d have a kitchen, so we could cook ourselves.｜我们会有厨房，这样我们就可以自己做饭了。\n[09:05.65]And we’d each have our own bedroom where we could study, instead of going to the library.｜我们每个人都会有自己的卧室，可以在里面学习，而不用去图书馆。\n[09:11.95]We’d just have more space and privacy.｜我们会有更多的空间和隐私。\n[09:15.28]M: I’m not convinced that the benefits are greater than the disadvantages, but I’ll discuss this with your mother.｜男：我不确定好处是否大于坏处，但我会和你妈妈商量一下这件事。\n[09:22.07]Questions 8 to 11 are based on the conversation you have just heard.｜请根据你刚听到的对话回答第8至11题。\n[09:27.52]8. What has the woman been thinking of doing next semester?｜8. 女士一直在考虑下学期做什么?\n[09:47.32]9. What does the man suggest the woman take into consideration?｜9. 男士建议女士考虑什么?\n[10:07.13]10. What does the woman say she did during high school?｜10. 女士说她在高中时做了什么?\n[10:26.12]11. What does the man say he’ll do at the end of the conversation?｜11. 男士在对话结束时说他要做什么?', NOW(), NOW()
WHERE @a_cet4_2025_06_2_08 IS NOT NULL
