  @a_cet4_2025_06_2_10, '/audio/exams/listening-cet4-2025-06-2.mp3', 'Conversation One\n对话一\n\nW: I’ve been thinking about moving off campus next semester.\n女：我一直在考虑下学期搬到校外住。\n\nM: Hmm, I don’t know if that’s a good idea as your mother and I would worry about you living all by yourself in an apartment so far from home.\n男：嗯，我不确定这是不是一个好主意，因为你妈妈和我会担心你一个人住在离家那么远的公寓里。\n\nAnd then there’s the expense too.\n而且，还有费用问题。\n\nI’m not sure we can afford it.\n我不确定我们是否能负担得起。\n\nW: Well, I wouldn’t be alone, actually.\n女：好吧，实际上我不会一个人住。\n\nThree of my friends from the dormitory would share the place with me.\n我的三个室友会和我合租这个公寓。\n\nAnd with four of us, it wouldn’t cost any more than living in the dorm.\n而且我们四个人一起住，费用不会比住在宿舍高。\n\nM: Are you sure about that?\n男：你确定吗？\n\nRents in big cities are high, and then there’s the cost of electricity and gas.\n大城市的房租很高，而且还有电费和煤气费。\n\nHave you factored those in?\n你把这些因素考虑在内了吗？\n\nW: We’ve budgeted for those and for Internet and transportation.\n女：我们已经把这些费用以及网络费和交通费都纳入预算了。\n\nAnd if we move far enough from the city center, the rent is low enough for us to afford all of it.\n如果我们搬到离市中心足够远的地方，租金就足够低，我们可以负担得起所有的费用。\n\nM: What about the commute to and from campus?\n男：那每天往返学校的通勤时间呢？\n\nIt sounds like you’ll be wasting several hours every day on the road instead of studying.\n听起来你每天都会在路上浪费几个小时，而不是用来学习。\n\nW: It’s about an hour to campus.\n女：到学校大约需要一个小时。\n\nBut there’s no reason I can’t study on the bus.\n但是我完全可以在公交车上学习。\n\nAfter all, I did that during high school, and my commute was even longer then.\n毕竟我在高中时就这样做，而且那时的通勤时间更长。\n\nM: That’s true.\n男：这倒是真的。\n\nBut I’m not sure why you want to leave campus and go through all that trouble when the cost is the same.\n但我不明白，既然费用一样，你为什么要离开学校，去受这份罪。\n\nW: For a lot of reasons.\n女：有很多原因。\n\nWe’d have a kitchen, so we could cook ourselves.\n我们会有厨房，这样我们就可以自己做饭了。\n\nAnd we’d each have our own bedroom where we could study, instead of going to the library.\n我们每个人都会有自己的卧室，可以在里面学习，而不用去图书馆。\n\nWe’d just have more space and