rs every day on the road instead of studying.｜听起来你每天都会在路上浪费几个小时，而不是用来学习。\n[08:42.85]W: It’s about an hour to campus.｜女：到学校大约需要一个小时。\n[08:45.06]But there’s no reason I can’t study on the bus.｜但是我完全可以在公交车上学习。\n[08:48.20]After all, I did that during high school, and my commute was even longer then.｜毕竟我在高中时就这样做，而且那时的通勤时间更长。\n[08:53.56]M: That’s true.｜男：这倒是真的。\n[08:54.76]But I’m not sure why you want to leave campus and go through all that trouble when the cost is the same.｜但我不明白，既然费用一样，你为什么要离开学校，去受这份罪。\n[09:00.72]W: For a lot of reasons.｜女：有很多原因。\n[09:02.39]We’d have a kitchen, so we could cook ourselves.｜我们会有厨房，这样我们就可以自己做饭了。\n[09:05.65]And we’d each have our own bedroom where we could study, instead of going to the library.｜我们每个人都会有自己的卧室，可以在里面学习，而不用去图书馆。\n[09:11.95]We’d just have more space and privacy.｜我们会有更多的空间和隐私。\n[09:15.28]M: I’m not convinced that the benefits are greater than the disadvantages, but I’ll discuss this with your mother.｜男：我不确定好处是否大于坏处，但我会和你妈妈商量一下这件事。\n[09:22.07]Questions 8 to 11 are based on the conversation you have just heard.｜请根据你刚听到的对话回答第8至11题。\n[09:27.52]8. What has the woman been thinking of doing next semester?｜8. 女士一直在考虑下学期做什么?\n[09:47.32]9. What does the man suggest the woman take into consideration?｜9. 男士建议女士考虑什么?\n[10:07.13]10. What does the woman say she did during high school?｜10. 女士说她在高中时做了什么?\n[10:26.12]11. What does the man say he’ll do at the end of the conversation?｜11. 男士在对话结束时说他要做什么?', NOW(), NOW()
