  @a_cet4_2025_06_2_15, '/audio/exams/listening-cet4-2025-06-2.mp3', 'Conversation Two\n对话二\n\nW: Good morning. I’m looking for a present for my nephew, Lawrence.\n女：早上好，我要为我的侄子劳伦斯挑选礼物。\n\nM: Hi. Do you have anything in mind?\n男：你好。你有想好买什么吗？\n\nW: I’m not sure. No.\n女：不太确定。没有。\n\nDo you know what boys aged around 10 typically like?\n你知道10岁左右的男孩通常喜欢什么吗？\n\nM: For that age group, our biggest seller this year has been this action figure.\n男：对于这个年龄段的孩子，我们今年卖得最好的是这个玩偶。\n\nIt’s called Bobo Man, and it’s incredibly popular.\n它叫波波人，特别受欢迎。\n\nW: Does it do anything?\n女：它有什么特别的功能吗？\n\nM: Not by itself. It has no batteries, if that’s what you mean.\n男：它本身没有功能。它没有电池，如果你问的是这个意思的话。\n\nThere’s a Bobo Man cartoon popular amongst young children, you see.\n你看，现在有一部很受小孩子欢迎的波波人动画片。\n\nAnd this toy is the lead character from the show.\n而这个玩偶就是那部动画片里的主角。\n\nW: Oh, I understand now.\n女：哦，我明白了。\n\nI’ve never heard of it, but I do know little Lawrence loves cartoons.\n我之前没听说过这个动画片，但我知道小劳伦斯很喜欢看动画片。\n\nDo you have any other popular toys, perhaps something educational?\n你们还有其他受欢迎的玩具吗，也许带点教育意义的？\n\nM: Yes, of course.\n男：当然有。\n\nRight over here, we have dozens of puzzles for children of all ages.\n就在这边，我们有几十种适合各个年龄段孩子的拼图游戏。\n\nThey are fun, great for exercising the mind and can be played either alone or in groups.\n这些游戏很有趣，对锻炼思维很有好处，而且既可以一个人单独玩，也可以组队一起玩。\n\nW: I like this sort of idea.\n女：我喜欢这个主意。\n\nLawrence has a sister who is slightly older, so maybe a game that they can play together would be good.\n劳伦斯有个姐姐，比他稍微大一点，所以也许找一个他们可以一起玩的游戏会比较好。\n\nM: What do you think of battleships then?\n男：那么，你觉得战舰棋怎么样？\n\nIt’s a total classic.\n这可是个经典游戏。\n\nIt has been around since the 1930s.\n早在20世纪30年代就有这款游戏了。\n\nW: Oh yeah. We had one of those when growing up.\n女：哦，对。我们小时候就玩过这个游戏。\n\nM: Of course you did. Everyone did.\n男：你当然玩过。大家都玩过。\n\nAnd kids enjoy it just as much today as you and I did when we were young.\n现在的小孩子和我们小时候一样喜欢玩这个游戏。\n\nSome games just never get old.\n有些游戏永远不会过时。\n\nW: I suppose you are right.\n女：我想你说得对。\n\nI have fond memories playing battleships when it was raining outside, and we had to stay indoors.\n我小时候下雨天不能出去玩，只能待在屋里时，就很喜欢玩战舰棋。\n\nThat’s decided then. How much?\n那就这么定了。多少钱？\n\nM: 19 pounds and 90 pence, please.\n男：19英镑90便士。\n\nW: There you are. Have a nice day.\n女：给你钱。祝你今天愉快。\n\nM: Thank you. You too.\n男：谢谢。也祝你愉快。\n\nQuestions 12 to 15 are based on the conversation you have just heard.\n请根据你刚听到的对话回答第12至15题。\n\n12. What is the woman doing?\n12. 女士正在做什么?\n\n13. How does the man describe Bobo Man, the action figure?\n13. 男士如何描述波波人这个玩偶?\n\n14. What kind of game does the woman think would be good for Lawrence?\n14. 女士认为劳伦斯适合玩什么样的游戏?\n\n15. What do we learn from the conversation about the game battleships?\n15. 关于战舰棋游戏，我们从对话中了解到了什么?', 110, 1425.61, 645.69, 755.87, 818.58, 838.58, 730.80, 735.21, 'cet4-2025-06-2-g05', 'LONG_DIALOGUE', '[10:45.69]Conversation Two｜对话二\n[10:48.13]W: Good morning. I’m looking for a present for my nephew, Lawrence.｜女：早上好，我要为我的侄子劳伦斯挑选礼物。\n[10:52.58]M: Hi. Do you have anything in mind?｜男：你好。你有想好买什么吗？\n[10:55.41]W: I’m not sure. No.｜女：不太确定。没有。\n[10:57.71]Do you know what boys aged around 10 typically like?｜你知道10岁左右的男孩通常喜欢什么吗？\n[11:02.24]M: For that age group, our biggest seller this year has been this action figure.｜男：对于这个年龄段的孩子，我们今年卖得最好的是这个玩偶。\n[11:07.70]It’s called Bobo Man, and it’s incredibly popular.｜它叫波波人，特别受欢迎。\n[11:11.00]W: Does it do anything?｜女：它有什么特别的功能吗？\n[11:12.68]M: Not by itself. It has no batteries, if that’s what you mean.｜男：它本身没有功能。它没有电池，如果你问的是这个意思的话。\n[11:17.17]There’s a Bobo Man cartoon popular amongst young children, you see.｜你看，现在有一部很受小孩子欢迎的波波人动画片。\n[11:21.32]And this toy is the lead character from the show.｜而这个玩偶就是那部动画片里的主角。\n[11:24.49]W: Oh, I understand now.｜女：哦，我明白了。\n[11:26.64]I’ve never heard of it, but I do know little Lawrence loves cartoons.｜我之前没听说过这个动画片，但我知道小劳伦斯很喜欢看动画片。\n[11:32.03]Do you have any other popular toys, perhaps something educational?｜你们还有其他受欢迎的玩具吗，也许带点教育意义的？\n[11:36.85]M: Yes, of course.｜男：当然有。\n[11:38.21]Right over here, we have dozens of puzzles for children of all ages.｜就在这边，我们有几十种适合各个年龄段孩子的拼图游戏。\n[11:42.77]They are fun, great for exercising the mind and can be played either alone or in groups.｜这些游戏很有趣，对锻炼思维很有好处，而且既可以一个人单独玩，也可以组队一起玩。\n[11:49.01]W: I like this sort of idea.｜女：我喜欢这个主意。\n[11:51.07]Lawrence has a sister who is slightly older, so maybe a game that they can play together would be good.｜劳伦斯有个姐姐，比他稍微大一点，所以也许找一个他们可以一起玩的游戏会比较好。\n[11:57.86]M: What do you think of battleships then?｜男：那么，你觉得战舰棋怎么样？\n[12:00.44]It’s a total classic.｜这可是个经典游戏。\n[12:02.06]It has been around since the 1930s.｜早在20世纪30年代就有这款游戏了。\n[12:05.11]W: Oh yeah. We had one of those when growing up.｜女：哦，对。我们小时候就玩过这个游戏。\n[12:08.09]M: Of course you did. Everyone did.｜男：你当然玩过。大家都玩过。\n[12:10.80]And kids enjoy it just as much today as you and I did when we were young.｜现在的小孩子和我们小时候一样喜欢玩这个游戏。\n[12:15.51]Some games just never get old.｜有些游戏永远不会过时。\n[12:18.04]W: I suppose you are right.｜女：我想你说得对。\n[12:19.63]I have fond memories playing battleships when it was raining outside, and we had to stay indoors.｜我小时候下雨天不能出去玩，只能待在屋里时，就很喜欢玩战舰棋。\n[12:25.93]That’s decided then. How much?｜那就这么定了。多少钱？\n[12:28.72]M: 19 pounds and 90 pence, please.｜男：19英镑90便士。\n[12:31.75]W: There you are. Have a nice day.｜女：给你钱。祝你今天愉快。\n[12:33.79]M: Thank you. You too.｜男：谢谢。也祝你愉快。\n[12:35.87]Questions 12 to 15 are based on the conversation you have just heard.｜请根据你刚听到的对话回答第12至15题。\n[12:41.28]12. What is the woman doing?｜12. 女士正在做什么?\n[12:58.40]13. How does the man describe Bobo Man, the action figure?｜13. 男士如何描述波波人这个玩偶?\n[13:18.43]14. What kind of game does the woman think would be good for Lawrence?｜14. 女士认为劳伦斯适合玩什么样的游戏?\n[13:38.58]15. What do we learn from the conversation about the game battleships?｜15. 关于战舰棋游戏，我们从对话中了解到了什么?', NOW(), NOW()
