SELECT
  @a_cet4_2025_06_2_16, '/audio/exams/listening-cet4-2025-06-2.mp3', 'Passage One\n短文一\n\nWe assume that if we offer our customers more choices, then they’ll be more likely to buy our products.\n我们通常认为，如果给顾客提供更多选择，他们就更有可能购买我们的产品。\n\nBut here’s the paradox of choice.\n但这里存在一个选择悖论。\n\nIf a person is presented with too many choices, they are actually less likely to buy.\n如果一个人面临太多选择，他实际上购买的可能性反而会降低。\n\nIn 2012, psychologists published a study about jams. 2012\n年，心理学家发表了一项关于果酱的研究。\n\nOn a regular day at a local food market, people would find a display table with 24 different kinds of jams.\n在某一天，人们在当地食品市场发现一个展示台上有24种不同的果酱。\n\nThen on another day, at that same food market, people were given only 6 different types of jam choices.\n而在另一天，同样是在这家食品市场，人们面前只有6种不同的果酱可供选择。\n\nGuess which display table led to more sales?\n猜猜哪个展示台的销量更高？\n\nThe study found that while the bigger display table created more interest, people were almost 10 times less likely to purchase a jar of jam than in the case of the smaller display.\n研究发现，虽然更大的展示台会引起更多的兴趣，但人们购买果酱的可能性却几乎是较小的展示台的十分之一。\n\nCustomer satisfaction takes a hit as well.\n顾客满意度也受到了影响。\n\nIn the study, the bigger display of jams leads to lower customer satisfaction than the smaller display.\n在这项研究中，与较小的展示台相比，较大的展示桌会导致更低的顾客满意度。\n\nIn an extensive study published in 2015, researchers analyzed a total of 99 choice studies and specifically looked at those cases in which reducing choices helped to boost sales.\n在2015年发表的一项广泛研究中，研究人员分析了总共99项关于选择的研究，并特别关注了那些通过减少选择来促进销售的情况。\n\nThey found four rules that motivate consumers to buy—when people want to make a quick and easy choice, when the product is complex, when it’s difficult to compare alternatives, and when consumers don’t have clear preferences.\n他们发现了4条促使消费者购买产品的规则：当人们想快速轻松地做出选择时，当产品本身很复杂时，当不同选择难以比较时，以及当消费者没有明确的偏好时。\n\nSo as you can see, when it comes to choices, less is more.\n因此正如你所看到的，在选择方面，少即是多。\n\nQuestions 16 to 18 are based on the passage you have just heard.\n请根据你刚听到的短文回答第16至18题。\n\n16. What do we learn from the passage about the paradox of choice?\n16. 关于选择悖论，我们从这篇短文了解到了什么?\n\n17. What did the psychologists want to find out in their 2012 study about jams?\n17. 在2012年关于果酱的研究中，心理学家想知道什么?\n\n18. What is the finding of an extensive study published in 2015? 18. 2015\n年发表的一项广泛研究的结果是什么?', 102, 1425.61, 870.48, 972.88, 978.47, 998.00, 882.78, 888.68, 'cet4-2025-06-2-g06', 'PASSAGE', '[14:30.48]Passage One｜短文一\n[14:32.37]We assume that if we offer our customers more choices, then they’ll be more likely to buy our products.｜我们通常认为，如果给顾客提供更多选择，他们就更有可能购买我们的产品。\n[14:40.13]But here’s the paradox of choice.｜但这里存在一个选择悖论。\n[14:42.78]If a person is presented with too many choices, they are actually less likely to buy.｜如果一个人面临太多选择，他实际上购买的可能性反而会降低。\n[14:48.98]In 2012, psychologists published a study about jams. 2012｜年，心理学家发表了一项关于果酱的研究。\n[14:53.89]On a regular day at a local food market, people would find a display table with 24 different kinds of jams.｜在某一天，人们在当地食品市场发现一个展示台上有24种不同的果酱。\n[15:02.26]Then on another day, at that same food market, people were given only 6 different types of jam choices.｜而在另一天，同样是在这家食品市场，人们面前只有6种不同的果酱可供选择。\n[15:10.40]Guess which display table led to more sales?｜猜猜哪个展示台的销量更高？\n[15:14.26]The study found that while the bigger display table created more interest, people were almost 10 times less likely to purchase a jar of jam than in the case of the smaller display.｜研究发现，虽然更大的展示台会引起更多的兴趣，但人们购买果酱的可能性却几乎是较小的展示台的十分之一。\n[15:26.74]Customer satisfaction takes a hit as well.｜顾客满意度也受到了影响。\n[15:29.73]In the study, the bigger display of jams leads to lower customer satisfaction than the smaller display.｜在这项研究中，与较小的展示台相比，较大的展示桌会导致更低的顾客满意度。\n[15:37.06]In an extensive study published in 2015, researchers analyzed a total of 99 choice studies and specifically looked at those cases in which reducing choices helped to boost sales.｜在2015年发表的一项广泛研究中，研究人员分析了总共99项关于选择的研究，并特别关注了那些通过减少选择来促进销售的情况。\n[15:51.59]They found four rules that motivate consumers to buy—when people want to make a quick and easy choice, when the product is complex, when it’s difficult to compare alternatives, and when consumers don’t have clear preferences.｜他们发现了4条促使消费者购买产品的规则：当人们想快速轻松地做出选择时，当产品本身很复杂时，当不同选择难以比较时，以及当消费者没有明确的偏好时。\n[16:07.78]So as you can see, when it comes to choices, less is more.｜因此正如你所看到的，在选择方面，少即是多。\n[16:12.88]Questions 16 to 18 are based on the passage you have just heard.｜请根据你刚听到的短文回答第16至18题。\n[16:18.47]16. What do we learn from the passage about the paradox of choice?｜16. 关于选择悖论，我们从这篇短文了解到了什么?\n[16:38.30]17. What did the psychologists want to find out in their 2012 study about jams?｜17. 在2012年关于果酱的研究中，心理学家想知道什么?\n[17:00.00]18. What is the finding of an extensive study published in 2015? 18. 2015｜年发表的一项广泛研究的结果是什么?', NOW(), NOW()
WHERE @a_cet4_2025_06_2_16 IS NOT NULL
