SELECT
  @a_cet4_2025_06_2_19, '/audio/exams/listening-cet4-2025-06-2.mp3', 'Passage Two\n短文二\n\nThe New Year has come and gone, and many may have already forgotten what they had resolved to do on January 1st.\n新年已经到来又悄然离去，许多人可能已经忘记了自己在1月1日时立下的决心。\n\nBut if that resolution was to volunteer more, now is the best time to start.\n但如果那个决心是多做志愿服务，那么现在就是开始行动的最佳时机。\n\nVolunteering can drop after the holiday season, and by February, some organizations lack the volunteers they had in surplus just a month ago.\n在节假日过后，志愿服务的人数往往会减少，到了2月，一些组织可能会面临志愿者短缺的问题，而就在一个月前，他们还拥有充裕的志愿者资源。\n\nAccording to one survey, only 26% of Americans volunteer, despite reports that many Americans view volunteering as worthwhile.\n据一项调查显示，尽管有报道称许多美国人认为志愿服务是值得做的，但实际参与志愿服务的美国人却只有26%。\n\nWhy such a disconnect?\n为何会出现这种脱节现象呢？\n\nMost people cite time and conflicting work schedules as major barriers, but employees and employers would actually benefit if companies made employee volunteering part of the job.\n大多数人将时间和工作安排冲突列为主要障碍，但如果公司让员工志愿服务成为工作职责的一部分，那么员工和雇主实际上都能从中受益。\n\nResearchers have found donating our time and talent to others can lower blood pressure, boost happiness and improve mental and physical health.\n研究人员发现，将自己的时间和才能奉献给他人可以降低血压、提升幸福感，并改善身心健康。\n\nStudies have also linked employee volunteer programs with more productive employees.\n研究还表明，实施员工志愿服务计划的公司，其员工的工作效率往往更高。\n\nWith so much emphasis on employee wellness these days, company volunteer programs could be the perfect 2025 resolution.\n在如今如此重视员工健康的背景下，公司志愿服务计划或许能成为2025年的完美计划。\n\nBut for volunteering to benefit employees and the workplace, the entire organization needs to be involved.\n但要想让志愿服务对员工和职场都产生益处，整个公司都需要参与进来。\n\nBy allowing employees to donate their time during work hours, the workplace becomes an outlet for personal fulfillment without affecting personal time.\n通过允许员工在工作时间内贡献自己的时间，职场就能成为实现个人价值的渠道，同时又不影响员工的私人时间。\n\nIn one survey, 89% of employees perceived companies that sponsored volunteer activities as creating a better working environment, and 75% said volunteering was critical to their well-being.\n在一项调查中，89%的员工认为赞助志愿服务活动的公司能营造出更好的工作环境，75%的员工表示志愿服务对他们的健康幸福至关重要。\n\nQuestions 19 to 21 are based on the passage you have just heard.\n请根据你刚听到的短文回答第19至21题。\n\n19. What do many Americans think of volunteering?\n19. 许多美国人如何看待志愿服务?\n\n20. How could companies ensure both employees and employers benefit from volunteering?\n20. 公司如何确保员工和雇主都能从志愿服务中受益?\n\n21. What did 75% of employees say about volunteering in a survey?\n21. 在一项调查中，75%的员工对志愿服务有什么看法?', 113, 1425.61, 1040.59, 1153.50, 1159.37, 1178.00, NULL, NULL, 'cet4-2025-06-2-g07', 'PASSAGE', '[17:20.59]Passage Two｜短文二\n[17:22.60]The New Year has come and gone, and many may have already forgotten what they had resolved to do on January 1st.｜新年已经到来又悄然离去，许多人可能已经忘记了自己在1月1日时立下的决心。\n[17:30.74]But if that resolution was to volunteer more, now is the best time to start.｜但如果那个决心是多做志愿服务，那么现在就是开始行动的最佳时机。\n[17:36.78]Volunteering can drop after the holiday season, and by February, some organizations lack the volunteers they had in surplus just a month ago.｜在节假日过后，志愿服务的人数往往会减少，到了2月，一些组织可能会面临志愿者短缺的问题，而就在一个月前，他们还拥有充裕的志愿者资源。\n[17:48.01]According to one survey, only 26% of Americans volunteer, despite reports that many Americans view volunteering as worthwhile.｜据一项调查显示，尽管有报道称许多美国人认为志愿服务是值得做的，但实际参与志愿服务的美国人却只有26%。\n[17:58.35]Why such a disconnect?｜为何会出现这种脱节现象呢？\n[18:00.54]Most people cite time and conflicting work schedules as major barriers, but employees and employers would actually benefit if companies made employee volunteering part of the job.｜大多数人将时间和工作安排冲突列为主要障碍，但如果公司让员工志愿服务成为工作职责的一部分，那么员工和雇主实际上都能从中受益。\n[18:13.26]Researchers have found donating our time and talent to others can lower blood pressure, boost happiness and improve mental and physical health.｜研究人员发现，将自己的时间和才能奉献给他人可以降低血压、提升幸福感，并改善身心健康。\n[18:23.00]Studies have also linked employee volunteer programs with more productive employees.｜研究还表明，实施员工志愿服务计划的公司，其员工的工作效率往往更高。\n[18:29.50]With so much emphasis on employee wellness these days, company volunteer programs could be the perfect 2025 resolution.｜在如今如此重视员工健康的背景下，公司志愿服务计划或许能成为2025年的完美计划。\n[18:39.01]But for volunteering to benefit employees and the workplace, the entire organization needs to be involved.｜但要想让志愿服务对员工和职场都产生益处，整个公司都需要参与进来。\n[18:47.10]By allowing employees to donate their time during work hours, the workplace becomes an outlet for personal fulfillment without affecting personal time.｜通过允许员工在工作时间内贡献自己的时间，职场就能成为实现个人价值的渠道，同时又不影响员工的私人时间。\n[18:57.94]In one survey, 89% of employees perceived companies that sponsored volunteer activities as creating a better working environment, and 75% said volunteering was critical to their well-being.｜在一项调查中，89%的员工认为赞助志愿服务活动的公司能营造出更好的工作环境，75%的员工表示志愿服务对他们的健康幸福至关重要。\n[19:13.50]Questions 19 to 21 are based on the passage you have just heard.｜请根据你刚听到的短文回答第19至21题。\n[19:19.37]19. What do many Americans think of volunteering?｜19. 许多美国人如何看待志愿服务?\n[19:38.30]20. How could companies ensure both employees and employers benefit from volunteering?｜20. 公司如何确保员工和雇主都能从志愿服务中受益?\n[19:59.90]21. What did 75% of employees say about volunteering in a survey?｜21. 在一项调查中，75%的员工对志愿服务有什么看法?', NOW(), NOW()
