SELECT
  @a_cet4_2025_06_2_25, '/audio/exams/listening-cet4-2025-06-2.mp3', 'Passage Three\n短文三\n\nThe vast majority of the UK’s 200,000 tons of retail sector’s annual food waste comes from supermarkets, but it’s a problem that impacts independent luxury food suppliers, too.\n英国零售业每年造成的20万吨食物浪费中，绝大部分来自超市，但这一问题同样影响着独立的奢侈食品供应商。\n\nThe scale is small.\n这些供应商产生的食物浪费规模较小。\n\nIt’s estimated at less than 1% of the UK’s food waste total, but the quality from these suppliers is high.\n据估计不到英国食物浪费总量的1%，但这些浪费的食物质量很高。\n\nEverything from specialist cheeses to sought-after coffee beans gets thrown away every day in the current food system.\n在当前的食物体系中，从特色奶酪到广受欢迎的咖啡豆，每天都有各种高品质食品被丢弃。\n\nThis is where French entrepreneur, Sophie André, comes in.\n这时，法国企业家索菲·安德烈出现了。\n\nIn 2016, she moved to London and began by setting up a business, delivering luxury hand-made food across the city. 2016\n年，她搬到伦敦开始创业，在全市范围内配送手工制作的奢侈食品。\n\n“Food delivery seems to be a big thing here,” she says, “So I started delivering products by bicycle. “\n食品配送在这里似乎很受欢迎，”她说，“所以我开始骑自行车配送产品。\n\nTalking with local producers, I learned that a small part of the production is sometimes wasted due to problems with size or shape, but the quality of the products remains unchanged.”\n在与当地生产商交流时，我了解到，由于尺寸或形状问题，有时会有一小部分产品被浪费掉，但产品的质量并没有改变。”\n\nUnlike many food waste projects that have sprung up in recent years, the idea is not simply to redistribute waste food, but to provide a high-quality product.\n与近年来涌现的许多食物浪费项目不同，索菲·安德烈的想法不仅仅是重新分配废弃食物，而是提供高质量的产品。\n\nAndré’s company, Elysia, offers breakfasts and snacks specifically aimed at business meetings and events.\n安德烈的公司艾丽西亚专门为商务会议和活动提供早餐和小吃。\n\nOnce sourced, Elysia uses waste products to create simple, natural, straightforward meals and snacks.\n一旦获得原料，艾丽西亚就会利用这些废弃产品制作简单、天然的美食和小吃。\n\nPerhaps unlike other waste food, the supply is regular.\n也许与其他废弃食物不同，这里的供应是稳定的。\n\nSuppliers will always have a certain amount of surplus.\n供应商总是会有一定数量的剩余产品。\n\nSo the menus remain regular, too.\n因此，菜单也能保持稳定。\n\nAndré believes this benefits both her business and her customers.\n安德烈认为这对她的生意和顾客都有好处。\n\nQuestions 22 to 25 are based on the passage you have just heard.\n请根据你刚听到的短文回答第22至25题。\n\n22. What do we learn about the UK’s retail sector food waste?\n22. 关于英国零售业的食物浪费，我们了解到了什么?\n\n23. What does Sophie André’s business do in London?\n23. 索菲·安德烈在伦敦做什么生意?\n\n24. In what way does Sophie André’s business differ from many food waste projects?\n24. 索菲·安德烈的生意与许多食物浪费项目有什么不同?\n\n25. Why will suppliers always have a certain amount of surplus?\n25. 为什么供应商总是有一定数量的剩余产品?', 113, 1425.61, 1221.64, 1334.19, 1401.93, 1413.93, 1318.89, 1322.72, 'cet4-2025-06-2-g08', 'PASSAGE', '[20:21.64]Passage Three｜短文三\n[20:23.51]The vast majority of the UK’s 200,000 tons of retail sector’s annual food waste comes from supermarkets, but it’s a problem that impacts independent luxury food suppliers, too.｜英国零售业每年造成的20万吨食物浪费中，绝大部分来自超市，但这一问题同样影响着独立的奢侈食品供应商。\n[20:37.88]The scale is small.｜这些供应商产生的食物浪费规模较小。\n[20:39.57]It’s estimated at less than 1% of the UK’s food waste total, but the quality from these suppliers is high.｜据估计不到英国食物浪费总量的1%，但这些浪费的食物质量很高。\n[20:49.35]Everything from specialist cheeses to sought-after coffee beans gets thrown away every day in the current food system.｜在当前的食物体系中，从特色奶酪到广受欢迎的咖啡豆，每天都有各种高品质食品被丢弃。\n[20:58.04]This is where French entrepreneur, Sophie André, comes in.｜这时，法国企业家索菲·安德烈出现了。\n[21:02.84]In 2016, she moved to London and began by setting up a business, delivering luxury hand-made food across the city. 2016｜年，她搬到伦敦开始创业，在全市范围内配送手工制作的奢侈食品。\n[21:12.10]“Food delivery seems to be a big thing here,” she says, “So I started delivering products by bicycle. “｜食品配送在这里似乎很受欢迎，”她说，“所以我开始骑自行车配送产品。\n[21:19.72]Talking with local producers, I learned that a small part of the production is sometimes wasted due to problems with size or shape, but the quality of the products remains unchanged.”｜在与当地生产商交流时，我了解到，由于尺寸或形状问题，有时会有一小部分产品被浪费掉，但产品的质量并没有改变。”\n[21:32.23]Unlike many food waste projects that have sprung up in recent years, the idea is not simply to redistribute waste food, but to provide a high-quality product.｜与近年来涌现的许多食物浪费项目不同，索菲·安德烈的想法不仅仅是重新分配废弃食物，而是提供高质量的产品。\n[21:43.10]André’s company, Elysia, offers breakfasts and snacks specifically aimed at business meetings and events.｜安德烈的公司艾丽西亚专门为商务会议和活动提供早餐和小吃。\n[21:51.02]Once sourced, Elysia uses waste products to create simple, natural, straightforward meals and snacks.｜一旦获得原料，艾丽西亚就会利用这些废弃产品制作简单、天然的美食和小吃。\n[21:58.89]Perhaps unlike other waste food, the supply is regular.｜也许与其他废弃食物不同，这里的供应是稳定的。\n[22:03.02]Suppliers will always have a certain amount of surplus.｜供应商总是会有一定数量的剩余产品。\n[22:06.65]So the menus remain regular, too.｜因此，菜单也能保持稳定。\n[22:09.58]André believes this benefits both her business and her customers.｜安德烈认为这对她的生意和顾客都有好处。\n[22:14.19]Questions 22 to 25 are based on the passage you have just heard.｜请根据你刚听到的短文回答第22至25题。\n[22:20.01]22. What do we learn about the UK’s retail sector food waste?｜22. 关于英国零售业的食物浪费，我们了解到了什么?\n[22:39.98]23. What does Sophie André’s business do in London?｜23. 索菲·安德烈在伦敦做什么生意?\n[22:59.93]24. In what way does Sophie André’s business differ from many food waste projects?｜24. 索菲·安德烈的生意与许多食物浪费项目有什么不同?\n[23:21.93]25. Why will suppliers always have a certain amount of surplus?｜25. 为什么供应商总是有一定数量的剩余产品?', NOW(), NOW()
