  @a_cet4_2025_12_1_02, '/audio/exams/listening-cet4-2025-12-1.mp3', 'News Report One\n新闻一\n\nA terrified cat has survived a five-mile round trip under the engine cover of a car on a school run.\n一只受到惊吓的猫在一辆汽车的引擎盖下，历经往返五英里的学校接送行程后竟奇迹生还。\n\nThe black cat was found curled up under the engine cover of David King’s car when he decided to do an oil check after dropping his grandson off at school in Kent.\n戴维·金在肯特送孙子上学后决定检查一下机油，这时他发现一只黑猫蜷缩在他汽车的引擎盖下。\n\nMr King’s wife said her husband had come “running in” and was “shouting for me to come have a look”.\n金的妻子说，丈夫“跑进来”，还“大喊着让我赶紧过去看看”。\n\n“We weren’t even sure it was alive, so I gently pushed it with a stick to check it was breathing and saw it was a terrified little cat.\n“我们甚至不确定它是否还活着，所以我用一根棍子轻轻推了推它，确认它是否还有呼吸，这才发现它是一只受到惊吓的小猫。\n\nIt reversed even further into the engine and was stuck.\n它又往引擎深处退了退，被卡住了。\n\nI tried to reach it, but it was too far down and there wasn’t any way I could get it out.”\n我试图伸手去够它，但它太靠里了，我根本够不到，也没办法把它弄出来。”\n\nFollowing a rescue by UK charity Cats Protection, the four-year-old cat was later reunited with its owner, Mr King’s neighbour.\n在英国慈善机构“猫咪保护”组织的救助下,这只4岁的猫后来与它的主人——金先生的邻居——团聚了。\n\nQuestions 1 and 2 are based on the news report you have just heard.\n请根据你刚听到的新闻报道回答第1题和第2题。\n\n1. Where was the black cat found?\n1.这只黑猫是在哪里被发现的？\n\n2. What do we learn about the cat at the end of the news report?\n2.在新闻报道的末尾，我们了解到关于这只猫的什么信息？', 61, 1370.96, 39.84, 100.88, 124.26, 143.74, 91.00, 100.58, 'cet4-2025-12-1-g01', 'NEWS', '[00:39.84]News Report One｜新闻一\n[00:41.80]A terrified cat has survived a five-mile round trip under the engine cover of a car on a school run.｜一只受到惊吓的猫在一辆汽车的引擎盖下，历经往返五英里的学校接送行程后竟奇迹生还。\n[00:49.64]The black cat was found curled up under the engine cover of David King’s car when he decided to do an oil check after dropping his grandson off at school in Kent.｜戴维·金在肯特送孙子上学后决定检查一下机油，这时他发现一只黑猫蜷缩在他汽车的引擎盖下。\n[01:01.72]Mr King’s wife said her husband had come “running in” and was “shouting for me to come have a look”.｜金的妻子说，丈夫“跑进来”，还“大喊着让我赶紧过去看看”。\n[01:09.08]“We weren’t even sure it was alive, so I gently pushed it with a stick to check it was breathing and saw it was a terrified little cat.｜“我们甚至不确定它是否还活着，所以我用一根棍子轻轻推了推它，确认它是否还有呼吸，这才发现它是一只受到惊吓的小猫。\n[01:19.00]It reversed even further into the engine and was stuck.｜它又往引擎深处退了退，被卡住了。\n[01:23.20]I tried to reach it, but it was too far down and there wasn’t any way I could get it out.”｜我试图伸手去够它，但它太靠里了，我根本够不到，也没办法把它弄出来。”\n[01:31.00]Following a rescue by UK charity Cats Protection, the four-year-old cat was later reunited with its owner, Mr King’s neighbour.｜在英国慈善机构“猫咪保护”组织的救助下,这只4岁的猫后来与它的主人——金先生的邻居——团聚了。\n[01:40.88]Questions 1 and 2 are based on the news report you have just heard.｜请根据你刚听到的新闻报道回答第1题和第2题。\n[01:45.84]1. Where was the black cat found?｜1.这只黑猫是在哪里被发现的？\n[02:04.26]2. What do we learn about the cat at the end of the news report?｜2.在新闻报道的末尾，我们了解到关于这只猫的什么信息？', NOW(), NOW()
