ays he’s excited that athletes will get a chance to come back and demonstrate their abilities.｜运动会的组织者本杰明·科瓦尔奇克表示，他很高兴运动员们能有机会重返赛场，展示自己的才能。\n[02:49.84]Organizers expect about 100 athletes will come out to compete in Fayetteville.｜主办方预计，届时将有约100名运动员来到费耶特维尔参赛。\n[02:55.20]They will have a variety of events to choose from, including running, throwing, and jumping.｜他们可以选择参加多种比赛项目，包括跑步、投掷和跳跃等。\n[03:01.32]There will also be a fun tent for children.｜现场还将为孩子们设置一个趣味帐篷。\n[03:04.76]Kowalczyk said it’s rewarding to see athletes with special needs triumph in the Games.｜科瓦尔奇克说，看到有特殊需求的运动员在运动会中取得胜利是很有意义的。\n[03:10.64]For anyone who wants to help make this year’s Games a massive success, there are still opportunities to volunteer for Fayetteville’s Special Olympics.｜对于任何想助力今年运动会圆满成功的人而言，目前仍有机会报名成为费耶特维尔特奥会的志愿者。\n[03:20.80]Organizers encourage them to visit the Games’ website to sign up.｜主办方鼓励他们访问运动会的网站进行报名。\n[03:26.86]Questions 3 and 4 are based on the news report you have just heard.｜请根据你刚听到的新闻报道回答第3题和第4题。\n[03:32.22]3. What will Fayetteville witness in less than a month?｜3.费耶特维尔将在不到一个月的时间里见证什么？\n[03:52.10]4. What did Benjamin Kowalczyk say is rewarding to see?｜4.本杰明·科瓦尔奇克说看到什么是很有意义的？', NOW(), NOW()
