mal rights group.\n他是当地动物权益组织的发言人。\n\nQuestions 8 to 11 are based on the conversation you have just heard.\n请根据你刚听到的对话回答第8至11题。\n\n8. What does the man request the woman to do?\n8.男士请求女士做什么？\n\n9. What does the woman say about eating vegetables only?\n9.女士对只吃蔬菜有什么看法？\n\n10. Why does the boyfriend of the man’s sister choose to be a vegetarian?\n10.男士姐姐的男朋友为什么选择成为素食主义者？\n\n11. On what point does the man agree with the woman at the end of the conversation?\n11.对话末尾，男士在哪个观点上和女士达成了一致？', 92, 1370.96, 424.66, 516.30, 559.76, 580.16, 512.00, 516.00, 'cet4-2025-12-1-g04', 'LONG_DIALOGUE', '[07:04.66]Conversation One｜对话一\n[07:08.16]M: Can you please hand me that book over there?｜男：能请你把那边的书递给我吗？\n[07:10.80]It has instructions for making a winter bean salad.｜那本书上有做冬季豆类沙拉的说明。\n[07:13.96]My sister’s boyfriend is coming over for dinner.｜我姐姐的男朋友要来吃晚饭。\n[07:16.60]He’s vegetarian, so I need to make a lot of vegetable dishes.｜他是素食主义者，所以我得做很多素菜。\n[07:20.40]W: He only eats vegetables, no meat?｜女：他只吃蔬菜，不吃肉？\n[07:23.24]That doesn’t sound like a very balanced diet.｜这听起来不像是很均衡的饮食。\n[07:26.16]How can he get enough protein?｜他如何摄取足够的蛋白质？\n[07:28.12]What does he do to strengthen his muscles and all that?｜他靠什么来增强肌肉之类的？\n[07:31.64]M: Apparently, that’s no problem.｜男：显然这不成问题。\n[07:33.68]He’s explained this to me when we first met.｜我们第一次见面时他就跟我解释过了。\n[07:36.36]He eats a variety of different vegetables and nuts, especially those with high amounts of protein.｜他吃各种各样的蔬菜和坚果，尤其是那些蛋白质含量高的种类。\n[07:42.48]W: It sounds a bit difficult, but he’s done his research, I suppose.｜女：这听起来有点难，不过我想他肯定做过研究。\n[07:46.72]What’s his reasoning for being vegetarian?｜他成为素食主义者的原因是什么？\n[07:49.28]Is it his religion, health condition, or lifestyle?｜是宗教信仰、健康状况还是生活方式？\n[07:53.36]M: He’s an animal activist.｜男：他是一名动物保护主义者。\n[07:55.12]He’s always been very sensitive and sympathizes with animals.｜他向来细腻敏感，同情动物。\n[07:58.80]He’s even written to his state senator about the torture of dolphins in sea parks.｜他甚至还写信给所在州的参议员反映海洋公园虐待海豚的问题。\n[08:03.64]He says that keeping animals in zoos and parks causes them great distress.｜他说把动物关在动物园和公园里会让它们非常痛苦。\n[08:08.64]W: That’s a little gloomy, but I can understand that to a point.｜女：这听着有点沉重，但在某种程度上我能理解。\n[08:13.04]Not all zoos and animal parks have the most favorable conditions, but without them it just wouldn’t be feasible to learn about animals and their environments.｜并非所有动物园和动物公园都具备最理想的条件，但要是没有这些地方就没办法了解动物及其生存环境。\n[08:23.20]Besides, I don’t think I could ever give up a good hot dog at a baseball game.｜而且，我觉得我永远无法放弃在棒球赛上吃美味的热狗。\n[08:28.04]M: Honestly, I agree, but just don’t let him hear you say that.｜男：说实话，我同意你的看法，但别让他听到你这么说。\n[08:32.00]He’s the spokesperson for his local animal rights group.｜他是当地动物权益组织的发言人。\n[08:36.30]Questions 8 to 11 are based on the conversation you have just heard.｜请根据你刚听到的对话回答第8至11题。\n[08:40.98]8. What does the man request the woman to do?｜8.男士请求女士做什么？\n[08:59.94]9. What does the woman say about eating vegetables only?｜9.女士对只吃蔬菜有什么看法？\n[09:19.76]10. Why does the boyfriend of the man’s sister choose to be a vegetarian?｜10.男士姐姐的男朋友为什么选择成为素食主义者？\n[09:40.46]11. On what point does the man agree with the woman at the end of the conversation?｜11.对话末尾，男士在哪个观点上和女士达成了一致？', NOW(), NOW()
