SELECT
  @a_cet4_2025_12_1_12, '/audio/exams/listening-cet4-2025-12-1.mp3', 'Conversation Two\n对话二\n\nW: Did you see that television program on air travel last night?\n女：你昨晚看那个关于航空旅行的电视节目了吗？\n\nM: Yes. The part about overcoming jetlag was interesting.\n男：看了，节目中关于克服时差反应的部分很有趣。\n\nI was surprised that the expert recommended not eating for the entire journey and avoiding sleeping on the plane.\n专家建议全程不吃东西，而且要避免在飞机上睡觉，对此我很惊讶。\n\nW: I was too, as I read an article on the subject in the past that suggested the opposite.\n女：我也很惊讶，因为我之前读过一篇关于这个主题的文章，其中给出的建议恰恰相反。\n\nIt claimed that it was important not to miss meals and that taking a nap on the plane was the best way to adjust to a new time zone.\n文章称，按时吃饭很重要，在飞机上小睡是适应新时区的最佳方式。\n\nM: Well, the expert on the show did cite research supporting her recommendations, so I guess I’ll give it a try next time I fly a long distance.\n男：嗯，节目里的专家确实引用了研究来支持她的建议，所以我想在下次长途飞行时试一试专家所说的方法。\n\nJetlag is a big problem for me and has been for the last few years, even though I never suffered from it before.\n时差反应对我来说是个大问题，过去几年一直如此，尽管我以前从未受其困扰。\n\nW: Well, she did say that jetlag often becomes more of a problem after 40, so I guess I’m lucky that I can still adjust to different time zones well.\n女：嗯，她确实说过时差问题在40岁之后往往会变得更严重，所以我觉得我挺幸运的，还能很好地适应不同的时区。\n\nMy problem is I’m afraid to fly.\n我的问题是我害怕坐飞机。\n\nM: Oh, I didn’t know that.\n男：哦，我不知道你有这个问题。\n\nActually, my mother is terrified of airplanes to the point where she can’t even fly, so our family vacations were always by car or train.\n实际上，我妈妈非常害怕坐飞机，甚至到了不敢坐的程度，所以我们家度假总是开车或坐火车。\n\nW: I’m not as bad as that.\n女：我没那么严重。\n\nI just get anxious before I fly and feel nervous the whole time we’re in the air, which is why I was hoping the television program would cover that topic more than it did.\n我只是在坐飞机前会感到焦虑，整个飞行过程中都很紧张，所以我原本希望电视节目能更多地涉及这个话题。\n\nM: Yeah. That segment was too brief, especially as so many people have that problem.\n男：是啊，那段内容太简短了，尤其是那么多人都有这个问题。\n\nShe said 20% of people are afraid to fly.\n她说有20%的人害怕坐飞机。\n\nW: Actually, it was a quarter of people, so the problem really is widespread and deserves attention.\n女：实际上有四分之一的人害怕坐飞机，所以这个问题确实很普遍，值得关注。\n\nQuestions 12 to 15 are based on the conversation you have just heard.\n请根据你刚听到的对话回答第12至15题。\n\n12. What part of the TV program does the man say was interesting?\n12.男士说电视节目的哪个部分很有趣？\n\n13. What does the man say he will do next time he flies a long distance?\n13.男士说下次长途飞行时他会做什么？\n\n14. Why does the woman think she is lucky?\n14.女士为什么觉得自己很幸运？\n\n15. Why does the woman think the problem of being afraid to fly deserves attention?\n15.女士为什么认为害怕坐飞机的问题值得关注？', 100, 1370.96, 601.28, 701.00, 705.96, 726.20, 607.76, 611.38, 'cet4-2025-12-1-g05', 'LONG_DIALOGUE', '[10:01.28]Conversation Two｜对话二\n[10:03.92]W: Did you see that television program on air travel last night?｜女：你昨晚看那个关于航空旅行的电视节目了吗？\n[10:07.76]M: Yes. The part about overcoming jetlag was interesting.｜男：看了，节目中关于克服时差反应的部分很有趣。\n[10:11.68]I was surprised that the expert recommended not eating for the entire journey and avoiding sleeping on the plane.｜专家建议全程不吃东西，而且要避免在飞机上睡觉，对此我很惊讶。\n[10:18.72]W: I was too, as I read an article on the subject in the past that suggested the opposite.｜女：我也很惊讶，因为我之前读过一篇关于这个主题的文章，其中给出的建议恰恰相反。\n[10:24.56]It claimed that it was important not to miss meals and that taking a nap on the plane was the best way to adjust to a new time zone.｜文章称，按时吃饭很重要，在飞机上小睡是适应新时区的最佳方式。\n[10:33.04]M: Well, the expert on the show did cite research supporting her recommendations, so I guess I’ll give it a try next time I fly a long distance.｜男：嗯，节目里的专家确实引用了研究来支持她的建议，所以我想在下次长途飞行时试一试专家所说的方法。\n[10:41.88]Jetlag is a big problem for me and has been for the last few years, even though I never suffered from it before.｜时差反应对我来说是个大问题，过去几年一直如此，尽管我以前从未受其困扰。\n[10:49.12]W: Well, she did say that jetlag often becomes more of a problem after 40, so I guess I’m lucky that I can still adjust to different time zones well.｜女：嗯，她确实说过时差问题在40岁之后往往会变得更严重，所以我觉得我挺幸运的，还能很好地适应不同的时区。\n[10:58.36]My problem is I’m afraid to fly.｜我的问题是我害怕坐飞机。\n[11:02.00]M: Oh, I didn’t know that.｜男：哦，我不知道你有这个问题。\n[11:04.16]Actually, my mother is terrified of airplanes to the point where she can’t even fly, so our family vacations were always by car or train.｜实际上，我妈妈非常害怕坐飞机，甚至到了不敢坐的程度，所以我们家度假总是开车或坐火车。\n[11:12.68]W: I’m not as bad as that.｜女：我没那么严重。\n[11:14.20]I just get anxious before I fly and feel nervous the whole time we’re in the air, which is why I was hoping the television program would cover that topic more than it did.｜我只是在坐飞机前会感到焦虑，整个飞行过程中都很紧张，所以我原本希望电视节目能更多地涉及这个话题。\n[11:24.48]M: Yeah. That segment was too brief, especially as so many people have that problem.｜男：是啊，那段内容太简短了，尤其是那么多人都有这个问题。\n[11:30.08]She said 20% of people are afraid to fly.｜她说有20%的人害怕坐飞机。\n[11:33.68]W: Actually, it was a quarter of people, so the problem really is widespread and deserves attention.｜女：实际上有四分之一的人害怕坐飞机，所以这个问题确实很普遍，值得关注。\n[11:41.00]Questions 12 to 15 are based on the conversation you have just heard.｜请根据你刚听到的对话回答第12至15题。\n[11:45.96]12. What part of the TV program does the man say was interesting?｜12.男士说电视节目的哪个部分很有趣？\n[12:06.50]13. What does the man say he will do next time he flies a long distance?｜13.男士说下次长途飞行时他会做什么？\n[12:27.36]14. Why does the woman think she is lucky?｜14.女士为什么觉得自己很幸运？\n[12:46.26]15. Why does the woman think the problem of being afraid to fly deserves attention?｜15.女士为什么认为害怕坐飞机的问题值得关注？', NOW(), NOW()
WHERE @a_cet4_2025_12_1_12 IS NOT NULL
ON DUPLICATE KEY UPDATE
