em is I’m afraid to fly.｜我的问题是我害怕坐飞机。\n[11:02.00]M: Oh, I didn’t know that.｜男：哦，我不知道你有这个问题。\n[11:04.16]Actually, my mother is terrified of airplanes to the point where she can’t even fly, so our family vacations were always by car or train.｜实际上，我妈妈非常害怕坐飞机，甚至到了不敢坐的程度，所以我们家度假总是开车或坐火车。\n[11:12.68]W: I’m not as bad as that.｜女：我没那么严重。\n[11:14.20]I just get anxious before I fly and feel nervous the whole time we’re in the air, which is why I was hoping the television program would cover that topic more than it did.｜我只是在坐飞机前会感到焦虑，整个飞行过程中都很紧张，所以我原本希望电视节目能更多地涉及这个话题。\n[11:24.48]M: Yeah. That segment was too brief, especially as so many people have that problem.｜男：是啊，那段内容太简短了，尤其是那么多人都有这个问题。\n[11:30.08]She said 20% of people are afraid to fly.｜她说有20%的人害怕坐飞机。\n[11:33.68]W: Actually, it was a quarter of people, so the problem really is widespread and deserves attention.｜女：实际上有四分之一的人害怕坐飞机，所以这个问题确实很普遍，值得关注。\n[11:41.00]Questions 12 to 15 are based on the conversation you have just heard.｜请根据你刚听到的对话回答第12至15题。\n[11:45.96]12. What part of the TV program does the man say was interesting?｜12.男士说电视节目的哪个部分很有趣？\n[12:06.50]13. What does the man say he will do next time he flies a long distance?｜13.男士说下次长途飞行时他会做什么？\n[12:27.36]14. Why does the woman think she is lucky?｜14.女士为什么觉得自己很幸运？\n[12:46.26]15. Why does the woman think the problem of being afraid to fly deserves attention?｜15.女士为什么认为害怕坐飞机的问题值得关注？', NOW(), NOW()
