 have just heard.\n请根据你刚听到的短文回答第16至18题。\n\n16. What does the speaker think is the best way to get started in user experience design?\n16.讲话者认为开始用户体验设计的最佳方式是什么？\n\n17. What does the speaker say being effective requires?\n17.讲话者称要想做事高效需要具备什么？\n\n18. What can people do as long as they know their end goal and strive for it?\n18.只要明确自己的最终目标并为之努力，人们可以做什么？', 102, 1370.96, 816.72, 918.80, 966.54, 987.48, 908.60, 918.50, 'cet4-2025-12-1-g06', 'PASSAGE', '[13:36.72]Passage One｜短文一\n[13:38.52]The most common question I’m asked always centers around how to get started in user experience design, to which my response is always that nothing can substitute real-world experience.｜我最常被问到的问题总是围绕用户体验设计如何开始展开，对此我的回答始终是，没有什么能替代真实世界的实践经验。\n[13:52.04]Building the skills required of a user experience designer takes time, patience, and commitment.｜掌握一名用户体验设计师所需的技能需要时间、耐心和投入。\n[13:59.48]Higher education is a great way to equip yourself with some core skills, but it will not prepare you for actual challenges you’ll face with clients’ work.｜接受高等教育是让自己掌握一些核心技能的好方法，但它无法让你为客户工作中即将面临的实际挑战做好准备。\n[14:09.60]In other words, being proficient with a design tool and a few methods doesn’t make you a user experience designer.｜换句话说，熟练使用一款设计工具和掌握几种方法并不能让你成为一名用户体验设计师。\n[14:18.44]There simply isn’t a one-size-fits-all process.｜根本不存在放之四海而皆准的流程。\n[14:22.36]Being effective requires adaptability-something you don’t really learn in school, much less in a 6-month training camp.｜要想做事高效，就得具备适应能力--这种能力你在学校里很难真正学到，更不用说在为期6个月的训练营里了。\n[14:32.36]It’s gained through experience on the job and learning what’s appropriate given the needs of the project.｜适应能力是通过工作中的实践经验以及根据项目需求学习恰当方法而获得的。\n[14:39.28]I found my way to user experience through graphic design and slowly over many different roles and experiences.｜我从平面设计起步，历经许多不同的角色和经验积累，找到了通往用户体验设计之路。\n[14:47.60]That led me to become a user experience designer.｜我由此成为一名用户体验设计师。\n[14:51.72]It took time and commitment to continue to pursue roles within teams that I knew could teach and challenge me.｜我投入了时间和精力，不断争取在那些能给我带来教益和挑战的团队岗位。\n[15:00.12]That’s not to say that I think my path is the only one.｜这并不是说我认为我的道路是唯一的。\n[15:03.96]But once again, nothing can substitute real-world experience.｜但我还是要再次强调，没有什么能替代真实世界的实践经验。\n[15:08.60]You can start anywhere as long as you know your end goal and you commit to actively pursuing opportunities to learn and grow along the way.｜只要你明确自己的最终目标，并且在过程中主动争取学习和成长的机会，你从任何地方开始都可以。\n[15:18.80]Questions 16 to 18 are based on the passage you have just heard.｜请根据你刚听到的短文回答第16至18题。\n[15:24.12]16. What does the speaker think is the best way to get started in user experience design?｜16.讲话者认为开始用户体验设计的最佳方式是什么？\n[15:45.96]17. What does the speaker say being effective requires?｜17.讲话者称要想做事高效需要具备什么？\n[16:06.54]18. What can people do as long as they know their end goal and strive for it?｜18.只要明确自己的最终目标并为之努力，人们可以做什么？', NOW(), NOW()
