SELECT
  @a_cet4_2025_12_1_19, '/audio/exams/listening-cet4-2025-12-1.mp3', 'Passage Two\n短文二\n\nWhen planning for this year, our principal asked what needed to change to engage students more in their learning.\n在规划今年的工作时，校长询问需要做出哪些改变才能让学生更投入地学习。\n\nI responded in a whisper “flexible seating”, thinking about our then-current classroom.\n我轻声回答“灵活座位安排”，脑海中浮现出当时我们教室的情景。\n\nIt had rows of desks with blue chairs and nameplates reminding each student where they should be sitting.\n一排排课桌，配有蓝色椅子和姓名牌，提醒着每个学生该坐在哪里。\n\nThis began a journey to transform our practice and challenge the ways of learning for a group of Year 6 students used to sitting in desks and rows for years.\n由此，我们开启了一场变革之旅，改变我们的教学方式，挑战一群六年级学生多年来习惯的排排坐的学习模式。\n\nFlexible seating has been defined as movable furniture to create an engaging learning environment.\n灵活座位安排被定义为可移动的家具，用以营造一个引人入胜的学习环境。\n\nIt is a shift in practice from being teacher-focused to student-focused learning.\n这是从以教师为中心的教学向以学生为中心的学习转变的一种实践。\n\nFor us, flexible seating has meant removing most of the traditional chairs and desks and introducing a variety of different seating options to promote student engagement.\n对我们而言，灵活座位安排意味着撤掉大部分传统的桌椅，引入多种不同的座位选择，以此来提高学生的课堂参与度。\n\nThe use of rows and their minimal adaptations to “U” shape were traditionally intended to maximize on-task behavior and reduce distraction from the teacher.\n传统上采用整齐排列或稍微调整成“U”字形的布局，是为了最大化提升学生的学习专注度，减少教师的干扰。\n\nTeachers tend to still use this format because of either the need to control students or the belief that the teacher is the most important person in the room.\n教师们往往仍沿用这种布局，要么是因为需要管控学生，要么是认为教师是教室里最重要的人。\n\nNow our students have a range of different seating options, including a floor desk, couches, stools, bean bags, and the traditional desk-and-chair.\n现在，我们的学生有了多种不同的座位选择，包括地桌、沙发、凳子、豆袋椅，以及传统的桌椅。\n\nFrom our experience so far, flexible seating enhances student ownership of space and engagement in learning, while reducing rates of student disengagement and disciplinary actions.\n从我们目前的实践经验来看，灵活座位安排能增强学生对学习空间的归属感，提高学习参与度，同时降低学生走神的概率，减少违纪行为。\n\nIt is a win for all concerned.\n这对所有相关人员来说都是一场胜利。\n\nQuestions 19 to 21 are based on the passage you have just heard.\n请根据你刚听到的短文回答第19至21题。\n\n19. Why did the school principal ask what needed to change?\n19.校长为何询问需要做出哪些改变？\n\n20. What has flexible seating meant at the speaker’s school?\n20.在讲话者所在学校，灵活座位安排意味着什么？\n\n21. What has flexible seating brought about at the speaker’s school?\n21.灵活座位安排为讲话者所在学校带来了什么？', 115, 1370.96, 987.78, 1102.52, 1107.80, 1127.46, 989.86, 998.00, 'cet4-2025-12-1-g07', 'PASSAGE', '[16:27.78]Passage Two｜短文二\n[16:29.86]When planning for this year, our principal asked what needed to change to engage students more in their learning.｜在规划今年的工作时，校长询问需要做出哪些改变才能让学生更投入地学习。\n[16:38.30]I responded in a whisper “flexible seating”, thinking about our then-current classroom.｜我轻声回答“灵活座位安排”，脑海中浮现出当时我们教室的情景。\n[16:45.58]It had rows of desks with blue chairs and nameplates reminding each student where they should be sitting.｜一排排课桌，配有蓝色椅子和姓名牌，提醒着每个学生该坐在哪里。\n[16:53.46]This began a journey to transform our practice and challenge the ways of learning for a group of Year 6 students used to sitting in desks and rows for years.｜由此，我们开启了一场变革之旅，改变我们的教学方式，挑战一群六年级学生多年来习惯的排排坐的学习模式。\n[17:05.52]Flexible seating has been defined as movable furniture to create an engaging learning environment.｜灵活座位安排被定义为可移动的家具，用以营造一个引人入胜的学习环境。\n[17:13.32]It is a shift in practice from being teacher-focused to student-focused learning.｜这是从以教师为中心的教学向以学生为中心的学习转变的一种实践。\n[17:19.88]For us, flexible seating has meant removing most of the traditional chairs and desks and introducing a variety of different seating options to promote student engagement.｜对我们而言，灵活座位安排意味着撤掉大部分传统的桌椅，引入多种不同的座位选择，以此来提高学生的课堂参与度。\n[17:31.80]The use of rows and their minimal adaptations to “U” shape were traditionally intended to maximize on-task behavior and reduce distraction from the teacher.｜传统上采用整齐排列或稍微调整成“U”字形的布局，是为了最大化提升学生的学习专注度，减少教师的干扰。\n[17:43.36]Teachers tend to still use this format because of either the need to control students or the belief that the teacher is the most important person in the room.｜教师们往往仍沿用这种布局，要么是因为需要管控学生，要么是认为教师是教室里最重要的人。\n[17:54.00]Now our students have a range of different seating options, including a floor desk, couches, stools, bean bags, and the traditional desk-and-chair.｜现在，我们的学生有了多种不同的座位选择，包括地桌、沙发、凳子、豆袋椅，以及传统的桌椅。\n[18:06.04]From our experience so far, flexible seating enhances student ownership of space and engagement in learning, while reducing rates of student disengagement and disciplinary actions.｜从我们目前的实践经验来看，灵活座位安排能增强学生对学习空间的归属感，提高学习参与度，同时降低学生走神的概率，减少违纪行为。\n[18:19.04]It is a win for all concerned.｜这对所有相关人员来说都是一场胜利。\n[18:22.52]Questions 19 to 21 are based on the passage you have just heard.｜请根据你刚听到的短文回答第19至21题。\n[18:27.80]19. Why did the school principal ask what needed to change?｜19.校长为何询问需要做出哪些改变？\n[18:47.76]20. What has flexible seating meant at the speaker’s school?｜20.在讲话者所在学校，灵活座位安排意味着什么？\n[19:07.62]21. What has flexible seating brought about at the speaker’s school?｜21.灵活座位安排为讲话者所在学校带来了什么？', NOW(), NOW()
