still use this format because of either the need to control students or the belief that the teacher is the most important person in the room.｜教师们往往仍沿用这种布局，要么是因为需要管控学生，要么是认为教师是教室里最重要的人。\n[17:54.00]Now our students have a range of different seating options, including a floor desk, couches, stools, bean bags, and the traditional desk-and-chair.｜现在，我们的学生有了多种不同的座位选择，包括地桌、沙发、凳子、豆袋椅，以及传统的桌椅。\n[18:06.04]From our experience so far, flexible seating enhances student ownership of space and engagement in learning, while reducing rates of student disengagement and disciplinary actions.｜从我们目前的实践经验来看，灵活座位安排能增强学生对学习空间的归属感，提高学习参与度，同时降低学生走神的概率，减少违纪行为。\n[18:19.04]It is a win for all concerned.｜这对所有相关人员来说都是一场胜利。\n[18:22.52]Questions 19 to 21 are based on the passage you have just heard.｜请根据你刚听到的短文回答第19至21题。\n[18:27.80]19. Why did the school principal ask what needed to change?｜19.校长为何询问需要做出哪些改变？\n[18:47.76]20. What has flexible seating meant at the speaker’s school?｜20.在讲话者所在学校，灵活座位安排意味着什么？\n[19:07.62]21. What has flexible seating brought about at the speaker’s school?｜21.灵活座位安排为讲话者所在学校带来了什么？', NOW(), NOW()
