  (`question_id`, `audio_url`, `transcript`, `duration_seconds`, `audio_total_seconds`, `audio_start_seconds`, `audio_end_seconds`, `question_start_seconds`, `question_end_seconds`, `answer_start_seconds`, `answer_end_seconds`, `group_key`, `listening_type`, `lrc_content`, `created_at`, `updated_at`)
SELECT
  @a_cet4_2025_12_1_22, '/audio/exams/listening-cet4-2025-12-1.mp3', 'Passage Three\n短文三\n\nDozens of British students arriving for their first day of school on Tuesday were sent home over their shoes.\n周二，数十名英国学生在开学第一天因鞋子问题被勒令回家。\n\nAbout 30 students were turned away from Taverham High School in Norfolk, England.\n英格兰诺福克的塔弗勒姆高中约有30名学生被拒绝入校。\n\nHeadteacher, Dr Roger Harris, confirmed that this was due to a change in the school’s uniform policy.\n校长罗杰·哈里斯博士证实，这是由于学校校服政策发生了变化。\n\nHarris, who became headteacher this year, said he notified parents of the updated rules in an email in June.\n哈里斯今年刚上任校长，他表示已在6月份通过电子邮件将更新后的规定通知了家长。\n\nThe price of school uniforms can spark panic among families struggling with the high cost of living.\n校服的价格可能会让那些正为高昂生活成本而挣扎的家庭感到恐慌。\n\nNearly all British schools have uniforms.\n几乎所有英国学校都要求学生穿校服。\n\nThey cost parents an average of ￡337 per year for each secondary school child.\n每位中学生家长平均每年需在校服上花费337英镑。\n\nAccording to the new rules, students of Taverham are required to wear smart black shoes appropriate for the workplace.\n根据新规定，塔弗勒姆中学的学生需穿着适合职场的黑色正式皮鞋。\n\nHarris held that strengthened rules around school uniforms improved student outcomes and behavior.\n哈里斯认为，强化校服相关规定有助于提高学生的学业成绩，改善学生的行为举止。\n\nBut for some parents, the school’s restrictions are an unnecessary burden.\n但对一些家长来说，学校的这些限制是不必要的负担。\n\nAs annual inflation climbs over 10%, many households are on tight budgets.\n随着年通货膨胀率攀升至10%以上，许多家庭预算紧张。\n\nPrivate rental prices in Britain rose 3.2% over the 12 months to July 2022, the largest jump since 2016.\n截至2022年7月的12个月里，英国私人租赁价格上涨了3.2%，创下2016年以来的最大涨幅。\n\nSoaring energy bills have made things worse.\n能源费用飙升更是让情况雪上加霜。\n\nLucinda May, mum of a Taverham student, said that she had to ask her parents for ￡65 to buy her child the correct pair of shoes.\n塔弗勒姆中学一名学生的母亲露辛达·梅表示，为了给孩子买到符合要求的鞋子，她不得不向自己的父母借了65英镑。\n\nMay said that the school’s uniform policy showed the lack of regard for parents dealing with the high cost of living.\n梅说，学校的校服政策反映出其对应付高昂生活成本的家长缺乏体谅。\n\nQuestions 22 to 25 are based on the passage you have just heard.\n请根据你刚听到的短文回答第22至25题。\n\n22. Why were dozens of British students sent home on Tuesday?\n22.为什么周二有数十名英国学生被勒令回家？\n\n23. What can the price of school uniforms spark among families in financial difficulty?\n23.校服的价格会给经济困难的家庭带来什么？\n\n24. What did the headteacher think of the school’s new uniform rules?\n24.校长如何看待学校新出台的校服规定？\n\n25. What did Lucinda May have to do to buy her child the correct pair of shoes?\n25.露辛达·梅为了给孩子买到符合要求的鞋子不得不做了什么？', 108, 1370.96, 1168.38, 1276.84, 1282.16, 1302.70, 1216.16, 1224.50, 'cet4-2025-12-1-g08', 'PASSAGE', '[19:28.38]Passage Three｜短文三\n[19:30.34]Dozens of British students arriving for their first day of school on Tuesday were sent home over their shoes.｜周二，数十名英国学生在开学第一天因鞋子问题被勒令回家。\n[19:38.02]About 30 students were turned away from Taverham High School in Norfolk, England.｜英格兰诺福克的塔弗勒姆高中约有30名学生被拒绝入校。\n[19:43.38]Headteacher, Dr Roger Harris, confirmed that this was due to a change in the school’s uniform policy.｜校长罗杰·哈里斯博士证实，这是由于学校校服政策发生了变化。\n[19:50.98]Harris, who became headteacher this year, said he notified parents of the updated rules in an email in June.｜哈里斯今年刚上任校长，他表示已在6月份通过电子邮件将更新后的规定通知了家长。\n[19:58.94]The price of school uniforms can spark panic among families struggling with the high cost of living.｜校服的价格可能会让那些正为高昂生活成本而挣扎的家庭感到恐慌。\n[20:05.12]Nearly all British schools have uniforms.｜几乎所有英国学校都要求学生穿校服。\n[20:08.32]They cost parents an average of ￡337 per year for each secondary school child.｜每位中学生家长平均每年需在校服上花费337英镑。\n[20:16.16]According to the new rules, students of Taverham are required to wear smart black shoes appropriate for the workplace.｜根据新规定，塔弗勒姆中学的学生需穿着适合职场的黑色正式皮鞋。\n[20:24.80]Harris held that strengthened rules around school uniforms improved student outcomes and behavior.｜哈里斯认为，强化校服相关规定有助于提高学生的学业成绩，改善学生的行为举止。\n[20:31.52]But for some parents, the school’s restrictions are an unnecessary burden.｜但对一些家长来说，学校的这些限制是不必要的负担。\n[20:37.04]As annual inflation climbs over 10%, many households are on tight budgets.｜随着年通货膨胀率攀升至10%以上，许多家庭预算紧张。\n[20:43.68]Private rental prices in Britain rose 3.2% over the 12 months to July 2022, the largest jump since 2016.｜截至2022年7月的12个月里，英国私人租赁价格上涨了3.2%，创下2016年以来的最大涨幅。\n[20:55.04]Soaring energy bills have made things worse.｜能源费用飙升更是让情况雪上加霜。\n[20:58.72]Lucinda May, mum of a Taverham student, said that she had to ask her parents for ￡65 to buy her child the correct pair of shoes.｜塔弗勒姆中学一名学生的母亲露辛达·梅表示，为了给孩子买到符合要求的鞋子，她不得不向自己的父母借了65英镑。\n[21:09.12]May said that the school’s uniform policy showed the lack of regard for parents dealing with the high cost of living.｜梅说，学校的校服政策反映出其对应付高昂生活成本的家长缺乏体谅。\n[21:16.84]Questions 22 to 25 are based on the passage you have just heard.｜请根据你刚听到的短文回答第22至25题。\n[21:22.16]22. Why were dozens of British students sent home on Tuesday?｜22.为什么周二有数十名英国学生被勒令回家？\n[21:43.00]23. What can the price of school uniforms spark among families in financial difficulty?｜23.校服的价格会给经济困难的家庭带来什么？\n[22:05.14]24. What did the headteacher think of the school’s new uniform rules?｜24.校长如何看待学校新出台的校服规定？\n[22:26.18]25. What did Lucinda May have to do to buy her child the correct pair of shoes?｜25.露辛达·梅为了给孩子买到符合要求的鞋子不得不做了什么？', NOW(), NOW()
