SELECT
  @a_cet4_2025_12_2_02, '/audio/exams/listening-cet4-2025-12-2.mp3', 'News Report One\n新闻一\n\nCustoms and Border Protection officials are seeing a rise in people illegally bringing eggs from Mexico into border states, such as Texas.\n美国海关与边境保护局的官员发现，非法携带鸡蛋从墨西哥进入得克萨斯州等边境州的人数有所增加。\n\nThe U.S. average price for a dozen large eggs last month hit $4.25.\n上个月，美国一打大号鸡蛋的均价达到了4.25美元。\n\nThat’s more than double their $1.78 price in December, 2023.\n这一价格比起2023年12月1.78美元的售价翻了一倍多。\n\nMeanwhile, 30 eggs in Mexico sell for just $3.40.\n与此同时，在墨西哥，30个鸡蛋的售价仅为3.40美元。\n\nThose bringing eggs into the U.S. risk fines of up to $10,000.\n那些携带鸡蛋入境美国的人可能面临高达1万美元的罚款。\n\nBut officials say they usually seize and destroy the eggs.\n但官员们表示，他们通常会没收并销毁这些鸡蛋。\n\nThey also impose a $300 penalty.\n他们还会处以300美元的罚款。\n\nThe Department of Agriculture banned eggs from Mexico in 2012.\n美国农业部早在2012年就禁止从墨西哥进口鸡蛋。\n\nThis was due to the risk of bird flu.\n原因是存在禽流感的风险。\n\nOfficials said most people arriving at international borders with eggs are truthful about their purchases.\n官员们表示，大多数携带鸡蛋入境的人员都会如实申报所购物品。\n\nThey simply don’t know bringing eggs is not allowed.\n他们只是不知道携带鸡蛋入境是不被允许的。\n\n“Generally, the items are declared during the first inspection.\n“一般来说，这些物品在首次检查时就会被申报。\n\nThen the person can abandon the eggs without consequence,” a Customs and Border Protection spokesperson said.\n然后，当事人可以舍弃鸡蛋，并且不会面临处罚。”一位海关与边境保护局的发言人说道。\n\nEven so, there have been a very small number of cases recently when authorities discovered eggs during further inspections.\n即便如此，最近仍有极少数案例是当局在进一步检查时发现了鸡蛋。\n\nQuestions 1 and 2 are based on the news report you have just heard.\n请根据你刚听到的新闻报道回答第1题和第2题。\n\n1. What do we learn from the news report about the egg price in the U.S.?\n1.从新闻报道中，我们能了解到美国鸡蛋价格的什么信息？\n\n2. What does the news report say about most people arriving at American borders with eggs?\n2.对于大多数携带鸡蛋进入美国边境的人员，新闻报道有何描述？', 90, 1406, 40.04, 130.08, 157.16, 177.16, 104.08, 108.34, 'cet4-2025-12-2-g01', 'NEWS', '[00:40.04]News Report One｜新闻一\n[00:42.80]Customs and Border Protection officials are seeing a rise in people illegally bringing eggs from Mexico into border states, such as Texas.｜美国海关与边境保护局的官员发现，非法携带鸡蛋从墨西哥进入得克萨斯州等边境州的人数有所增加。\n[00:53.04]The U.S. average price for a dozen large eggs last month hit $4.25.｜上个月，美国一打大号鸡蛋的均价达到了4.25美元。\n[01:00.20]That’s more than double their $1.78 price in December, 2023.｜这一价格比起2023年12月1.78美元的售价翻了一倍多。\n[01:07.56]Meanwhile, 30 eggs in Mexico sell for just $3.40.｜与此同时，在墨西哥，30个鸡蛋的售价仅为3.40美元。\n[01:13.72]Those bringing eggs into the U.S. risk fines of up to $10,000.｜那些携带鸡蛋入境美国的人可能面临高达1万美元的罚款。\n[01:19.40]But officials say they usually seize and destroy the eggs.｜但官员们表示，他们通常会没收并销毁这些鸡蛋。\n[01:24.00]They also impose a $300 penalty.｜他们还会处以300美元的罚款。\n[01:28.04]The Department of Agriculture banned eggs from Mexico in 2012.｜美国农业部早在2012年就禁止从墨西哥进口鸡蛋。\n[01:33.12]This was due to the risk of bird flu.｜原因是存在禽流感的风险。\n[01:36.88]Officials said most people arriving at international borders with eggs are truthful about their purchases.｜官员们表示，大多数携带鸡蛋入境的人员都会如实申报所购物品。\n[01:44.08]They simply don’t know bringing eggs is not allowed.｜他们只是不知道携带鸡蛋入境是不被允许的。\n[01:48.64]“Generally, the items are declared during the first inspection.｜“一般来说，这些物品在首次检查时就会被申报。\n[01:52.60]Then the person can abandon the eggs without consequence,” a Customs and Border Protection spokesperson said.｜然后，当事人可以舍弃鸡蛋，并且不会面临处罚。”一位海关与边境保护局的发言人说道。\n[02:00.52]Even so, there have been a very small number of cases recently when authorities discovered eggs during further inspections.｜即便如此，最近仍有极少数案例是当局在进一步检查时发现了鸡蛋。\n[02:10.08]Questions 1 and 2 are based on the news report you have just heard.｜请根据你刚听到的新闻报道回答第1题和第2题。\n[02:15.76]1. What do we learn from the news report about the egg price in the U.S.?｜1.从新闻报道中，我们能了解到美国鸡蛋价格的什么信息？\n[02:37.16]2. What does the news report say about most people arriving at American borders with eggs?｜2.对于大多数携带鸡蛋进入美国边境的人员，新闻报道有何描述？', NOW(), NOW()
