SELECT
  @a_cet4_2025_12_2_06, '/audio/exams/listening-cet4-2025-12-2.mp3', 'News Report Three\n新闻三\n\nSecurity officers were searching a suburb in Australia where an adult snake was believed to be wandering after the discovery of a huge, “freshly shed” snake skin.\n安保人员正在澳大利亚的一个郊区展开搜寻，此前这里发现了一张新脱落的巨大蛇皮，人们认为有一条成年蛇正在该区域四处游荡。\n\nThe skin was found at a construction site, and the government wrote to residents to warn them.\n这张蛇皮是在一个建筑工地被发现的，政府已写信警告当地居民。\n\nThey were told to observe and, if possible, photograph the animal.\n居民们被告知要注意观察这条蛇，如果可能的话，拍下它的照片。\n\nIf it was moving, watch where it went.\n如果蛇在移动，就留意它的去向。\n\nIt was recommended not to make contact with the animal.\n政府建议居民不要与这条蛇接触。\n\nThe type of snake was determined to be one of the world’s largest snake species.\n经确认，这种蛇是世界上体形最大的蛇类之一。\n\nIt is not poisonous, but can still attack and kill its victims.\n它没有毒性，但仍然可以攻击并杀死猎物。\n\nThis type of snake is classified as a threat to humans, especially small children, as well as pets.\n这种蛇被归类为对人类，尤其是小孩，以及宠物有威胁的物种。\n\nThey may carry viruses that are fatal to native snakes, which do not have resistance.\n它们可能携带一些病毒，这对当地那些没有抵抗力的蛇来说是致命的。\n\nIf officers found the snake, they would employ a licensed snake catcher to catch it and transport it to a specialist animal doctor, the government said.\n政府表示，如果安保人员找到这条蛇，他们会聘请持有执照的捕蛇人将其捕获，并送往专业的兽医处。\n\nIf caught, the snake would be examined to determine where it came from, how long it had been in the area, what it had been eating, whether it was carrying any diseases of concern and whether it had produced babies.\n这条蛇若被捕获，将会接受检查以确定它来自何处、在该区域待了多久、以什么为食、是否携带任何令人担忧的疾病，以及是否已产下幼蛇。\n\nQuestions 5 to 7 are based on the news report you have just heard.\n请根据你刚听到的新闻报道回答第5至7题。\n\n5. What does the report say security officers were searching for?\n5.报道称安保人员正在搜寻什么？\n\n6. Where does the report say the discovery was made?\n6.报道称发现地点位于何处？\n\n7. What did the government say would be done if security officers found what they were searching for?\n7.政府表示，如果安保人员找到他们正在搜寻的目标，将会采取何种措施？', 82, 1406, 291.76, 374.06, 399.48, 418.96, 305.88, 311.94, 'cet4-2025-12-2-g03', 'NEWS', '[04:51.76]News Report Three｜新闻三\n[04:54.20]Security officers were searching a suburb in Australia where an adult snake was believed to be wandering after the discovery of a huge, “freshly shed” snake skin.｜安保人员正在澳大利亚的一个郊区展开搜寻，此前这里发现了一张新脱落的巨大蛇皮，人们认为有一条成年蛇正在该区域四处游荡。\n[05:05.88]The skin was found at a construction site, and the government wrote to residents to warn them.｜这张蛇皮是在一个建筑工地被发现的，政府已写信警告当地居民。\n[05:12.24]They were told to observe and, if possible, photograph the animal.｜居民们被告知要注意观察这条蛇，如果可能的话，拍下它的照片。\n[05:16.68]If it was moving, watch where it went.｜如果蛇在移动，就留意它的去向。\n[05:19.52]It was recommended not to make contact with the animal.｜政府建议居民不要与这条蛇接触。\n[05:24.04]The type of snake was determined to be one of the world’s largest snake species.｜经确认，这种蛇是世界上体形最大的蛇类之一。\n[05:29.68]It is not poisonous, but can still attack and kill its victims.｜它没有毒性，但仍然可以攻击并杀死猎物。\n[05:34.68]This type of snake is classified as a threat to humans, especially small children, as well as pets.｜这种蛇被归类为对人类，尤其是小孩，以及宠物有威胁的物种。\n[05:42.04]They may carry viruses that are fatal to native snakes, which do not have resistance.｜它们可能携带一些病毒，这对当地那些没有抵抗力的蛇来说是致命的。\n[05:47.96]If officers found the snake, they would employ a licensed snake catcher to catch it and transport it to a specialist animal doctor, the government said.｜政府表示，如果安保人员找到这条蛇，他们会聘请持有执照的捕蛇人将其捕获，并送往专业的兽医处。\n[05:58.16]If caught, the snake would be examined to determine where it came from, how long it had been in the area, what it had been eating, whether it was carrying any diseases of concern and whether it had produced babies.｜这条蛇若被捕获，将会接受检查以确定它来自何处、在该区域待了多久、以什么为食、是否携带任何令人担忧的疾病，以及是否已产下幼蛇。\n[06:14.06]Questions 5 to 7 are based on the news report you have just heard.｜请根据你刚听到的新闻报道回答第5至7题。\n[06:19.34]5. What does the report say security officers were searching for?｜5.报道称安保人员正在搜寻什么？\n[06:39.48]6. Where does the report say the discovery was made?｜6.报道称发现地点位于何处？\n[06:59.26]7. What did the government say would be done if security officers found what they were searching for?｜7.政府表示，如果安保人员找到他们正在搜寻的目标，将会采取何种措施？', NOW(), NOW()
