  @a_cet4_2025_12_2_10, '/audio/exams/listening-cet4-2025-12-2.mp3', 'Conversation One\n对话一\n\nW: Poor Hannah!\n女：可怜的汉娜！\n\nM: Why? What happened?\n男：为什么？发生什么事了？\n\nW: Didn’t you hear?\n女：你没听说吗？\n\nShe won a TV competition and became a millionaire overnight.\n她在一场电视竞赛中获胜，一夜之间成了百万富翁。\n\nM: No way. That’s incredible.\n男：不可能。这太不可思议了。\n\nAre you kidding?\n你在开玩笑吧？\n\nW: No, I’m serious. I swear it.\n女：不，我是认真的。我发誓。\n\nShe went on a TV show where they quiz on general knowledge, and she won first prize.\n她参加了一个考验常识的电视节目，并且赢得了一等奖。\n\nM: Wow. That’s so lucky of her.\n男：哇。她真是太幸运了。\n\nHow much did she win?\n她赢了多少钱？\n\nW: I’m not sure of the exact figure, but it’s a few million Euros, maybe five million Euros after tax.\n女：我不确定具体数字，但有好几百万欧元，税后也许有五百万欧元。\n\nM: I can’t believe it.\n男：我简直不敢相信。\n\nYou’re really not joking, are you?\n你真的不是在开玩笑，对吧？\n\nW: Honestly, look at my face.\n女：说真的，看我的表情。\n\nOur friend Hannah won a ton of money.\n我们的朋友汉娜赢了一大笔钱。\n\nM: Unbelievable.\n男：难以置信。\n\nThen why were you saying “poor Hannah”?\n那你为什么还说“可怜的汉娜”呢？\n\nW: Well, it turns out that she’s spent it all already.\n女：唉，结果她已经把钱都花光了。\n\nM: Five million Euros?\n男：五百万欧元？\n\nHow is that even possible?\n这怎么可能？\n\nW: She bought a house for herself and her husband, a house for her parents, and then a house for each of her four brothers and sisters.\n女：她给自己和丈夫买了一套房，给父母买了一套房，然后给四个兄弟姐妹各买了一套房。\n\nAnd then she bought her husband a ridiculously expensive sports car.\n之后她还给丈夫买了一辆贵得离谱的跑车。\n\nM: Wow. Are they all happy?\n男：哇。那他们都开心吗？\n\nBecause that’s what matters, isn’t it?\n因为开心才是最重要的，不是吗？\n\nW: I know for a fact Hannah isn’t.\n女：我敢肯定汉娜并不开心。\n\nYou see, she was planning to quit the job she hates and retire early.\n你看，她原本打算辞掉那份讨厌的工作，提前退休。\n\nBut now that she ran out of money, she can’t.\n但现在钱花光了，她就不能这么做了。\n\nBasically, she miscalculated how fast she was burning through the money, and she’s now full of regret.\n说白了，她错误地估计了自己花钱的速度，现在后悔不已。\n\nM: Why don’t they sell that flashy new car?\n男：他们为什么不把那辆招摇的新车卖掉呢？\n\nW: She wants to, but her husband refuses to get rid of it.\n女：她想卖，但她丈夫拒绝卖车。\n\nHe says the car is the best thing that has ever happened to him, and if she sells it, he will divorce her.\n他说这辆车是他遇到过的最好的东西，要是汉娜把车卖了，他就跟她离婚。\n\nQuestions 8 to 11 are based on the conversation you have just heard.\n请根据你刚听到的对话回答第8至11题。\n\n8. Why does the woman say she swears it?\n8.为什么女士说她对此发誓？\n\n9. What do we learn about Hannah from the conversation?\n9.从对话中我们能了解到汉娜的什么情况？\n\n10. What does the man think really matters to people?\n10.男士认为对人们而言真正重要的是什么？\n\n11. What does Hannah’s husband say he’ll do if she sells the new car?\n11.汉娜的丈夫说如果她卖掉新车，他会怎么做？', 104, 1406, 470.74, 574.36, 618.66, 637.66, NULL, NULL, 'cet4-2025-12-2-g04', 'LONG_DIALOGUE', '[07:50.74]Conversation One｜对话一\n[07:52.42]W: Poor Hannah!｜女：可怜的汉娜！\n[07:53.98]M: Why? What happened?｜男：为什么？发生什么事了？\n[07:55.78]W: Didn’t you hear?｜女：你没听说吗？\n[07:56.98]She won a TV competition and became a millionaire overnight.｜她在一场电视竞赛中获胜，一夜之间成了百万富翁。\n[08:01.60]M: No way. That’s incredible.｜男：不可能。这太不可思议了。\n[08:03.80]Are you kidding?｜你在开玩笑吧？\n[08:05.00]W: No, I’m serious. I swear it.｜女：不，我是认真的。我发誓。\n[08:07.40]She went on a TV show where they quiz on general knowledge, and she won first prize.｜她参加了一个考验常识的电视节目，并且赢得了一等奖。\n[08:13.40]M: Wow. That’s so lucky of her.｜男：哇。她真是太幸运了。\n[08:15.64]How much did she win?｜她赢了多少钱？\n[08:17.00]W: I’m not sure of the exact figure, but it’s a few million Euros, maybe five million Euros after tax.｜女：我不确定具体数字，但有好几百万欧元，税后也许有五百万欧元。\n[08:25.08]M: I can’t believe it.｜男：我简直不敢相信。\n[08:26.64]You’re really not joking, are you?｜你真的不是在开玩笑，对吧？\n[08:28.52]W: Honestly, look at my face.｜女：说真的，看我的表情。\n[08:30.28]Our friend Hannah won a ton of money.｜我们的朋友汉娜赢了一大笔钱。\n[08:33.48]M: Unbelievable.｜男：难以置信。\n[08:34.64]Then why were you saying “poor Hannah”?｜那你为什么还说“可怜的汉娜”呢？\n[08:37.44]W: Well, it turns out that she’s spent it all already.｜女：唉，结果她已经把钱都花光了。\n[08:41.32]M: Five million Euros?｜男：五百万欧元？\n[08:43.08]How is that even possible?｜这怎么可能？\n[08:44.80]W: She bought a house for herself and her husband, a house for her parents, and then a house for each of her four brothers and sisters.｜女：她给自己和丈夫买了一套房，给父母买了一套房，然后给四个兄弟姐妹各买了一套房。\n[08:53.24]And then she bought her husband a ridiculously expensive sports car.｜之后她还给丈夫买了一辆贵得离谱的跑车。\n[08:58.16]M: Wow. Are they all happy?｜男：哇。那他们都开心吗？\n[09:00.84]Because that’s what matters, isn’t it?｜因为开心才是最重要的，不是吗？\n[09:02.92]W: I know for a fact Hannah isn’t.｜女：我敢肯定汉娜并不开心。\n[09:05.40]You see, she was planning to quit the job she hates and retire early.｜你看，她原本打算辞掉那份讨厌的工作，提前退休。\n[09:10.12]But now that she ran out of money, she can’t.｜但现在钱花光了，她就不能这么做了。\n[09:13.52]Basically, she miscalculated how fast she was burning through the money, and she’s now full of regret.｜说白了，她错误地估计了自己花钱的速度，现在后悔不已。\n[09:20.80]M: Why don’t they sell that flashy new car?｜男：他们为什么不把那辆招摇的新车卖掉呢？\n[09:23.56]W: She wants to, but her husband refuses to get rid of it.｜女：她想卖，但她丈夫拒绝卖车。\n[09:27.16]He says the car is the best thing that has ever happened to him, and if she sells it, he will divorce her.｜他说这辆车是他遇到过的最好的东西，要是汉娜把车卖了，他就跟她离婚。\n[09:34.36]Questions 8 to 11 are based on the conversation you have just heard.｜请根据你刚听到的对话回答第8至11题。\n[09:39.72]8. Why does the woman say she swears it?｜8.为什么女士说她对此发誓？\n[09:59.02]9. What do we learn about Hannah from the conversation?｜9.从对话中我们能了解到汉娜的什么情况？\n[10:18.66]10. What does the man think really matters to people?｜10.男士认为对人们而言真正重要的是什么？\n[10:37.96]11. What does Hannah’s husband say he’ll do if she sells the new car?｜11.汉娜的丈夫说如果她卖掉新车，他会怎么做？', NOW(), NOW()
