  @a_cet4_2025_12_2_12, '/audio/exams/listening-cet4-2025-12-2.mp3', 'Conversation Two\n对话二\n\nW: If you have time right now, I think we need to sit down and discuss what exactly we are going to do for Jake’s education next year.\n女：要是你现在有时间，我觉得我们得坐下来好好讨论一下明年杰克的教育安排。\n\nI’ve been thinking it over, and I’d like to send him to Westwood Elementary.\n我仔细考虑过了，我想送他去韦斯特伍德小学。\n\nM: You mean that boarding school?\n男：你是说那所寄宿学校？\n\nI thought we agreed that we would not be sending him away at such a young age.\n我以为我们达成共识了，不会在他这么小的时候就送他离开家。\n\nI admit that their academic record is very strong with many outstanding awards for achievements in Science and Math, but he is just not mature enough to live on his own at this point.\n我承认他们在学术方面成绩斐然，在科学和数学领域获得过许多杰出奖项，但他现在还没成熟到能独立生活的地步。\n\nWhat about enrolling him in Lakeview School?\n让他去湖景学校怎么样？\n\nW: They do have a great outdoor campus where he could finally learn all those outdoor sports you have been wanting him to try.\n女：他们确实有个很棒的户外校园，在那里他终于可以学那些你一直想让他尝试的户外运动了。\n\nWith so much greenery and fresh air, I think his current breathing problems would probably disappear.\n那里有那么多绿色植物，还有新鲜空气，我觉得他目前的呼吸问题说不定能得到改善。\n\nThey did just open, though, so I don’t think I feel comfortable having our son in the first class of a brand-new school.\n不过，这所学校刚开办，所以我不放心让儿子去一所全新的学校当第一届学生。\n\nM: Yeah, the classrooms would probably smell like paint, making the air in the school all stuffy.\n男：是啊，教室里可能还弥漫着油漆味，会让学校里的空气变得很闷。\n\nWhat about our local school then?\n那咱们本地的学校怎么样？\n\nThey have a wonderful arts program that would really challenge Jake in terms of creativity and imagination.\n他们有很棒的艺术课程，能充分锻炼杰克的创造力和想象力。\n\nBeing practically next door, one of us could take him to school every day before going to work.\n而且学校离家近，我们俩其中一个可以每天在上班前送他上学。\n\nW: I don’t know.\n女：我不太确定。\n\nThey have a reputation of being overly strict with the students, not to mention the overwhelming amount of homework they assign, which would lead to a lot of pressure for Jake and me.\n那所学校对学生过于严格是出了名的，更别提他们布置的作业量多得惊人，这会给杰克和我带来很大压力。\n\nWhat if we send him to the place near your mother’s house?\n如果我们把他送到你母亲家附近的那所学校呢？\n\nQuestions 12 to 15 are based on the conversation you have just heard.\n请根据你刚听到的对话回答第12至15题。\n\n12. What does the man say about Jake?\n12.关于杰克，男士说了什么？\n\n13. Why does the woman feel uncomfortable about sending Jake to Lakeview School?\n13.为什么女士对送杰克去湖景学校感到不放心？\n\n14. What does the man say about their local school?\n14.关于本地的那所学校，男士说了什么？\n\n15. What does the woman suggest at the end of the conversation?\n15.对话末尾，女士提出了什么建议？\n\nSection C\nC节', 96, 1406, 658.88, 754.68, 759.80, 778.54, 680.94, 691.12, 'cet4-2025-12-2-g05', 'LONG_DIALOGUE', '[10:58.88]Conversation Two｜对话二\n[11:01.66]W: If you have time right now, I think we need to sit down and discuss what exactly we are going to do for Jake’s education next year.｜女：要是你现在有时间，我觉得我们得坐下来好好讨论一下明年杰克的教育安排。\n[11:10.10]I’ve been thinking it over, and I’d like to send him to Westwood Elementary.｜我仔细考虑过了，我想送他去韦斯特伍德小学。\n[11:15.02]M: You mean that boarding school?｜男：你是说那所寄宿学校？\n[11:16.90]I thought we agreed that we would not be sending him away at such a young age.｜我以为我们达成共识了，不会在他这么小的时候就送他离开家。\n[11:20.94]I admit that their academic record is very strong with many outstanding awards for achievements in Science and Math, but he is just not mature enough to live on his own at this point.｜我承认他们在学术方面成绩斐然，在科学和数学领域获得过许多杰出奖项，但他现在还没成熟到能独立生活的地步。\n[11:31.42]What about enrolling him in Lakeview School?｜让他去湖景学校怎么样？\n[11:34.78]W: They do have a great outdoor campus where he could finally learn all those outdoor sports you have been wanting him to try.｜女：他们确实有个很棒的户外校园，在那里他终于可以学那些你一直想让他尝试的户外运动了。\n[11:42.42]With so much greenery and fresh air, I think his current breathing problems would probably disappear.｜那里有那么多绿色植物，还有新鲜空气，我觉得他目前的呼吸问题说不定能得到改善。\n[11:49.50]They did just open, though, so I don’t think I feel comfortable having our son in the first class of a brand-new school.｜不过，这所学校刚开办，所以我不放心让儿子去一所全新的学校当第一届学生。\n[11:57.10]M: Yeah, the classrooms would probably smell like paint, making the air in the school all stuffy.｜男：是啊，教室里可能还弥漫着油漆味，会让学校里的空气变得很闷。\n[12:03.40]What about our local school then?｜那咱们本地的学校怎么样？\n[12:05.48]They have a wonderful arts program that would really challenge Jake in terms of creativity and imagination.｜他们有很棒的艺术课程，能充分锻炼杰克的创造力和想象力。\n[12:12.00]Being practically next door, one of us could take him to school every day before going to work.｜而且学校离家近，我们俩其中一个可以每天在上班前送他上学。\n[12:17.92]W: I don’t know.｜女：我不太确定。\n[12:18.76]They have a reputation of being overly strict with the students, not to mention the overwhelming amount of homework they assign, which would lead to a lot of pressure for Jake and me.｜那所学校对学生过于严格是出了名的，更别提他们布置的作业量多得惊人，这会给杰克和我带来很大压力。\n[12:30.44]What if we send him to the place near your mother’s house?｜如果我们把他送到你母亲家附近的那所学校呢？\n[12:34.68]Questions 12 to 15 are based on the conversation you have just heard.｜请根据你刚听到的对话回答第12至15题。\n[12:39.80]12. What does the man say about Jake?｜12.关于杰克，男士说了什么？\n[12:58.84]13. Why does the woman feel uncomfortable about sending Jake to Lakeview School?｜13.为什么女士对送杰克去湖景学校感到不放心？\n[13:20.28]14. What does the man say about their local school?｜14.关于本地的那所学校，男士说了什么？\n[13:39.56]15. What does the woman suggest at the end of the conversation?｜15.对话末尾，女士提出了什么建议？\n[13:59.50]Section C｜C节', NOW(), NOW()
