SELECT
  @a_cet4_2025_12_2_16, '/audio/exams/listening-cet4-2025-12-2.mp3', 'Passage One\n短文一\n\nAnalytical decision-making is a decision-making approach where a manager makes important business decisions only with solid data.\n分析型决策是一种决策方式，在这种方式下，管理者仅依据可靠的数据来做出重要的商业决策。\n\nThis style contrasts with more instinctive leadership styles where managers make many decisions using instinct or opinion.\n这种风格与更多依赖直觉的领导风格形成鲜明对比，在直觉型领导风格中，管理者会凭借直觉或观点做出许多决策。\n\nWhile analytical decision-makers benefit from a deliberate, thoughtful approach, this style also has some shortcomings.\n虽然分析型决策者能从深思熟虑、审慎周全的决策方式中获益，但这种风格也存在一些缺点。\n\nA key flaw with analytical decision-making is that it takes time.\n分析型决策的一个关键缺陷是耗费时间。\n\nWhile this approach is beneficial when you have the time and the decision is important, it is problematic when time is crucial.\n虽然当你有足够时间且决策很重要时，这种方式很有益处，但当时间紧迫时，就会产生问题。\n\nAnalytical decision-makers struggle with deadlines and a sense of urgency with decisions.\n分析型决策者在面对最后期限和决策的紧迫感时会感到棘手。\n\nIn situations where you need more timely action, decisions based on some information and instinct may work better.\n在需要更加及时地采取行动的情况下，基于部分信息和直觉做出的决策可能效果更好。\n\nThe desire to be right is a major driver of analytical decision-making.\n追求正确无误是分析型决策的主要驱动力。\n\nLeaders who use this style don’t want to make mistakes.\n采用这种决策风格的领导者不愿出现任何失误。\n\nThis commitment, one right way of thinking or doing things, hinders the manager’s flexibility.\n这种对“唯一正确的思路或做法”的执念，会削弱管理者的灵活性。\n\nInflexibility causes you to ignore or avoid listening to the thoughts and ideas of others.\n缺乏灵活性会让你忽视甚至拒绝听取他人的想法与建议。\n\nYou only want to utilize hard data or facts.\n你只想使用确凿的数据或事实。\n\nDespite its restrictions, analytical decision-making does have several key strengths.\n尽管分析型决策存在局限性，但它仍具备多项关键优势。\n\nBy relying on facts and data, you minimize your potential for a wrong decision.\n通过依托事实与数据，决策者能够最大限度地降低做出错误决策的可能性。\n\nYou also get away from the habit of making guesses or following instincts.\n你也能摆脱依赖猜测或听从直觉的习惯。\n\nDatabase technology enables business leaders to look to hard evidence in analyzing target markets and promotional strategies, rather than making assumptions or guesses on what works.\n数据库技术使企业领导者能够依靠确凿证据来分析目标市场和促销策略，而不是假设或猜测什么会有效果。\n\nQuestions 16 to 18 are based on the passage you have just heard.\n请根据你刚听到的短文回答第16至18题。\n\n16. What does the passage say is a major flaw of analytical decision-making?\n16.短文指出分析型决策的一个主要缺陷是什么？\n\n17. What does a leader tend to do when they are committed to analytical decision-making?\n17.当领导者奉行分析型决策时，他们往往会怎么做？\n\n18. What is a key strength of analytical decision-making?\n18.分析型决策的一项关键优势是什么？', 112, 1406, 868.74, 980.96, 986.16, 1007.52, NULL, NULL, 'cet4-2025-12-2-g06', 'PASSAGE', '[14:28.74]Passage One｜短文一\n[14:31.10]Analytical decision-making is a decision-making approach where a manager makes important business decisions only with solid data.｜分析型决策是一种决策方式，在这种方式下，管理者仅依据可靠的数据来做出重要的商业决策。\n[14:40.10]This style contrasts with more instinctive leadership styles where managers make many decisions using instinct or opinion.｜这种风格与更多依赖直觉的领导风格形成鲜明对比，在直觉型领导风格中，管理者会凭借直觉或观点做出许多决策。\n[14:48.90]While analytical decision-makers benefit from a deliberate, thoughtful approach, this style also has some shortcomings.｜虽然分析型决策者能从深思熟虑、审慎周全的决策方式中获益，但这种风格也存在一些缺点。\n[14:57.58]A key flaw with analytical decision-making is that it takes time.｜分析型决策的一个关键缺陷是耗费时间。\n[15:02.64]While this approach is beneficial when you have the time and the decision is important, it is problematic when time is crucial.｜虽然当你有足够时间且决策很重要时，这种方式很有益处，但当时间紧迫时，就会产生问题。\n[15:11.24]Analytical decision-makers struggle with deadlines and a sense of urgency with decisions.｜分析型决策者在面对最后期限和决策的紧迫感时会感到棘手。\n[15:17.12]In situations where you need more timely action, decisions based on some information and instinct may work better.｜在需要更加及时地采取行动的情况下，基于部分信息和直觉做出的决策可能效果更好。\n[15:26.08]The desire to be right is a major driver of analytical decision-making.｜追求正确无误是分析型决策的主要驱动力。\n[15:31.00]Leaders who use this style don’t want to make mistakes.｜采用这种决策风格的领导者不愿出现任何失误。\n[15:35.00]This commitment, one right way of thinking or doing things, hinders the manager’s flexibility.｜这种对“唯一正确的思路或做法”的执念，会削弱管理者的灵活性。\n[15:41.40]Inflexibility causes you to ignore or avoid listening to the thoughts and ideas of others.｜缺乏灵活性会让你忽视甚至拒绝听取他人的想法与建议。\n[15:47.92]You only want to utilize hard data or facts.｜你只想使用确凿的数据或事实。\n[15:52.48]Despite its restrictions, analytical decision-making does have several key strengths.｜尽管分析型决策存在局限性，但它仍具备多项关键优势。\n[15:57.80]By relying on facts and data, you minimize your potential for a wrong decision.｜通过依托事实与数据，决策者能够最大限度地降低做出错误决策的可能性。\n[16:03.12]You also get away from the habit of making guesses or following instincts.｜你也能摆脱依赖猜测或听从直觉的习惯。\n[16:08.20]Database technology enables business leaders to look to hard evidence in analyzing target markets and promotional strategies, rather than making assumptions or guesses on what works.｜数据库技术使企业领导者能够依靠确凿证据来分析目标市场和促销策略，而不是假设或猜测什么会有效果。\n[16:20.96]Questions 16 to 18 are based on the passage you have just heard.｜请根据你刚听到的短文回答第16至18题。\n[16:26.16]16. What does the passage say is a major flaw of analytical decision-making?｜16.短文指出分析型决策的一个主要缺陷是什么？\n[16:47.82]17. What does a leader tend to do when they are committed to analytical decision-making?｜17.当领导者奉行分析型决策时，他们往往会怎么做？\n[17:09.60]18. What is a key strength of analytical decision-making?｜18.分析型决策的一项关键优势是什么？', NOW(), NOW()
