SELECT
  @a_cet4_2025_12_2_19, '/audio/exams/listening-cet4-2025-12-2.mp3', 'Passage Two\n短文二\n\nWhat is the secret to living past 100?\n活过一百岁的秘诀是什么？\n\nPlaying the piano is among the things the world’s oldest person believes has contributed to her long life.\n据这位全球最长寿的老人所言，弹钢琴是助力她长寿的因素之一。\n\nBranyas Morera is now 115 years and 320 days old.\n布兰尼亚斯·莫雷拉如今已是115岁零320天的高龄。\n\nThat means she’s been alive longer than any other living individual.\n这意味着她比其他任何在世的人都活得久。\n\nBranyas was born in the United States on April 4th, 1907.\n布兰尼亚斯于1907年4月4日出生在美国。\n\nBut her family moved to Spain, where they were originally from when she was a young child.\n但在她小时候，他们一家就搬回了祖籍西班牙。\n\nShe has lived there ever since.\n此后她一直生活在那里。\n\nThe 115-year-old is active on social media, regularly sharing aspects of her life.\n这位115岁的老人在社交媒体上很活跃，经常分享自己生活的方方面面。\n\nShe also shares some of her secrets to living so long.\n她还会分享一些长寿秘诀。\n\nThese include playing the piano from a young age.\n其中包括从小弹钢琴。\n\nUnfortunately, she had to give up the practice seven years ago at 108.\n遗憾的是，七年前，也就是她108岁时，她不得不放弃弹钢琴。\n\nHer other secrets for living a long life?\n她还有哪些长寿秘诀呢？\n\nShe led an active lifestyle until her later years, but has never followed a specific diet.\n她直到晚年都一直保持着积极的生活方式，但从未遵循过特定的饮食方案。\n\n“Many people ask me what diet I follow to live so many years,” Branyas wrote.\n“很多人问我遵循什么饮食方案才能活这么久，”布兰尼亚斯写道。\n\n“I have always eaten little, but everything, and I have never followed any plan.”\n“我一直吃得很少，但什么都吃，而且从未遵循过任何计划。”\n\nBut she does eat yogurt every day, which she said has “an infinite number of positive properties” for the body.\n不过她确实每天都喝酸奶，她说这对身体有“无数益处”。\n\nShe has also said that the secret to a long life is “knowing how to choose” what to forget.\n她还说过，长寿的秘诀是“懂得如何选择”要忘记什么。\n\n“Life would be impossible if we remembered everything,” she said.\n“如果我们什么都记得，生活将无法继续，”她说道。\n\nQuestions 19 to 21 are based on the passage you have just heard.\n请根据你刚听到的短文回答第19至21题。\n\n19. What do we learn about Branyas Morera?\n19.关于布兰尼亚斯·莫雷拉，我们能了解到什么？\n\n20. What is one of Branyas Morera’s secrets to living a long life?\n20.布兰尼亚斯·莫雷拉的长寿秘诀之一是什么？\n\n21. What does Branyas Morera think also contributes to a long life?\n21.布兰尼亚斯·莫雷拉认为，还有什么因素有助于长寿？', 101, 1406, 1049.70, 1150.66, 1155.98, 1174.88, NULL, NULL, 'cet4-2025-12-2-g07', 'PASSAGE', '[17:29.70]Passage Two｜短文二\n[17:31.58]What is the secret to living past 100?｜活过一百岁的秘诀是什么？\n[17:35.02]Playing the piano is among the things the world’s oldest person believes has contributed to her long life.｜据这位全球最长寿的老人所言，弹钢琴是助力她长寿的因素之一。\n[17:42.58]Branyas Morera is now 115 years and 320 days old.｜布兰尼亚斯·莫雷拉如今已是115岁零320天的高龄。\n[17:49.22]That means she’s been alive longer than any other living individual.｜这意味着她比其他任何在世的人都活得久。\n[17:54.10]Branyas was born in the United States on April 4th, 1907.｜布兰尼亚斯于1907年4月4日出生在美国。\n[18:00.08]But her family moved to Spain, where they were originally from when she was a young child.｜但在她小时候，他们一家就搬回了祖籍西班牙。\n[18:06.20]She has lived there ever since.｜此后她一直生活在那里。\n[18:08.76]The 115-year-old is active on social media, regularly sharing aspects of her life.｜这位115岁的老人在社交媒体上很活跃，经常分享自己生活的方方面面。\n[18:16.28]She also shares some of her secrets to living so long.｜她还会分享一些长寿秘诀。\n[18:20.44]These include playing the piano from a young age.｜其中包括从小弹钢琴。\n[18:23.80]Unfortunately, she had to give up the practice seven years ago at 108.｜遗憾的是，七年前，也就是她108岁时，她不得不放弃弹钢琴。\n[18:30.16]Her other secrets for living a long life?｜她还有哪些长寿秘诀呢？\n[18:33.08]She led an active lifestyle until her later years, but has never followed a specific diet.｜她直到晚年都一直保持着积极的生活方式，但从未遵循过特定的饮食方案。\n[18:39.80]“Many people ask me what diet I follow to live so many years,” Branyas wrote.｜“很多人问我遵循什么饮食方案才能活这么久，”布兰尼亚斯写道。\n[18:45.64]“I have always eaten little, but everything, and I have never followed any plan.”｜“我一直吃得很少，但什么都吃，而且从未遵循过任何计划。”\n[18:51.84]But she does eat yogurt every day, which she said has “an infinite number of positive properties” for the body.｜不过她确实每天都喝酸奶，她说这对身体有“无数益处”。\n[19:00.24]She has also said that the secret to a long life is “knowing how to choose” what to forget.｜她还说过，长寿的秘诀是“懂得如何选择”要忘记什么。\n[19:05.52]“Life would be impossible if we remembered everything,” she said.｜“如果我们什么都记得，生活将无法继续，”她说道。\n[19:10.66]Questions 19 to 21 are based on the passage you have just heard.｜请根据你刚听到的短文回答第19至21题。\n[19:15.98]19. What do we learn about Branyas Morera?｜19.关于布兰尼亚斯·莫雷拉，我们能了解到什么？\n[19:35.18]20. What is one of Branyas Morera’s secrets to living a long life?｜20.布兰尼亚斯·莫雷拉的长寿秘诀之一是什么？\n[19:56.60]21. What does Branyas Morera think also contributes to a long life?｜21.布兰尼亚斯·莫雷拉认为，还有什么因素有助于长寿？', NOW(), NOW()
