SELECT
  @a_cet4_2025_12_2_22, '/audio/exams/listening-cet4-2025-12-2.mp3', 'Passage Three\n短文三\n\nIt’s the first day of school, and your teacher tells you to find a seat in the classroom.\n开学第一天，老师让你在教室里找个座位坐下。\n\nWhere do you sit?\n你会坐在哪里呢？\n\nDoes it matter?\n这重要吗？\n\nYes. It does matter where you sit in your classroom, so choose and choose carefully.\n是的。你在教室里坐哪个位置确实很重要，所以要慎重选择。\n\nStudies report that where you sit in the classroom can impact your ability to learn and the way your teacher perceives you.\n研究表明，你在教室里坐哪个位置会影响你的学习能力以及老师对你的看法。\n\nGuess what else?\n猜猜还有什么？\n\nYour grade.\n还会影响你的成绩。\n\nThen what is the best seat in the classroom?\n那么，教室里哪个座位最好呢？\n\nIn one study, students who sat in the front and center of the classroom received a higher grade average and scored higher on tests than those sitting towards the back of the classroom.\n在一项研究中，坐在教室前排和中间位置的学生平均成绩更高，考试成绩也比坐在教室后排的学生更好。\n\nGet this.\n看看这个。\n\nStudents sitting in the middle of the classroom also outscored students sitting behind them.\n坐在教室中间的学生得分超过坐在他们后面的学生。\n\nThis study gathered that students had a clearer vision of the blackboard and were able to focus more attention on the instructor.\n这项研究认为，这些学生看黑板看得更清楚，能够将更多的注意力集中在教师身上。\n\nBy sitting front and center, students were able to hear better too.\n坐在前排和中间位置，学生也能听得更清楚。\n\nThe instructors said that they also formed a better connection with the students who sat in front.\n教师们表示，他们也能与坐在前排的学生建立更好的联系。\n\nPerhaps the connection is made because of eye contact and visibility and more interaction.\n或许这种联系是因为眼神交流、视线接触以及更多互动而产生的。\n\nBut when you sit in the front row, you may be called on more by your teacher, mainly due to the fact that you are easier to see.\n但当你坐在前排时，老师可能会更频繁地叫你回答问题，这主要是因为你更容易被看到。\n\nSo for students who are not prepared and for those who are extremely shy, the attention could cause some unwanted stress.\n因此，对于那些没有做好准备的学生以及性格特别腼腆的学生来说，教师们的这种关注可能会带来一些不必要的压力。\n\nQuestions 22 to 25 are based on the passage you have just heard.\n请根据你刚听到的短文回答第22至25题。\n\n22. What is of great importance to students according to the speaker?\n22.根据讲话者的观点，对学生而言什么至关重要？\n\n23. What did one study find about students seated in the middle of the classroom?\n23.关于坐在教室中间的学生，研究有何发现？\n\n24. What can eye contact, visibility and more interaction probably bring about?\n24.眼神交流、视线接触以及更多互动可能会带来什么？\n\n25. What do we learn about extremely shy students sitting in the front row of the classroom?\n25.关于坐在教室前排性格特别腼腆的学生，我们能了解到什么？', 91, 1406, 1218.92, 1309.94, 1315.14, 1335.62, 1228.60, 1234.46, 'cet4-2025-12-2-g08', 'PASSAGE', '[20:18.92]Passage Three｜短文三\n[20:20.96]It’s the first day of school, and your teacher tells you to find a seat in the classroom.｜开学第一天，老师让你在教室里找个座位坐下。\n[20:25.92]Where do you sit?｜你会坐在哪里呢？\n[20:27.28]Does it matter?｜这重要吗？\n[20:28.60]Yes. It does matter where you sit in your classroom, so choose and choose carefully.｜是的。你在教室里坐哪个位置确实很重要，所以要慎重选择。\n[20:34.76]Studies report that where you sit in the classroom can impact your ability to learn and the way your teacher perceives you.｜研究表明，你在教室里坐哪个位置会影响你的学习能力以及老师对你的看法。\n[20:42.12]Guess what else?｜猜猜还有什么？\n[20:43.32]Your grade.｜还会影响你的成绩。\n[20:44.96]Then what is the best seat in the classroom?｜那么，教室里哪个座位最好呢？\n[20:47.84]In one study, students who sat in the front and center of the classroom received a higher grade average and scored higher on tests than those sitting towards the back of the classroom.｜在一项研究中，坐在教室前排和中间位置的学生平均成绩更高，考试成绩也比坐在教室后排的学生更好。\n[20:59.52]Get this.｜看看这个。\n[21:01.08]Students sitting in the middle of the classroom also outscored students sitting behind them.｜坐在教室中间的学生得分超过坐在他们后面的学生。\n[21:06.96]This study gathered that students had a clearer vision of the blackboard and were able to focus more attention on the instructor.｜这项研究认为，这些学生看黑板看得更清楚，能够将更多的注意力集中在教师身上。\n[21:14.44]By sitting front and center, students were able to hear better too.｜坐在前排和中间位置，学生也能听得更清楚。\n[21:19.24]The instructors said that they also formed a better connection with the students who sat in front.｜教师们表示，他们也能与坐在前排的学生建立更好的联系。\n[21:25.78]Perhaps the connection is made because of eye contact and visibility and more interaction.｜或许这种联系是因为眼神交流、视线接触以及更多互动而产生的。\n[21:32.26]But when you sit in the front row, you may be called on more by your teacher, mainly due to the fact that you are easier to see.｜但当你坐在前排时，老师可能会更频繁地叫你回答问题，这主要是因为你更容易被看到。\n[21:40.58]So for students who are not prepared and for those who are extremely shy, the attention could cause some unwanted stress.｜因此，对于那些没有做好准备的学生以及性格特别腼腆的学生来说，教师们的这种关注可能会带来一些不必要的压力。\n[21:49.94]Questions 22 to 25 are based on the passage you have just heard.｜请根据你刚听到的短文回答第22至25题。\n[21:55.14]22. What is of great importance to students according to the speaker?｜22.根据讲话者的观点，对学生而言什么至关重要？\n[22:15.92]23. What did one study find about students seated in the middle of the classroom?｜23.关于坐在教室中间的学生，研究有何发现？\n[22:37.76]24. What can eye contact, visibility and more interaction probably bring about?｜24.眼神交流、视线接触以及更多互动可能会带来什么？\n[23:00.60]25. What do we learn about extremely shy students sitting in the front row of the classroom?｜25.关于坐在教室前排性格特别腼腆的学生，我们能了解到什么？', NOW(), NOW()
