  (`question_id`, `audio_url`, `transcript`, `duration_seconds`, `audio_total_seconds`, `audio_start_seconds`, `audio_end_seconds`, `question_start_seconds`, `question_end_seconds`, `answer_start_seconds`, `answer_end_seconds`, `group_key`, `listening_type`, `lrc_content`, `created_at`, `updated_at`)
SELECT
  @a_cet4_2026_06_1_01, '/audio/exams/listening-cet4-2026-06-1.mp3', 'News Report One\n新闻一\n\nA man was left with a $1,000 bill after his 6-year-old son ordered a virtual buffet of food from several restaurants last weekend.\n上周末，一名男子6岁的儿子在网上从多家餐厅订购了各种美食，结果该男子收到了一张1,000美元的账单。\n\nThis led to a string of unexpected deliveries and maybe a starring role in an advertisement campaign.\n此事不仅引发了一连串意料之外的外卖配送，或许还会让这家人成为广告宣传活动的主角。\n\nKeith Stonehouse said the food piled up quickly at his home Saturday night after he let his son use his cell phone to play a game before bed.\n基思·斯通豪斯说，周六晚上，他让儿子在睡前用他的手机玩游戏，结果食物很快就在家里堆积起来。\n\nHe said the youngster instead used his father''s online food ordering account to order food from one restaurant after another.\n他表示，小家伙反而用父亲的在线订餐账户从一家又一家餐厅订购食物。\n\nThe boy''s mother, Kristin Stonehouse, said that the online food app has reached out to the family and offered them a $1,000 gift card.\n男孩的母亲克里斯廷·斯通豪斯说，这家在线订餐应用已经联系了他们一家，并提供了一张1,000美元的礼品卡。\n\nThe company also is considering using the family in an online promotional campaign.\n该公司还考虑让这家人参与线上推广活动。\n\nMost of the food went into the family''s refrigerators.\n大部分食物被放进了家里的冰箱。\n\nThey also invited some neighbors over to eat some of it.\n他们还邀请了一些邻居来吃了一些。\n\nThe father is planning to change his password.\n这位父亲打算修改自己的密码。\n\nQuestions 1 and 2 are based on the news report you have just heard.\n请根据你刚听到的新闻报道回答第1题和第2题。\n\n1. Why was Keith Stonehouse left with a $1,000 bill?\n1. 基思·斯通豪斯为什么收到了一张1,000美元的账单？\n\n2. What does the news report say Keith Stonehouse is planning to do?\n2. 新闻提到基思·斯通豪斯打算做什么？', 69, 1426.55, 39.32, 108.00, 113.00, 133.60, 41.16, 50.98, 'cet4-2026-06-1-g01', 'NEWS', '[00:39.32]News Report One｜新闻一\n[00:41.16]A man was left with a $1,000 bill after his 6-year-old son ordered a virtual buffet of food from several restaurants last weekend.｜上周末，一名男子6岁的儿子在网上从多家餐厅订购了各种美食，结果该男子收到了一张1,000美元的账单。\n[00:51.28]This led to a string of unexpected deliveries and maybe a starring role in an advertisement campaign.｜此事不仅引发了一连串意料之外的外卖配送，或许还会让这家人成为广告宣传活动的主角。\n[00:59.44]Keith Stonehouse said the food piled up quickly at his home Saturday night after he let his son use his cell phone to play a game before bed.｜基思·斯通豪斯说，周六晚上，他让儿子在睡前用他的手机玩游戏，结果食物很快就在家里堆积起来。\n[01:09.52]He said the youngster instead used his father''s online food ordering account to order food from one restaurant after another.｜他表示，小家伙反而用父亲的在线订餐账户从一家又一家餐厅订购食物。\n[01:18.88]The boy''s mother, Kristin Stonehouse, said that the online food app has reached out to the family and offered them a $1,000 gift card.｜男孩的母亲克里斯廷·斯通豪斯说，这家在线订餐应用已经联系了他们一家，并提供了一张1,000美元的礼品卡。\n[01:29.52]The company also is considering using the family in an online promotional campaign.｜该公司还考虑让这家人参与线上推广活动。\n[01:36.64]Most of the food went into the family''s refrigerators.｜大部分食物被放进了家里的冰箱。\n[01:40.48]They also invited some neighbors over to eat some of it.｜他们还邀请了一些邻居来吃了一些。\n[01:44.40]The father is planning to change his password.｜这位父亲打算修改自己的密码。\n[01:48.00]Questions 1 and 2 are based on the news report you have just heard.｜请根据你刚听到的新闻报道回答第1题和第2题。\n[01:53.00]1. Why was Keith Stonehouse left with a $1,000 bill?｜1. 基思·斯通豪斯为什么收到了一张1,000美元的账单？\n[02:13.90]2. What does the news report say Keith Stonehouse is planning to do?｜2. 新闻提到基思·斯通豪斯打算做什么？', NOW(), NOW()
