  @a_cet4_2026_06_1_10, '/audio/exams/listening-cet4-2026-06-1.mp3', 'Conversation One\n对话一\n\nW: Hey, Mike.\n女：嘿，迈克。\n\nWhat do you think of the museum you visited today?\n你觉得你今天去参观的博物馆怎么样？\n\nM: Hey, Sue.\n男：嘿，休。\n\nThe museum is great.\n博物馆很棒。\n\nVery interesting.\n非常有意思。\n\nThey have loads of stuff there on display.\n里面展出了很多展品。\n\nThe primitive tools early humans used tell a lot about their life, but my favourite is the coin collection.\n早期人类使用的原始工具讲述了很多关于他们生活的故事，但我最喜欢的是硬币收藏品。\n\nThey have some coins that are over 2,000 years old.\n馆里一些硬币有两千多年的历史。\n\nW: That sounds cool.\n女：听起来很酷。\n\nM: Yeah. What did you do today?\n男：是的。你今天做了什么？\n\nW: Kathy and I just wandered through the old city centre.\n女：我和凯茜就在老城中心闲逛。\n\nThe streets are narrow but beautiful with plenty of charm.\n那里的街道虽然狭窄，但很漂亮，富有魅力。\n\nWe saw the Trevi Fountain, which is in all the guidebooks.\n我们看了特雷维喷泉，所有旅游指南里都有它。\n\nM: How do you like it?\n男：你觉得喷泉怎么样？\n\nW: It''s very pretty.\n女：特别好看。\n\nBut it was overcrowded with tourists.\n但是挤满了游客。\n\nM: Yeah, well, it''s crowded everywhere.\n男：是啊，到处都很拥挤。\n\nIt is August after all, the busiest month of the year.\n毕竟现在是八月，一年中最繁忙的月份。\n\nW: Yes, it''s like the whole world is here on holiday, including us.\n女：没错，感觉好像全世界的人都来这里度假了，我们也一样。\n\nWhat will you do tomorrow?\n你明天打算做什么？\n\nM: I haven''t decided yet.\n男：我还没决定。\n\nI was thinking of doing what you did today, wandering the old streets and taking pictures.\n我在想就做你今天做的事，逛逛老街拍拍照。\n\nI was also thinking of visiting the square with the Spanish Steps.\n我还想去那个有西班牙大台阶的广场看看。\n\nW: What is that?\n女：那是什么地方？\n\nI haven''t heard of it.\n我没听说过。\n\nM: It''s a square where on one side there are some very wide steps with flowers that go up to a church.\n男：那个广场的一边有一些很宽的台阶，上面种着鲜花，通向一座教堂。\n\nIt''s also in all the tourist guidebooks.\n所有旅游指南上也都有它的介绍。\n\nIt''s very famous and pretty.\n它非常有名，也很好看。\n\nI was also thinking of seeing that tomorrow.\n我也在考虑明天去看一看。\n\nW: It sounds very nice.\n女：听起来很不错。\n\nDo you mind if Kathy and I join you tomorrow?\n你介意我和凯茜明天跟你一起去吗？\n\nM: Not at all.\n男：完全不介意。\n\nI spent the whole day today pretty much alone.\n我今天一整天基本都是独自游玩。\n\nDoing tourist stuff with others would be a welcome change.\n和别人结伴游玩是个不错的改变。\n\nW: Let me ask her first, but I''m sure she''ll be up for it.\n女：我先去问问凯茜，不过我确定她会愿意的。\n\nQuestions 8 to 11 are based on the conversation you have just heard.\n请根据你刚听到的对话回答第8至11题。\n\n8. What exhibit does the man like best in the museum he visited?\n8. 在男士参观的博物馆里，他最喜欢什么展品？\n\n9. What does the woman say about the old city centre?\n9. 关于老城中心，女士说了什么？\n\n10. What does the man say about the square with the Spanish Steps?\n10. 关于那个有西班牙大台阶的广场，男士说了什么？\n\n11. What does the woman say she is going to do first?\n11. 女士说她将首先做什么？', 100, 1426.55, 462.36, 561.88, 607.34, 627.26, 541.28, 543.18, 'cet4-2026-06-1-g04', 'LONG_DIALOGUE', '[07:42.36]Conversation One｜对话一\n[07:44.24]W: Hey, Mike.｜女：嘿，迈克。\n[07:45.39]What do you think of the museum you visited today?｜你觉得你今天去参观的博物馆怎么样？\n[07:48.30]M: Hey, Sue.｜男：嘿，休。\n[07:49.34]The museum is great.｜博物馆很棒。\n[07:51.02]Very interesting.｜非常有意思。\n[07:52.34]They have loads of stuff there on display.｜里面展出了很多展品。\n[07:55.30]The primitive tools early humans used tell a lot about their life, but my favourite is the coin collection.｜早期人类使用的原始工具讲述了很多关于他们生活的故事，但我最喜欢的是硬币收藏品。\n[08:02.28]They have some coins that are over 2,000 years old.｜馆里一些硬币有两千多年的历史。\n[08:05.84]W: That sounds cool.｜女：听起来很酷。\n[08:07.20]M: Yeah. What did you do today?｜男：是的。你今天做了什么？\n[08:09.27]W: Kathy and I just wandered through the old city centre.｜女：我和凯茜就在老城中心闲逛。\n[08:13.08]The streets are narrow but beautiful with plenty of charm.｜那里的街道虽然狭窄，但很漂亮，富有魅力。\n[08:17.00]We saw the Trevi Fountain, which is in all the guidebooks.｜我们看了特雷维喷泉，所有旅游指南里都有它。\n[08:20.40]M: How do you like it?｜男：你觉得喷泉怎么样？\n[08:21.64]W: It''s very pretty.｜女：特别好看。\n[08:23.00]But it was overcrowded with tourists.｜但是挤满了游客。\n[08:26.04]M: Yeah, well, it''s crowded everywhere.｜男：是啊，到处都很拥挤。\n[08:28.60]It is August after all, the busiest month of the year.｜毕竟现在是八月，一年中最繁忙的月份。\n[08:32.00]W: Yes, it''s like the whole world is here on holiday, including us.｜女：没错，感觉好像全世界的人都来这里度假了，我们也一样。\n[08:36.48]What will you do tomorrow?｜你明天打算做什么？\n[08:38.12]M: I haven''t decided yet.｜男：我还没决定。\n[08:40.08]I was thinking of doing what you did today, wandering the old streets and taking pictures.｜我在想就做你今天做的事，逛逛老街拍拍照。\n[08:45.68]I was also thinking of visiting the square with the Spanish Steps.｜我还想去那个有西班牙大台阶的广场看看。\n[08:49.64]W: What is that?｜女：那是什么地方？\n[08:50.44]I haven''t heard of it.｜我没听说过。\n[08:51.76]M: It''s a square where on one side there are some very wide steps with flowers that go up to a church.｜男：那个广场的一边有一些很宽的台阶，上面种着鲜花，通向一座教堂。\n[08:58.88]It''s also in all the tourist guidebooks.｜所有旅游指南上也都有它的介绍。\n[09:01.28]It''s very famous and pretty.｜它非常有名，也很好看。\n[09:03.48]I was also thinking of seeing that tomorrow.｜我也在考虑明天去看一看。\n[09:05.88]W: It sounds very nice.｜女：听起来很不错。\n[09:07.40]Do you mind if Kathy and I join you tomorrow?｜你介意我和凯茜明天跟你一起去吗？\n[09:10.08]M: Not at all.｜男：完全不介意。\n[09:11.12]I spent the whole day today pretty much alone.｜我今天一整天基本都是独自游玩。\n[09:14.04]Doing tourist stuff with others would be a welcome change.｜和别人结伴游玩是个不错的改变。\n[09:17.16]W: Let me ask her first, but I''m sure she''ll be up for it.｜女：我先去问问凯茜，不过我确定她会愿意的。\n[09:21.88]Questions 8 to 11 are based on the conversation you have just heard.｜请根据你刚听到的对话回答第8至11题。\n[09:27.16]8. What exhibit does the man like best in the museum he visited?｜8. 在男士参观的博物馆里，他最喜欢什么展品？\n[09:47.74]9. What does the woman say about the old city centre?｜9. 关于老城中心，女士说了什么？\n[10:07.34]10. What does the man say about the square with the Spanish Steps?｜10. 关于那个有西班牙大台阶的广场，男士说了什么？\n[10:27.56]11. What does the woman say she is going to do first?｜11. 女士说她将首先做什么？', NOW(), NOW()
