  @a_cet4_2026_06_1_12, '/audio/exams/listening-cet4-2026-06-1.mp3', 'Conversation Two\n对话二\n\nM: Can you give me advice about being successful at a new job?\n男：你能给我一些关于如何在新工作中取得成功的建议吗？\n\nI start mine next week.\n我下周就要开始新工作了。\n\nW: Sure.\n女：当然可以。\n\nIt''s important not to undermine the significance of the first few days of your job, since this is the best time to create a solid first impression.\n不要小看入职头几天的重要性，因为这是建立良好第一印象的最佳时机。\n\nM: That''s a good point.\n男：说得很有道理。\n\nI''ll need to collaborate with my coworkers, and I''m very aware of just how important others are for my success at work.\n我需要和同事合作，我也很清楚别人对我能否做好工作至关重要。\n\nW: It''s also important to understand your role thoroughly to gain a comprehensive picture of your job.\n女：全面了解自己的职能也很重要，这样才能对你的工作有一个整体的认识。\n\nThe most important thing for you to do at first is to understand your role from multiple perspectives.\n你一开始要做的最重要的事情，就是从多个角度理解你的职能。\n\nM: Why is that?\n男：为什么这么说？\n\nW: Well, what you do at work is not just limited to your job description.\n女：嗯，你在工作中要做的并不仅限于职位描述里的那些。\n\nYou need to consider how your work relates to other people within the organization.\n你需要考虑自己的工作与组织中的其他人有怎样的关联。\n\nM: Oh, right.\n男：噢，对。\n\nSo, for example, certain reports that I create at the end of the month may be used by a team in another department.\n那么，举例来说，我月底制作的某些报告可能会被另一个部门的团队使用。\n\nW: That''s right.\n女：没错。\n\nAnd in that respect, it''s also important to learn about the business to see the big picture.\n从这个角度来说，熟悉公司业务以把握整体大局也很重要。\n\nM: You mean like knowing about the history of the company?\n男：你是说要了解公司历史吗？\n\nW: Kind of, but more like knowing the details of the products and services that the company exists to deliver.\n女：差不多，但更多的是了解公司所要提供的产品和服务的细节。\n\nLearning about the business will give you a chance to understand how your role fits into the bigger picture.\n了解公司业务会让你有机会理解自己的职能如何融入整体大局。\n\nM: Okay. I''m feeling a bit uneasy about meeting my boss as well.\n男：好的。我还对见我的老板感到有些忐忑不安。\n\nW: That''s to be expected.\n女：这是正常的。\n\nHowever, it''s crucial that you get to know the people who have decision-making authority to gain insight regarding how the business is run and decisions are made.\n不过，至关重要的是，你要去认识那些拥有决策权的人，这样才能深入了解公司是如何运营的、决策是如何做出的。\n\nM: Great advice. Thanks.\n男：很好的建议。谢谢你。\n\nQuestions 12 to 15 are based on the conversation you have just heard.\n请根据你刚听到的对话回答第12至15题。\n\n12. What advice does the man want to get from the woman?\n12. 男士想从女士那里得到什么建议？\n\n13. What does the woman say is the most important thing for the man to do at first?\n13. 女士认为男士一开始要做的最重要的事情是什么？\n\n14. What does the man say he is feeling a bit uneasy about?\n14. 男士说他对什么感到有些忐忑不安？\n\n15. What does the woman suggest the man do to gain insight about the running of the business?\n15. 女士建议男士做什么来深入了解公司的运营情况？', 101, 1426.55, 647.22, 748.64, 753.84, 773.36, 649.66, 653.08, 'cet4-2026-06-1-g05', 'LONG_DIALOGUE', '[10:47.22]Conversation Two｜对话二\n[10:49.66]M: Can you give me advice about being successful at a new job?｜男：你能给我一些关于如何在新工作中取得成功的建议吗？\n[10:53.38]I start mine next week.｜我下周就要开始新工作了。\n[10:55.26]W: Sure.｜女：当然可以。\n[10:56.06]It''s important not to undermine the significance of the first few days of your job, since this is the best time to create a solid first impression.｜不要小看入职头几天的重要性，因为这是建立良好第一印象的最佳时机。\n[11:05.44]M: That''s a good point.｜男：说得很有道理。\n[11:06.72]I''ll need to collaborate with my coworkers, and I''m very aware of just how important others are for my success at work.｜我需要和同事合作，我也很清楚别人对我能否做好工作至关重要。\n[11:14.12]W: It''s also important to understand your role thoroughly to gain a comprehensive picture of your job.｜女：全面了解自己的职能也很重要，这样才能对你的工作有一个整体的认识。\n[11:20.52]The most important thing for you to do at first is to understand your role from multiple perspectives.｜你一开始要做的最重要的事情，就是从多个角度理解你的职能。\n[11:27.08]M: Why is that?｜男：为什么这么说？\n[11:28.16]W: Well, what you do at work is not just limited to your job description.｜女：嗯，你在工作中要做的并不仅限于职位描述里的那些。\n[11:32.88]You need to consider how your work relates to other people within the organization.｜你需要考虑自己的工作与组织中的其他人有怎样的关联。\n[11:37.56]M: Oh, right.｜男：噢，对。\n[11:38.84]So, for example, certain reports that I create at the end of the month may be used by a team in another department.｜那么，举例来说，我月底制作的某些报告可能会被另一个部门的团队使用。\n[11:46.40]W: That''s right.｜女：没错。\n[11:47.24]And in that respect, it''s also important to learn about the business to see the big picture.｜从这个角度来说，熟悉公司业务以把握整体大局也很重要。\n[11:53.16]M: You mean like knowing about the history of the company?｜男：你是说要了解公司历史吗？\n[11:56.52]W: Kind of, but more like knowing the details of the products and services that the company exists to deliver.｜女：差不多，但更多的是了解公司所要提供的产品和服务的细节。\n[12:03.84]Learning about the business will give you a chance to understand how your role fits into the bigger picture.｜了解公司业务会让你有机会理解自己的职能如何融入整体大局。\n[12:09.68]M: Okay. I''m feeling a bit uneasy about meeting my boss as well.｜男：好的。我还对见我的老板感到有些忐忑不安。\n[12:14.25]W: That''s to be expected.｜女：这是正常的。\n[12:16.12]However, it''s crucial that you get to know the people who have decision-making authority to gain insight regarding how the business is run and decisions are made.｜不过，至关重要的是，你要去认识那些拥有决策权的人，这样才能深入了解公司是如何运营的、决策是如何做出的。\n[12:25.88]M: Great advice. Thanks.｜男：很好的建议。谢谢你。\n[12:28.64]Questions 12 to 15 are based on the conversation you have just heard.｜请根据你刚听到的对话回答第12至15题。\n[12:33.84]12. What advice does the man want to get from the woman?｜12. 男士想从女士那里得到什么建议？\n[12:53.66]13. What does the woman say is the most important thing for the man to do at first?｜13. 女士认为男士一开始要做的最重要的事情是什么？\n[13:15.40]14. What does the man say he is feeling a bit uneasy about?｜14. 男士说他对什么感到有些忐忑不安？\n[13:36.24]15. What does the woman suggest the man do to gain insight about the running of the business?｜15. 女士建议男士做什么来深入了解公司的运营情况？', NOW(), NOW()
