  @a_cet4_2026_06_1_18, '/audio/exams/listening-cet4-2026-06-1.mp3', 'Passage One\n短文一\n\nContrary to popular belief, consumers aren''t as smart as they like to believe.\n与大众普遍认知相反，消费者并没有他们自以为的那么聪明。\n\nMany consumers report comparing multiple competing brands and prices when evaluating a purchase.\n许多消费者声称在评估购买时会对比多家互相竞争的品牌与价格。\n\nHowever, research indicates that this is not actually the case.\n然而，研究表明事实并非如此。\n\nWhat consumers really think or feel often contradicts what they say.\n消费者真实的想法与感受往往和他们所说的相矛盾。\n\nA big reason is that they are driven by unconscious urges, the biggest of which is emotion.\n一个主要原因是他们会被无意识的冲动所驱使，其中影响最大的就是情感。\n\nEmotion is what really drives the purchasing behaviours and also decision-making in general.\n情感才是真正推动购买行为乃至所有决策的因素。\n\nGood marketers keep in mind this important fact all the time, and examples of emotion-based campaigns are everywhere.\n优秀的营销人员始终牢记这一重要事实，依托情感打造的营销活动随处可见。\n\nThink for a moment what is actually being sold in most marketing campaigns.\n不妨想一想大多数营销活动中真正售卖的是什么。\n\nLuxury goods target our feelings of self-worth, acceptance, and status in the world.\n奢侈品瞄准的是我们对自我价值、被接纳感以及社会地位的感受。\n\nCommunication devices excite us by offering a connection to friends, family, and a broader network of people.\n通信设备通过提供与朋友、家人以及更广泛人际网络的连接来激发我们的热情。\n\nAnd many other products, such as rings, target emotions related to love and relationships.\n而许多其他产品，比如戒指，则瞄准与爱情和人际关系相关的情感。\n\nAs marketers, we should focus on the features of the product.\n作为营销人员，我们应该关注产品的特性。\n\nBut we must also sell the lifestyle and the feeling.\n但我们也必须推销生活方式和情感体验。\n\nThe key is to highlight the emotional response a consumer will have by using the product.\n关键在于突出消费者在使用该产品时会产生的情感反应。\n\nTo achieve the highest emotional response, we should target our consumer through many different senses.\n为了获得最强的情感反应，我们应通过多种不同的感官来触动消费者。\n\nA lot of what drives consumers is subconscious behaviour.\n许多驱动消费者的都是潜意识行为。\n\nBut this isn''t a bad thing.\n但这并不是坏事。\n\nThere''s nothing manipulative about helping consumers achieve desired states of emotion.\n帮助消费者达到他们期望的情感状态，算不上刻意操控人心。\n\nQuestions 16 to 18 are based on the passage you have just heard.\n请根据你刚听到的短文回答第16至18题。\n\n16. What does research indicate about many consumers when they evaluate a purchase?\n16. 研究表明许多消费者在评估购买时实际情况如何？\n\n17. What do good marketers keep in mind all the time?\n17. 优秀的营销人员始终牢记什么？\n\n18. What should marketers do besides stressing the features of a product?\n18. 除了强调产品特性之外，营销人员还应该做些什么？', 111, 1426.55, 866.90, 977.62, 1025.48, 1046.40, 950.32, 956.38, 'cet4-2026-06-1-g06', 'PASSAGE', '[14:26.90]Passage One｜短文一\n[14:28.86]Contrary to popular belief, consumers aren''t as smart as they like to believe.｜与大众普遍认知相反，消费者并没有他们自以为的那么聪明。\n[14:34.38]Many consumers report comparing multiple competing brands and prices when evaluating a purchase.｜许多消费者声称在评估购买时会对比多家互相竞争的品牌与价格。\n[14:41.04]However, research indicates that this is not actually the case.｜然而，研究表明事实并非如此。\n[14:46.74]What consumers really think or feel often contradicts what they say.｜消费者真实的想法与感受往往和他们所说的相矛盾。\n[14:51.94]A big reason is that they are driven by unconscious urges, the biggest of which is emotion.｜一个主要原因是他们会被无意识的冲动所驱使，其中影响最大的就是情感。\n[14:58.78]Emotion is what really drives the purchasing behaviours and also decision-making in general.｜情感才是真正推动购买行为乃至所有决策的因素。\n[15:05.84]Good marketers keep in mind this important fact all the time, and examples of emotion-based campaigns are everywhere.｜优秀的营销人员始终牢记这一重要事实，依托情感打造的营销活动随处可见。\n[15:14.68]Think for a moment what is actually being sold in most marketing campaigns.｜不妨想一想大多数营销活动中真正售卖的是什么。\n[15:19.68]Luxury goods target our feelings of self-worth, acceptance, and status in the world.｜奢侈品瞄准的是我们对自我价值、被接纳感以及社会地位的感受。\n[15:26.28]Communication devices excite us by offering a connection to friends, family, and a broader network of people.｜通信设备通过提供与朋友、家人以及更广泛人际网络的连接来激发我们的热情。\n[15:34.36]And many other products, such as rings, target emotions related to love and relationships.｜而许多其他产品，比如戒指，则瞄准与爱情和人际关系相关的情感。\n[15:41.56]As marketers, we should focus on the features of the product.｜作为营销人员，我们应该关注产品的特性。\n[15:45.76]But we must also sell the lifestyle and the feeling.｜但我们也必须推销生活方式和情感体验。\n[15:50.32]The key is to highlight the emotional response a consumer will have by using the product.｜关键在于突出消费者在使用该产品时会产生的情感反应。\n[15:56.68]To achieve the highest emotional response, we should target our consumer through many different senses.｜为了获得最强的情感反应，我们应通过多种不同的感官来触动消费者。\n[16:03.68]A lot of what drives consumers is subconscious behaviour.｜许多驱动消费者的都是潜意识行为。\n[16:08.24]But this isn''t a bad thing.｜但这并不是坏事。\n[16:10.32]There''s nothing manipulative about helping consumers achieve desired states of emotion.｜帮助消费者达到他们期望的情感状态，算不上刻意操控人心。\n[16:17.62]Questions 16 to 18 are based on the passage you have just heard.｜请根据你刚听到的短文回答第16至18题。\n[16:22.98]16. What does research indicate about many consumers when they evaluate a purchase?｜16. 研究表明许多消费者在评估购买时实际情况如何？\n[16:45.46]17. What do good marketers keep in mind all the time?｜17. 优秀的营销人员始终牢记什么？\n[17:05.48]18. What should marketers do besides stressing the features of a product?｜18. 除了强调产品特性之外，营销人员还应该做些什么？', NOW(), NOW()
