  @a_cet4_2026_06_1_20, '/audio/exams/listening-cet4-2026-06-1.mp3', 'Passage Two\n短文二\n\nPlastics have for years been used to make nearly everything that surrounds us.\n多年来，塑料被用来制造我们周围几乎所有的东西。\n\nBut along the way, they escaped the confines of packaging and objects and settled in the environment, the food we eat and the air we breathe.\n但在这个过程中，塑料脱离了包装和物体的限制，积聚在环境中、我们吃的食物里以及我们呼吸的空气中。\n\nAmericans are consuming and breathing in a lot of plastic.\n美国人正在摄入和吸入大量塑料。\n\nBased on available data, Americans take in an estimated 74,000 to 121,000 microplastic particles every year.\n根据现有数据，美国人每年大约会摄入7.4万至12.1万个微塑料颗粒。\n\nHowever, scientists believe the true number is probably much higher, because for some likely sources of microplastics, there was no strong data available.\n然而，科学家认为真实的数字可能要高得多，因为对于一些可能的微塑料来源，目前还没有可靠的数据。\n\nMicroplastics get into food and air in several ways.\n微塑料通过多种途径进入食物和空气。\n\nMany start off as part of larger plastic objects, which over time fragment into smaller and smaller pieces until they become tiny: 5 millimetres or less in diameter.\n许多微塑料最初是较大塑料物体的一部分，随着时间推移，它们不断分解成越来越小的碎片，最终变成直径为5毫米或更小的微粒。\n\nThey are breathed in or consumed by animals that then become our food.\n它们被动物吸入或摄入，而这些动物随后成为我们的食物。\n\nThe particles float through the air until people breathe them in.\n这些颗粒飘浮在空气中，直到被人吸入。\n\nThey also settle on the food that people eat.\n它们也会飘落到人们吃的食物上。\n\nData shows that for Americans, air, bottled water and seafood were the biggest sources for breathed in or consumed microplastics.\n数据显示，对美国人而言，空气、瓶装水和海鲜是吸入或摄入微塑料的最大来源。\n\nAdded sugars accounted for less, and salts, tap water and beer contributed minimal amounts.\n添加糖占比较少，而食盐、自来水和啤酒的贡献量微乎其微。\n\nThese estimates are conservative.\n这些估算结果比较保守。\n\nThe included foods only make up about 15% of the average American diet.\n统计所包含的食物仅占美国人日常饮食的15%。\n\nIt''s not yet known how much plastic is contained in the remaining 85% of the typical diet.\n目前尚不清楚典型饮食中剩余85%的食物含有多少塑料。\n\nQuestions 19 to 21 are based on the passage you have just heard.\n请根据你刚听到的短文回答第19至21题。\n\n19. What does the passage say about Americans?\n19. 关于美国人，短文说了什么？\n\n20. What counted as the biggest sources for Americans breathing in or consuming microplastics?\n20. 美国人吸入或摄入微塑料的最大来源是什么？\n\n21. What does the passage say is still unknown?\n21. 短文提到什么仍然是未知的？', 107, 1426.55, 1046.70, 1153.80, 1178.76, 1198.76, 1119.45, 1129.30, 'cet4-2026-06-1-g07', 'PASSAGE', '[17:26.70]Passage Two｜短文二\n[17:28.66]Plastics have for years been used to make nearly everything that surrounds us.｜多年来，塑料被用来制造我们周围几乎所有的东西。\n[17:34.02]But along the way, they escaped the confines of packaging and objects and settled in the environment, the food we eat and the air we breathe.｜但在这个过程中，塑料脱离了包装和物体的限制，积聚在环境中、我们吃的食物里以及我们呼吸的空气中。\n[17:43.82]Americans are consuming and breathing in a lot of plastic.｜美国人正在摄入和吸入大量塑料。\n[17:48.05]Based on available data, Americans take in an estimated 74,000 to 121,000 microplastic particles every year.｜根据现有数据，美国人每年大约会摄入7.4万至12.1万个微塑料颗粒。\n[17:58.47]However, scientists believe the true number is probably much higher, because for some likely sources of microplastics, there was no strong data available.｜然而，科学家认为真实的数字可能要高得多，因为对于一些可能的微塑料来源，目前还没有可靠的数据。\n[18:09.06]Microplastics get into food and air in several ways.｜微塑料通过多种途径进入食物和空气。\n[18:13.84]Many start off as part of larger plastic objects, which over time fragment into smaller and smaller pieces until they become tiny: 5 millimetres or less in diameter.｜许多微塑料最初是较大塑料物体的一部分，随着时间推移，它们不断分解成越来越小的碎片，最终变成直径为5毫米或更小的微粒。\n[18:26.44]They are breathed in or consumed by animals that then become our food.｜它们被动物吸入或摄入，而这些动物随后成为我们的食物。\n[18:31.64]The particles float through the air until people breathe them in.｜这些颗粒飘浮在空气中，直到被人吸入。\n[18:36.24]They also settle on the food that people eat.｜它们也会飘落到人们吃的食物上。\n[18:39.45]Data shows that for Americans, air, bottled water and seafood were the biggest sources for breathed in or consumed microplastics.｜数据显示，对美国人而言，空气、瓶装水和海鲜是吸入或摄入微塑料的最大来源。\n[18:49.60]Added sugars accounted for less, and salts, tap water and beer contributed minimal amounts.｜添加糖占比较少，而食盐、自来水和啤酒的贡献量微乎其微。\n[18:58.00]These estimates are conservative.｜这些估算结果比较保守。\n[19:00.52]The included foods only make up about 15% of the average American diet.｜统计所包含的食物仅占美国人日常饮食的15%。\n[19:06.00]It''s not yet known how much plastic is contained in the remaining 85% of the typical diet.｜目前尚不清楚典型饮食中剩余85%的食物含有多少塑料。\n[19:13.80]Questions 19 to 21 are based on the passage you have just heard.｜请根据你刚听到的短文回答第19至21题。\n[19:19.04]19. What does the passage say about Americans?｜19. 关于美国人，短文说了什么？\n[19:38.76]20. What counted as the biggest sources for Americans breathing in or consuming microplastics?｜20. 美国人吸入或摄入微塑料的最大来源是什么？\n[20:02.34]21. What does the passage say is still unknown?｜21. 短文提到什么仍然是未知的？', NOW(), NOW()
