SELECT
  @a_cet4_2026_06_1_22, '/audio/exams/listening-cet4-2026-06-1.mp3', 'Passage Three\n短文三\n\nPeople looking to stay well as they age may want to adopt a pet animal, according to new data from the University of Michigan National Poll on Healthy Aging.\n根据密歇根大学健康老龄化全国民意调查的最新数据，希望在变老过程中保持健康的人或许可以考虑养一只宠物。\n\nFor the survey, researchers polled about 2,000 U.S. adults from ages 50 to 80.\n在这项调查中，研究人员对约2,000名年龄在50至80岁的美国成年人进行了民意调查。\n\nFifty-five percent said they owned at least one pet.\n55%的受访者表示他们至少养了一只宠物。\n\nDogs were the most common pet, followed by cats.\n狗是最常见的宠物，其次是猫。\n\nBut whatever the type of animal, the vast majority of owners said their pets boosted their mental and physical health.\n但无论养的是哪种宠物，绝大多数宠物主人都表示宠物改善了他们的身心健康。\n\nNearly 90% of older pet owners said their animals helped them enjoy life and feel loved.\n近90%的老年宠物主人表示，他们的宠物帮助他们享受生活并感受到被爱。\n\nRoughly 80% said their pets reduced stress.\n约80%的人说宠物减轻了他们的压力。\n\nAnd almost three-quarters said their pets provided a sense of purpose.\n而近四分之三的人说宠物给了他们一种目标感。\n\nHowever, people did report a few disadvantages to pet ownership.\n不过，人们确实报告了养宠物的一些弊端。\n\nThese included difficulty traveling and financial strains.\n这些弊端包括出行不便和经济负担。\n\nSix percent of pet owners said they''d fallen or injured themselves as a result of having a pet.\n6%的宠物主人表示，他们曾因养宠物而摔倒或受伤。\n\nStill, plenty of research has shown that just about anyone can benefit from their pet, since animals can lower stress, reduce symptoms of depression and anxiety, and encourage physical activity.\n尽管如此，大量研究已表明，几乎每个人都能从宠物身上受益，因为动物能够减轻压力、减少抑郁和焦虑症状，并促进身体活动。\n\nThe new poll suggests that pet ownership may be especially beneficial for older adults, given how common loneliness and social isolation are within this age group.\n这项新的民意调查表明，对老年人来说，养宠物的益处可能尤为突出，因为孤独感和社会孤立感在这个年龄段非常普遍。\n\nHuman social support comes with a host of health benefits—less stress, lower rates of long-term disease, and more—and research shows that interacting with pets can bring many of the same benefits.\n人类社会支持能带来诸多健康益处，例如减轻压力、降低长期疾病发生率等，而且研究表明，与宠物互动也能带来许多相同的益处。\n\nQuestions 22 to 25 are based on the passage you have just heard.\n请根据你刚听到的短文回答第22至25题。\n\n22. What did over half of the respondents say in the survey?\n22. 在调查中，超过一半的受访者说了什么？\n\n23. What did most older pet owners in the survey say their pets provided?\n23. 在调查中，大多数老年宠物主人说他们的宠物给他们带来了什么？\n\n24. What does the passage say people did report in the survey?\n24. 短文中提到在调查中，人们确实报告了什么？\n\n25. What does research show interacting with pets can do?\n25. 研究表明与宠物互动有什么作用？', 112, 1426.55, 1222.54, 1334.34, 1339.86, 1360.32, 1243.58, 1247.34, 'cet4-2026-06-1-g08', 'PASSAGE', '[20:22.54]Passage Three｜短文三\n[20:24.62]People looking to stay well as they age may want to adopt a pet animal, according to new data from the University of Michigan National Poll on Healthy Aging.｜根据密歇根大学健康老龄化全国民意调查的最新数据，希望在变老过程中保持健康的人或许可以考虑养一只宠物。\n[20:36.14]For the survey, researchers polled about 2,000 U.S. adults from ages 50 to 80.｜在这项调查中，研究人员对约2,000名年龄在50至80岁的美国成年人进行了民意调查。\n[20:43.58]Fifty-five percent said they owned at least one pet.｜55%的受访者表示他们至少养了一只宠物。\n[20:47.64]Dogs were the most common pet, followed by cats.｜狗是最常见的宠物，其次是猫。\n[20:51.82]But whatever the type of animal, the vast majority of owners said their pets boosted their mental and physical health.｜但无论养的是哪种宠物，绝大多数宠物主人都表示宠物改善了他们的身心健康。\n[20:59.45]Nearly 90% of older pet owners said their animals helped them enjoy life and feel loved.｜近90%的老年宠物主人表示，他们的宠物帮助他们享受生活并感受到被爱。\n[21:06.69]Roughly 80% said their pets reduced stress.｜约80%的人说宠物减轻了他们的压力。\n[21:11.24]And almost three-quarters said their pets provided a sense of purpose.｜而近四分之三的人说宠物给了他们一种目标感。\n[21:15.74]However, people did report a few disadvantages to pet ownership.｜不过，人们确实报告了养宠物的一些弊端。\n[21:21.20]These included difficulty traveling and financial strains.｜这些弊端包括出行不便和经济负担。\n[21:25.56]Six percent of pet owners said they''d fallen or injured themselves as a result of having a pet.｜6%的宠物主人表示，他们曾因养宠物而摔倒或受伤。\n[21:31.92]Still, plenty of research has shown that just about anyone can benefit from their pet, since animals can lower stress, reduce symptoms of depression and anxiety, and encourage physical activity.｜尽管如此，大量研究已表明，几乎每个人都能从宠物身上受益，因为动物能够减轻压力、减少抑郁和焦虑症状，并促进身体活动。\n[21:46.04]The new poll suggests that pet ownership may be especially beneficial for older adults, given how common loneliness and social isolation are within this age group.｜这项新的民意调查表明，对老年人来说，养宠物的益处可能尤为突出，因为孤独感和社会孤立感在这个年龄段非常普遍。\n[21:58.32]Human social support comes with a host of health benefits—less stress, lower rates of long-term disease, and more—and research shows that interacting with pets can bring many of the same benefits.｜人类社会支持能带来诸多健康益处，例如减轻压力、降低长期疾病发生率等，而且研究表明，与宠物互动也能带来许多相同的益处。\n[22:14.34]Questions 22 to 25 are based on the passage you have just heard.｜请根据你刚听到的短文回答第22至25题。\n[22:19.86]22. What did over half of the respondents say in the survey?｜22. 在调查中，超过一半的受访者说了什么？\n[22:40.62]23. What did most older pet owners in the survey say their pets provided?｜23. 在调查中，大多数老年宠物主人说他们的宠物给他们带来了什么？\n[23:02.24]24. What does the passage say people did report in the survey?｜24. 短文中提到在调查中，人们确实报告了什么？\n[23:22.92]25. What does research show interacting with pets can do?｜25. 研究表明与宠物互动有什么作用？', NOW(), NOW()
