  @a_cet4_2026_06_2_08, '/audio/exams/listening-cet4-2026-06-2.mp3', 'Conversation One\n对话一\n\nM: Good afternoon, Theatre Bookings International.\n男：下午好，这里是国际剧院订票中心。\n\nMy name''s Philip.\n我是菲利普。\n\nHow may I help you today?\n今天有什么可以帮你的？\n\nW: Oh, good afternoon, my name''s Helen.\n女：哦，下午好，我是海伦。\n\nI''ve been trying to book tickets for the musical Cats in London on the evening of May 28th, but I can''t get the computer to accept my card payment.\n我一直在尝试预订5月28日晚上在伦敦上演的音乐剧《猫》的票，但电脑不接受我的银行卡付款。\n\nI''ve tried three times, but it just doesn''t want to take it.\n我试了三次，但它就是不行。\n\nM: That''s okay, madam.\n男：没关系，女士。\n\nI can book it and take the payment over the phone if that''s not a problem for you.\n如果你不介意的话，我可以通过电话帮你订票并完成付款。\n\nW: That would be wonderful.\n女：那太好了。\n\nI''m not very good with computers.\n我不太会操作电脑。\n\nMy husband usually does all of these things, but he is in Italy on a business trip until next Thursday.\n这些事通常是我丈夫做的，但他去意大利出差了，要到下周四才回来。\n\nAnd I know how quickly these things can sell out.\n而且我知道这些票很快就会售罄。\n\nM: They do indeed, madam.\n男：确实如此，女士。\n\nFirstly, can you confirm that it''s the performance of Cats on May 28th at the Lion Theatre in London at 7:30 p.m.?\n首先，请你确认一下，是5月28日晚上7点30分在伦敦狮子剧院上演的《猫》吗？\n\nW: Yes, that''s the one.\n女：没错，就是那场。\n\nAnd I will need two tickets, please, not too close to the front.\n我需要两张票，位置不要太靠前。\n\nM: Actually, all the tickets at the front are already sold out anyway.\n男：其实前排的票都已经卖完了。\n\nBut I can offer you two upstairs near the middle.\n不过我可以给你订两张楼上靠近中间的座位。\n\nI assume that you don''t want to be too high up.\n我想你应该不想坐得太高。\n\nW: Oh, my goodness, no.\n女：哦，天哪，当然不想。\n\nI''m scared of heights, and you can never see anything if you are too high up anyway.\n我恐高，而且坐太高的话什么也看不见。\n\nM: No problem, madam.\n男：没问题，女士。\n\nI''ll reserve those for you now.\n我现在就为你预订这两张票。\n\nAnd all we need after that is the details of your card number and your full name.\n接下来只需要你提供银行卡号和全名。\n\nAnd then we are done.\n然后就办理完毕了。\n\nQuestions 8 to 11 are based on the conversation you have just heard.\n请根据你刚听到的对话回答第8至11题。\n\n8. Why does the woman call the man?\n8. 女士为什么给男士打电话？\n\n9. What do we learn about the woman''s husband?\n9. 关于女士的丈夫，我们了解到什么？\n\n10. What does the man say about the tickets at the front?\n10. 关于前排的票，男士说了什么？\n\n11. What does the woman say she is scared of?\n11. 女士说自己害怕什么？', 89, 1387.37, 442.39, 531.28, 536.24, 554.84, 454.28, 464.10, 'cet4-2026-06-2-g04', 'LONG_DIALOGUE', '[07:22.39]Conversation One｜对话一\n[07:25.04]M: Good afternoon, Theatre Bookings International.｜男：下午好，这里是国际剧院订票中心。\n[07:28.20]My name''s Philip.｜我是菲利普。\n[07:29.44]How may I help you today?｜今天有什么可以帮你的？\n[07:31.12]W: Oh, good afternoon, my name''s Helen.｜女：哦，下午好，我是海伦。\n[07:34.28]I''ve been trying to book tickets for the musical Cats in London on the evening of May 28th, but I can''t get the computer to accept my card payment.｜我一直在尝试预订5月28日晚上在伦敦上演的音乐剧《猫》的票，但电脑不接受我的银行卡付款。\n[07:44.40]I''ve tried three times, but it just doesn''t want to take it.｜我试了三次，但它就是不行。\n[07:48.20]M: That''s okay, madam.｜男：没关系，女士。\n[07:49.60]I can book it and take the payment over the phone if that''s not a problem for you.｜如果你不介意的话，我可以通过电话帮你订票并完成付款。\n[07:54.08]W: That would be wonderful.｜女：那太好了。\n[07:55.56]I''m not very good with computers.｜我不太会操作电脑。\n[07:57.92]My husband usually does all of these things, but he is in Italy on a business trip until next Thursday.｜这些事通常是我丈夫做的，但他去意大利出差了，要到下周四才回来。\n[08:04.64]And I know how quickly these things can sell out.｜而且我知道这些票很快就会售罄。\n[08:07.52]M: They do indeed, madam.｜男：确实如此，女士。\n[08:09.28]Firstly, can you confirm that it''s the performance of Cats on May 28th at the Lion Theatre in London at 7:30 p.m.?｜首先，请你确认一下，是5月28日晚上7点30分在伦敦狮子剧院上演的《猫》吗？\n[08:17.92]W: Yes, that''s the one.｜女：没错，就是那场。\n[08:19.56]And I will need two tickets, please, not too close to the front.｜我需要两张票，位置不要太靠前。\n[08:23.34]M: Actually, all the tickets at the front are already sold out anyway.｜男：其实前排的票都已经卖完了。\n[08:27.76]But I can offer you two upstairs near the middle.｜不过我可以给你订两张楼上靠近中间的座位。\n[08:31.20]I assume that you don''t want to be too high up.｜我想你应该不想坐得太高。\n[08:33.80]W: Oh, my goodness, no.｜女：哦，天哪，当然不想。\n[08:35.24]I''m scared of heights, and you can never see anything if you are too high up anyway.｜我恐高，而且坐太高的话什么也看不见。\n[08:40.68]M: No problem, madam.｜男：没问题，女士。\n[08:42.16]I''ll reserve those for you now.｜我现在就为你预订这两张票。\n[08:44.00]And all we need after that is the details of your card number and your full name.｜接下来只需要你提供银行卡号和全名。\n[08:48.96]And then we are done.｜然后就办理完毕了。\n[08:51.28]Questions 8 to 11 are based on the conversation you have just heard.｜请根据你刚听到的对话回答第8至11题。\n[08:56.24]8. Why does the woman call the man?｜8. 女士为什么给男士打电话？\n[09:15.14]9. What do we learn about the woman''s husband?｜9. 关于女士的丈夫，我们了解到什么？\n[09:34.56]10. What does the man say about the tickets at the front?｜10. 关于前排的票，男士说了什么？\n[09:54.50]11. What does the woman say she is scared of?｜11. 女士说自己害怕什么？', NOW(), NOW()
