SELECT
  @a_cet4_2026_06_2_12, '/audio/exams/listening-cet4-2026-06-2.mp3', 'Conversation Two\n对话二\n\nW: Hi, John.\n女：嗨，约翰。\n\nWhy haven''t you answered my text messages lately?\n你最近为什么不回复我的短信？\n\nM: Oh, I didn''t know you had sent any.\n男：噢，我不知道你发过消息。\n\nI turned off my phone almost a week ago and haven''t turned it back on since then.\n我差不多一周前就把手机关机了，之后一直没再开机。\n\nW: Why would you do something like that when our phones make our lives so much more convenient?\n女：手机给我们的生活带来了那么多便利，你为什么还要这样做？\n\nM: Well, I downloaded an app that recorded how much time I spent on my phone.\n男：嗯，我下载了一个可以统计手机使用时长的应用。\n\nAnd I was shocked to realize I was using my phone an average of 8 hours a day.\n然后我震惊地意识到，我平均每天要用8个小时的手机。\n\nAnd on my worst day, I used it for 12 hours.\n用得最多的一天达到了12个小时。\n\nW: Were you addicted to mobile phone games?\n女：你是沉迷手机游戏吗？\n\nI had a friend who was, and he sometimes played them all day and into the night.\n我有个朋友就是，他有时候会从白天玩到深夜。\n\nM: No, my problem was I was spending too much time on social media, messaging friends and commenting on other people''s posts.\n男：不是，我的问题是在社交媒体上花了太多时间，给朋友发消息，评论别人的帖子。\n\nW: I do all of that too, as well as shopping online and paying for everything with my phone.\n女：这些我也都会做，我还用手机网购并支付所有费用。\n\nThat is really why I don''t see how anyone could live without a mobile phone.\n所以我实在无法想象有人离了手机怎么生活。\n\nHow do you buy things or communicate with your friends?\n那你现在怎么购物或者联系朋友？\n\nM: Since I stopped using my phone, I go to physical stores and pay in cash.\n男：自从我不再用手机之后，我就去实体店用现金付款。\n\nI''ve actually met friends for meals at cafés and restaurants.\n我其实还会和朋友在咖啡馆或餐厅见面吃饭。\n\nW: That''s great for you.\n女：对你来说这样挺好。\n\nBut my friends and family don''t live in this city, so we can''t see each other often, and I don''t have any choice but to chat with them online.\n但我的朋友和家人都不在这个城市，所以我们没法经常见面，我别无选择，只能在网上和他们聊天。\n\nQuestions 12 to 15 are based on the conversation you have just heard.\n请根据你刚听到的对话回答第12至15题。\n\n12. Why hasn''t the man answered the woman''s text messages lately?\n12. 男士最近为什么没有回复女士的短信？\n\n13. What was the man shocked to realize after he downloaded the app?\n13. 男士下载应用后震惊地意识到什么？\n\n14. What did the man spend much time doing with his phone?\n14. 男士花大量时间用手机做什么？\n\n15. Why does the woman say she has to use her mobile phone?\n15. 女士为什么说自己必须使用手机？', 90, 1387.37, 614.12, 704.00, 709.56, 730.02, 624.36, 629.46, 'cet4-2026-06-2-g05', 'LONG_DIALOGUE', '[10:14.12]Conversation Two｜对话二\n[10:16.84]W: Hi, John.｜女：嗨，约翰。\n[10:17.96]Why haven''t you answered my text messages lately?｜你最近为什么不回复我的短信？\n[10:21.04]M: Oh, I didn''t know you had sent any.｜男：噢，我不知道你发过消息。\n[10:24.36]I turned off my phone almost a week ago and haven''t turned it back on since then.｜我差不多一周前就把手机关机了，之后一直没再开机。\n[10:29.76]W: Why would you do something like that when our phones make our lives so much more convenient?｜女：手机给我们的生活带来了那么多便利，你为什么还要这样做？\n[10:35.68]M: Well, I downloaded an app that recorded how much time I spent on my phone.｜男：嗯，我下载了一个可以统计手机使用时长的应用。\n[10:41.44]And I was shocked to realize I was using my phone an average of 8 hours a day.｜然后我震惊地意识到，我平均每天要用8个小时的手机。\n[10:47.52]And on my worst day, I used it for 12 hours.｜用得最多的一天达到了12个小时。\n[10:51.84]W: Were you addicted to mobile phone games?｜女：你是沉迷手机游戏吗？\n[10:54.96]I had a friend who was, and he sometimes played them all day and into the night.｜我有个朋友就是，他有时候会从白天玩到深夜。\n[11:00.44]M: No, my problem was I was spending too much time on social media, messaging friends and commenting on other people''s posts.｜男：不是，我的问题是在社交媒体上花了太多时间，给朋友发消息，评论别人的帖子。\n[11:09.16]W: I do all of that too, as well as shopping online and paying for everything with my phone.｜女：这些我也都会做，我还用手机网购并支付所有费用。\n[11:15.52]That is really why I don''t see how anyone could live without a mobile phone.｜所以我实在无法想象有人离了手机怎么生活。\n[11:20.28]How do you buy things or communicate with your friends?｜那你现在怎么购物或者联系朋友？\n[11:24.20]M: Since I stopped using my phone, I go to physical stores and pay in cash.｜男：自从我不再用手机之后，我就去实体店用现金付款。\n[11:29.20]I''ve actually met friends for meals at cafés and restaurants.｜我其实还会和朋友在咖啡馆或餐厅见面吃饭。\n[11:33.16]W: That''s great for you.｜女：对你来说这样挺好。\n[11:34.72]But my friends and family don''t live in this city, so we can''t see each other often, and I don''t have any choice but to chat with them online.｜但我的朋友和家人都不在这个城市，所以我们没法经常见面，我别无选择，只能在网上和他们聊天。\n[11:44.00]Questions 12 to 15 are based on the conversation you have just heard.｜请根据你刚听到的对话回答第12至15题。\n[11:49.56]12. Why hasn''t the man answered the woman''s text messages lately?｜12. 男士最近为什么没有回复女士的短信？\n[12:10.32]13. What was the man shocked to realize after he downloaded the app?｜13. 男士下载应用后震惊地意识到什么？\n[12:31.86]14. What did the man spend much time doing with his phone?｜14. 男士花大量时间用手机做什么？\n[12:52.44]15. Why does the woman say she has to use her mobile phone?｜15. 女士为什么说自己必须使用手机？', NOW(), NOW()
WHERE @a_cet4_2026_06_2_12 IS NOT NULL
ON DUPLICATE KEY UPDATE
  `audio_url` = VALUES(`audio_url`),
  `transcript` = VALUES(`transcript`),
  `duration_seconds` = VALUES(`duration_seconds`),
  `audio_total_seconds` = VALUES(`audio_total_seconds`),
  `audio_start_seconds` = VALUES(`audio_start_seconds`),
  `audio_end_seconds` = VALUES(`audio_end_seconds`),
