%，而留在原岗位的人加薪5.4%。\n[15:08.32]That suggests the demand for workers has reached, or is at least nearing, its peak.｜这表明对劳动力的需求已经到达峰值，或至少接近峰值。\n[15:15.38]The labor market is likely cooling, because even a shortage of workers isn''t overcoming the historic imbalance between employers and employees in the U.S.｜劳动力市场可能正在降温，因为即便劳动力短缺也无法扭转美国雇主与雇员之间长期存在的不平衡。\n[15:27.02]The volume of income that workers take home as a proportion of what the U.S. economy produces is still falling.｜雇员实际到手收入在美国经济总产出中所占的比例仍在下滑。\n[15:35.90]Questions 16 to 18 are based on the passage you have just heard.｜请根据你刚听到的短文回答第16至18题。\n[15:41.30]16. What does the passage say about the gap in wage gains between job switchers and those who stay in their jobs?｜16. 关于跳槽的人与留在原岗位的人之间的薪资涨幅差距，短文说了什么？\n[16:05.30]17. What do we learn about wage growth now?｜17. 关于如今薪资增长的情况，我们了解到什么？\n[16:25.50]18. What is the labor market likely doing, according to the passage?｜18. 根据短文，劳动力市场可能正在发生什么？', NOW(), NOW()
