  (`question_id`, `audio_url`, `transcript`, `duration_seconds`, `audio_total_seconds`, `audio_start_seconds`, `audio_end_seconds`, `question_start_seconds`, `question_end_seconds`, `answer_start_seconds`, `answer_end_seconds`, `group_key`, `listening_type`, `lrc_content`, `created_at`, `updated_at`)
SELECT
  @a_cet4_2026_06_2_19, '/audio/exams/listening-cet4-2026-06-2.mp3', 'Passage Two\n短文二\n\nHighly processed foods, the kinds made with lots of sugar, fat and salt, make up as much as 60% of the average American diet.\n高度加工食品，也就是添加了大量糖、脂肪和盐的食品，占美国人日常饮食的60%。\n\nBut a new study shows that their low price and convenience come at a cost to health.\n但一项新的研究表明，高度加工食品低廉的价格与便捷性是以损害健康为代价的。\n\nThe study found that when people ate a highly processed diet, they consumed about 500 more calories per day than they did when they ate a less processed diet.\n研究发现，人们吃高度加工食品时，每天摄入的热量比吃较少加工的食品多出约500卡路里。\n\nThey also gained 2 pounds over 2 weeks, even though both diets had the same amounts of nutrients, like sugar, fat, fiber and salt.\n即便两种饮食中糖、脂肪、纤维、盐分等营养物质的含量一致，吃高度加工食品的人在2周内还是增重了2磅。\n\nIt wasn''t a shock to find highly processed foods weren''t healthy.\n高度加工食品不健康这一点并不令人意外。\n\nOther research has linked them to a higher risk of cancer and obesity.\n其他研究已将这类食品与更高的癌症与肥胖患病风险联系起来。\n\nWhat was unexpected was that sugar, fat and salt didn''t seem to be what caused people to overeat.\n出乎意料的是，糖、脂肪和盐似乎并非导致人们过量进食的原因。\n\nThis is the first trial that demonstrates that there is something about highly processed foods, independent of those nutrients, that causes people to overeat.\n这项试验首次证明，高度加工食品中存在某种独立于这些营养物质之外的因素，会促使人们过量进食。\n\nThe study also found that when eating a highly processed diet, people ate faster.\n研究还发现，人们吃高度加工食品时会吃得更快。\n\nThis could be one reason why they gained more weight.\n这可能是他们体重增加更多的一个原因。\n\nHighly processed food tends to be softer, which makes it easier to chew and swallow.\n高度加工食品通常质地更松软，更容易咀嚼和吞咽。\n\nOne theory is that if you''re eating more quickly, you''re not giving your gut enough time to signal to your brain that you''ve had enough calories and that you''re full.\n有一种理论认为，如果你吃得太快，肠道就没有足够的时间向大脑传递已经摄入足够热量、感到饱腹的信号。\n\nBy the time the brain gets that signal, you''ve already overeaten.\n等大脑收到这一信号时，你其实已经吃得过多了。\n\nQuestions 19 to 21 are based on the passage you have just heard.\n请根据你刚听到的短文回答第19至21题。\n\n19. What does a new study show about highly processed foods?\n19. 关于高度加工食品，一项新的研究表明了什么？\n\n20. What are highly processed foods linked to, according to other research?\n20. 根据其他研究，高度加工食品和什么有联系？\n\n21. What do people tend to do when eating highly processed foods?\n21. 人们在吃高度加工食品时往往会做什么？', 102, 1387.37, 1006.84, 1108.40, 1114.12, 1134.68, 1019.24, 1025.54, 'cet4-2026-06-2-g07', 'PASSAGE', '[16:46.84]Passage Two｜短文二\n[16:49.04]Highly processed foods, the kinds made with lots of sugar, fat and salt, make up as much as 60% of the average American diet.｜高度加工食品，也就是添加了大量糖、脂肪和盐的食品，占美国人日常饮食的60%。\n[16:59.24]But a new study shows that their low price and convenience come at a cost to health.｜但一项新的研究表明，高度加工食品低廉的价格与便捷性是以损害健康为代价的。\n[17:05.84]The study found that when people ate a highly processed diet, they consumed about 500 more calories per day than they did when they ate a less processed diet.｜研究发现，人们吃高度加工食品时，每天摄入的热量比吃较少加工的食品多出约500卡路里。\n[17:17.48]They also gained 2 pounds over 2 weeks, even though both diets had the same amounts of nutrients, like sugar, fat, fiber and salt.｜即便两种饮食中糖、脂肪、纤维、盐分等营养物质的含量一致，吃高度加工食品的人在2周内还是增重了2磅。\n[17:27.76]It wasn''t a shock to find highly processed foods weren''t healthy.｜高度加工食品不健康这一点并不令人意外。\n[17:31.89]Other research has linked them to a higher risk of cancer and obesity.｜其他研究已将这类食品与更高的癌症与肥胖患病风险联系起来。\n[17:37.56]What was unexpected was that sugar, fat and salt didn''t seem to be what caused people to overeat.｜出乎意料的是，糖、脂肪和盐似乎并非导致人们过量进食的原因。\n[17:45.44]This is the first trial that demonstrates that there is something about highly processed foods, independent of those nutrients, that causes people to overeat.｜这项试验首次证明，高度加工食品中存在某种独立于这些营养物质之外的因素，会促使人们过量进食。\n[17:55.56]The study also found that when eating a highly processed diet, people ate faster.｜研究还发现，人们吃高度加工食品时会吃得更快。\n[18:01.88]This could be one reason why they gained more weight.｜这可能是他们体重增加更多的一个原因。\n[18:05.52]Highly processed food tends to be softer, which makes it easier to chew and swallow.｜高度加工食品通常质地更松软，更容易咀嚼和吞咽。\n[18:11.92]One theory is that if you''re eating more quickly, you''re not giving your gut enough time to signal to your brain that you''ve had enough calories and that you''re full.｜有一种理论认为，如果你吃得太快，肠道就没有足够的时间向大脑传递已经摄入足够热量、感到饱腹的信号。\n[18:23.28]By the time the brain gets that signal, you''ve already overeaten.｜等大脑收到这一信号时，你其实已经吃得过多了。\n[18:28.40]Questions 19 to 21 are based on the passage you have just heard.｜请根据你刚听到的短文回答第19至21题。\n[18:34.12]19. What does a new study show about highly processed foods?｜19. 关于高度加工食品，一项新的研究表明了什么？\n[18:54.98]20. What are highly processed foods linked to, according to other research?｜20. 根据其他研究，高度加工食品和什么有联系？\n[19:17.10]21. What do people tend to do when eating highly processed foods?｜21. 人们在吃高度加工食品时往往会做什么？', NOW(), NOW()
