  @a_cet4_2026_06_2_24, '/audio/exams/listening-cet4-2026-06-2.mp3', 'Passage Three\n短文三\n\nWomen continue to spend more time than men taking care of children and doing chores around the house.\n女性在照顾孩子和做家务上花费的时间依旧多于男性。\n\nThis is generally attributed to backward thinking and conservative values.\n人们通常将这归因于落后的思想与保守的价值观。\n\nBut new research shows that such differences could be linked to differences in the preferences of males and females.\n但新的研究表明，这种差异可能与男性和女性的偏好差异有关。\n\nThe new study looked at how men and women were dividing work at home and why they divided it that way.\n这项新研究探究了男性和女性在家如何对家务进行分工以及为何这样分工。\n\nIn general, both men and women took more responsibility for tasks they liked.\n总体而言，男性和女性都会更多地承担自己喜欢的家务。\n\nFor example, men liked yard care and home maintenance more than women.\n例如，男性比女性更喜欢打理庭院和维修房屋。\n\nThey leaned toward wanting primary responsibility for such tasks.\n他们倾向于承担这类工作的主要责任。\n\nThe researchers stated that differences in enjoyment of household and childcare tasks matched how men and women chose to split tasks.\n研究人员表示，男女对家务及照顾孩子这些工作的喜好差异与双方选择分工的方式相契合。\n\nThe researchers added that there was not a single childcare task that men liked more than women.\n研究人员补充道，没有任何一项照顾孩子的工作是男性比女性更喜欢去做的。\n\nKeep in mind, however, that as with any research on group differences, there were large within-group differences.\n但需要记住的是，与任何关于群体差异的研究一样，群体内部也存在巨大差异。\n\nThe study''s authors concluded that differences in men''s and women''s time spent on childcare and household tasks do not mean dissatisfaction.\n该研究的作者总结称，男性和女性在照顾孩子和家务上所花时间的差异并不意味着不满。\n\nThe authors noted that previous research revealed gender differences in attitudes towards family and career.\n作者指出，先前的研究揭示了男女在家庭和职业态度上的差异。\n\nThese differences appear as early as 6 years old.\n这种差异早在6岁就已出现。\n\nGirls that age already show more interest in helping and caring for others than boys do.\n这个年龄的女孩已经比男孩表现出更多帮助和照顾他人的兴趣。\n\nAnd they already exhibit a greater orientation toward family versus career.\n而且她们已经表现得更倾向于家庭而非职业。\n\nQuestions 22 to 25 are based on the passage you have just heard.\n请根据你刚听到的短文回答第22至25题。\n\n22. How do people generally account for differences between men and women in the amount of time spent on housework?\n22. 人们通常如何解释男女在家务上所花时间的差异？\n\n23. What did men lean toward doing, according to the new study?\n23. 根据新研究，男性倾向于做什么？\n\n24. What should we keep in mind as regards any research on group differences?\n24. 关于群体差异的任何研究，我们应该记住什么？\n\n25. What did previous research reveal about gender differences in attitudes toward family and career?\n25. 关于男女在家庭和职业态度上的差异，先前的研究揭示了什么？', 108, 1387.37, 1178.16, 1285.94, 1337.30, 1357.30, 1241.76, 1249.58, 'cet4-2026-06-2-g08', 'PASSAGE', '[19:38.16]Passage Three｜短文三\n[19:40.10]Women continue to spend more time than men taking care of children and doing chores around the house.｜女性在照顾孩子和做家务上花费的时间依旧多于男性。\n[19:47.56]This is generally attributed to backward thinking and conservative values.｜人们通常将这归因于落后的思想与保守的价值观。\n[19:53.12]But new research shows that such differences could be linked to differences in the preferences of males and females.｜但新的研究表明，这种差异可能与男性和女性的偏好差异有关。\n[20:01.48]The new study looked at how men and women were dividing work at home and why they divided it that way.｜这项新研究探究了男性和女性在家如何对家务进行分工以及为何这样分工。\n[20:08.24]In general, both men and women took more responsibility for tasks they liked.｜总体而言，男性和女性都会更多地承担自己喜欢的家务。\n[20:14.60]For example, men liked yard care and home maintenance more than women.｜例如，男性比女性更喜欢打理庭院和维修房屋。\n[20:20.28]They leaned toward wanting primary responsibility for such tasks.｜他们倾向于承担这类工作的主要责任。\n[20:24.92]The researchers stated that differences in enjoyment of household and childcare tasks matched how men and women chose to split tasks.｜研究人员表示，男女对家务及照顾孩子这些工作的喜好差异与双方选择分工的方式相契合。\n[20:35.08]The researchers added that there was not a single childcare task that men liked more than women.｜研究人员补充道，没有任何一项照顾孩子的工作是男性比女性更喜欢去做的。\n[20:41.76]Keep in mind, however, that as with any research on group differences, there were large within-group differences.｜但需要记住的是，与任何关于群体差异的研究一样，群体内部也存在巨大差异。\n[20:49.88]The study''s authors concluded that differences in men''s and women''s time spent on childcare and household tasks do not mean dissatisfaction.｜该研究的作者总结称，男性和女性在照顾孩子和家务上所花时间的差异并不意味着不满。\n[21:00.80]The authors noted that previous research revealed gender differences in attitudes towards family and career.｜作者指出，先前的研究揭示了男女在家庭和职业态度上的差异。\n[21:08.72]These differences appear as early as 6 years old.｜这种差异早在6岁就已出现。\n[21:12.88]Girls that age already show more interest in helping and caring for others than boys do.｜这个年龄的女孩已经比男孩表现出更多帮助和照顾他人的兴趣。\n[21:19.52]And they already exhibit a greater orientation toward family versus career.｜而且她们已经表现得更倾向于家庭而非职业。\n[21:25.94]Questions 22 to 25 are based on the passage you have just heard.｜请根据你刚听到的短文回答第22至25题。\n[21:31.66]22. How do people generally account for differences between men and women in the amount of time spent on housework?｜22. 人们通常如何解释男女在家务上所花时间的差异？\n[21:56.04]23. What did men lean toward doing, according to the new study?｜23. 根据新研究，男性倾向于做什么？\n[22:17.30]24. What should we keep in mind as regards any research on group differences?｜24. 关于群体差异的任何研究，我们应该记住什么？\n[22:39.72]25. What did previous research reveal about gender differences in attitudes toward family and career?｜25. 关于男女在家庭和职业态度上的差异，先前的研究揭示了什么？', NOW(), NOW()
