  @a_cet6_2022_06_1_05, '/audio/exams/listening-cet6-2022-06-1.mp3', 'Conversation Two\n对话二\n\nM: In this episode of Money Talks, our guest is Molly Sanders, a university student and a successful young entrepreneur.\n男：在这一集《金钱对话》中，我们的嘉宾是莫莉·桑德斯，她是一名大学生，也是一位成功的年轻企业家。\n\nMolly, tell us about your business.\n莫莉，跟我们说说你的生意吧。\n\nW: Well, I sell specialty clothes through a website, mainly for women who have trouble finding suitable clothes in main street shops because of their height or weight.\n女：嗯，我通过网站销售特色服装，主要面向那些因为身高或体重而在商业街的店铺中找不到合适衣服的女性。\n\nBut I do some men''s clothes too.\n但我也做一些男装。\n\nM: How did you get started in this business at such a young age?\n男：你这么年轻，是怎么开始做这行的？\n\nAre you studying fashion design?\n你在学时装设计吗？\n\nW: Actually, I''m majoring in finance, but I''ve always loved clothes.\n女：事实上，我主修金融，但我一直喜欢服装。\n\nAnd I started making my own at 14.\n我14岁就开始自己做衣服了。\n\nM: Did you have any sort of training in design or sewing? Or was it a natural ability?\n男：你接受过设计或缝纫方面的培训吗？还是天生的能力？\n\nW: I''d have to say no to both.\n女：我不得不说哪一个都不是。\n\nNo one taught me to make clothes and most of the things I made at first were disasters.\n没有人教我做衣服，起初我做的大多数衣服都是灾难。\n\nM: Why did you persevere?\n男：那你为什么还坚持做呢？\n\nI think most people would give up if they kept failing, especially at that age.\n我认为，如果不断地失败，大多数人都会放弃的，尤其是在那个年龄。\n\nW: I kept on out of necessity.\n女：我之所以能坚持下去，是因为我有这方面的需要。\n\nAs you can see, I''m very tall and I couldn''t find clothes that fit me in ordinary shops.\n你也能看得出来，我很高，在普通商店里找不到适合我的衣服。\n\nSo I kept trying and developed my skills over time.\n所以我一直在努力，随着时间的推移，我的技能不断提高。\n\nM: Well, my notes say you earned $50,000 in profits last year, an extraordinary amount for a 20-year-old student.\n男：嗯，我的资料上说，你去年赚了5万美元，对一个20岁的学生来说，这是一个非常可观的数额。\n\nHow did that happen? Did you see a gap in the market and decide to fill it?\n这是怎么发生的？你是发现了市场存在缺口并决定填补这个缺口吗？\n\nW: No. When I started university, some classmates complimented my clothes.\n女：不是的，我开始上大学时，有些同学称赞我的衣服。\n\nAnd when I said I made them myself, other tall women started asking if I would make theirs.\n当我说衣服是我自己做的时，那些高个子女孩儿开始问我是否愿意给她们也做几件衣服。\n\nAnd I did. And before I knew it, I was an entrepreneur.\n我做了。在我还没意识到的时候，我已经成了一名企业家。\n\nM: So what are your plans for the future?\n男：那么你对未来有什么计划？\n\nDo you intend to open a physical store?\n您是否打算开设实体店？\n\nW: No. I''ll keep things online to keep costs down.\n女：没这个打算，我还会在网上进行以降低成本。\n\nBut I will add more clothes for children, both girls and boys, and possibly even for infants.\n但我会增加更多童装，男童女童都包括，甚至可能会做一些婴儿服装。\n\nAnd I hope to add to my range of designs for men.\n我还希望增加男士服装设计的系列。\n\nQuestions 5 to 8 are based on the conversation you have just heard.\n请根据你刚刚听到的对话回答问题5到8。\n\n5. What do we learn about the woman?\n5. 关于这位女士，我们了解到什么？\n\n6. What does the woman say about the clothes she made at first?\n6. 关于自己最初制作的衣服，这位女士说了什么？\n\n7. Why did the woman persevere in making clothes for herself?\n7. 为什么这位女士坚持为自己做衣服？\n\n8. What does the woman plan to do in the future?\n8. 这位女士打算将来做什么？\n\nSection B\nB节\n\nDirections: In this section, you will hear two passages.\n说明：在本节中，你将会听到两篇短文。', 140, 1708.83, 262.86, 402.71, 408.25, 424.13, 265.58, 276.07, 'cet6-2022-06-1-g02', 'LONG_DIALOGUE', '[04:22.86]Conversation Two｜对话二\n[04:25.58]M: In this episode of Money Talks, our guest is Molly Sanders, a university student and a successful young entrepreneur.｜男：在这一集《金钱对话》中，我们的嘉宾是莫莉·桑德斯，她是一名大学生，也是一位成功的年轻企业家。\n[04:36.37]Molly, tell us about your business.｜莫莉，跟我们说说你的生意吧。\n[04:39.05]W: Well, I sell specialty clothes through a website, mainly for women who have trouble finding suitable clothes in main street shops because of their height or weight.｜女：嗯，我通过网站销售特色服装，主要面向那些因为身高或体重而在商业街的店铺中找不到合适衣服的女性。\n[04:51.62]But I do some men''s clothes too.｜但我也做一些男装。\n[04:54.38]M: How did you get started in this business at such a young age?｜男：你这么年轻，是怎么开始做这行的？\n[04:58.96]Are you studying fashion design?｜你在学时装设计吗？\n[05:01.34]W: Actually, I''m majoring in finance, but I''ve always loved clothes.｜女：事实上，我主修金融，但我一直喜欢服装。\n[05:06.20]And I started making my own at 14.｜我14岁就开始自己做衣服了。\n[05:09.47]M: Did you have any sort of training in design or sewing? Or was it a natural ability?｜男：你接受过设计或缝纫方面的培训吗？还是天生的能力？\n[05:16.52]W: I''d have to say no to both.｜女：我不得不说哪一个都不是。\n[05:19.47]No one taught me to make clothes and most of the things I made at first were disasters.｜没有人教我做衣服，起初我做的大多数衣服都是灾难。\n[05:25.96]M: Why did you persevere?｜男：那你为什么还坚持做呢？\n[05:28.07]I think most people would give up if they kept failing, especially at that age.｜我认为，如果不断地失败，大多数人都会放弃的，尤其是在那个年龄。\n[05:33.65]W: I kept on out of necessity.｜女：我之所以能坚持下去，是因为我有这方面的需要。\n[05:36.34]As you can see, I''m very tall and I couldn''t find clothes that fit me in ordinary shops.｜你也能看得出来，我很高，在普通商店里找不到适合我的衣服。\n[05:43.43]So I kept trying and developed my skills over time.｜所以我一直在努力，随着时间的推移，我的技能不断提高。\n[05:47.74]M: Well, my notes say you earned $50,000 in profits last year, an extraordinary amount for a 20-year-old student.｜男：嗯，我的资料上说，你去年赚了5万美元，对一个20岁的学生来说，这是一个非常可观的数额。\n[05:57.31]How did that happen? Did you see a gap in the market and decide to fill it?｜这是怎么发生的？你是发现了市场存在缺口并决定填补这个缺口吗？\n[06:02.90]W: No. When I started university, some classmates complimented my clothes.｜女：不是的，我开始上大学时，有些同学称赞我的衣服。\n[06:08.71]And when I said I made them myself, other tall women started asking if I would make theirs.｜当我说衣服是我自己做的时，那些高个子女孩儿开始问我是否愿意给她们也做几件衣服。\n[06:16.20]And I did. And before I knew it, I was an entrepreneur.｜我做了。在我还没意识到的时候，我已经成了一名企业家。\n[06:20.30]M: So what are your plans for the future?｜男：那么你对未来有什么计划？\n[06:23.28]Do you intend to open a physical store?｜您是否打算开设实体店？\n[06:26.43]W: No. I''ll keep things online to keep costs down.｜女：没这个打算，我还会在网上进行以降低成本。\n[06:30.60]But I will add more clothes for children, both girls and boys, and possibly even for infants.｜但我会增加更多童装，男童女童都包括，甚至可能会做一些婴儿服装。\n[06:38.15]And I hope to add to my range of designs for men.｜我还希望增加男士服装设计的系列。\n[06:42.71]Questions 5 to 8 are based on the conversation you have just heard.｜请根据你刚刚听到的对话回答问题5到8。\n[06:48.25]5. What do we learn about the woman?｜5. 关于这位女士，我们了解到什么？\n[07:04.43]6. What does the woman say about the clothes she made at first?｜6. 关于自己最初制作的衣服，这位女士说了什么？\n[07:24.70]7. Why did the woman persevere in making clothes for herself?｜7. 为什么这位女士坚持为自己做衣服？\n[07:43.70]8. What does the woman plan to do in the future?｜8. 这位女士打算将来做什么？\n[08:01.66]Section B｜B节\n[08:03.15]Directions: In this section, you will hear two passages.｜说明：在本节中，你将会听到两篇短文。', NOW(), NOW()
