SELECT
  @a_cet6_2022_09_1_11, '/audio/exams/listening-cet6-2022-09-1.mp3', 'Passage One\n短文一\n\nA new study has found a positive correlation between how much television children watch and their parents'' stress levels.\n一项新的研究发现，孩子看电视的时间与父母的压力水平之间存在正向关联。\n\nWhy? Because the more television kids watch, the more they''re exposed to advertising.\n为什么呢？因为孩子们看的电视越多，他们接触到的广告就越多。\n\nThe more advertising they see, the more likely they are to insist on purchasing items when they go with their parents to the store.\n他们看到的广告越多，当他们和父母一起去商店时，他们就越有可能坚持购买（某些）物品。\n\nThis could generate conflict if the parents refuse.\n如果父母拒绝，就可能会产生冲突。\n\nAll that, researchers say, can contribute to parents'' overall stress levels.\n研究人员说，所有这些都会导致父母的整体压力水平上升。\n\nWhat''s the solution? Perhaps the most obvious is curtailing screen time.\n解决办法是什么呢？也许最显而易见的就是缩短看屏幕的时间。\n\nCommercial content is there for a reason—to elicit purchasing behavior.\n商业内容的存在是有原因的——为了引发购买行为。\n\nSo parents might want to shut off the TV.\n所以，父母也许想要关掉电视。\n\nResearchers concede that this is easier said than done.\n研究人员承认，这说起来容易做起来难。\n\nSo they suggest another option.\n因此，他们提出了另一种选择。\n\nParents can change how they talk to their kids about purchases.\n父母可以转换与孩子讨论购买行为的方式。\n\nThe researchers suggest that parents seek input from their children on family purchasing decisions.\n研究人员建议，父母在做出家庭购买决策时去寻求孩子的意见。\n\nThey shouldn''t try to control all purchases.\n他们不应该试图全面掌控购买行为。\n\nInstead, parents might tell their children things like “I will listen to your advice on certain products or brands.”\n相反，父母或许应该告诉孩子某些信息，比如“我会听取你对某些产品或品牌的建议。”\n\nThis type of communication, the researchers assert, can lead to children making fewer purchasing demands.\n研究人员断言，这种类型的沟通会导致儿童购买需求的减少。\n\nThat means less parents'' stress.\n这意味着父母的压力会减小。\n\nHowever, the protective effect of this kind of communication diminishes with greater exposure to television.\n然而，这种交流的保护作用会随着接触电视的增加而减弱。\n\nThis is because advertising aimed at children is especially persuasive.\n这是因为针对儿童的广告特别具有说服力。\n\nAdvertisers use an assortment of tactics, such as bright colors, happy music and celebrity endorsements to appeal to children.\n广告商使用各种各样的策略，如鲜艳的色彩、欢快的音乐和名人代言来吸引儿童。\n\nPlus, children don''t have the cognitive ability to fully understand advertising''s intent.\n此外，儿童没有充分理解广告意图的认知能力。\n\nThat makes them particularly vulnerable to advertisements.\n这使他们特别容易受到广告的影响。\n\nQuestions 9 to 11 are based on the passage you have just heard.\n请根据你刚刚听到的短文回答问题9到11。\n\n9. What has the new study found about children watching television?\n9. 关于儿童观看电视，新研究有何发现？\n\n10. What are parents advised to do to reduce the impact of TV commercials?\n10. 为了减少电视广告的影响，建议家长们该做些什么？\n\n11. What makes children particularly vulnerable to TV commercials?\n11. 是什么使儿童特别容易受到电视广告的影响？', 125, 1642.1, 476.30, 600.89, 645.16, 665.04, 589.79, 596.29, 'cet6-2022-09-1-g03', 'PASSAGE', '[07:56.30]Passage One｜短文一\n[07:57.93]A new study has found a positive correlation between how much television children watch and their parents'' stress levels.｜一项新的研究发现，孩子看电视的时间与父母的压力水平之间存在正向关联。\n[08:06.75]Why? Because the more television kids watch, the more they''re exposed to advertising.｜为什么呢？因为孩子们看的电视越多，他们接触到的广告就越多。\n[08:13.54]The more advertising they see, the more likely they are to insist on purchasing items when they go with their parents to the store.｜他们看到的广告越多，当他们和父母一起去商店时，他们就越有可能坚持购买（某些）物品。\n[08:21.90]This could generate conflict if the parents refuse.｜如果父母拒绝，就可能会产生冲突。\n[08:25.86]All that, researchers say, can contribute to parents'' overall stress levels.｜研究人员说，所有这些都会导致父母的整体压力水平上升。\n[08:31.85]What''s the solution? Perhaps the most obvious is curtailing screen time.｜解决办法是什么呢？也许最显而易见的就是缩短看屏幕的时间。\n[08:37.82]Commercial content is there for a reason—to elicit purchasing behavior.｜商业内容的存在是有原因的——为了引发购买行为。\n[08:43.34]So parents might want to shut off the TV.｜所以，父母也许想要关掉电视。\n[08:47.05]Researchers concede that this is easier said than done.｜研究人员承认，这说起来容易做起来难。\n[08:51.23]So they suggest another option.｜因此，他们提出了另一种选择。\n[08:53.50]Parents can change how they talk to their kids about purchases.｜父母可以转换与孩子讨论购买行为的方式。\n[08:58.12]The researchers suggest that parents seek input from their children on family purchasing decisions.｜研究人员建议，父母在做出家庭购买决策时去寻求孩子的意见。\n[09:05.01]They shouldn''t try to control all purchases.｜他们不应该试图全面掌控购买行为。\n[09:08.22]Instead, parents might tell their children things like “I will listen to your advice on certain products or brands.”｜相反，父母或许应该告诉孩子某些信息，比如“我会听取你对某些产品或品牌的建议。”\n[09:16.32]This type of communication, the researchers assert, can lead to children making fewer purchasing demands.｜研究人员断言，这种类型的沟通会导致儿童购买需求的减少。\n[09:23.84]That means less parents'' stress.｜这意味着父母的压力会减小。\n[09:26.53]However, the protective effect of this kind of communication diminishes with greater exposure to television.｜然而，这种交流的保护作用会随着接触电视的增加而减弱。\n[09:34.62]This is because advertising aimed at children is especially persuasive.｜这是因为针对儿童的广告特别具有说服力。\n[09:39.91]Advertisers use an assortment of tactics, such as bright colors, happy music and celebrity endorsements to appeal to children.｜广告商使用各种各样的策略，如鲜艳的色彩、欢快的音乐和名人代言来吸引儿童。\n[09:49.79]Plus, children don''t have the cognitive ability to fully understand advertising''s intent.｜此外，儿童没有充分理解广告意图的认知能力。\n[09:56.59]That makes them particularly vulnerable to advertisements.｜这使他们特别容易受到广告的影响。\n[10:00.89]Questions 9 to 11 are based on the passage you have just heard.｜请根据你刚刚听到的短文回答问题9到11。\n[10:06.48]9. What has the new study found about children watching television?｜9. 关于儿童观看电视，新研究有何发现？\n[10:24.90]10. What are parents advised to do to reduce the impact of TV commercials?｜10. 为了减少电视广告的影响，建议家长们该做些什么？\n[10:45.16]11. What makes children particularly vulnerable to TV commercials?｜11. 是什么使儿童特别容易受到电视广告的影响？', NOW(), NOW()
