SET @a_cet6_2023_06_2_02 = (SELECT `id` FROM `question_info` WHERE `external_key` = 'cet6-2023-06-2-q02' AND `module_type` = 4 LIMIT 1);
INSERT INTO `listening_audio`
  (`question_id`, `audio_url`, `transcript`, `duration_seconds`, `audio_total_seconds`, `audio_start_seconds`, `audio_end_seconds`, `question_start_seconds`, `question_end_seconds`, `answer_start_seconds`, `answer_end_seconds`, `group_key`, `listening_type`, `lrc_content`, `created_at`, `updated_at`)
SELECT
  @a_cet6_2023_06_2_02, '/audio/exams/listening-cet6-2023-06-2.mp3', 'Conversation One\n对话一\n\nM: Have you decided what you wish to study?\n男：你决定要学什么了吗？\n\nW: Yes, professor. I wish to study architecture.\n女：是的，教授。我希望学习建筑。\n\nM: Ah, that''s a wonderful profession.\n男：啊，这是一个很棒的专业。\n\nWhy did you choose it?\n你为什么选择它？\n\nW: I gave a lot of thought to things you said during our last discussion, and I decided architecture made the most sense for me.\n女：我仔细考虑了您在上次讨论中所说的话，我认为建筑对我来说最有意义。\n\nIn particular, I''m attracted to the marriage of design and engineering.\n特别是，设计和工程结合对我很有吸引力。\n\nM: That''s great, but I seem to remember you were preoccupied with all the lofty mathematics.\n男：这很好，但我好像记得高深的数学让你忧心忡忡。\n\nYou no longer think this aspect will be too hard for you?\n你不再认为这方面对你来说太难了吗？\n\nW: No. I was doing some online research and I think I should be able to manage.\n女：是的。我在网上做了一些调查，我想我应该能够应付。\n\nMath might be the toughest subject I encounter in the curriculum, but I''ll simply put in the work required.\n数学可能是所有课程中我感觉最难的科目，但我会投入所需的努力。\n\nI''m certain the fruits of my labor will pay off.\n我确信我的劳动成果会有回报的。\n\nM: I''m sure that''s true.\n男：我也确信是那样的。\n\nDue to its material nature, architecture is one field where you will be able to clearly witness the contribution you make to a city.\n由于其物质性质，在建筑这个领域，你将能够清楚地见证你对城市的贡献。\n\nAnd the legacies you build will last much longer than any of us mortals.\n而你所建造的（建筑）遗产将比我们任何一个普通人都能存在更长的时间。\n\nW: Yeah, I guess that''s true too.\n女：是的，我想也是这样的。\n\nSo what subjects do you think I should start brushing up on in preparation?\n那么，您认为我在准备阶段应该开始学习哪些科目呢？\n\nI have the whole summer.\n我整个暑期都有时间。\n\nM: These days, architecture is a very diverse and dynamic degree.\n男：如今，建筑是一个非常多样化和充满活力的领域。\n\nMost universities will encourage you to learn different things from fields as wide-ranging as philosophy and economics.\n大多数大学都会鼓励你从哲学和经济学等广泛的领域学习不同的东西。\n\nNevertheless, I would suggest you start with computer science because there will be many intricate visuals you will have to produce as part of your projects.\n不过，我还是建议你从计算机科学开始，因为每个项目中都包含许多复杂的视觉效果。\n\nW: Any software in particular you think I should start with?\n女：您认为我应该从哪个软件开始呢？\n\nM: Photoshop is a good place.\n男：Photoshop是个很好的开始。\n\nIf you aren''t yet, try to become as proficient as you can with it.\n如果你还不能熟练应用，尽量让自己变得熟练。\n\nAnd another thing that I would recommend you learn as much as you can is fine arts, in particular, the history of Western art.\n还有就是我建议你尽可能地多学习美术，尤其是西方艺术史。\n\nQuestions 1 to 4 are based on the conversation you have just heard.\n请根据你刚刚听到的对话回答问题1到4。\n\n1. Why does the woman wish to study architecture?\n1. 为什么女士希望学习建筑？\n\n2.How does the woman say she will overcome the difficulty in learning mathematics?\n2. 女士说她将如何克服数学学习上的困难？\n\n3.What does the man say about architects'' contribution to a city?\n3. 关于建筑师对城市的贡献，这位男士说了什么？\n\n4.What subject does the man suggest the woman start with?\n4. 男士建议女士从什么科目开始？', 116, 1652.78, 34.05, 150.38, 172.43, 192.45, NULL, NULL, 'cet6-2023-06-2-g01', 'LONG_DIALOGUE', '[00:34.05]Conversation One｜对话一\n[00:36.66]M: Have you decided what you wish to study?｜男：你决定要学什么了吗？\n[00:39.45]W: Yes, professor. I wish to study architecture.｜女：是的，教授。我希望学习建筑。\n[00:42.49]M: Ah, that''s a wonderful profession.｜男：啊，这是一个很棒的专业。\n[00:45.22]Why did you choose it?｜你为什么选择它？\n[00:47.01]W: I gave a lot of thought to things you said during our last discussion, and I decided architecture made the most sense for me.｜女：我仔细考虑了您在上次讨论中所说的话，我认为建筑对我来说最有意义。\n[00:54.39]In particular, I''m attracted to the marriage of design and engineering.｜特别是，设计和工程结合对我很有吸引力。\n[00:58.96]M: That''s great, but I seem to remember you were preoccupied with all the lofty mathematics.｜男：这很好，但我好像记得高深的数学让你忧心忡忡。\n[01:05.14]You no longer think this aspect will be too hard for you?｜你不再认为这方面对你来说太难了吗？\n[01:08.48]W: No. I was doing some online research and I think I should be able to manage.｜女：是的。我在网上做了一些调查，我想我应该能够应付。\n[01:13.93]Math might be the toughest subject I encounter in the curriculum, but I''ll simply put in the work required.｜数学可能是所有课程中我感觉最难的科目，但我会投入所需的努力。\n[01:20.70]I''m certain the fruits of my labor will pay off.｜我确信我的劳动成果会有回报的。\n[01:23.71]M: I''m sure that''s true.｜男：我也确信是那样的。\n[01:25.22]Due to its material nature, architecture is one field where you will be able to clearly witness the contribution you make to a city.｜由于其物质性质，在建筑这个领域，你将能够清楚地见证你对城市的贡献。\n[01:33.56]And the legacies you build will last much longer than any of us mortals.｜而你所建造的（建筑）遗产将比我们任何一个普通人都能存在更长的时间。\n[01:38.33]W: Yeah, I guess that''s true too.｜女：是的，我想也是这样的。\n[01:40.66]So what subjects do you think I should start brushing up on in preparation?｜那么，您认为我在准备阶段应该开始学习哪些科目呢？\n[01:45.57]I have the whole summer.｜我整个暑期都有时间。\n[01:46.95]M: These days, architecture is a very diverse and dynamic degree.｜男：如今，建筑是一个非常多样化和充满活力的领域。\n[01:52.03]Most universities will encourage you to learn different things from fields as wide-ranging as philosophy and economics.｜大多数大学都会鼓励你从哲学和经济学等广泛的领域学习不同的东西。\n[02:00.00]Nevertheless, I would suggest you start with computer science because there will be many intricate visuals you will have to produce as part of your projects.｜不过，我还是建议你从计算机科学开始，因为每个项目中都包含许多复杂的视觉效果。\n[02:10.40]W: Any software in particular you think I should start with?｜女：您认为我应该从哪个软件开始呢？\n[02:13.72]M: Photoshop is a good place.｜男：Photoshop是个很好的开始。\n[02:16.00]If you aren''t yet, try to become as proficient as you can with it.｜如果你还不能熟练应用，尽量让自己变得熟练。\n[02:20.29]And another thing that I would recommend you learn as much as you can is fine arts, in particular, the history of Western art.｜还有就是我建议你尽可能地多学习美术，尤其是西方艺术史。\n[02:30.38]Questions 1 to 4 are based on the conversation you have just heard.｜请根据你刚刚听到的对话回答问题1到4。\n[02:35.22]1. Why does the woman wish to study architecture?｜1. 为什么女士希望学习建筑？\n[02:52.43]2.How does the woman say she will overcome the difficulty in learning mathematics?｜2. 女士说她将如何克服数学学习上的困难？\n[03:12.75]3.What does the man say about architects'' contribution to a city?｜3. 关于建筑师对城市的贡献，这位男士说了什么？\n[03:32.61]4.What subject does the man suggest the woman start with?｜4. 男士建议女士从什么科目开始？', NOW(), NOW()
