  @a_cet6_2023_06_2_08, '/audio/exams/listening-cet6-2023-06-2.mp3', 'Conversation Two\n对话二\n\nW: So as I mentioned over the phone, we are looking for someone who is very discreet.\n女：正如我在电话中提到的，我们要找的是一个非常谨慎的人。\n\nI can''t stress this enough.\n（这一点）再怎么强调也不为过。\n\nM: I fully understand.\n男：我完全理解。\n\nW: As we all know, being such a famous football player at Real Madrid, Mr. Sanchez has a very high public profile.\n女：众所周知，桑切斯先生是皇家马德里队的一位著名足球运动员，他的公众知名度很高。\n\nThis means he cannot leave the house without being recognized and harassed.\n这意味着他一出家门就会被认出或受到骚扰。\n\nM: Yes, I completely understand how imperative it would be to respect Mr. Sanchez''s private life.\n男：是的，我完全理解尊重桑切斯先生的私生活有多么重要。\n\nW: Good. As his personal assistant, you would be required to run common everyday chores for Mr. Sanchez, things he cannot do himself due to his fame, like going to the supermarket or post office.\n女：很好。作为桑切斯的私人助理，你需要为桑切斯先生做一些日常琐事，比如去超市或邮局等，因为他太出名了，这些事情他不可能自己去做。\n\nSo, well, at first sight it may appear that working for a celebrity is very glamorous.\n所以，嗯，乍一看，为名人工作似乎很光鲜。\n\nNothing could be further from the truth.\n但事实远非如此。\n\nI''m telling you this so that you don''t get any false expectations of what the job has to offer you.\n我跟你说这些的目的是希望你不会对这份工作能给予你的东西有任何错误的期望。\n\nM: Thanks. I understand this too.\n男：谢谢。我对此也很理解。\n\nThis is my first job after graduating from university.So frankly, I don''t have much prior working experience.\n这是我大学毕业后的第一份工作。所以坦率地说，我之前没有太多的工作经验。\n\nI am, however, very excited about the prospect of joining this company and very keen to start from the bottom in whatever capacity I may be of use.\n不过，想到能加入这家公司，我就很兴奋，也非常渴望能够尽我所能从底层做起。\n\nW: That''s good to hear.\n女：很高兴听你这么说。\n\nYou sound very energetic.\n你听起来很是积极。\n\nTell me why do you think you are well suited for this job?\n告诉我你为什么认为自己非常适合这份工作？\n\nM: Well, firstly, I love football.\n男：嗯，首先，我热爱足球。\n\nI''m a lifelong Real Madrid supporter and go to their games every weekend I can.\n我是皇马的终身球迷，每个周末都会去看他们比赛。\n\nI would simply love to have a job where I''m involved in some capacity with Real Madrid, regardless of the position and salary.\n我对职位和薪水没有要求，只想拥有一份能在皇马发挥作用的工作。\n\nAnd secondly, I think what this company does in sports consultancy is very cool.\n第二，我认为贵公司在体育咨询方面做得很酷。\n\nAnd I think my language skills could prove very useful down the road.\n并且，我觉得我的语言技能在今后将会非常有用。\n\nW: Please tell me more about your language skills.\n女：请再多谈一谈你的语言技能。\n\nM: I am fully fluent in English and Spanish and have a working proficiency in French.\n男：我的英语和西班牙语都很流利，也可以熟练地用法语来处理工作。\n\nQuestions 5 to 8 are based on the conversation you have just heard.\n请根据你刚刚听到的对话回答问题5到8。\n\n5. What do we learn from the conversation about Mr. Sanchez?\n5. 通过对话，我们对桑切斯先生有何了解？\n\n6.What will the man do if he gets the job?\n6. 如果男士能够得到这份工作，他将做些什么？\n\n7.What does the man say about himself?\n7. 关于自己，男士说了什么？\n\n8.Why does the man think he is a very competitive candidate?\n8. 为什么男士认为自己是一个很有竞争力的候选人？\n\nSection B Directions: In this section, you will hear two passages.\nB节 说明：在本节中，你将会听到两篇短文。', 119, 1652.78, 231.64, 350.86, 408.98, 428.98, NULL, NULL, 'cet6-2023-06-2-g02', 'LONG_DIALOGUE', '[03:51.64]Conversation Two｜对话二\n[03:53.65]W: So as I mentioned over the phone, we are looking for someone who is very discreet.｜女：正如我在电话中提到的，我们要找的是一个非常谨慎的人。\n[03:58.85]I can''t stress this enough.｜（这一点）再怎么强调也不为过。\n[04:00.52]M: I fully understand.｜男：我完全理解。\n[04:02.29]W: As we all know, being such a famous football player at Real Madrid, Mr. Sanchez has a very high public profile.｜女：众所周知，桑切斯先生是皇家马德里队的一位著名足球运动员，他的公众知名度很高。\n[04:10.10]This means he cannot leave the house without being recognized and harassed.｜这意味着他一出家门就会被认出或受到骚扰。\n[04:14.75]M: Yes, I completely understand how imperative it would be to respect Mr. Sanchez''s private life.｜男：是的，我完全理解尊重桑切斯先生的私生活有多么重要。\n[04:22.10]W: Good. As his personal assistant, you would be required to run common everyday chores for Mr. Sanchez, things he cannot do himself due to his fame, like going to the supermarket or post office.｜女：很好。作为桑切斯的私人助理，你需要为桑切斯先生做一些日常琐事，比如去超市或邮局等，因为他太出名了，这些事情他不可能自己去做。\n[04:34.42]So, well, at first sight it may appear that working for a celebrity is very glamorous.｜所以，嗯，乍一看，为名人工作似乎很光鲜。\n[04:40.21]Nothing could be further from the truth.｜但事实远非如此。\n[04:42.26]I''m telling you this so that you don''t get any false expectations of what the job has to offer you.｜我跟你说这些的目的是希望你不会对这份工作能给予你的东西有任何错误的期望。\n[04:47.95]M: Thanks. I understand this too.｜男：谢谢。我对此也很理解。\n[04:50.35]This is my first job after graduating from university.So frankly, I don''t have much prior working experience.｜这是我大学毕业后的第一份工作。所以坦率地说，我之前没有太多的工作经验。\n[04:57.90]I am, however, very excited about the prospect of joining this company and very keen to start from the bottom in whatever capacity I may be of use.｜不过，想到能加入这家公司，我就很兴奋，也非常渴望能够尽我所能从底层做起。\n[05:07.89]W: That''s good to hear.｜女：很高兴听你这么说。\n[05:09.16]You sound very energetic.｜你听起来很是积极。\n[05:10.74]Tell me why do you think you are well suited for this job?｜告诉我你为什么认为自己非常适合这份工作？\n[05:14.74]M: Well, firstly, I love football.｜男：嗯，首先，我热爱足球。\n[05:17.04]I''m a lifelong Real Madrid supporter and go to their games every weekend I can.｜我是皇马的终身球迷，每个周末都会去看他们比赛。\n[05:22.49]I would simply love to have a job where I''m involved in some capacity with Real Madrid, regardless of the position and salary.｜我对职位和薪水没有要求，只想拥有一份能在皇马发挥作用的工作。\n[05:31.25]And secondly, I think what this company does in sports consultancy is very cool.｜第二，我认为贵公司在体育咨询方面做得很酷。\n[05:37.58]And I think my language skills could prove very useful down the road.｜并且，我觉得我的语言技能在今后将会非常有用。\n[05:42.49]W: Please tell me more about your language skills.｜女：请再多谈一谈你的语言技能。\n[05:45.21]M: I am fully fluent in English and Spanish and have a working proficiency in French.｜男：我的英语和西班牙语都很流利，也可以熟练地用法语来处理工作。\n[05:50.86]Questions 5 to 8 are based on the conversation you have just heard.｜请根据你刚刚听到的对话回答问题5到8。\n[05:56.02]5. What do we learn from the conversation about Mr. Sanchez?｜5. 通过对话，我们对桑切斯先生有何了解？\n[06:13.70]6.What will the man do if he gets the job?｜6. 如果男士能够得到这份工作，他将做些什么？\n[06:31.17]7.What does the man say about himself?｜7. 关于自己，男士说了什么？\n[06:48.98]8.Why does the man think he is a very competitive candidate?｜8. 为什么男士认为自己是一个很有竞争力的候选人？\n[07:07.34]Section B Directions: In this section, you will hear two passages.｜B节 说明：在本节中，你将会听到两篇短文。', NOW(), NOW()
