SELECT
  @a_cet6_2023_06_2_14, '/audio/exams/listening-cet6-2023-06-2.mp3', 'Passage Two\n短文二\n\nThe shiny gadgets of today will be waste tomorrow.\n今天还闪闪发光的小玩意明天就会变成废品。\n\nManufacturers don''t talk much about this when they announce the big new thing that will replace your mostly just as good old thing.\n当生产商们宣布将用高大上的新产品来取代那些还挺好用的旧产品时，他们不会多说什么。\n\nIn fact, technology firms often purposely design devices that will not last long and cannot be repaired so that consumers will have to spend their money on a new one.\n事实上，科技公司经常故意将设备设计得使用寿命较短且无法修复，这样消费者就不得不花钱购买新设备。\n\nThis year, the French government began requiring tech manufacturers to list a repairability score.\n今年，法国政府开始要求科技产品生产商们列出可修复性评分。\n\nIf a device can be repaired, then its life can be extended, saving consumers money and the planet the burden of so many trashed gadgets.\n如果设备可以修好，那么它的寿命就可以延长，消费者就可以省钱，被丢弃的小玩意儿也会减少，从而减轻地球的负担。\n\nEquipped with this knowledge, consumers can make better choices about which products to buy.\n有了这些知识，消费者可以更好地选择购买哪些产品。\n\nSome 59 million tons of old TVs, computers, screens, smartphones, washers and other electronics are discarded every year.\n每年约有5,900万吨旧电视、电脑、显示器、智能手机、洗衣机和其他电子产品被丢弃。\n\nThis waste is dangerous.\n这种浪费是很危险的。\n\nBatteries explode in recycling facilities.\n电池在回收设施中爆炸。\n\nToxic substances like mercury leak into soil and groundwater and disperse in the air.\n汞等有毒物质泄漏到土壤和地下水中，并在空气中扩散。\n\nManufacturing flat screens adds greenhouse gases to the atmosphere.\n制造平面屏会增加大气中的温室气体。\n\nWe need tech companies to take the lead to solve this problem.\n我们需要科技公司带头解决这个问题。\n\nIf they won''t, governments must make them do so.\n如果他们不作为，政府必须让他们有所作为。\n\nAlthough tech companies will often speak of environmental sustainability, many lobby against repair legislation, fearful it will eat into their profits.\n尽管科技公司经常提到环境的可持续性，许多人却四处游说反对维修立法，担心这会侵蚀他们的利润。\n\nSustainability matters, but marketable design appears to matter more to these companies.\n可持续性很重要，但对这些公司来说，适销对路的设计似乎更加重要。\n\nConsumers should support right-to-repair legislation.\n消费者应支持维修权立法。\n\nIn this world, damage is a certainty.\n在这个世界上，损毁是必然的。\n\nBut we cannot leave things broken: A problem of our creation is a problem that can be fixed.\n但我们不能就让它们坏着：既然是我们的创造所导致问题，那这一定是可以解决的问题。\n\nQuestions 12 to 15 are based on the passage you have just heard.\n请根据你刚刚听到的短文回答问题12到15。\n\n12. Why did new tech products soon become waste?\n12. 为什么新的科技产品很快就变成了废品？\n\n13.What did the French government require tech companies to do to help consumers make better choices?\n13. 法国政府要求科技公司做些什么来帮助消费者做出更好的选择？\n\n14.What should tech companies do to help ensure environmental sustainability?\n14. 科技公司应该做些什么来帮助确保环境的可持续性？\n\n15.What does the speaker think of the problem of waste?\n15. 讲话者对浪费问题有何看法？\n\nSection C Directions: In this section, you will hear three recordings of lectures or talks followed by three or four questions.\nC节 说明：在本节中，你将会听到三篇讲座或讲话，每篇讲座或讲话后面都有三个或四个问题。', 130, 1652.78, 631.72, 761.75, 806.45, 826.85, 686.88, 701.57, 'cet6-2023-06-2-g04', 'PASSAGE', '[10:31.72]Passage Two｜短文二\n[10:33.99]The shiny gadgets of today will be waste tomorrow.｜今天还闪闪发光的小玩意明天就会变成废品。\n[10:38.05]Manufacturers don''t talk much about this when they announce the big new thing that will replace your mostly just as good old thing.｜当生产商们宣布将用高大上的新产品来取代那些还挺好用的旧产品时，他们不会多说什么。\n[10:47.50]In fact, technology firms often purposely design devices that will not last long and cannot be repaired so that consumers will have to spend their money on a new one.｜事实上，科技公司经常故意将设备设计得使用寿命较短且无法修复，这样消费者就不得不花钱购买新设备。\n[11:00.98]This year, the French government began requiring tech manufacturers to list a repairability score.｜今年，法国政府开始要求科技产品生产商们列出可修复性评分。\n[11:08.71]If a device can be repaired, then its life can be extended, saving consumers money and the planet the burden of so many trashed gadgets.｜如果设备可以修好，那么它的寿命就可以延长，消费者就可以省钱，被丢弃的小玩意儿也会减少，从而减轻地球的负担。\n[11:20.44]Equipped with this knowledge, consumers can make better choices about which products to buy.｜有了这些知识，消费者可以更好地选择购买哪些产品。\n[11:26.88]Some 59 million tons of old TVs, computers, screens, smartphones, washers and other electronics are discarded every year.｜每年约有5,900万吨旧电视、电脑、显示器、智能手机、洗衣机和其他电子产品被丢弃。\n[11:39.29]This waste is dangerous.｜这种浪费是很危险的。\n[11:41.87]Batteries explode in recycling facilities.｜电池在回收设施中爆炸。\n[11:45.16]Toxic substances like mercury leak into soil and groundwater and disperse in the air.｜汞等有毒物质泄漏到土壤和地下水中，并在空气中扩散。\n[11:53.41]Manufacturing flat screens adds greenhouse gases to the atmosphere.｜制造平面屏会增加大气中的温室气体。\n[11:58.65]We need tech companies to take the lead to solve this problem.｜我们需要科技公司带头解决这个问题。\n[12:03.66]If they won''t, governments must make them do so.｜如果他们不作为，政府必须让他们有所作为。\n[12:07.24]Although tech companies will often speak of environmental sustainability, many lobby against repair legislation, fearful it will eat into their profits.｜尽管科技公司经常提到环境的可持续性，许多人却四处游说反对维修立法，担心这会侵蚀他们的利润。\n[12:19.70]Sustainability matters, but marketable design appears to matter more to these companies.｜可持续性很重要，但对这些公司来说，适销对路的设计似乎更加重要。\n[12:26.58]Consumers should support right-to-repair legislation.｜消费者应支持维修权立法。\n[12:31.21]In this world, damage is a certainty.｜在这个世界上，损毁是必然的。\n[12:34.53]But we cannot leave things broken: A problem of our creation is a problem that can be fixed.｜但我们不能就让它们坏着：既然是我们的创造所导致问题，那这一定是可以解决的问题。\n[12:41.75]Questions 12 to 15 are based on the passage you have just heard.｜请根据你刚刚听到的短文回答问题12到15。\n[12:46.95]12. Why did new tech products soon become waste?｜12. 为什么新的科技产品很快就变成了废品？\n[13:04.67]13.What did the French government require tech companies to do to help consumers make better choices?｜13. 法国政府要求科技公司做些什么来帮助消费者做出更好的选择？\n[13:26.45]14.What should tech companies do to help ensure environmental sustainability?｜14. 科技公司应该做些什么来帮助确保环境的可持续性？\n[13:47.15]15.What does the speaker think of the problem of waste?｜15. 讲话者对浪费问题有何看法？\n[14:05.58]Section C Directions: In this section, you will hear three recordings of lectures or talks followed by three or four questions.｜C节 说明：在本节中，你将会听到三篇讲座或讲话，每篇讲座或讲话后面都有三个或四个问题。', NOW(), NOW()
