SELECT
  @a_cet6_2023_12_1_02, '/audio/exams/listening-cet6-2023-12-1.mp3', 'Conversation One\n对话一\n\nM: Hello, doctor.\n男：你好，大夫。\n\nW: Hello, please take a seat. I have your test results here.\n女：你好，请坐。我这有你的测试结果了。\n\nAnd it''s good news. The blood test came back clear.\n是个好消息。验血结果很清楚。\n\nThere is no indication of any digestive issues.\n没有迹象表明有任何消化问题。\n\nM: So then, why do I feel so poorly all the time?\n男：那为什么我总是感觉这么不舒服呢？\n\nW: It''s probably due to overwork and stress.\n女：可能是因为超负荷的工作和压力。\n\nM: No, it can''t be. I''ve always been working hard but I''ve never felt stress.\n男：不，不可能。我工作一直很努力，但我从未感到有压力。\n\nOther people suffering complain about that, but I don''t. It must be something else.\n其他有压力的人会抱怨，但我没有。肯定是别的问题。\n\nW: What you have just described is a common sentiment.\n女：你所描述的现象很普遍。\n\nMany people who suffer from stress fail to recognise it.\n许多承受压力的人都没有意识到这一点。\n\nYou told me you often work long into the night, right?\n你告诉过我你经常工作到深夜，对吧？\n\nM: Yes, most days, in fact.\n男：是的，事实上多数日子都是这样。\n\nBut I''ve been doing that for about 20 years now.\n但我已经这么做了快20年了。\n\nW: That doesn''t matter.\n女：那不重要。\n\nYou could have been suffering from stress for 20 years without knowing it.\n你可能在不知不觉中承受了20年的压力。\n\nAnd now it''s catching up to you.\n现在开始有感觉了。\n\nM: But what about my feeling tired all the time and not being able to sleep well at night?\n男：但是，我总觉得累，晚上睡不好，是怎么回事呢？\n\nW: Those are common consequences of stress.\n女：这都是压力的常见影响。\n\nAnd if you don''t sleep well, then of course you will feel fatigued.\n如果睡得不好，你自然会感到疲劳。\n\nI''m going to prescribe some special sleeping pills for you.\n我会给你开一些特殊的安眠药。\n\nThey have a soft, gentle effect and are made from natural ingredients.\n它们效果轻柔温和，由天然成分制成。\n\nSo your stomach should tolerate them fine, and there shouldn''t be any negative side effects.\n所以你的胃应该能很好地承受这些药物，不会有任何不好的副作用。\n\nTake one with your dinner and come see me after a month.\n晚饭时吃一片，一个月后再来找我看看。\n\nIf there is no improvement, I''ll give you something stronger.\n如果没有任何改善，我再给你开些药效更强的。\n\nM: Thank you, doctor.\n男：谢谢你，医生。\n\nW: That''s not all. You should try and work less.\n女：还没完。你应该努力减少些工作。\n\nIs there any way you can decrease your workload?\n有什么办法可以减少工作量吗？\n\nM: Hmm... I''d have to think about it.\n男： 嗯……我得想想。\n\nI''m a restaurant manager and this industry is very competitive.\n我一名餐厅经理，这个行业竞争激烈。\n\nThere are many things to keep track of and stay on top of.\n有很多事情需要跟踪和掌握。\n\nW: I recommend you think about delegating some responsibilities to someone else.\n女：我建议你考虑一下将部分职责委派给其他人。\n\nI''m not asking you to retire, just to slow down a bit.\n我并不是要你退休，只是让你放慢一下脚步。\n\nIt''s for your own health.\n这是为了你自己的健康着想。\n\nQuestions 1 to 4 are based on the conversation you have just heard.\n请根据你刚刚听到的对话回答问题1到4。\n\n1. What do we learn about the man from his test results?\n1. 我们从男士的化验结果了解到关于他的什么信息？\n\n2. What does the woman think is a common phenomenon among many people?\n2. 女士认为在很多人中都很常见的一个现象是什么？\n\n3. What does the woman say she will do for the man?\n3. 女士说她会为男士做什么？\n\n4. What does the man say about the industry he is engaged in?\n4. 关于自己所从事的行业，男士说了什么？', 111, 1566.81, 37.95, 148.64, 169.55, 189.90, NULL, NULL, 'cet6-2023-12-1-g01', 'LONG_DIALOGUE', '[00:37.95]Conversation One｜对话一\n[00:40.26]M: Hello, doctor.｜男：你好，大夫。\n[00:41.68]W: Hello, please take a seat. I have your test results here.｜女：你好，请坐。我这有你的测试结果了。\n[00:45.22]And it''s good news. The blood test came back clear.｜是个好消息。验血结果很清楚。\n[00:48.40]There is no indication of any digestive issues.｜没有迹象表明有任何消化问题。\n[00:51.72]M: So then, why do I feel so poorly all the time?｜男：那为什么我总是感觉这么不舒服呢？\n[00:55.06]W: It''s probably due to overwork and stress.｜女：可能是因为超负荷的工作和压力。\n[00:58.15]M: No, it can''t be. I''ve always been working hard but I''ve never felt stress.｜男：不，不可能。我工作一直很努力，但我从未感到有压力。\n[01:02.92]Other people suffering complain about that, but I don''t. It must be something else.｜其他有压力的人会抱怨，但我没有。肯定是别的问题。\n[01:07.77]W: What you have just described is a common sentiment.｜女：你所描述的现象很普遍。\n[01:11.04]Many people who suffer from stress fail to recognise it.｜许多承受压力的人都没有意识到这一点。\n[01:14.80]You told me you often work long into the night, right?｜你告诉过我你经常工作到深夜，对吧？\n[01:18.34]M: Yes, most days, in fact.｜男：是的，事实上多数日子都是这样。\n[01:20.44]But I''ve been doing that for about 20 years now.｜但我已经这么做了快20年了。\n[01:23.80]W: That doesn''t matter.｜女：那不重要。\n[01:25.06]You could have been suffering from stress for 20 years without knowing it.｜你可能在不知不觉中承受了20年的压力。\n[01:29.11]And now it''s catching up to you.｜现在开始有感觉了。\n[01:31.19]M: But what about my feeling tired all the time and not being able to sleep well at night?｜男：但是，我总觉得累，晚上睡不好，是怎么回事呢？\n[01:36.36]W: Those are common consequences of stress.｜女：这都是压力的常见影响。\n[01:39.22]And if you don''t sleep well, then of course you will feel fatigued.｜如果睡得不好，你自然会感到疲劳。\n[01:42.92]I''m going to prescribe some special sleeping pills for you.｜我会给你开一些特殊的安眠药。\n[01:46.45]They have a soft, gentle effect and are made from natural ingredients.｜它们效果轻柔温和，由天然成分制成。\n[01:50.68]So your stomach should tolerate them fine, and there shouldn''t be any negative side effects.｜所以你的胃应该能很好地承受这些药物，不会有任何不好的副作用。\n[01:55.60]Take one with your dinner and come see me after a month.｜晚饭时吃一片，一个月后再来找我看看。\n[01:59.09]If there is no improvement, I''ll give you something stronger.｜如果没有任何改善，我再给你开些药效更强的。\n[02:02.46]M: Thank you, doctor.｜男：谢谢你，医生。\n[02:03.70]W: That''s not all. You should try and work less.｜女：还没完。你应该努力减少些工作。\n[02:06.76]Is there any way you can decrease your workload?｜有什么办法可以减少工作量吗？\n[02:09.61]M: Hmm... I''d have to think about it.｜男： 嗯……我得想想。\n[02:12.13]I''m a restaurant manager and this industry is very competitive.｜我一名餐厅经理，这个行业竞争激烈。\n[02:15.70]There are many things to keep track of and stay on top of.｜有很多事情需要跟踪和掌握。\n[02:18.63]W: I recommend you think about delegating some responsibilities to someone else.｜女：我建议你考虑一下将部分职责委派给其他人。\n[02:23.13]I''m not asking you to retire, just to slow down a bit.｜我并不是要你退休，只是让你放慢一下脚步。\n[02:26.49]It''s for your own health.｜这是为了你自己的健康着想。\n[02:28.64]Questions 1 to 4 are based on the conversation you have just heard.｜请根据你刚刚听到的对话回答问题1到4。\n[02:32.91]1. What do we learn about the man from his test results?｜1. 我们从男士的化验结果了解到关于他的什么信息？\n[02:49.55]2. What does the woman think is a common phenomenon among many people?｜2. 女士认为在很多人中都很常见的一个现象是什么？\n[03:10.20]3. What does the woman say she will do for the man?｜3. 女士说她会为男士做什么？\n[03:27.64]4. What does the man say about the industry he is engaged in?｜4. 关于自己所从事的行业，男士说了什么？', NOW(), NOW()
