  @a_cet6_2023_12_1_06, '/audio/exams/listening-cet6-2023-12-1.mp3', 'Conversation Two\n对话二\n\nW: Today on People in the News, our guest is John Williams.\n女：在今天的《新闻人物》节目中，我们的嘉宾是约翰·威廉姆斯。\n\nThe name may not sound familiar to you, but John was once an acclaimed basketball player.\n这个名字可能听上去并不熟悉，但约翰曾经是一位备受赞誉的篮球运动员。\n\nJohn, you stunned fans by leaving the sport at just 25.\n约翰，你25岁就离开了这项运动，让球迷们大吃一惊。\n\nWhy did you retire so early?\n你为什么这么早就退休了？\n\nM: Meg, I loved being an athlete, but I didn''t love being a celebrity.\n男：梅格，我喜欢当运动员，但我不喜欢当名人。\n\nI was in the limelight when I was still a high school student and went professional right after high school graduation, which was a mistake.\n我还是一名高中生的时候就成了众人瞩目的焦点，高中毕业后就成了职业篮球运动员，这是一个错误。\n\nI was a shy kid and I wasn''t ready for all the media attention.\n我是个腼腆的孩子，还没有准备好承受媒体的关注。\n\nW: But walking away from millions of dollars at the height of your career?\n女：可是，在职业生涯的巅峰时期放弃数百万美元？\n\nMost people wouldn''t be able to resist the lure of such a high salary.\n大多数人都无法抗拒如此高薪的诱惑。\n\nWhen you left the sport, there was speculation that you were having issues with your teammates or even an injury.\n你离开这项运动时，有人猜测是你与队友有嫌隙，或是受伤了。\n\nM: Not at all. It was hard to quit.\n男：根本不是。结束的时候是很难。\n\nI was tempted to stay in the game, because I loved basketball and I loved my team.\n我忍不住想留下来继续比赛，因为我爱篮球，我爱我的球队。\n\nAs for money, I turned professional at 18, so I''d actually earned a lot and saved most of it because I had great financial advisors.\n至于钱，我18岁就成为了职业选手，所以实际上我赚了很多钱，并且大部分都存下来了，因为我有很棒的财务顾问。\n\nI knew basketball wasn''t a career with a lot of longevity for most players, so I wanted to change careers while I was still young.\n我知道篮球对大多数球员来说并不是一个长寿的职业，所以我想趁自己还年轻的时候转行。\n\nW: Okay, that was 20 years ago, and you''re back in the news.\n女：好吧，那是20年前的事了，现在你又上新闻了。\n\nYou''ve created a foundation that works to get more kids playing team sports. Why?\n你建立了一个致力于让更多孩子参加团队运动的基金会。为什么？\n\nM: I went to university and I studied public health and learned about the seriousness of the obesity epidemic, particularly among kids and adolescents in poor communities.\n男：我去上了大学，学习的是公共健康，了解了肥胖流行病问题，这一问题在贫困社区的儿童和青少年人群中尤为严重。\n\nI''ve spent the last two decades trying to alleviate the problem.\n过去的20年里，我一直在努力缓解这个问题。\n\nThe foundation is just the latest attempt.\n这个基金会只是最新的尝试。\n\nW: The foundation uses private donations to support basketball teams for girls and boys in primary school, right?\n女：这个基金会使用私人捐款给小学男女篮球队提供帮助，对吧？\n\nM: Actually, we support teams for secondary school students too, and also have some public funding.\n男：事实上，我们也为中学球队提供支持，而且我们还有些公共资金。\n\nQuestions 5 to 8 are based on the conversation you have just heard.\n请根据你刚刚听到的对话回答问题5到8。\n\n5. Why did John Williams leave the sport of basketball at just 25?\n5. 为什么约翰·威廉姆斯在25岁时就离开了篮球运动？\n\n6. What does the man say about basketball as a career for most players?\n6. 关于大多数球员的篮球生涯，男士说了什么？\n\n7. What do we learn from the woman about John Williams 20 years later?\n7. 我们从女士那里了解到20年后的约翰·威廉姆斯的什么事情？\n\n8. What has the man spent the last two decades trying to do?\n8. 在过去的20年里，这位男士一直在努力做些什么？\n\nSection B Directions: In this section, you will hear two passages.\nB节 说明：在本节中，你将会听到两篇短文。', 122, 1566.81, 225.88, 347.42, 369.52, 389.80, NULL, NULL, 'cet6-2023-12-1-g02', 'LONG_DIALOGUE', '[03:45.88]Conversation Two｜对话二\n[03:48.85]W: Today on People in the News, our guest is John Williams.｜女：在今天的《新闻人物》节目中，我们的嘉宾是约翰·威廉姆斯。\n[03:54.15]The name may not sound familiar to you, but John was once an acclaimed basketball player.｜这个名字可能听上去并不熟悉，但约翰曾经是一位备受赞誉的篮球运动员。\n[04:00.57]John, you stunned fans by leaving the sport at just 25.｜约翰，你25岁就离开了这项运动，让球迷们大吃一惊。\n[04:05.81]Why did you retire so early?｜你为什么这么早就退休了？\n[04:08.42]M: Meg, I loved being an athlete, but I didn''t love being a celebrity.｜男：梅格，我喜欢当运动员，但我不喜欢当名人。\n[04:13.04]I was in the limelight when I was still a high school student and went professional right after high school graduation, which was a mistake.｜我还是一名高中生的时候就成了众人瞩目的焦点，高中毕业后就成了职业篮球运动员，这是一个错误。\n[04:21.28]I was a shy kid and I wasn''t ready for all the media attention.｜我是个腼腆的孩子，还没有准备好承受媒体的关注。\n[04:25.26]W: But walking away from millions of dollars at the height of your career?｜女：可是，在职业生涯的巅峰时期放弃数百万美元？\n[04:29.82]Most people wouldn''t be able to resist the lure of such a high salary.｜大多数人都无法抗拒如此高薪的诱惑。\n[04:34.21]When you left the sport, there was speculation that you were having issues with your teammates or even an injury.｜你离开这项运动时，有人猜测是你与队友有嫌隙，或是受伤了。\n[04:40.94]M: Not at all. It was hard to quit.｜男：根本不是。结束的时候是很难。\n[04:43.59]I was tempted to stay in the game, because I loved basketball and I loved my team.｜我忍不住想留下来继续比赛，因为我爱篮球，我爱我的球队。\n[04:48.38]As for money, I turned professional at 18, so I''d actually earned a lot and saved most of it because I had great financial advisors.｜至于钱，我18岁就成为了职业选手，所以实际上我赚了很多钱，并且大部分都存下来了，因为我有很棒的财务顾问。\n[04:57.14]I knew basketball wasn''t a career with a lot of longevity for most players, so I wanted to change careers while I was still young.｜我知道篮球对大多数球员来说并不是一个长寿的职业，所以我想趁自己还年轻的时候转行。\n[05:04.87]W: Okay, that was 20 years ago, and you''re back in the news.｜女：好吧，那是20年前的事了，现在你又上新闻了。\n[05:09.31]You''ve created a foundation that works to get more kids playing team sports. Why?｜你建立了一个致力于让更多孩子参加团队运动的基金会。为什么？\n[05:15.16]M: I went to university and I studied public health and learned about the seriousness of the obesity epidemic, particularly among kids and adolescents in poor communities.｜男：我去上了大学，学习的是公共健康，了解了肥胖流行病问题，这一问题在贫困社区的儿童和青少年人群中尤为严重。\n[05:26.01]I''ve spent the last two decades trying to alleviate the problem.｜过去的20年里，我一直在努力缓解这个问题。\n[05:29.66]The foundation is just the latest attempt.｜这个基金会只是最新的尝试。\n[05:32.36]W: The foundation uses private donations to support basketball teams for girls and boys in primary school, right?｜女：这个基金会使用私人捐款给小学男女篮球队提供帮助，对吧？\n[05:39.90]M: Actually, we support teams for secondary school students too, and also have some public funding.｜男：事实上，我们也为中学球队提供支持，而且我们还有些公共资金。\n[05:47.42]Questions 5 to 8 are based on the conversation you have just heard.｜请根据你刚刚听到的对话回答问题5到8。\n[05:52.03]5. Why did John Williams leave the sport of basketball at just 25?｜5. 为什么约翰·威廉姆斯在25岁时就离开了篮球运动？\n[06:09.52]6. What does the man say about basketball as a career for most players?｜6. 关于大多数球员的篮球生涯，男士说了什么？\n[06:30.10]7. What do we learn from the woman about John Williams 20 years later?｜7. 我们从女士那里了解到20年后的约翰·威廉姆斯的什么事情？\n[06:47.72]8. What has the man spent the last two decades trying to do?｜8. 在过去的20年里，这位男士一直在努力做些什么？\n[07:06.49]Section B Directions: In this section, you will hear two passages.｜B节 说明：在本节中，你将会听到两篇短文。', NOW(), NOW()
