SELECT
  @a_cet6_2023_12_2_03, '/audio/exams/listening-cet6-2023-12-2.mp3', 'Conversation One\n对话一\n\nW: So, I''ve been thinking, this summer, instead of our usual holiday rental, I''d like to try renting a camper van and exploring a bit more.\n女:所以，我一直在想，今年夏天试着租一辆露营车去探索更多的地方，而不是像以往那样租个度假屋。\n\nM: A camper van? You mean to spend the summer living out of a car?\n男:露营车?你是说整个夏天都住在车里吗?\n\nW: Yes, a camper van. And no, it''s nothing like living out of a car.\n女:是的，露营车。不，这一点也不像住在车里。\n\nThese are proper vans with full-size beds to sleep in. Some even have kitchens.\n这些都是专有的货车，有双人床可以睡觉。有些甚至还有厨房。\n\nThis way, we wouldn''t have to be locked into one place during our holiday.\n这样，我们在假期就不用被限制在一个地方了。\n\nWe''d be able to visit so many more places and travel at our own pace.\n我们可以参观更多的地方，按照我们自己的节奏旅行。\n\nThe rates of most hotels and holiday homes really soar in the summer anyway.\n加之，大多数酒店和度假屋的房价在夏季确实会飙升。\n\nWe''d probably save a lot of money as well.\n我们可能也会省下很多钱。\n\nM: I think my grandfather had a van like that.\n男:我想我祖父有一辆那样的面包车。\n\nIt doesn''t sound that appealing to me.\n听起来不怎么吸引我。\n\nW: Today''s camper vans are completely different.\n女:现在的露营车完全不同了。\n\nThese days, they''re equipped with all the modern comforts.\n如今，它们配备了所有现代化的舒适设施。\n\nI''ve seen quite a few with solar panels that provide electricity for when you''re stopped.\n我见过不少装有太阳能板的车，当你停下来的时候可以提供电力。\n\nThis way you can still use your computer or charge your phone.\n这样你仍然可以使用电脑或给手机充电。\n\nAnd most even have Wi-Fi, so if the weather''s not great, you could stream videos.\n大多数（露营车）甚至有Wi-Fi，所以如果天气不好，你可以流播视频。\n\nM: I''m warming up to the idea. Keep talking.\n男:我对这个主意有点兴趣了。继续说。\n\nW: Loads of people are committing to this trend full time.\n女:很多人都全职投入到这一趋势。\n\nCheck it out online. Lots of people stream videos of their alternative lifestyles and actually earn a salary.\n上网看看吧。很多人流播他们另类生活方式的视频，而且实际上赚到了钱。\n\nImagine having that kind of freedom to go anywhere you want and work from anywhere in the world.\n想象一下拥有这种自由的画面，你可以自由地去任何你想去的地方，在世界上任何地方都可以工作。\n\nM: Okay, we can consider it.\n男:好的，我们可以考虑一下。\n\nAs long as the basic needs like toilets and showers are covered, I''m definitely in.\n只要能满足厕所和淋浴等基本需求，我绝对会加入。\n\nDo you think there''ll be enough room for my mountain bike?\n你认为有足够的地方放我的山地车吗?\n\nWhat about food delivery?\n送餐呢?\n\nWill we be able to order to the van?\n我们可以点餐送到我们的露营车吗?\n\nWill there be enough space for the dog?\n有足够的空间给我们的狗吗?\n\nWe wouldn''t want to leave him behind.\n我们不会想丢下它的。\n\nW: Slow down. Glad you''re excited about it.\n女:慢点。很高兴你对此感到兴奋。\n\nLet''s start by looking at what''s available first.\n让我们先看看有什么可用的。\n\nQuestions 1 to 4 are based on the conversation you have just heard.\n请根据你刚刚听到的对话回答问题1到4。\n\n1. What has the woman been thinking of doing for this summer?\n1. 女士今年夏天想做什么?\n\n2. What do we learn about the man''s grandfather from the conversation?\n2. 我们从对话中了解到男士祖父的什么信息?\n\n3. What can many camper vans do nowadays according to the woman?\n3. 根据女士的说法，现在许多露营车能做什么?\n\n4. What idea does the woman find attractive?\n4. 女士觉得什么想法有吸引力?', 115, 1563.93, 37.82, 153.26, 193.83, 211.95, NULL, NULL, 'cet6-2023-12-2-g01', 'LONG_DIALOGUE', '[00:37.82]Conversation One｜对话一\n[00:39.94]W: So, I''ve been thinking, this summer, instead of our usual holiday rental, I''d like to try renting a camper van and exploring a bit more.｜女:所以，我一直在想，今年夏天试着租一辆露营车去探索更多的地方，而不是像以往那样租个度假屋。\n[00:48.85]M: A camper van? You mean to spend the summer living out of a car?｜男:露营车?你是说整个夏天都住在车里吗?\n[00:53.03]W: Yes, a camper van. And no, it''s nothing like living out of a car.｜女:是的，露营车。不，这一点也不像住在车里。\n[00:57.80]These are proper vans with full-size beds to sleep in. Some even have kitchens.｜这些都是专有的货车，有双人床可以睡觉。有些甚至还有厨房。\n[01:04.22]This way, we wouldn''t have to be locked into one place during our holiday.｜这样，我们在假期就不用被限制在一个地方了。\n[01:08.73]We''d be able to visit so many more places and travel at our own pace.｜我们可以参观更多的地方，按照我们自己的节奏旅行。\n[01:13.73]The rates of most hotels and holiday homes really soar in the summer anyway.｜加之，大多数酒店和度假屋的房价在夏季确实会飙升。\n[01:18.92]We''d probably save a lot of money as well.｜我们可能也会省下很多钱。\n[01:21.78]M: I think my grandfather had a van like that.｜男:我想我祖父有一辆那样的面包车。\n[01:24.83]It doesn''t sound that appealing to me.｜听起来不怎么吸引我。\n[01:27.21]W: Today''s camper vans are completely different.｜女:现在的露营车完全不同了。\n[01:30.07]These days, they''re equipped with all the modern comforts.｜如今，它们配备了所有现代化的舒适设施。\n[01:33.61]I''ve seen quite a few with solar panels that provide electricity for when you''re stopped.｜我见过不少装有太阳能板的车，当你停下来的时候可以提供电力。\n[01:38.76]This way you can still use your computer or charge your phone.｜这样你仍然可以使用电脑或给手机充电。\n[01:42.56]And most even have Wi-Fi, so if the weather''s not great, you could stream videos.｜大多数（露营车）甚至有Wi-Fi，所以如果天气不好，你可以流播视频。\n[01:48.15]M: I''m warming up to the idea. Keep talking.｜男:我对这个主意有点兴趣了。继续说。\n[01:51.53]W: Loads of people are committing to this trend full time.｜女:很多人都全职投入到这一趋势。\n[01:54.82]Check it out online. Lots of people stream videos of their alternative lifestyles and actually earn a salary.｜上网看看吧。很多人流播他们另类生活方式的视频，而且实际上赚到了钱。\n[02:02.21]Imagine having that kind of freedom to go anywhere you want and work from anywhere in the world.｜想象一下拥有这种自由的画面，你可以自由地去任何你想去的地方，在世界上任何地方都可以工作。\n[02:08.37]M: Okay, we can consider it.｜男:好的，我们可以考虑一下。\n[02:10.96]As long as the basic needs like toilets and showers are covered, I''m definitely in.｜只要能满足厕所和淋浴等基本需求，我绝对会加入。\n[02:15.97]Do you think there''ll be enough room for my mountain bike?｜你认为有足够的地方放我的山地车吗?\n[02:18.94]What about food delivery?｜送餐呢?\n[02:20.88]Will we be able to order to the van?｜我们可以点餐送到我们的露营车吗?\n[02:22.88]Will there be enough space for the dog?｜有足够的空间给我们的狗吗?\n[02:25.32]We wouldn''t want to leave him behind.｜我们不会想丢下它的。\n[02:27.46]W: Slow down. Glad you''re excited about it.｜女:慢点。很高兴你对此感到兴奋。\n[02:30.04]Let''s start by looking at what''s available first.｜让我们先看看有什么可用的。\n[02:33.26]Questions 1 to 4 are based on the conversation you have just heard.｜请根据你刚刚听到的对话回答问题1到4。\n[02:38.47]1. What has the woman been thinking of doing for this summer?｜1. 女士今年夏天想做什么?\n[02:55.92]2. What do we learn about the man''s grandfather from the conversation?｜2. 我们从对话中了解到男士祖父的什么信息?\n[03:13.83]3. What can many camper vans do nowadays according to the woman?｜3. 根据女士的说法，现在许多露营车能做什么?\n[03:32.25]4. What idea does the woman find attractive?｜4. 女士觉得什么想法有吸引力?', NOW(), NOW()
