  @a_cet6_2023_12_2_07, '/audio/exams/listening-cet6-2023-12-2.mp3', 'Conversation Two\n对话二\n\nW: You wanted to see me?\n女:您找我?\n\nM: Yes, I''ll get straight to the point.\n男:是的，我就开门见山了。\n\nOver the past month or so, it has become apparent that your performance has dipped.\n在过去一个月左右的时间里，你的表现明显下降了。\n\nYou''ve been late to work several times these past few weeks, which is very uncharacteristic of you.\n在过去的几个星期里，你迟到了好几次，这很不像你的作风。\n\nBut what really concerns me is your curtailed output.\n但我真正担心的是你的减产。\n\nLately, you seem to be constantly one step behind.\n最近，你似乎总是落后别人一步。\n\nWhat''s going on?\n发生了什么？\n\nW: I''m sorry. I''m going through some unfortunate family issues at the moment.\n女:抱歉。我现在正经历一些不幸的家庭问题。\n\nIt''s a personal matter. So if you don''t mind, I much prefer we don''t get into it.\n这是个人问题。所以如果你不介意的话，我希望我们不要谈这个。\n\nNevertheless, I expect it to have all blown over in another month or so.\n不过，我预计再过一个月左右，一切都会平息。\n\nM: Do you need some time off?\n男:你需要请假吗?\n\nW: Actually, yes. Would it be possible to take the next two Mondays off?\n女:事实上，是的。接下来的两个星期一我可以请假吗?\n\nI was deliberating whether I should ask for this, but now that we''re here...\n我还在考虑要不要提出这个要求，但既然我们说到这里……\n\nM: Sure thing! But if you needed some leave, why didn''t you ask for it earlier?\n男:当然!但如果你需要请假，为什么不早点说呢?\n\nW: I''m not sure why. I guess I kind of felt bad asking for it.\n女:我不知道为什么。我想我有点不好意思开口。\n\nM: You shouldn''t feel bad asking for leave, especially if you need it.\n男:你请假不应该觉得不好意思，尤其是你需要请假的时候。\n\nW: I know. You''re right. I''m sorry.\n女:我知道。你是对的。我很抱歉。\n\nM: Look, you''ve been with us almost five years and I personally really value your proficiency at your job.\n男:听着，你在我们公司已经快5年了，我个人很欣赏你对工作的熟练程度。\n\nIt makes my job far easier.\n这让我的工作轻松多了。\n\nIn addition, I can assure you that management as a whole also holds you in high regard.\n此外，我可以向你保证，整个管理层对你评价都很高。\n\nW: Thank you.\n女:谢谢。\n\nM: What I need is for you to be back at your 100%.\n男:我需要的是你能100%恢复。\n\nAre you sure taking two Mondays off will suffice?\n你确定请两个星期一的假就够了吗?\n\nW: It''ll be enough. I''m sure of it.\n女:足够了。我确定。\n\nM: Okay, good. So this is what we''re going to do.\n男:好的，很好。那接下来我们要做的是。\n\nYou will take those days off and I expect that you will gradually come back to your usual self.\n你请那两天的假，我希望你能逐渐恢复到以往的自己。\n\nThen in two months'' time, we will catch up again to see how you are faring.\n然后两个月后，我们会再次见面，看看你的情况怎么样。\n\nW: Sounds good. Thank you for your understanding.\n女: 听起来不错。谢谢您的理解。\n\nQuestions 5 to 8 are based on the conversation you have just heard.\n请根据你刚刚听到的对话回答问题5到8。\n\n5. What do we learn about the woman from the man''s description?\n5. 我们从男士的描述中可以了解到女士的什么信息?\n\n6. What does the woman say she''s experiencing at the moment?\n6. 女士说她此刻正在经历什么?\n\n7. What does the man say makes his job far easier?\n7. 男士说是什么使他的工作轻松得多?\n\n8. What agreement have the speakers reached by the end of the conversation?\n8. 对话结束时，讲话者达成了什么共识?\n\nSection B Directions: In this section, you will hear two passages.\nB节 说明：在本节中，你将会听到两篇短文。', 105, 1563.93, 230.06, 335.00, 374.88, 391.84, NULL, NULL, 'cet6-2023-12-2-g02', 'LONG_DIALOGUE', '[03:50.06]Conversation Two｜对话二\n[03:52.24]W: You wanted to see me?｜女:您找我?\n[03:54.49]M: Yes, I''ll get straight to the point.｜男:是的，我就开门见山了。\n[03:56.87]Over the past month or so, it has become apparent that your performance has dipped.｜在过去一个月左右的时间里，你的表现明显下降了。\n[04:01.47]You''ve been late to work several times these past few weeks, which is very uncharacteristic of you.｜在过去的几个星期里，你迟到了好几次，这很不像你的作风。\n[04:06.99]But what really concerns me is your curtailed output.｜但我真正担心的是你的减产。\n[04:10.59]Lately, you seem to be constantly one step behind.｜最近，你似乎总是落后别人一步。\n[04:13.83]What''s going on?｜发生了什么？\n[04:15.13]W: I''m sorry. I''m going through some unfortunate family issues at the moment.｜女:抱歉。我现在正经历一些不幸的家庭问题。\n[04:19.58]It''s a personal matter. So if you don''t mind, I much prefer we don''t get into it.｜这是个人问题。所以如果你不介意的话，我希望我们不要谈这个。\n[04:24.20]Nevertheless, I expect it to have all blown over in another month or so.｜不过，我预计再过一个月左右，一切都会平息。\n[04:29.20]M: Do you need some time off?｜男:你需要请假吗?\n[04:31.08]W: Actually, yes. Would it be possible to take the next two Mondays off?｜女:事实上，是的。接下来的两个星期一我可以请假吗?\n[04:35.56]I was deliberating whether I should ask for this, but now that we''re here...｜我还在考虑要不要提出这个要求，但既然我们说到这里……\n[04:40.16]M: Sure thing! But if you needed some leave, why didn''t you ask for it earlier?｜男:当然!但如果你需要请假，为什么不早点说呢?\n[04:44.82]W: I''m not sure why. I guess I kind of felt bad asking for it.｜女:我不知道为什么。我想我有点不好意思开口。\n[04:49.27]M: You shouldn''t feel bad asking for leave, especially if you need it.｜男:你请假不应该觉得不好意思，尤其是你需要请假的时候。\n[04:53.09]W: I know. You''re right. I''m sorry.｜女:我知道。你是对的。我很抱歉。\n[04:55.43]M: Look, you''ve been with us almost five years and I personally really value your proficiency at your job.｜男:听着，你在我们公司已经快5年了，我个人很欣赏你对工作的熟练程度。\n[05:01.81]It makes my job far easier.｜这让我的工作轻松多了。\n[05:03.84]In addition, I can assure you that management as a whole also holds you in high regard.｜此外，我可以向你保证，整个管理层对你评价都很高。\n[05:09.21]W: Thank you.｜女:谢谢。\n[05:10.17]M: What I need is for you to be back at your 100%.｜男:我需要的是你能100%恢复。\n[05:13.91]Are you sure taking two Mondays off will suffice?｜你确定请两个星期一的假就够了吗?\n[05:17.08]W: It''ll be enough. I''m sure of it.｜女:足够了。我确定。\n[05:19.11]M: Okay, good. So this is what we''re going to do.｜男:好的，很好。那接下来我们要做的是。\n[05:22.00]You will take those days off and I expect that you will gradually come back to your usual self.｜你请那两天的假，我希望你能逐渐恢复到以往的自己。\n[05:26.84]Then in two months'' time, we will catch up again to see how you are faring.｜然后两个月后，我们会再次见面，看看你的情况怎么样。\n[05:31.19]W: Sounds good. Thank you for your understanding.｜女: 听起来不错。谢谢您的理解。\n[05:35.00]Questions 5 to 8 are based on the conversation you have just heard.｜请根据你刚刚听到的对话回答问题5到8。\n[05:39.22]5. What do we learn about the woman from the man''s description?｜5. 我们从男士的描述中可以了解到女士的什么信息?\n[05:57.04]6. What does the woman say she''s experiencing at the moment?｜6. 女士说她此刻正在经历什么?\n[06:14.88]7. What does the man say makes his job far easier?｜7. 男士说是什么使他的工作轻松得多?\n[06:32.14]8. What agreement have the speakers reached by the end of the conversation?｜8. 对话结束时，讲话者达成了什么共识?\n[06:51.78]Section B Directions: In this section, you will hear two passages.｜B节 说明：在本节中，你将会听到两篇短文。', NOW(), NOW()
