SELECT
  @a_cet6_2024_06_1_02, '/audio/exams/listening-cet6-2024-06-1.mp3', 'Conversation One\n对话一\n\nW：Thank you for meeting with me, Stephen, at such short notice.\n女：谢谢你在这么短的时间内和我见面，斯蒂芬。\n\nM：Not a problem, Margaret. Now, please give me some good news. Have you agreed to my last proposal?\n男：不是问题，玛格丽特。现在，请给我一些好消息。你同意我上次的提议了吗?\n\nW：I have, indeed. And I wish to sign the agreement pending one small change to be made to the contract.\n女：我同意，确实是。而且我希望在协议上签字，但合同需要稍作修改。\n\nM：Margaret, we have been through this for almost a year now, back and forth, making alterations.\n男：玛格丽特，我们已经讨论这个问题快一年了，来来回回，不断修改。\n\nAre you sure you want to make a sponsorship deal for your clients, or not?\n你确定想为你的客户做赞助协议，还是不想做?\n\nI ask this, because, frankly, some people at my end are running out of patience.\n我问这个问题，是因为，坦率地说，我这边的一些人已经要失去耐心了。\n\nW：I understand your concerns. But as I''m sure you understand, we hold our clients'' best interests to be of the utmost concern.\n女：我理解你的担忧。但我相信你能理解，我们把客户的最大利益放在第一位。\n\nWe therefore come through the fine details of all contracts, rest assured, we all appreciate your firm''s patience.\n因此，我们仔细检查了所有合同的细节，请放心，我们非常感谢贵公司的耐心。\n\nM：OK, fine. So what changes do you wish to make?\n男：好，很好。那么你希望做什么改变呢?\n\nW：Essentially, we would like the new deal to exclude the Middle East. That''s all.\n女：从本质上讲，我们希望新协议将中东排除在外。就这些。\n\nM：The Middle East. Why?\n男：中东。为什么?\n\nW：My client has a couple of other prospective marketing deals from companies in the Middle East.\n女：我的客户与一些中东公司还有其他几笔有望谈成的市场交易。\n\nThose offers, should they materialize, would exclusively employ my client''s image in the Middle East only.\n那些提议，如果成为现实，只会在中东地区使用我委托人的形象。\n\nTherefore, in order to avoid any conflict, we would need to ensure that both marketing campaigns do not overlap geographically.\n因此，为了避免冲突，我们需要确保两个营销活动在地理上不重叠。\n\nM：What business sector in the Middle East are we talking about here?\n男：我们在这里谈论的是中东的哪个商业部门?\n\nW：Real estate.\n女：房地产。\n\nM：Well, that should be okay then. So long as the product is very different from our food and beverage market, there should be no conflict of interest.\n男：嗯，那应该没问题。只要产品与我们的餐饮市场有很大的不同，就不应该存在利益冲突。\n\nNevertheless, I will have to run this through my people.\n尽管如此，我还是得跟我的人说一下。\n\nI don''t foresee any problem, though.\n不过我不认为会有什么问题。\n\nThe Middle East is a negligible market for us, but I still need to check this with a couple of departments.\n中东对我们来说是一个微不足道的市场，但我还需要和几个部门核实一下。\n\nQuestions 1 to 4 are based on the conversation you have just heard.\n请根据你刚刚听到的对话回答问题1到4。\n\n1. What does the woman say she will do?\n1.女士说她要做什么?\n\n2.What does the man say about some people he represents?\n2.关于自己所代表的一些人，男士说了什么？\n\n3.What reason does the woman give for the new deal to exclude the Middle East?\n3.新协议要排除中东，女士给出的理由是什么?\n\n4.What does the man say about the Middle East?\n4. 关于中东，男士说了什么?', 111, 1620.24, 34.48, 145.64, 167.04, 185.27, NULL, NULL, 'cet6-2024-06-1-g01', 'LONG_DIALOGUE', '[00:34.48]Conversation One｜对话一\n[00:36.16]W：Thank you for meeting with me, Stephen, at such short notice.｜女：谢谢你在这么短的时间内和我见面，斯蒂芬。\n[00:40.08]M：Not a problem, Margaret. Now, please give me some good news. Have you agreed to my last proposal?｜男：不是问题，玛格丽特。现在，请给我一些好消息。你同意我上次的提议了吗?\n[00:47.13]W：I have, indeed. And I wish to sign the agreement pending one small change to be made to the contract.｜女：我同意，确实是。而且我希望在协议上签字，但合同需要稍作修改。\n[00:53.34]M：Margaret, we have been through this for almost a year now, back and forth, making alterations.｜男：玛格丽特，我们已经讨论这个问题快一年了，来来回回，不断修改。\n[00:59.03]Are you sure you want to make a sponsorship deal for your clients, or not?｜你确定想为你的客户做赞助协议，还是不想做?\n[01:03.39]I ask this, because, frankly, some people at my end are running out of patience.｜我问这个问题，是因为，坦率地说，我这边的一些人已经要失去耐心了。\n[01:08.47]W：I understand your concerns. But as I''m sure you understand, we hold our clients'' best interests to be of the utmost concern.｜女：我理解你的担忧。但我相信你能理解，我们把客户的最大利益放在第一位。\n[01:16.66]We therefore come through the fine details of all contracts, rest assured, we all appreciate your firm''s patience.｜因此，我们仔细检查了所有合同的细节，请放心，我们非常感谢贵公司的耐心。\n[01:24.34]M：OK, fine. So what changes do you wish to make?｜男：好，很好。那么你希望做什么改变呢?\n[01:28.76]W：Essentially, we would like the new deal to exclude the Middle East. That''s all.｜女：从本质上讲，我们希望新协议将中东排除在外。就这些。\n[01:34.49]M：The Middle East. Why?｜男：中东。为什么?\n[01:36.18]W：My client has a couple of other prospective marketing deals from companies in the Middle East.｜女：我的客户与一些中东公司还有其他几笔有望谈成的市场交易。\n[01:42.20]Those offers, should they materialize, would exclusively employ my client''s image in the Middle East only.｜那些提议，如果成为现实，只会在中东地区使用我委托人的形象。\n[01:49.00]Therefore, in order to avoid any conflict, we would need to ensure that both marketing campaigns do not overlap geographically.｜因此，为了避免冲突，我们需要确保两个营销活动在地理上不重叠。\n[01:58.17]M：What business sector in the Middle East are we talking about here?｜男：我们在这里谈论的是中东的哪个商业部门?\n[02:01.90]W：Real estate.｜女：房地产。\n[02:03.60]M：Well, that should be okay then. So long as the product is very different from our food and beverage market, there should be no conflict of interest.｜男：嗯，那应该没问题。只要产品与我们的餐饮市场有很大的不同，就不应该存在利益冲突。\n[02:12.62]Nevertheless, I will have to run this through my people.｜尽管如此，我还是得跟我的人说一下。\n[02:16.50]I don''t foresee any problem, though.｜不过我不认为会有什么问题。\n[02:19.20]The Middle East is a negligible market for us, but I still need to check this with a couple of departments.｜中东对我们来说是一个微不足道的市场，但我还需要和几个部门核实一下。\n[02:25.64]Questions 1 to 4 are based on the conversation you have just heard.｜请根据你刚刚听到的对话回答问题1到4。\n[02:30.35]1. What does the woman say she will do?｜1.女士说她要做什么?\n[02:47.04]2.What does the man say about some people he represents?｜2.关于自己所代表的一些人，男士说了什么？\n[03:05.57]3.What reason does the woman give for the new deal to exclude the Middle East?｜3.新协议要排除中东，女士给出的理由是什么?\n[03:25.45]4.What does the man say about the Middle East?｜4. 关于中东，男士说了什么?', NOW(), NOW()
