hat store-bought juice is like 10% sugar?\n你知道商店买来的果汁里10%是糖吗？\n\nW：Right. So then you bought it for the health benefits?\n女：是啊。那你买搅拌机是出于健康原因吗？\n\nM：Mostly yes. Basically, it allows me to have a more varied diet with a far wider assortment of nutrients.\n男：主要是。从根本上说，它让我的饮食更加多样化，营养成分种类更丰富。\n\nBecause it''s not only fruit in my morning juices you see, I can also throw in vegetables, nuts, yogurts, cereals, anything that tickles my fancy.\n因为你所看到的我早上的果汁里不仅有水果，我还可以加入蔬菜、坚果、酸奶、谷物，只要是我喜欢的东西就行。\n\nQuestions 1 to 4 are based on the conversation you have just heard.\n请根据你刚刚听到的对话回答问题1到4。\n\n1. What does the man say he did before buying the blender?\n1. 男士说他在买搅拌机之前做了什么？\n\n2.What does the woman say she has never thought of doing?\n2. 女士说她从来没有想过要做什么？\n\n3.What does the man say is a really healthy habit?\n3. 男士说什么是真正健康的习惯？\n\n4.What do we learn about store-bought juice from the conversation?\n4. 从对话中，我们对从商店里买来的果汁有何了解？', 116, 1548.89, 33.87, 149.79, 207.00, 225.35, NULL, NULL, 'cet6-2024-06-2-g01', 'LONG_DIALOGUE', '[00:33.87]Conversation One｜对话一\n[00:36.34]M：I''ve just bought a new blender.｜男：我刚买了一台新的搅拌机。\n[00:39.27]W：What''s that?｜女：那是什么？\n[00:40.57]M：A blender, you know, a machine that blends food.｜男：搅拌机，你知道，一种搅拌食物的机器。\n[00:44.30]W：Ah, yes, of course. The electric kitchen appliance.｜女：啊，是的，当然。厨房电器。\n[00:48.00]M：Exactly. This one is state of the art. I''ve been meaning to buy one for a while and I did thorough research on which specific model to get.｜男：没错。这台是最先进的。我想买台搅拌机已经有一段时间了，对该买哪种型号做了全面的研究。\n[00:57.24]I read through maybe hundreds of online user reviews. Anyway, it''s amazing.｜我阅读了数百条在线用户评论。不管怎样，它太棒了。\n[01:02.35]W：Really? What could be so special about it? I mean, it''s just a blender.｜女：真的吗？它有什么特别之处？我的意思是，它只是一台搅拌机。\n[01:06.61]M：Well, basically, it''s just a very good one. It feels heavy and sturdy and well-made.｜男：好吧，根本上说，这台机器非常好。它手感很沉稳，很结实，而且制作精良。\n[01:12.73]It also has lots of power and can easily cut and crush practically anything.｜它功率也很大，可以很容易地切割和粉碎几乎任何东西。\n[01:17.69]This way, the soups and juices I make come out really fine and smooth, with no lumpy bits.｜这样，我做出来的汤和果汁就非常细腻，没有结块。\n[01:23.65]W：Hmm, I see. I''ve never thought of getting one myself.｜女：嗯，我明白了。我自己从没想过要买一台。\n[01:27.83]It sounds like the kind of thing that, for me personally, I would rarely use.｜这听起来就像是我自己几乎用不到的东西。\n[01:32.44]M：I''ve never had one before.｜男：我之前也没有。\n[01:34.16]And now that I do, I use it all the time.｜现在有了它，我就一直在用。\n[01:36.91]I make a fresh fruit juice in the morning, maybe not every morning, but three or four times a week, and it feels fantastic.｜早上我会（用它）做新鲜的果汁，也不是每天早上，一周三四次吧，感觉好极了。\n[01:45.00]It''s a really healthy habit.｜这是个非常健康的习惯。\n[01:46.61]W：I can imagine that must feel quite satisfying.｜女：可以想象，那肯定让人感觉心满意足。\n[01:50.13]I can picture you getting all creative in the kitchen and trying out a multitude of different ingredients.｜我可以想象你在厨房里发挥创意，尝试多种不同的食材。\n[01:56.00]And it''s obviously going to be healthier than buying packaged juice from a supermarket.｜而且，很明显，那肯定比从超市买包装好的果汁更健康。\n[02:01.28]M：It''s so much healthier. It''s not even close.｜男：健康多了。根本没法比。\n[02:04.67]Did you know that store-bought juice is like 10% sugar?｜你知道商店买来的果汁里10%是糖吗？\n[02:08.51]W：Right. So then you bought it for the health benefits?｜女：是啊。那你买搅拌机是出于健康原因吗？\n[02:12.21]M：Mostly yes. Basically, it allows me to have a more varied diet with a far wider assortment of nutrients.｜男：主要是。从根本上说，它让我的饮食更加多样化，营养成分种类更丰富。\n[02:19.66]Because it''s not only fruit in my morning juices you see, I can also throw in vegetables, nuts, yogurts, cereals, anything that tickles my fancy.｜因为你所看到的我早上的果汁里不仅有水果，我还可以加入蔬菜、坚果、酸奶、谷物，只要是我喜欢的东西就行。\n[02:29.79]Questions 1 to 4 are based on the conversation you have just heard.｜请根据你刚刚听到的对话回答问题1到4。\n[02:34.32]1. What does the man say he did before buying the blender?｜1. 男士说他在买搅拌机之前做了什么？\n[02:52.34]2.What does the woman say she has never thought of doing?｜2. 女士说她从来没有想过要做什么？\n[03:09.44]3.What does the man say is a really healthy habit?｜3. 男士说什么是真正健康的习惯？\n[03:27.00]4.What do we learn