SELECT
  @a_cet6_2024_06_2_15, '/audio/exams/listening-cet6-2024-06-2.mp3', 'Passage Two\n短文二\n\nI don''t want to boast or anything, but I''ve always considered myself something of an elite sleeper.\n我不想吹嘘什么，但我一直认为自己是个精英睡眠者。\n\nGiven the opportunity, I will sleep for marathon stretches and can doze through the most extreme situations.\n只要有机会，我的睡眠时间可以达到马拉松式的长度，并且我在最极端的情况下也能睡着。\n\nOn one very rough ferry crossing on the route to the Isles of Scilly, for example, my travelling companions spent the entire three-hour ride throwing up in the bathroom while I dozed happily on a plastic chair.\n例如，有一次乘渡轮前往锡利群岛，路途十分艰难，我的旅伴们在浴室里吐了整整三个小时，而我则在塑料椅子上愉快地打瞌睡。\n\nUnfortunately, it has come to my attention that I am not an elite sleeper after all. It seems I am just lazy.\n不幸的是，我后来意识到我其实不算是精英睡眠者，看起来我只是比较懒。\n\nBecause elite sleepers are defined as the approximately 3% of the population who are biologically programmed to need less sleep than the rest of us.\n依照定义，只有大约3%的人口是精英睡眠者，从生理上，他们就比我们其他人需要的睡眠更少。\n\nAccording to a study that came out in March, elite sleepers have rare genetic changes, which means they can sleep fewer hours than mere mortals without any risk of cognitive decline.\n根据3月份发布的一项研究，精英睡眠者拥有罕见的基因变化，这意味着他们可以比普通人睡更少的时间，但却不会出现任何认知能力下降的风险。\n\nIt may not be possible to change your own genes, but can you train yourself to need less sleep? Is there a non-biological way to reach elite sleeper status?\n改变你自己的基因也许并不可能，但你能通过训练减少自己的睡眠吗？有没有一种非生物学的方式可以（让普通人）达到精英睡眠者的状态呢？\n\nI have spent the past year trying to answer that question.\n在过去的一年里，我一直在努力寻找这个问题的答案。\n\nNot for fun, I should add, but because having a baby has severely disrupted my sleep, for which I still have a great passion.\n我应该补充说明，这么做不是为了好玩，而是因为生孩子严重扰乱了我的睡眠，可我对睡眠一事却满怀热情。\n\nFor a while, I assumed I''d be forced to become one of those people who jump out of bed at the crack of dawn.\n有一段时间，我以为我会被迫成为那种在黎明时分就能从床上跳起来的人。\n\nAfter a year of tough scientific study, however, I have discovered being forced to get up early in the morning is very different from being an early bird.\n然而，经过一年的艰苦的科学研究，我发现被迫早起与天生能够早起还是有很大的不同。\n\nQuestions 12 to 15 are based on the passage you have just heard.\n请根据你刚刚听到的短文回答问题12到15。\n\n12. What does the speaker say she did on her ride to the Isles of Scilly?\n12. 讲话者说她在去锡利群岛的路上做了什么？\n\n13.What do we learn from the passage about elite sleepers?\n13. 关于精英睡眠者，我们可以从这篇文章中了解到什么？\n\n14.What has the speaker been trying to find out over the past year?\n14. 讲话者在过去的一年里一直试图了解什么？\n\n15.What has the speaker discovered after a year of tough scientific study?\n15. 经过一年艰难的科学研究，讲话者有何发现？\n\nSection C Directions: In this section, you will hear three recordings of lectures or talks followed by three or four questions.\nC节 说明：在本节中，你将会听到三篇讲座或讲话，每篇讲座或讲话后面都有三个或四个问题。', 109, 1548.89, 623.75, 732.45, 793.80, 813.80, 722.51, 732.15, 'cet6-2024-06-2-g04', 'PASSAGE', '[10:23.75]Passage Two｜短文二\n[10:30.81]I don''t want to boast or anything, but I''ve always considered myself something of an elite sleeper.｜我不想吹嘘什么，但我一直认为自己是个精英睡眠者。\n[10:37.40]Given the opportunity, I will sleep for marathon stretches and can doze through the most extreme situations.｜只要有机会，我的睡眠时间可以达到马拉松式的长度，并且我在最极端的情况下也能睡着。\n[10:44.73]On one very rough ferry crossing on the route to the Isles of Scilly, for example, my travelling companions spent the entire three-hour ride throwing up in the bathroom while I dozed happily on a plastic chair.｜例如，有一次乘渡轮前往锡利群岛，路途十分艰难，我的旅伴们在浴室里吐了整整三个小时，而我则在塑料椅子上愉快地打瞌睡。\n[10:58.77]Unfortunately, it has come to my attention that I am not an elite sleeper after all. It seems I am just lazy.｜不幸的是，我后来意识到我其实不算是精英睡眠者，看起来我只是比较懒。\n[11:06.74]Because elite sleepers are defined as the approximately 3% of the population who are biologically programmed to need less sleep than the rest of us.｜依照定义，只有大约3%的人口是精英睡眠者，从生理上，他们就比我们其他人需要的睡眠更少。\n[11:17.48]According to a study that came out in March, elite sleepers have rare genetic changes, which means they can sleep fewer hours than mere mortals without any risk of cognitive decline.｜根据3月份发布的一项研究，精英睡眠者拥有罕见的基因变化，这意味着他们可以比普通人睡更少的时间，但却不会出现任何认知能力下降的风险。\n[11:29.93]It may not be possible to change your own genes, but can you train yourself to need less sleep? Is there a non-biological way to reach elite sleeper status?｜改变你自己的基因也许并不可能，但你能通过训练减少自己的睡眠吗？有没有一种非生物学的方式可以（让普通人）达到精英睡眠者的状态呢？\n[11:42.16]I have spent the past year trying to answer that question.｜在过去的一年里，我一直在努力寻找这个问题的答案。\n[11:46.36]Not for fun, I should add, but because having a baby has severely disrupted my sleep, for which I still have a great passion.｜我应该补充说明，这么做不是为了好玩，而是因为生孩子严重扰乱了我的睡眠，可我对睡眠一事却满怀热情。\n[11:55.15]For a while, I assumed I''d be forced to become one of those people who jump out of bed at the crack of dawn.｜有一段时间，我以为我会被迫成为那种在黎明时分就能从床上跳起来的人。\n[12:02.51]After a year of tough scientific study, however, I have discovered being forced to get up early in the morning is very different from being an early bird.｜然而，经过一年的艰苦的科学研究，我发现被迫早起与天生能够早起还是有很大的不同。\n[12:12.45]Questions 12 to 15 are based on the passage you have just heard.｜请根据你刚刚听到的短文回答问题12到15。\n[12:17.60]12. What does the speaker say she did on her ride to the Isles of Scilly?｜12. 讲话者说她在去锡利群岛的路上做了什么？\n[12:36.40]13.What do we learn from the passage about elite sleepers?｜13. 关于精英睡眠者，我们可以从这篇文章中了解到什么？\n[12:55.05]14.What has the speaker been trying to find out over the past year?｜14. 讲话者在过去的一年里一直试图了解什么？\n[13:13.80]15.What has the speaker discovered after a year of tough scientific study?｜15. 经过一年艰难的科学研究，讲话者有何发现？\n[13:33.29]Section C Directions: In this section, you will hear three recordings of lectures or talks followed by three or four questions.｜C节 说明：在本节中，你将会听到三篇讲座或讲话，每篇讲座或讲话后面都有三个或四个问题。', NOW(), NOW()
