  @a_cet6_2024_12_1_02, '/audio/exams/listening-cet6-2024-12-1.mp3', 'Conversation One\n对话一\n\nM: OK then, this here is your yearly performance review.\n男：好吧，这是你的年度绩效评估。\n\nYou''ve been with the company for 3 years and under my direct supervision for the past 12 months.\n你已经在公司工作3年了，过去的12个月里一直在我的直接管理下。\n\nYour report is mostly good. But there are a couple of issues we must discuss.\n你的评估报告大部分还不错。但有几个问题我们必须讨论一下。\n\nThe report is yours to take with you. We''ll go through the main points together now.\n这份报告你可以拿着。我们现在要一起把要点过一遍。\n\nAnd you can comb through it in greater detail later.\n稍后你可以详细地梳理一遍评估报告。\n\nDo you have any questions before we start?\n在我们开始之前你有什么问题吗？\n\nW: No, sir.\n女：没有，先生。\n\nM: I''ll get straight to it then.\n男：那我就直说了。\n\nIt is evident that you are a hard worker. You are punctual and industrious.\n很明显你工作很努力。你守时而且勤奋。\n\nFurthermore, you have strong analytical skills and attention to detail.\n此外，你有很强的分析能力并且非常关注细节。\n\nThe company, myself included, are happy with your productivity and overall performance.\n公司，包括我自己，对你的工作效率和整体表现都很满意。\n\nW: Thank you. I appreciate the recognition.\n女：谢谢。我感谢您的认可。\n\nM: Do you agree, then, with this depiction so far?\n男：那么，目前为止，你同意这些描述吗？\n\nW: Yeah, it''s a little simplistic perhaps.\n女：是的，这可能有点过于简单了。\n\nBut that''s to be expected from this kind of evaluation.\n但这种评估是意料之中的\n\nM: Sure. Would you want to add anything?\n男：当然。你想要补充什么吗？\n\nYour comments can be added to the report if you wish.\n如果你愿意的话，你的意见可以添加到评估报告中。\n\nW: Oh, there''s no need. It''s a flattering portrayal really. Thank you, though.\n女：哦，没有必要。这真的是一种讨人喜欢的描述。不过还是谢谢你。\n\nM: OK. This leads me to the not-so-good part.\n男：好吧。这就引出了不太好的部分。\n\nThis mostly centers around one behavioral aspect—your ability to work with others.\n这主要集中在一个行为方面——你与他人合作的能力。\n\nW: I see.\n女：我明白了。\n\nM: Yes. As you already know, over the last several months, there have been some complaints raised about your communication style.\n男：是的。如你所知，在过去的几个月里, 有人对你的沟通方式提出了一些抱怨。\n\nW: Of course, we already had like three meetings about this.\n女：当然，我们已经为此开了三次会了。\n\nLook, all I''m going to say is that it was never my intention to offend anyone.\n听着，我要说的是我从来没有想要冒犯任何人。\n\nSimply put, I don''t like to write long emails, because, frankly, I think they''re a waste of time.\n简单地说，我不喜欢写冗长的电子邮件，因为坦率地说，我认为那是浪费时间。\n\nConciseness is efficiency.\n简洁就是效率。\n\nI feel that writing long emails hurts that same productivity you praised me for just a minute ago.\n我觉得写冗长的电子邮件同样会影响效率，您一分钟前还夸过我有效率。\n\nAnd I already apologized if anyone was offended.\n如果有人被冒犯了，我已经道歉了。\n\nBut to be perfectly honest, I think anyone who was offended was being a little too sensitive.\n但说实话，我认为被冒犯的人都有点太敏感了。\n\nQuestions 1 to 4 are based on the conversation you have just heard.\n请根据你刚刚听到的对话回答问题1到4。\n\n1. What are the speakers most probably doing?\n1.讲话者最有可能在干什么?\n\n2.What does the woman say she appreciates?\n2.女士说她感谢什么？\n\n3.What has given rise to some complaints about the woman?\n3.是什么引起了对该女士的一些抱怨？\n\n4.Why doesn''t the woman like to write long emails?\n4.为什么女士不喜欢写冗长的电子邮件？', 136, 1666.14, 33.80, 170.25, 191.10, 209.79, NULL, NULL, 'cet6-2024-12-1-g01', 'LONG_DIALOGUE', '[00:33.80]Conversation One｜对话一\n[00:36.85]M: OK then, this here is your yearly performance review.｜男：好吧，这是你的年度绩效评估。\n[00:41.81]You''ve been with the company for 3 years and under my direct supervision for the past 12 months.｜你已经在公司工作3年了，过去的12个月里一直在我的直接管理下。\n[00:47.40]Your report is mostly good. But there are a couple of issues we must discuss.｜你的评估报告大部分还不错。但有几个问题我们必须讨论一下。\n[00:53.16]The report is yours to take with you. We''ll go through the main points together now.｜这份报告你可以拿着。我们现在要一起把要点过一遍。\n[00:58.79]And you can comb through it in greater detail later.｜稍后你可以详细地梳理一遍评估报告。\n[01:01.98]Do you have any questions before we start?｜在我们开始之前你有什么问题吗？\n[01:04.83]W: No, sir.｜女：没有，先生。\n[01:05.76]M: I''ll get straight to it then.｜男：那我就直说了。\n[01:07.64]It is evident that you are a hard worker. You are punctual and industrious.｜很明显你工作很努力。你守时而且勤奋。\n[01:14.65]Furthermore, you have strong analytical skills and attention to detail.｜此外，你有很强的分析能力并且非常关注细节。\n[01:19.40]The company, myself included, are happy with your productivity and overall performance.｜公司，包括我自己，对你的工作效率和整体表现都很满意。\n[01:25.43]W: Thank you. I appreciate the recognition.｜女：谢谢。我感谢您的认可。\n[01:28.10]M: Do you agree, then, with this depiction so far?｜男：那么，目前为止，你同意这些描述吗？\n[01:32.02]W: Yeah, it''s a little simplistic perhaps.｜女：是的，这可能有点过于简单了。\n[01:35.73]But that''s to be expected from this kind of evaluation.｜但这种评估是意料之中的\n[01:38.75]M: Sure. Would you want to add anything?｜男：当然。你想要补充什么吗？\n[01:42.50]Your comments can be added to the report if you wish.｜如果你愿意的话，你的意见可以添加到评估报告中。\n[01:46.67]W: Oh, there''s no need. It''s a flattering portrayal really. Thank you, though.｜女：哦，没有必要。这真的是一种讨人喜欢的描述。不过还是谢谢你。\n[01:52.00]M: OK. This leads me to the not-so-good part.｜男：好吧。这就引出了不太好的部分。\n[01:56.62]This mostly centers around one behavioral aspect—your ability to work with others.｜这主要集中在一个行为方面——你与他人合作的能力。\n[02:04.43]W: I see.｜女：我明白了。\n[02:05.14]M: Yes. As you already know, over the last several months, there have been some complaints raised about your communication style.｜男：是的。如你所知，在过去的几个月里, 有人对你的沟通方式提出了一些抱怨。\n[02:14.69]W: Of course, we already had like three meetings about this.｜女：当然，我们已经为此开了三次会了。\n[02:18.84]Look, all I''m going to say is that it was never my intention to offend anyone.｜听着，我要说的是我从来没有想要冒犯任何人。\n[02:24.00]Simply put, I don''t like to write long emails, because, frankly, I think they''re a waste of time.｜简单地说，我不喜欢写冗长的电子邮件，因为坦率地说，我认为那是浪费时间。\n[02:30.71]Conciseness is efficiency.｜简洁就是效率。\n[02:33.48]I feel that writing long emails hurts that same productivity you praised me for just a minute ago.｜我觉得写冗长的电子邮件同样会影响效率，您一分钟前还夸过我有效率。\n[02:39.83]And I already apologized if anyone was offended.｜如果有人被冒犯了，我已经道歉了。\n[02:43.25]But to be perfectly honest, I think anyone who was offended was being a little too sensitive.｜但说实话，我认为被冒犯的人都有点太敏感了。\n[02:50.25]Questions 1 to 4 are based on the conversation you have just heard.｜请根据你刚刚听到的对话回答问题1到4。\n[02:55.40]1. What are the speakers most probably doing?｜1.讲话者最有可能在干什么?\n[03:11.10]2.What does the woman say she appreciates?｜2.女士说她感谢什么？\n[03:30.09]3.What has given rise to some complaints about the woman?｜3.是什么引起了对该女士的一些抱怨？\n[03:48.92]4.Why doesn''t the woman like to write long emails?｜4.为什么女士不喜欢写冗长的电子邮件？', NOW(), NOW()
