SELECT
  @a_cet6_2024_12_1_05, '/audio/exams/listening-cet6-2024-12-1.mp3', 'Conversation Two\n对话二\n\nM: So tell me, why do you wish to study medicine?\n男：告诉我，你为什么想学医？\n\nW: I''ve always wanted to be a doctor.\n女：我一直想成为一名医生。\n\nI come from a small town where healthcare was never the best.\n我来自一个小镇，那里的医疗保健从来都不是最好的。\n\nAnd I think that had a profound effect on me.\n我认为这对我影响深远。\n\nAs a child, I remember thinking how great it would be to serve the community and cure people!\n我记得小时候，我一直在想，如果能服务社区，治愈病人，那该有多好啊！\n\nM: What other people or events in your life have shaped your interest in becoming a doctor?\n男：你生活中的其他什么人或事件使你对成为一名医生产生了兴趣？\n\nW: Well, that''s hard to say.\n女：嗯，这很难说。\n\nI would certainly say my parents have been a key factor.\n我肯定地说我的父母是一个关键因素。\n\nThey always pushed me to study hard.\n他们总是督促我努力学习。\n\nAnd I certainly wouldn''t be here without their support.\n而且如果没有他们的支持，我今天也不会站在这里。\n\nI guess I was also immensely fortunate to have good teachers and friends around me.\n我想我也非常幸运，身边有好老师和好朋友。\n\nAt the end of the day, I''ve always been surrounded by a positive environment conducive to my working hard and pursuing my dreams.\n在一天结束的时候，我总是被一个积极的环境所包围，有利于我努力工作和追求梦想。\n\nM: Is there any medical branch that you would like to specialize in?\n男：有没有你想专攻的医学分支？\n\nW: I haven''t decided yet. It''s still early days.\n女：我还没决定。现在还为时尚早。\n\nHowever, if I had to say, internal medicine.\n但是，如果非得说的话，那就是内科。\n\nM: Why internal medicine?\n男：为什么是内科？\n\nW: I know it''s no picnic.\n女：我知道这并不容易。\n\nBut I find it the most intriguing, because it covers so much and ties together so many other specialties.\n但我觉得它是最有趣的，因为它涵盖的内容太多了，而且把许多其他专业联系在一起。\n\nM: Thank you. Now I''d like to address your academic history and projected grades.\n男：谢谢。现在我想谈谈你的学习经历和预期成绩。\n\nWe like to think of ourselves as a prestigious institution with a highly competitive and promising student body.\n我们认为我们是一所享有盛誉的学校，拥有竞争激烈、前途光明的学生群体。\n\nAs you know, to get into our programmes, you need at least 85% score in the entrance exam.\n如你所知，要进入我们大学，你需要在入学考试中获得至少85%的分数。\n\nDo you think you can attain this?\n你认为你能做到这一点吗？\n\nW: I think so. Yes.\n女：我想是的。是的。\n\nM: I''m looking at your school grades now and I''ll be honest.\n男：我现在正在看你的学习成绩，我会实话实说。\n\nIt''s a bit of a mixed bag. You do get top grades here and there, but you are not very...Shall we say “consistent”?\n你的学习成绩参差不齐。你确实时不时得高分。但你并不是特别……我们可以说“稳定”吗？\n\nI see no problem in making you a conditional offer, but consider yourself warned, our entrance exam is, to use your own words, no picnic.\n我觉得给你一个有条件的录取是没有问题的，但你要小心，用你自己的话来说，我们的入学考试可不容易。\n\nQuestions 5 to 8 are based on the conversation you have just heard.\n请根据你刚刚听到的对话回答问题5到8。\n\n5. What does the woman say she has always wanted to do since childhood?\n5. 女士说她从小就一直想做什么？\n\n6.What do we learn about the woman''s parents from the conversation?\n6. 关于女士的父母，我们从对话中了解到什么？\n\n7.Why does the woman say she wants to choose internal medicine as her specialty?\n7. 为什么女士说她想选择内科作为她的专业？\n\n8.How does the man describe the woman''s school grades?\n8. 关于女士的学习成绩，男士是如何描述的？\n\nSection B Directions: In this section, you will hear two passages.\nB节 说明：在本节中，你将会听到两篇短文。', 122, 1666.14, 247.48, 369.74, 374.20, 392.20, NULL, NULL, 'cet6-2024-12-1-g02', 'LONG_DIALOGUE', '[04:07.48]Conversation Two｜对话二\n[04:10.15]M: So tell me, why do you wish to study medicine?｜男：告诉我，你为什么想学医？\n[04:14.57]W: I''ve always wanted to be a doctor.｜女：我一直想成为一名医生。\n[04:16.82]I come from a small town where healthcare was never the best.｜我来自一个小镇，那里的医疗保健从来都不是最好的。\n[04:20.63]And I think that had a profound effect on me.｜我认为这对我影响深远。\n[04:23.58]As a child, I remember thinking how great it would be to serve the community and cure people!｜我记得小时候，我一直在想，如果能服务社区，治愈病人，那该有多好啊！\n[04:29.47]M: What other people or events in your life have shaped your interest in becoming a doctor?｜男：你生活中的其他什么人或事件使你对成为一名医生产生了兴趣？\n[04:34.91]W: Well, that''s hard to say.｜女：嗯，这很难说。\n[04:37.01]I would certainly say my parents have been a key factor.｜我肯定地说我的父母是一个关键因素。\n[04:40.37]They always pushed me to study hard.｜他们总是督促我努力学习。\n[04:42.63]And I certainly wouldn''t be here without their support.｜而且如果没有他们的支持，我今天也不会站在这里。\n[04:46.09]I guess I was also immensely fortunate to have good teachers and friends around me.｜我想我也非常幸运，身边有好老师和好朋友。\n[04:51.02]At the end of the day, I''ve always been surrounded by a positive environment conducive to my working hard and pursuing my dreams.｜在一天结束的时候，我总是被一个积极的环境所包围，有利于我努力工作和追求梦想。\n[04:59.39]M: Is there any medical branch that you would like to specialize in?｜男：有没有你想专攻的医学分支？\n[05:03.24]W: I haven''t decided yet. It''s still early days.｜女：我还没决定。现在还为时尚早。\n[05:06.77]However, if I had to say, internal medicine.｜但是，如果非得说的话，那就是内科。\n[05:11.09]M: Why internal medicine?｜男：为什么是内科？\n[05:13.21]W: I know it''s no picnic.｜女：我知道这并不容易。\n[05:14.62]But I find it the most intriguing, because it covers so much and ties together so many other specialties.｜但我觉得它是最有趣的，因为它涵盖的内容太多了，而且把许多其他专业联系在一起。\n[05:21.28]M: Thank you. Now I''d like to address your academic history and projected grades.｜男：谢谢。现在我想谈谈你的学习经历和预期成绩。\n[05:26.32]We like to think of ourselves as a prestigious institution with a highly competitive and promising student body.｜我们认为我们是一所享有盛誉的学校，拥有竞争激烈、前途光明的学生群体。\n[05:34.83]As you know, to get into our programmes, you need at least 85% score in the entrance exam.｜如你所知，要进入我们大学，你需要在入学考试中获得至少85%的分数。\n[05:41.53]Do you think you can attain this?｜你认为你能做到这一点吗？\n[05:43.69]W: I think so. Yes.｜女：我想是的。是的。\n[05:45.70]M: I''m looking at your school grades now and I''ll be honest.｜男：我现在正在看你的学习成绩，我会实话实说。\n[05:49.64]It''s a bit of a mixed bag. You do get top grades here and there, but you are not very...Shall we say “consistent”?｜你的学习成绩参差不齐。你确实时不时得高分。但你并不是特别……我们可以说“稳定”吗？\n[05:58.72]I see no problem in making you a conditional offer, but consider yourself warned, our entrance exam is, to use your own words, no picnic.｜我觉得给你一个有条件的录取是没有问题的，但你要小心，用你自己的话来说，我们的入学考试可不容易。\n[06:09.74]Questions 5 to 8 are based on the conversation you have just heard.｜请根据你刚刚听到的对话回答问题5到8。\n[06:14.20]5. What does the woman say she has always wanted to do since childhood?｜5. 女士说她从小就一直想做什么？\n[06:32.50]6.What do we learn about the woman''s parents from the conversation?｜6. 关于女士的父母，我们从对话中了解到什么？\n[06:49.81]7.Why does the woman say she wants to choose internal medicine as her specialty?｜7. 为什么女士说她想选择内科作为她的专业？\n[07:10.06]8.How does the man describe the woman''s school grades?｜8. 关于女士的学习成绩，男士是如何描述的？\n[07:27.87]Section B Directions: In this section, you will hear two passages.｜B节 说明：在本节中，你将会听到两篇短文。', NOW(), NOW()
