SELECT
  @a_cet6_2024_12_1_10, '/audio/exams/listening-cet6-2024-12-1.mp3', 'Passage One\n短文一\n\nLogging into your email account can sometimes feel like trying to hack into the Pentagon.\n登录你的电子邮件账户有时感觉就像黑进五角大楼。\n\nIf you follow all of the guidelines, you need to use a different password for every one of your accounts;\n如果你遵循所有的指南，你需要为你的每个帐户使用不同的密码；\n\nuse an incomprehensible variety of letters, numbers, and symbols;\n使用各种难以理解的字母、数字和符号；\n\nsign up for two-step verification;\n注册两步验证；\n\nand change every password every time one of them is compromised.\n每次一个密码被泄露就更改所有密码。\n\nMore often than not, you then have to choose photos that include a street sign, as this apparently provides solid evidence to your computer that you are, in fact, a human being.\n通常情况下，你必须选择包含路牌的照片，因为这显然为你的电脑提供了确凿的证据，证明你实际上是一个人。\n\nIt''s no small wonder most of us forget our passwords more often than our keys.\n难怪我们大多数人忘记密码的次数比忘记钥匙的次数还多。\n\nNow a new peer-reviewed study by researchers at Aalto University in Finland is attempting to figure out why we forget our passwords in order to help put an end to this frustrating phenomenon.\n现在，芬兰阿尔托大学的研究人员进行了一项新的同行评议研究，试图找出我们忘记密码的原因，以帮助结束这一令人沮丧的现象。\n\nTheir findings suggest that how likely you are to remember your password has less to do with the intricacy of the password itself and more to do with how often you anticipate using it.\n他们的研究结果表明，你记住密码的可能性与密码本身的复杂性关系不大，而更多地与你预期使用密码的频率有关。\n\nWhich is to say: you are far more likely to remember a complicated password if you know you''ll frequently be using it to log into an account than you are to remember a simple password for an account that you don''t expect to log into very often.\n也就是说，如果你知道自己将会经常使用一个复杂的密码来登录一个账户，那么你更有可能记住这个密码，而不是为一个你不打算经常登录的账户记住一个简单的密码。\n\nThe researchers advise websites to include more of an incentive for users to log in more often in order to help them remember their secret codes.\n研究人员建议网站提供更多的激励让用户频繁地登录，以帮助他们记住自己的密码。\n\nQuestions 9 to 11 are based on the passage you have just heard.\n请根据你刚刚听到的短文回答问题9到11。\n\n9. Why do we often have to choose photos that include a street sign to log into our email accounts?\n9. 为什么我们经常要选择带有路牌的照片来登录我们的电子邮件账户？\n\n10.What do researchers at a university in Finland aim to do in their new study?\n10. 芬兰一所大学的研究人员进行的新研究的目的是什么？\n\n11.What do the researchers advise websites to do at the end of the passage?\n11.在文章的最后，研究人员建议网站做什么？', 100, 1666.14, 474.45, 574.73, 600.95, 620.95, 520.76, 547.48, 'cet6-2024-12-1-g03', 'PASSAGE', '[07:54.45]Passage One｜短文一\n[07:56.37]Logging into your email account can sometimes feel like trying to hack into the Pentagon.｜登录你的电子邮件账户有时感觉就像黑进五角大楼。\n[08:02.69]If you follow all of the guidelines, you need to use a different password for every one of your accounts;｜如果你遵循所有的指南，你需要为你的每个帐户使用不同的密码；\n[08:08.86]use an incomprehensible variety of letters, numbers, and symbols;｜使用各种难以理解的字母、数字和符号；\n[08:13.98]sign up for two-step verification;｜注册两步验证；\n[08:16.60]and change every password every time one of them is compromised.｜每次一个密码被泄露就更改所有密码。\n[08:21.94]More often than not, you then have to choose photos that include a street sign, as this apparently provides solid evidence to your computer that you are, in fact, a human being.｜通常情况下，你必须选择包含路牌的照片，因为这显然为你的电脑提供了确凿的证据，证明你实际上是一个人。\n[08:34.32]It''s no small wonder most of us forget our passwords more often than our keys.｜难怪我们大多数人忘记密码的次数比忘记钥匙的次数还多。\n[08:40.76]Now a new peer-reviewed study by researchers at Aalto University in Finland is attempting to figure out why we forget our passwords in order to help put an end to this frustrating phenomenon.｜现在，芬兰阿尔托大学的研究人员进行了一项新的同行评议研究，试图找出我们忘记密码的原因，以帮助结束这一令人沮丧的现象。\n[08:55.08]Their findings suggest that how likely you are to remember your password has less to do with the intricacy of the password itself and more to do with how often you anticipate using it.｜他们的研究结果表明，你记住密码的可能性与密码本身的复杂性关系不大，而更多地与你预期使用密码的频率有关。\n[09:07.78]Which is to say: you are far more likely to remember a complicated password if you know you''ll frequently be using it to log into an account than you are to remember a simple password for an account that you don''t expect to log into very often.｜也就是说，如果你知道自己将会经常使用一个复杂的密码来登录一个账户，那么你更有可能记住这个密码，而不是为一个你不打算经常登录的账户记住一个简单的密码。\n[09:24.00]The researchers advise websites to include more of an incentive for users to log in more often in order to help them remember their secret codes.｜研究人员建议网站提供更多的激励让用户频繁地登录，以帮助他们记住自己的密码。\n[09:34.73]Questions 9 to 11 are based on the passage you have just heard.｜请根据你刚刚听到的短文回答问题9到11。\n[09:39.89]9. Why do we often have to choose photos that include a street sign to log into our email accounts?｜9. 为什么我们经常要选择带有路牌的照片来登录我们的电子邮件账户？\n[10:00.95]10.What do researchers at a university in Finland aim to do in their new study?｜10. 芬兰一所大学的研究人员进行的新研究的目的是什么？\n[10:21.25]11.What do the researchers advise websites to do at the end of the passage?｜11.在文章的最后，研究人员建议网站做什么？', NOW(), NOW()
