 to log into an account than you are to remember a simple password for an account that you don''t expect to log into very often.｜也就是说，如果你知道自己将会经常使用一个复杂的密码来登录一个账户，那么你更有可能记住这个密码，而不是为一个你不打算经常登录的账户记住一个简单的密码。\n[09:24.00]The researchers advise websites to include more of an incentive for users to log in more often in order to help them remember their secret codes.｜研究人员建议网站提供更多的激励让用户频繁地登录，以帮助他们记住自己的密码。\n[09:34.73]Questions 9 to 11 are based on the passage you have just heard.｜请根据你刚刚听到的短文回答问题9到11。\n[09:39.89]9. Why do we often have to choose photos that include a street sign to log into our email accounts?｜9. 为什么我们经常要选择带有路牌的照片来登录我们的电子邮件账户？\n[10:00.95]10.What do researchers at a university in Finland aim to do in their new study?｜10. 芬兰一所大学的研究人员进行的新研究的目的是什么？\n[10:21.25]11.What do the researchers advise websites to do at the end of the passage?｜11.在文章的最后，研究人员建议网站做什么？', NOW(), NOW()
