s the largest and most comprehensive and widespread survey of morals ever conducted and aimed to find out whether different societies had different versions of morality.\n发表在《当代人类学》杂志上的这项研究是迄今为止规模最大、最全面、最广泛的道德调查，其目的是找出不同的社会是否有不同版本的道德观念。\n\nThe team accessed the world''s best archives to analyze accounts from more than 600 sources of 60 societies around the world.\n该团队访问了世界上最好的档案以分析600多个来自全球60个社会的账户。\n\nThey found that the seven rules were considered morally good in all societies and were observed across all continents, religions and politics.\n他们发现，这七条准则在所有社会中都被认为是合乎道德的，并且在所有大陆、宗教和政治中都得到遵守。\n\nHowever, some communities valued certain rules more highly than others.\n然而，有些团体比其他团体更重视某些规则。\n\nDr.Curry hopes that this research helps to promote mutual understanding between people of different cultures and appreciation of what we have in common and how and why we differ.\n库里博士希望这项研究有助于促进不同文化背景的人之间的相互理解，并欣赏我们的共同点以及我们如何以及为什么不同。\n\nCo-author professor Harvey Whitehouse said social scientists should now set about testing the theory in the field, rather than relying on old data.\n合著者哈维·怀特豪斯教授说，社会科学家现在应该着手在实地检验这一理论，而不是依靠旧数据。\n\n“This study was based on historical descriptions of cultures around the world,” he said.\n他说：“这项研究是基于对世界各地文化的历史描述。\n\n“These descriptions were made independent of and prior to the theory we''re testing.\n这些描述是独立于且先于我们测试的理论的。\n\nIn future, if social scientists are serious about testing theories of morality, they will need to gather new data, more systematically, out in the field.”\n未来，如果社会科学家认真对待道德理论的测试，他们就需要实地更系统地收集新的数据。”\n\nQuestions 16 to 18 are based on the recording you have just heard.\n请根据你刚刚听到的录音回答问题16到18。\n\n16. What do we learn from the conclusion of the Oxford University researchers?\n16. 我们从牛津大学研究人员的结论中了解到什么？\n\n17.What did the new study by Oxford researchers aim to do?\n17. 牛津大学研究人员的这项新研究的目的是什么？\n\n18.What does Harvey Whitehouse think social scientists should do to test theories of morality?\n18. 哈维·怀特豪斯认为社会科学家应该如何检验道德理论？', 197, 1666.14, 880.4