as measured using the single question:\n幸福感是用与第一项研究相同的问题来衡量的，而意义是用一个简单的问题来衡量的：\n\n“Do you feel your life has an important purpose or meaning?”.\n“你觉得你的生活有重要的意义吗？”\n\nAgain, the strength of the relationship between meaning and happiness depended on participants'' income:\n同样，意义和幸福之间关系的强弱取决于参与者的收入：\n\nmeaning had a greater influence on happiness for those on lower incomes compared to those in higher brackets.\n与收入较高的人相比，意义对收入较低的人的幸福影响更大。\n\nIn the final study, French participants indicated the extent to which they felt they led a purposeful and meaningful life and how much they considered themselves a happy person.\n在最后一项研究中，法国参与者指出了他们认为自己的生活在多大程度上是有目的和有意义的，以及他们认为自己在多大程度上是一个幸福的人。\n\nFinally, rather than using specific income brackets, they placed themselves on a “social ladder”, representing where they stand in society with regard to wealth, education, and career.\n最后，他们没有使用特定的收入等级，而是把自己放在一个“社会阶梯”上，代表他们在财富、教育和职业方面的社会地位。\n\nThe results from the study duplicated those of the first two.\n这项研究的结果与前两项相同。\n\nSo overall, meaning and happiness had a stronger relationship in those with fewer resources than those with more.\n所以总的来讲，在资源少的人中，意义和幸福感的关系比资源多的人更强。\n\nThis might be the case because rich individuals have more access to other sources of happiness—many of which will be external, like lack of stress or community.\n这可能是因为富有的人有更多的机会获得其他的幸福来源——其中许多是外在的，比如没有压力或社区方面。\n\nThus, a focus on an internal sense of satisfaction, purpose or meaning is less important.\n因此，关注内在的满足感、目的或意义就不那么重要了。\n\nQuestions 22 to 25 are based on the recording you have just heard.\n请根据你刚刚听到的录音回答问题22到25。\n\n22.What does the speaker say many of us search for throughout our lives?\n22. 讲话者说我们许多人的一生都在寻找什么？\n\n23.What do Rhia Catapano and colleagues find about economic resources?\n23. 关于经济资源，瑞亚·卡塔帕诺及其同事发现了什么？\n\n24.What do we learn about Rhia Catapano and colleagues'' second study?\n24. 关于瑞亚·卡塔帕诺及其同事的第二项研究，我们了解到什么？\n\n25.Why do meaning and happiness have a weaker relationship in those with more resources?\n25. 为什么意义和幸福感在那些拥有更多资源的人身上关系较弱？', 209, 1666.14, 1365.65, 1574.31, 1619.90, 1639.51, 1407.25, 1423.30, 'cet6-2024-12-1-g07', 'LECTURE', '[22:45.65]Recording Three｜讲座三\n[22:47.40]Searching for meaning is something many of us experience throughout our lives.｜寻找意义是我们许多人一生都在经历的事情。\n[22:52.61]For some, this meaning is religious, some political and some interpersonal.｜对一些人来说，这种意义是宗教的；对一些人来说，这种意义是政治的；对一些人来说，这种意义是人际关系的。\n[22:58.75]And having a sense of meaning can bring us happiness.｜拥有意义感可以给我们带来幸福。\n[23:02.82]A new study looks at the relationship between meaning and happiness in the context of financial resources.｜一项新的研究着眼于经济资源背景下的意义和幸福之间的关系。\n[23:09.42]Rhia Catapano from the University of Toronto and colleagues find meaning is a far weaker predictor of happiness for rich people than poorer people, suggesting economic resources can impact how we experience meaning.｜多伦多大学的瑞亚·卡塔帕诺及其同事发现，意义对富人幸福感的预测作用远远弱于穷人，这表明经济资源会影响我们对意义的体验。\n[23:27.25]The team analysed data from over 500,000 people across 123 countries.｜该团队分析了来自123个国家的50多万人的数据。\n[23:34.32]The first study used data from a daily poll of US residents collected between 2013 and 2015.｜第一项研究使用了2013年至2015年期间对美国居民进行的每日民意调查的数据。\n[23:43.60]Well-being was tracked using measures of positive affect—whether, during the day before they were surveyed, participants had smiled or laughed a lot or experienced a lot of happiness.｜幸福感是通过测量积极情绪来跟踪的——在接受调查的前一天，参与者是否经常微笑或大笑，或者体验到很多快乐。\n[23:58.63]Meaning was measured through a daily “purpose index”, which explored the extent to which participants felt that they like what they do every day and are motivated to achieve their goals.｜意义是通过每日“目标指数”来衡量的，该指数探讨了参与者觉得自己喜欢每天所做的事情的程度，以及实现目标的动力。\n[24:14.13]Finally, income levels were assessed.｜最后，还对收入水平进行了评估。\n[24:17.61]The results showed that the correlation between meaning and happiness was strongest among those in lower income brackets.｜结果显示，在收入较低的人群中，意义和幸福之间的相关性最强。\n[24:27.51]But as income levels increased, the correlation became weaker.｜但随着收入水平的提高，这种相关性变得越来越弱。\n[24:33.20]The second study looked at worldwide data.｜第二项研究着眼于世界范围的数据。\n[24:37.48]Happiness was measured using the same questions as in the first study, while meaning was measured using the single question:｜幸福感是用与第一项研究相同的问题来衡量的，而意义是用一个简单的问题来衡量的：\n[24:46.43]“Do you feel your life has an important purpose or meaning?”.｜“你觉得你的生活有重要的意义吗？”\n[24:50.89]Again, the strength of the relationship between meaning and happiness depended on participants'' income:｜同样，意义和幸福之间关系的强弱取决于参与者的收入：\n[24:58.14]meaning had a greater influence on happiness for those on lower incomes compared to those in higher brackets.｜与收入较高的人相比，意义对收入较低的人的幸福影响更大。\n[25:06.80]In the final study, French participants indicated the extent to which they felt they led a purposeful and meaningful life and how much they considered themselves a happy person.｜在最后一项研究中，法国参与者指出了他们认为自己的生活在多大程度上是有目的和有意义的，以及他们认为自己在多大程度上是一个幸福的人。\n[25:21.81]Finally, rather than using specific income brackets, they placed themselves on a “social ladder”, representing where they stand in society with regard to wealth, education, and career.｜最后，他们没有使用特定的收入等级，而是把自己放在一个“社会阶梯”上，代表他们在财富、教育和职业方面的社会地位。\n[25:36.99]The results from the study duplicated those of the first two.｜这项研究的结果与前两项相同。\n[25:43.49]So overall, meaning and happiness had a stronger relationship in those with fewer resources than those with more.｜所以总的来讲，在资源少的人中，意义和幸福感的关系比资源多的人更强。\n[25:52.90]This might be the case because rich individuals have more access to other sources of happiness—many of which will be external, like lack of stress or community.｜这可能是因为富有的人有更多的机会获得其他的幸福来源——其中许多是外在的，比如没有压力或社区方面。\n[26:05.81]Thus, a focus on an internal sense of satisfaction, purpose or meaning is less important.｜因此，关注内在的满足感、目的或意义就不那么重要了。\n[26:14.31]Questions 22 to 25 are based on the recording you have just heard.｜请根据你刚刚听到的录音回答问题22到25。\n[26:19.61]22.What does the speaker say many of us search for throughout our lives?｜22. 讲话者说我们许多人的一生都在寻找什么？\n[26:38.50]23.What do Rhia Catapano and colleagues find about economic resources?｜23. 关于经济资源，瑞亚·卡塔帕诺及其同事发现了什么？\n[26:59.90]24.What do we learn about Rhia Catapano and colleagues'' second study?｜24. 关于瑞亚·卡塔帕诺及其同事的第二项研究，我们了解到什么？\n[27:19.81]25.Why do meaning and happiness have a weaker relationship in those with more resources?｜25. 为什么意义和幸福感在那些拥有更多资源的人身上关系较弱？', NOW(), NOW()
