SELECT
  @a_cet6_2024_12_2_01, '/audio/exams/listening-cet6-2024-12-2.mp3', 'Conversation One\n对话一\n\nW: Hi, Alan. Sorry for not calling you back sooner.\n女：嗨，艾伦。很抱歉没有早点给你回电话。\n\nYou said on the phone you had something you needed to discuss with me?\n你在电话里说有事情需要和我讨论？\n\nM: Well, to get right down to it, I''m having second thoughts about my major.\n男：好吧，直接说吧，关于我的专业，我改变了主意。\n\nWith my family situation getting more complicated and the end of my university education nearing, persisting with Art History just doesn''t seem the right choice.\n我的家庭状况越来越复杂，大学学业也即将结束，坚持学习艺术史似乎不是正确的选择。\n\nW: Alan, in the last 3 years, I have heard nothing but how passionate you are about the Art History programme.\n女：艾伦，在过去的3年里，我听到的都是你对艺术史课程有多热诚。\n\nYou often told fellow classmates how fabulous the instructors were and that you finally felt accepted.\n你经常跟同学们说老师们有多棒，你终于觉得融入其中了。\n\nWhat would cause you to abandon it?\n是什么原因让你放弃的呢？\n\nM: My father''s current financial situation has helped me realize that a more financially viable employment opportunity is not necessarily a bad thing.\n男：我父亲目前的经济状况让我意识到，更能解决经济问题的就业机会也许不是一件坏事。\n\nArt History nourishes my soul, but does nothing to put food on my plate.\n艺术史滋养了我的灵魂，但并不能为我提供餐盘上的食物。\n\nW: What about all the work opportunities I discussed with you last month?\n女：上个月我和你讨论过的那些工作机会呢？\n\nHave you gone to those places of business to investigate whether any legitimate positions might be available for someone with your background?\n你有没有去那些企业调查过，有你这样背景的人是否能找到合适的职位？\n\nM: Ah, well...\n男：啊，那个……\n\nW: Look, Alan, if your heart is set on working in the art industry, you need to be more assertive and start talking with people.\n女：你看，艾伦，如果你一心想在艺术行业工作，你需要更加坚定自信，并且要开始与人交谈。\n\nNetworking is key if you want to become a celebrity in the world of museums and galleries.\n如果你想成为博物馆和画廊界的名人，建立人脉是关键。\n\nM: Time is a very precious commodity right now.\n男：现在时间非常宝贵。\n\nMy social life does not exist.\n我没有社交生活。\n\nI can barely keep up with my studies and thesis is due by the end of this year.\n我快跟不上学习进度了，今年年底就要交毕业论文了。\n\nWhen can I find time to research jobs when I have so much to do as it is?\n我现在有这么多事情要做，哪还能找到时间来收集工作信息呢？\n\nW: What you do now will determine your future options.\n女：你现在所做的事情将决定你未来的机遇。\n\nNow is the optimum time to put forth your best effort.\n现在是你全力以赴的最佳时机。\n\nM: I will take what you said into consideration.\n男：我会考虑您的话的。\n\nThe advice is much appreciated.\n非常感谢您的建议。\n\nQuestions 1 to 4 are based on the conversation you have just heard.\n请根据你刚刚听到的对话回答问题1到4。\n\n1. What did the man want to discuss with the woman?\n1. 男士想和女士讨论什么事情？\n\n2.Why does the man want to give up Art History?\n2. 男士为什么想放弃艺术史？\n\n3.What does the woman advise the man to do?\n3. 女士建议男士怎么做？\n\n4.What does the man say he really lacks right now?\n4. 男士说他现阶段最缺的是什么？', 122, 1640.31, 33.98, 155.57, 159.88, 175.83, NULL, NULL, 'cet6-2024-12-2-g01', 'LONG_DIALOGUE', '[00:33.98]Conversation One｜对话一\n[00:36.45]W: Hi, Alan. Sorry for not calling you back sooner.｜女：嗨，艾伦。很抱歉没有早点给你回电话。\n[00:40.39]You said on the phone you had something you needed to discuss with me?｜你在电话里说有事情需要和我讨论？\n[00:43.92]M: Well, to get right down to it, I''m having second thoughts about my major.｜男：好吧，直接说吧，关于我的专业，我改变了主意。\n[00:49.41]With my family situation getting more complicated and the end of my university education nearing, persisting with Art History just doesn''t seem the right choice.｜我的家庭状况越来越复杂，大学学业也即将结束，坚持学习艺术史似乎不是正确的选择。\n[01:00.56]W: Alan, in the last 3 years, I have heard nothing but how passionate you are about the Art History programme.｜女：艾伦，在过去的3年里，我听到的都是你对艺术史课程有多热诚。\n[01:07.82]You often told fellow classmates how fabulous the instructors were and that you finally felt accepted.｜你经常跟同学们说老师们有多棒，你终于觉得融入其中了。\n[01:14.42]What would cause you to abandon it?｜是什么原因让你放弃的呢？\n[01:16.99]M: My father''s current financial situation has helped me realize that a more financially viable employment opportunity is not necessarily a bad thing.｜男：我父亲目前的经济状况让我意识到，更能解决经济问题的就业机会也许不是一件坏事。\n[01:27.75]Art History nourishes my soul, but does nothing to put food on my plate.｜艺术史滋养了我的灵魂，但并不能为我提供餐盘上的食物。\n[01:34.86]W: What about all the work opportunities I discussed with you last month?｜女：上个月我和你讨论过的那些工作机会呢？\n[01:39.56]Have you gone to those places of business to investigate whether any legitimate positions might be available for someone with your background?｜你有没有去那些企业调查过，有你这样背景的人是否能找到合适的职位？\n[01:47.16]M: Ah, well...｜男：啊，那个……\n[01:48.88]W: Look, Alan, if your heart is set on working in the art industry, you need to be more assertive and start talking with people.｜女：你看，艾伦，如果你一心想在艺术行业工作，你需要更加坚定自信，并且要开始与人交谈。\n[01:56.61]Networking is key if you want to become a celebrity in the world of museums and galleries.｜如果你想成为博物馆和画廊界的名人，建立人脉是关键。\n[02:02.99]M: Time is a very precious commodity right now.｜男：现在时间非常宝贵。\n[02:06.41]My social life does not exist.｜我没有社交生活。\n[02:08.94]I can barely keep up with my studies and thesis is due by the end of this year.｜我快跟不上学习进度了，今年年底就要交毕业论文了。\n[02:14.38]When can I find time to research jobs when I have so much to do as it is?｜我现在有这么多事情要做，哪还能找到时间来收集工作信息呢？\n[02:20.89]W: What you do now will determine your future options.｜女：你现在所做的事情将决定你未来的机遇。\n[02:24.54]Now is the optimum time to put forth your best effort.｜现在是你全力以赴的最佳时机。\n[02:28.67]M: I will take what you said into consideration.｜男：我会考虑您的话的。\n[02:32.58]The advice is much appreciated.｜非常感谢您的建议。\n[02:35.57]Questions 1 to 4 are based on the conversation you have just heard.｜请根据你刚刚听到的对话回答问题1到4。\n[02:39.88]1. What did the man want to discuss with the woman?｜1. 男士想和女士讨论什么事情？\n[02:56.13]2.Why does the man want to give up Art History?｜2. 男士为什么想放弃艺术史？\n[03:14.13]3.What does the woman advise the man to do?｜3. 女士建议男士怎么做？\n[03:31.62]4.What does the man say he really lacks right now?｜4. 男士说他现阶段最缺的是什么？', NOW(), NOW()
