other people do.\n虽然有很多人不在乎他们的车看起来怎么样，但也有很多人在乎。\n\nYou got yourself a vast and continual market.\n你有一个广阔且持续的市场。\n\nM: Right. So the idea is a large self-cleaning car wash, but I mean really big and well-outfitted like they have in America.\n男：是的。所以我设想的是一个大型的自动清洗洗车场，但我指的是真正的大型洗车场，设备齐全，像美国那些洗车场那样。\n\nI was thinking of having it cater to high-end consumers in large cities.\n我在考虑去迎合大城市的高端消费者。\n\nIt could charge a profitable markup by offering just a bit more technical equipment and professional service than competitors.\n可以通过提供比竞争对手更先进的技术设备和更专业的服务来获取利润。\n\nQuestions 5 to 8 are based on the conversation you have just heard.\n请根据你刚刚听到的对话回答问题5到8。\n\n5. What are the speakers mainly talking about in the conversation?\n5. 对话中，讲话者主要谈论的是什么？\n\n6.What does the man say makes perfect sense?\n6. 男士认为什么是很有道理的？\n\n7.What business does the woman say has a vast and continual market?\n7. 女士说什么生意有着广阔且持续的市场？\n\n8.Who would the man''s imagined business cater to?\n8. 男士设想中的生意会迎合什么样的顾客？\n\nSection B Directions: In this section, you will hear two passages.\nB节 说明：在本节中，你将会听到两篇短文。', 125, 1640.31, 229.25, 353.97, 375.34, 393.21, NULL, NULL, 'cet6-2024-12-2-g02', 'LONG_DIALOGUE', '[03:49.25]Conversation Two｜对话二\n[03:51.61]M: Have you decided yet what your end-of-semester business project will be on?｜男：你期末的商业项目定下来了吗？\n[03:57.16]W: Yes. How about you?｜女：是的。你呢？\n[03:58.90]M: Yes. Go on. You go first.｜男：定了。来吧，你先说。\n[04:02.68]W: I am going to do it about beef.｜女：我的项目是牛肉。\n[04:04.97]M: Beef?｜男：牛肉？\n[04:06.20]W: Yeah, beef. I''m going to design a business case study for a cow farm that supplies beef for the domestic market.｜女：是的，牛肉。我打算为一家为国内市场供应牛肉的养牛场设计一个商业案例研究。\n[04:14.05]M: Well, that sounds very interesting and original.｜男：嗯，听起来很有趣，也很有创意。\n[04:17.25]Where ever did you get that idea?｜你这个想法是从哪里来的？\n[04:19.92]W: I don''t know. It just came to me, I guess.｜女：我也不知道。我猜，它就是这么冒出来的。\n[04:22.54]But think about it. Beef consumption has been rising strongly over the past 20 years.｜不过，你想一下，在过去20年里，牛肉消费一直在强劲增长。\n[