SELECT
  @a_cet6_2024_12_2_13, '/audio/exams/listening-cet6-2024-12-2.mp3', 'Passage Two\n短文二\n\nHumans are aspirational goal-seeking beings.\n人类是有抱负的、追求目标的生物。\n\nEach of us, according to research, has an inborn drive to acquire.\n据研究，我们每个人生来就有获取的欲望。\n\nThe “dark side” of this drive to acquire is being mindlessly driven to possess more and more “things” and to socially compare our “stuff” with all the stuff other people have in their lives.\n这种获取的欲望的“黑暗面”是人类被无意识地驱使着想要拥有越来越多的“东西”，并将我们（所拥有）的“东西”与其他人生活中拥有的所有东西进行社会性的比较。\n\nSo the question is, how do we ensure we tap into our drive to acquire in positive ways that will benefit our well-being?\n所以，问题是，我们怎样才能确保自己以积极的方式利用这种获取欲望，从而提升我们的幸福感？\n\nOne way is to become more intentionally aspirational.\n一种方法是更加有意识地追求目标。\n\nTo be intentionally aspirational includes consciously aspiring to be the person you need to be to succeed in your professional and personal life.\n这包括有意识地成为在职业和个人生活中取得成功的人。\n\nIt also includes consciously aspiring to acquire things in your life that will positively impact your sense of well-being.\n它还包括有意识地获取生活中会对你的幸福感产生积极影响的东西。\n\nIf you''re not consciously, mindfully and intentionally harnessing this inborn drive to acquire, you might be mindlessly pursuing all the wrong things.\n如果不去有意识地、深思熟虑地且有目的地去控制这种与生俱来的获取欲望，你可能就会在无意识状态下追求那些错误的东西。\n\nWhile your intentional aspirational goals will include pursuit of acquiring things that will increase your sense of well-being, they ought to also include goals to help other people in your various life roles.\n尽管你有意设定的高远目标包括获得那些能增加自己幸福感的东西，但这些目标也应该包括在自己的各种生命角色中去帮助他人。\n\nYour intentional aspirational goals will also include striving to be your personal best—a person of “good” character, integrity, and trustworthiness.\n有意识设定的高远目标还应该包括努力成为最好的自己——成为一个性格品格优秀、正直且值得信赖的人。\n\nThink about this from a practical, rather than theoretical viewpoint.\n从实践的角度而不是理论的角度来考虑这个问题。\n\nIf you''re not pursuing intentional aspirational goals, you have nothing to strive for.\n如果没有有意设定的高远目标去追求，你也就没了奋斗的目标。\n\nIf you have nothing to strive for, you''re putting yourself in the dangerous position of simply drifting through life, and you will not be able to experience, live and enjoy all that life has to offer.\n如果没有奋斗目标，你就把自己置于随波逐流的危险境地，而且无法去体验并享受生活所提供的一切。\n\nQuestions 12 to 15 are based on the passage you have just heard.\n请根据你刚刚听到的短文回答问题12到15。\n\n12. What is the dark side of our inborn drive to acquire?\n12. 我们与生俱来的获取欲望的黑暗面是什么？\n\n13.What might happen if we do not harness our inborn drive to acquire?\n13. 如果我们对与生俱来的获取欲望不加以控制，会发生什么？\n\n14.What does the passage say about our intentional aspirational goals?\n14. 关于我们有意设定的高远目标，这篇文章说了什么？\n\n15.What will you end up doing without pursuing intentional aspirational goals?\n15. 如果没有去追求有意设定的高远目标，你最终会变成什么样子？\n\nSection C Directions: In this section, you will hear three recordings of lectures or talks followed by three or four questions.\nC节 说明：在本节中，你将会听到三篇讲座或讲话，每篇讲座或讲话后面都有三个或四个问题。', 130, 1640.31, 655.41, 785.70, 810.18, 828.73, 715.68, 729.41, 'cet6-2024-12-2-g04', 'PASSAGE', '[10:55.41]Passage Two｜短文二\n[10:57.03]Humans are aspirational goal-seeking beings.｜人类是有抱负的、追求目标的生物。\n[11:01.54]Each of us, according to research, has an inborn drive to acquire.｜据研究，我们每个人生来就有获取的欲望。\n[11:05.95]The “dark side” of this drive to acquire is being mindlessly driven to possess more and more “things” and to socially compare our “stuff” with all the stuff other people have in their lives.｜这种获取的欲望的“黑暗面”是人类被无意识地驱使着想要拥有越来越多的“东西”，并将我们（所拥有）的“东西”与其他人生活中拥有的所有东西进行社会性的比较。\n[11:21.11]So the question is, how do we ensure we tap into our drive to acquire in positive ways that will benefit our well-being?｜所以，问题是，我们怎样才能确保自己以积极的方式利用这种获取欲望，从而提升我们的幸福感？\n[11:31.80]One way is to become more intentionally aspirational.｜一种方法是更加有意识地追求目标。\n[11:36.71]To be intentionally aspirational includes consciously aspiring to be the person you need to be to succeed in your professional and personal life.｜这包括有意识地成为在职业和个人生活中取得成功的人。\n[11:46.89]It also includes consciously aspiring to acquire things in your life that will positively impact your sense of well-being.｜它还包括有意识地获取生活中会对你的幸福感产生积极影响的东西。\n[11:55.68]If you''re not consciously, mindfully and intentionally harnessing this inborn drive to acquire, you might be mindlessly pursuing all the wrong things.｜如果不去有意识地、深思熟虑地且有目的地去控制这种与生俱来的获取欲望，你可能就会在无意识状态下追求那些错误的东西。\n[12:09.71]While your intentional aspirational goals will include pursuit of acquiring things that will increase your sense of well-being, they ought to also include goals to help other people in your various life roles.｜尽管你有意设定的高远目标包括获得那些能增加自己幸福感的东西，但这些目标也应该包括在自己的各种生命角色中去帮助他人。\n[12:25.65]Your intentional aspirational goals will also include striving to be your personal best—a person of “good” character, integrity, and trustworthiness.｜有意识设定的高远目标还应该包括努力成为最好的自己——成为一个性格品格优秀、正直且值得信赖的人。\n[12:37.42]Think about this from a practical, rather than theoretical viewpoint.｜从实践的角度而不是理论的角度来考虑这个问题。\n[12:43.09]If you''re not pursuing intentional aspirational goals, you have nothing to strive for.｜如果没有有意设定的高远目标去追求，你也就没了奋斗的目标。\n[12:50.15]If you have nothing to strive for, you''re putting yourself in the dangerous position of simply drifting through life, and you will not be able to experience, live and enjoy all that life has to offer.｜如果没有奋斗目标，你就把自己置于随波逐流的危险境地，而且无法去体验并享受生活所提供的一切。\n[13:05.70]Questions 12 to 15 are based on the passage you have just heard.｜请根据你刚刚听到的短文回答问题12到15。\n[13:11.18]12. What is the dark side of our inborn drive to acquire?｜12. 我们与生俱来的获取欲望的黑暗面是什么？\n[13:30.18]13.What might happen if we do not harness our inborn drive to acquire?｜13. 如果我们对与生俱来的获取欲望不加以控制，会发生什么？\n[13:49.03]14.What does the passage say about our intentional aspirational goals?｜14. 关于我们有意设定的高远目标，这篇文章说了什么？\n[14:08.79]15.What will you end up doing without pursuing intentional aspirational goals?｜15. 如果没有去追求有意设定的高远目标，你最终会变成什么样子？\n[14:28.17]Section C Directions: In this section, you will hear three recordings of lectures or talks followed by three or four questions.｜C节 说明：在本节中，你将会听到三篇讲座或讲话，每篇讲座或讲话后面都有三个或四个问题。', NOW(), NOW()
