SELECT
  @a_cet6_2024_12_2_16, '/audio/exams/listening-cet6-2024-12-2.mp3', 'Recording One\n讲座一\n\nIt''s revision time for exams and dissertations.\n到了复习准备考试和（提交）论文的时间了。\n\nThe pressure is on, so you want all the help you can get to aid your memory and raise your grades.\n压力很大，所以你想要利用一切可以得到的辅助来帮助自己提高记忆力和成绩。\n\nAs a nutrition expert, I want to say that eating well can make a real difference to your revision regime—so what brain-boosting food and drink would I recommend?\n作为一名营养专家，我想说的是，吃得好可以对你的复习计划产生真实的影响——那么我会推荐些什么样的健脑食物和饮品呢？\n\nCoffee can have numerous benefits.\n喝咖啡有很多好处。\n\nHowever, while coffee may make you more alert, individuals can build up a tolerance, meaning this is short-lived.\n然而，虽然咖啡可能会让你更有精神，但是个体会产生耐受性，这意味着咖啡的影响是短暂的。\n\nCoffee can also increase blood sugar and eventually cause lack of focus and energy.\n咖啡还会提高血糖，最终导致专注力和精力不足。\n\nIt''s also worth noting that people react differently to coffee.\n值得注意的是，人们对咖啡的反应也各不相同。\n\nSome people can drink it at midnight and go straight to sleep, whereas others get feelings of anxiety after a small amount.\n有些人半夜喝了咖啡，转头就可以直接入睡，而有些人喝少量咖啡就会感到焦虑。\n\nAlso remember that coffee from a coffee shop may be stronger than coffee made at home.\n还要记住，咖啡店里的咖啡可能比家里煮的咖啡更浓。\n\nSo stop drinking coffee by 2 pm and have a maximum of 2 cups of coffee a day, but be aware of your own reaction to it.\n因此，下午2点后不要再饮用咖啡了，并且每天最多喝两杯，同时，要注意自己对咖啡的反应。\n\nWhole grain foods will ward off hunger.\n全谷物食物可以抵御饥饿。\n\nExamples include porridge and whole wheat bread.\n例如粥和全麦面包。\n\nCombining whole grain foods with protein will help keep your blood sugar levels balanced, which is essential for mood and concentration.\n全谷物食物与蛋白质的相结合，有助于保持血糖水平平衡，这对情绪和注意力的集中至关重要。\n\nBerries and nuts are a convenient and nutritious snack.\n浆果和坚果是方便且有营养的零食。\n\nBlueberries, like many dark colored fruits and vegetables, can slow down brain damage and age related decline.\n和许多深色水果和蔬菜一样，蓝莓可以减缓脑损伤和与年龄相关的衰退。\n\nFrozen berries are also a good choice.\n冷冻浆果也是一个不错的选择。\n\nThey are usually cheap, last longer and don''t lose their nutrients when frozen.\n它们通常很便宜，保存时间较长且冷冻后营养成分不会流失。\n\nBut flavored and coated nuts are less healthy as they contain added oil, salt, and sugar.\n但经过调味和包衣的坚果就不太健康了，因为它们被添加了油、盐和糖。\n\nDoctors often recommend taking vitamin supplements to top up on the nutrients you need.\n医生经常建议服用维生素补充剂来补充所需的营养。\n\nBut I would say food should always come before supplements and the key to getting as many nutrients as possible is to eat a varied diet with lots of different colors such as frozen berries and dark green vegetables.\n但我想说的是，食物始终应该排在补充剂之前，尽可能多地摄入营养的关键是饮食多样化，多吃各种不同颜色的食物，如冷冻浆果、深绿色蔬菜等。\n\nIt''s better to get everything you need from food and drink.\n最好是从食物和饮品中获得你需要的一切。\n\nFor example, oranges contain not only vitamin C which boosts the immune system, but also fiber and other components that you can''t get packaged together in a tablet.\n例如，橙子不仅含有能够增强免疫系统的维生素C，还含有纤维和其它无法通过包装好的片剂所获取的成分。\n\nDon''t forget to drink a proper amount of water, which can boost attention by almost 25 percent and can elevate your mood as well.\n别忘了适量饮水，它可以让专注力提高近25%，也可以提升你的情绪。\n\nFinally, don''t skip meals.\n最后，不要不吃饭。\n\nEating regularly will help keep blood sugar balanced and feed the brain with the fuel it needs.\n有规律地进食有助于保持血糖平衡，并为大脑提供所需的能量。\n\nQuestions 16 to 18 are based on the recording you have just heard.\n请根据你刚刚听到的录音回答问题16到18。\n\n16. What does the speaker recommend in this talk?\n16. 讲话者在讲座中推荐了什么？\n\n17.What does the speaker warn against about coffee?\n17. 关于咖啡，讲话者提出警告，应避免什么？\n\n18.How can we get sufficient nutrients according to the speaker?\n18. 讲话者认为，我们如何才能获得充足的营养？', 174, 1640.31, 895.44, 1069.11, 1075.73, 1092.64, 908.67, 920.21, 'cet6-2024-12-2-g05', 'LECTURE', '[14:55.44]Recording One｜讲座一\n[14:57.90]It''s revision time for exams and dissertations.｜到了复习准备考试和（提交）论文的时间了。\n[15:02.06]The pressure is on, so you want all the help you can get to aid your memory and raise your grades.｜压力很大，所以你想要利用一切可以得到的辅助来帮助自己提高记忆力和成绩。\n[15:08.67]As a nutrition expert, I want to say that eating well can make a real difference to your revision regime—so what brain-boosting food and drink would I recommend?｜作为一名营养专家，我想说的是，吃得好可以对你的复习计划产生真实的影响——那么我会推荐些什么样的健脑食物和饮品呢？\n[15:20.51]Coffee can have numerous benefits.｜喝咖啡有很多好处。\n[15:23.16]However, while coffee may make you more alert, individuals can build up a tolerance, meaning this is short-lived.｜然而，虽然咖啡可能会让你更有精神，但是个体会产生耐受性，这意味着咖啡的影响是短暂的。\n[15:31.40]Coffee can also increase blood sugar and eventually cause lack of focus and energy.｜咖啡还会提高血糖，最终导致专注力和精力不足。\n[15:37.82]It''s also worth noting that people react differently to coffee.｜值得注意的是，人们对咖啡的反应也各不相同。\n[15:42.10]Some people can drink it at midnight and go straight to sleep, whereas others get feelings of anxiety after a small amount.｜有些人半夜喝了咖啡，转头就可以直接入睡，而有些人喝少量咖啡就会感到焦虑。\n[15:50.29]Also remember that coffee from a coffee shop may be stronger than coffee made at home.｜还要记住，咖啡店里的咖啡可能比家里煮的咖啡更浓。\n[15:56.96]So stop drinking coffee by 2 pm and have a maximum of 2 cups of coffee a day, but be aware of your own reaction to it.｜因此，下午2点后不要再饮用咖啡了，并且每天最多喝两杯，同时，要注意自己对咖啡的反应。\n[16:07.29]Whole grain foods will ward off hunger.｜全谷物食物可以抵御饥饿。\n[16:10.94]Examples include porridge and whole wheat bread.｜例如粥和全麦面包。\n[16:14.53]Combining whole grain foods with protein will help keep your blood sugar levels balanced, which is essential for mood and concentration.｜全谷物食物与蛋白质的相结合，有助于保持血糖水平平衡，这对情绪和注意力的集中至关重要。\n[16:24.32]Berries and nuts are a convenient and nutritious snack.｜浆果和坚果是方便且有营养的零食。\n[16:28.96]Blueberries, like many dark colored fruits and vegetables, can slow down brain damage and age related decline.｜和许多深色水果和蔬菜一样，蓝莓可以减缓脑损伤和与年龄相关的衰退。\n[16:37.16]Frozen berries are also a good choice.｜冷冻浆果也是一个不错的选择。\n[16:40.25]They are usually cheap, last longer and don''t lose their nutrients when frozen.｜它们通常很便宜，保存时间较长且冷冻后营养成分不会流失。\n[16:46.12]But flavored and coated nuts are less healthy as they contain added oil, salt, and sugar.｜但经过调味和包衣的坚果就不太健康了，因为它们被添加了油、盐和糖。\n[16:53.91]Doctors often recommend taking vitamin supplements to top up on the nutrients you need.｜医生经常建议服用维生素补充剂来补充所需的营养。\n[17:00.69]But I would say food should always come before supplements and the key to getting as many nutrients as possible is to eat a varied diet with lots of different colors such as frozen berries and dark green vegetables.｜但我想说的是，食物始终应该排在补充剂之前，尽可能多地摄入营养的关键是饮食多样化，多吃各种不同颜色的食物，如冷冻浆果、深绿色蔬菜等。\n[17:14.37]It''s better to get everything you need from food and drink.｜最好是从食物和饮品中获得你需要的一切。\n[17:18.86]For example, oranges contain not only vitamin C which boosts the immune system, but also fiber and other components that you can''t get packaged together in a tablet.｜例如，橙子不仅含有能够增强免疫系统的维生素C，还含有纤维和其它无法通过包装好的片剂所获取的成分。\n[17:31.19]Don''t forget to drink a proper amount of water, which can boost attention by almost 25 percent and can elevate your mood as well.｜别忘了适量饮水，它可以让专注力提高近25%，也可以提升你的情绪。\n[17:39.63]Finally, don''t skip meals.｜最后，不要不吃饭。\n[17:43.18]Eating regularly will help keep blood sugar balanced and feed the brain with the fuel it needs.｜有规律地进食有助于保持血糖平衡，并为大脑提供所需的能量。\n[17:49.11]Questions 16 to 18 are based on the recording you have just heard.｜请根据你刚刚听到的录音回答问题16到18。\n[17:55.73]16. What does the speaker recommend in this talk?｜16. 讲话者在讲座中推荐了什么？\n[18:12.94]17.What does the speaker warn against about coffee?｜17. 关于咖啡，讲话者提出警告，应避免什么？\n[18:33.35]18.How can we get sufficient nutrients according to the speaker?｜18. 讲话者认为，我们如何才能获得充足的营养？', NOW(), NOW()
