  (`question_id`, `audio_url`, `transcript`, `duration_seconds`, `audio_total_seconds`, `audio_start_seconds`, `audio_end_seconds`, `question_start_seconds`, `question_end_seconds`, `answer_start_seconds`, `answer_end_seconds`, `group_key`, `listening_type`, `lrc_content`, `created_at`, `updated_at`)
SELECT
  @a_cet6_2024_12_2_19, '/audio/exams/listening-cet6-2024-12-2.mp3', 'Recording Two\n讲座二\n\nThe late Swedish academic Hans Rosling has identified a worrying trend: not only do many people across advanced economies have no idea that the world is becoming a much better place, but they actually even think the opposite.\n已故瑞典学者汉斯·罗斯林发现了一个令人担忧的趋势：发达经济体内许多人不仅不知道世界正在变得更好，他们还认为情况恰恰相反。\n\nThis is no wonder, when the news focuses on reporting catastrophes, terrorist attacks, wars, and famines.\n这也难怪，因为新闻报道的重点是灾难、恐怖袭击、战争和饥荒。\n\nWho wants to hear about the fact that every day some 200,000 people around the world are lifted above the $2-a-day poverty line?\n谁愿意听到这样的报道：全世界每天约有20万人能够跨过日收入2美元的贫困线？\n\nOr that more than 300,000 people get access to electricity and clean water for the first time every day?\n或者每天有30多万人首次用上了电和清洁用水？\n\nThese stories of people in low-income countries simply don''t make for exciting news coverage.\n这些低收入国家人民的故事根本无法成为令人兴奋的新闻报道。\n\nBut, as Rosling pointed out in his book Factfulness, it''s important to put all the bad news in perspective.\n但是，正如罗斯林在他的《事实》一书中所指出的，重要的是要正确看待所有的负面消息。\n\nWhile it is true that globalization has put some downward pressure on middle-class wages in advanced economies in recent decades, it has also helped lift hundreds of millions of people above the global poverty line.\n虽然近几十年来全球化确实给发达经济体内中产阶级的薪酬带来了一定的下行压力，但它也帮助数亿人摆脱了全球贫困线。\n\nIf we really care about global welfare, globalization is the only way forward to ensure that economic prosperity is shared among all countries and not only a select few advanced economies.\n如果我们真的关心全球福祉，那么全球化就是确保所有国家共享经济繁荣的唯一推进途径，而不是只维持少数发达经济体的经济繁荣。\n\nWhile some people glorify the past, one of the big facts of economic history is that until quite recently a significant part of the world population has lived under quite miserable conditions—and this has been true throughout most of human history.\n虽然有些人赞美过去，但经济史上的一个重大事实是，直到最近，世界上还有相当一部分人生活在相当悲惨的境况中——这在人类历史的大部分时间里都是如此。\n\nWhile there were many long-lasting ups and downs, like the Great Depression or the recent Great Recession, the constancy of the long-run growth rate is actually quite miraculous.\n虽然有许多长期的起伏，比如大萧条时期或最近的大衰退时期，但长期增长率的稳定性其实是不可思议的。\n\nLow-income countries, including China and India, have been growing at a significantly faster pace in recent decades and are quickly catching up to the West.\n近几十年来，包括中国和印度在内的低收入国家的经济增长速度明显加快，正在迅速赶上西方。\n\nA 10% growth rate over a prolonged period means that income levels double roughly every seven years.\n长期维持10%的增长率意味着收入水平大约每七年翻一番。\n\nIt is obviously good news if prosperity is more shared across the globe.\n如果繁荣能够在全球范围内得以更广泛的共享，这显然是个好消息。\n\nWhile inequality within countries has gone up as a result of globalization, global inequality has been on a steady downward trend for several decades.\n虽然全球化导致国家内部的不平等现象加剧，但几十年来，全球不平等现象一直呈稳步下降趋势。\n\nThis is mostly a result of the improvement of hundreds of millions of people''s living standards.\n这主要是数亿人生活水平提高的结果。\n\nIn fact, for the first time ever since the Industrial Revolution, about half of the global population can be considered middle class.\n事实上，自工业革命以来，全球约有一半人口首次可被视为中产阶级。\n\nQuestions 19 to 21 are based on the recording you have just heard.\n请根据你刚刚听到的录音回答问题19到21。\n\n19. What is the worrying trend the late Swedish academic has identified?\n19. 已故瑞典学者发现了什么令人担忧的趋势？\n\n20.What does the speaker say about globalization?\n20. 关于全球化，讲话者说了什么？\n\n21.What do we learn about half of the global population?\n21. 关于全球半数人口，我们了解到什么？', 186, 1640.31, 1131.96, 1317.63, 1323.11, 1341.28, 1134.26, 1152.42, 'cet6-2024-12-2-g06', 'LECTURE', '[18:51.96]Recording Two｜讲座二\n[18:54.26]The late Swedish academic Hans Rosling has identified a worrying trend: not only do many people across advanced economies have no idea that the world is becoming a much better place, but they actually even think the opposite.｜已故瑞典学者汉斯·罗斯林发现了一个令人担忧的趋势：发达经济体内许多人不仅不知道世界正在变得更好，他们还认为情况恰恰相反。\n[19:12.72]This is no wonder, when the news focuses on reporting catastrophes, terrorist attacks, wars, and famines.｜这也难怪，因为新闻报道的重点是灾难、恐怖袭击、战争和饥荒。\n[19:21.90]Who wants to hear about the fact that every day some 200,000 people around the world are lifted above the $2-a-day poverty line?｜谁愿意听到这样的报道：全世界每天约有20万人能够跨过日收入2美元的贫困线？\n[19:32.33]Or that more than 300,000 people get access to electricity and clean water for the first time every day?｜或者每天有30多万人首次用上了电和清洁用水？\n[19:41.06]These stories of people in low-income countries simply don''t make for exciting news coverage.｜这些低收入国家人民的故事根本无法成为令人兴奋的新闻报道。\n[19:48.28]But, as Rosling pointed out in his book Factfulness, it''s important to put all the bad news in perspective.｜但是，正如罗斯林在他的《事实》一书中所指出的，重要的是要正确看待所有的负面消息。\n[19:57.29]While it is true that globalization has put some downward pressure on middle-class wages in advanced economies in recent decades, it has also helped lift hundreds of millions of people above the global poverty line.｜虽然近几十年来全球化确实给发达经济体内中产阶级的薪酬带来了一定的下行压力，但它也帮助数亿人摆脱了全球贫困线。\n[20:13.95]If we really care about global welfare, globalization is the only way forward to ensure that economic prosperity is shared among all countries and not only a select few advanced economies.｜如果我们真的关心全球福祉，那么全球化就是确保所有国家共享经济繁荣的唯一推进途径，而不是只维持少数发达经济体的经济繁荣。\n[20:29.71]While some people glorify the past, one of the big facts of economic history is that until quite recently a significant part of the world population has lived under quite miserable conditions—and this has been true throughout most of human history.｜虽然有些人赞美过去，但经济史上的一个重大事实是，直到最近，世界上还有相当一部分人生活在相当悲惨的境况中——这在人类历史的大部分时间里都是如此。\n[20:48.44]While there were many long-lasting ups and downs, like the Great Depression or the recent Great Recession, the constancy of the long-run growth rate is actually quite miraculous.｜虽然有许多长期的起伏，比如大萧条时期或最近的大衰退时期，但长期增长率的稳定性其实是不可思议的。\n[21:01.64]Low-income countries, including China and India, have been growing at a significantly faster pace in recent decades and are quickly catching up to the West.｜近几十年来，包括中国和印度在内的低收入国家的经济增长速度明显加快，正在迅速赶上西方。\n[21:13.13]A 10% growth rate over a prolonged period means that income levels double roughly every seven years.｜长期维持10%的增长率意味着收入水平大约每七年翻一番。\n[21:21.61]It is obviously good news if prosperity is more shared across the globe.｜如果繁荣能够在全球范围内得以更广泛的共享，这显然是个好消息。\n[21:27.94]While inequality within countries has gone up as a result of globalization, global inequality has been on a steady downward trend for several decades.｜虽然全球化导致国家内部的不平等现象加剧，但几十年来，全球不平等现象一直呈稳步下降趋势。\n[21:40.53]This is mostly a result of the improvement of hundreds of millions of people''s living standards.｜这主要是数亿人生活水平提高的结果。\n[21:47.99]In fact, for the first time ever since the Industrial Revolution, about half of the global population can be considered middle class.｜事实上，自工业革命以来，全球约有一半人口首次可被视为中产阶级。\n[21:57.63]Questions 19 to 21 are based on the recording you have just heard.｜请根据你刚刚听到的录音回答问题19到21。\n[22:03.11]19. What is the worrying trend the late Swedish academic has identified?｜19. 已故瑞典学者发现了什么令人担忧的趋势？\n[22:21.58]20.What does the speaker say about globalization?｜20. 关于全球化，讲话者说了什么？\n[22:40.24]21.What do we learn about half of the global population?｜21. 关于全球半数人口，我们了解到什么？', NOW(), NOW()
WHERE @a_cet6_2024_12_2_19 IS NOT NULL
