  @a_cet6_2025_06_1_04, '/audio/exams/listening-cet6-2025-06-1.mp3', 'Conversation One\n对话一\n\nM: Good morning. My name is Bob Fetterman.\n男：早上好。我叫鲍勃·费特曼。\n\nI''m the computer technician.\n我是电脑技术员。\n\nW: Didn''t I call for you last week?\n女：我不是上周叫你来的吗？\n\nM: Maybe. I work for Alpha Maintenance.\n男：可能吧。我是阿尔法维修公司的员工。\n\nI imagine someone from your office called our central office, and I''m the engineer designated to your case.\n我猜是你们办公室的人联系了我们总部，我是被指派来处理您的问题的工程师。\n\nW: Yeah, I spoke to a lady there last Tuesday, which is now 10 days ago.\n女：是的，我上周二和一位女士通过电话，现在已经过去10天了。\n\nI made it clear it was an urgent matter and “please send someone as soon as possible”.\n我明确说过这事很紧急，“请尽快派人来”。\n\nCouldn''t you or someone else have come sooner?\n你或者其他人难道不能早点过来吗？\n\nM: I''m sorry, but I''m not in charge of scheduling or logistics.\n男：很抱歉，但我不管排班调度的事。\n\nI simply do not know. All I can tell you is I got the call this week and came as soon as I could.\n我不清楚（具体情况）。我只能告诉您，我是这周接到电话后就尽快过来了。\n\nW: I see. Well, I''ll have you know my manager is rather indignant that it''s taken you this long to come.\n女：明白了。不过，我得告诉你，我经理对你们拖了这么久才来非常气愤。\n\nI understand it might not be your fault, but nevertheless, you should know what the feeling is around here.\n我知道这可能不是你的责任，但你应该知道我们这边的感受如何。\n\nM: I understand. And I''m sorry for any inconvenience.\n男：我理解。对造成的任何不便我深表歉意。\n\nI will try to resolve your computer problem as swiftly and optimally as I can.\n我会尽全力快速、有效地解决您的电脑问题。\n\nWhat and where is the issue?\n具体是什么故障？在哪里？\n\nW: It''s this machine right here.\n女：就是这台机器。\n\nIt was running slow for a while, I guess, and gradually got worse and worse.\n我想有一段时间它运行有点慢，后来就越来越糟。\n\nLast Tuesday, it just stopped working altogether.\n上周二直接彻底瘫痪了。\n\nIf you switch it on, you will see what I mean.\n你开机看看就知道我说的是什么意思了。\n\nM: OK. Do you know if it''s backed up?\n男：好的。你知道它的数据备份过了吗？\n\nW: Backed up?\n女：备份？\n\nM: I mean do you know if its contents have been copied and saved somewhere else?\n男：我的意思是你知道它里面的内容有没有复制保存到其他地方？\n\nW: I don''t know.\n女：我不清楚。\n\nM: Well, depending on the ensuing operative scenario, if I need to wipe the system directories clean in order to reconfigure default protocols, then my first intervention should be to intricately retrieve all inventories that I can.\n男：这样，根据后续操作情况，如果为了重置默认协议需要清除系统目录，我的首要操作就是先精细恢复所有能找回的库存数据。\n\nOtherwise, all data that was stored on its hard drive will be forever lost.\n否则，存储在硬盘里的所有资料都会永久丢失。\n\nW: My manager would know. Let me go get him.\n女：我们经理应该知道。我去叫他。\n\nQuestions 1 to 4 are based on the conversation you have just heard.\n请根据你刚刚听到的对话回答问题1到4。\n\n1. What did the woman do last Tuesday?\n女士上周二做了什么？\n\n2.What does the man say he did when he got the call?\n男士说他接到电话后做了什么？\n\n3.What is the feeling about the problem around the woman''s workplace?\n女士的办公室里对这个问题是什么感受？\n\n4.What does the woman say her manager would know?\n女士说她的经理会知道什么？', 109, 1557.69, 38.52, 147.69, 205.64, 223.20, 117.64, 122.55, 'cet6-2025-06-1-g01', 'LONG_DIALOGUE', '[00:38.52]Conversation One｜对话一\n[00:40.84]M: Good morning. My name is Bob Fetterman.｜男：早上好。我叫鲍勃·费特曼。\n[00:43.72]I''m the computer technician.｜我是电脑技术员。\n[00:45.38]W: Didn''t I call for you last week?｜女：我不是上周叫你来的吗？\n[00:47.80]M: Maybe. I work for Alpha Maintenance.｜男：可能吧。我是阿尔法维修公司的员工。\n[00:50.57]I imagine someone from your office called our central office, and I''m the engineer designated to your case.｜我猜是你们办公室的人联系了我们总部，我是被指派来处理您的问题的工程师。\n[00:56.47]W: Yeah, I spoke to a lady there last Tuesday, which is now 10 days ago.｜女：是的，我上周二和一位女士通过电话，现在已经过去10天了。\n[01:01.27]I made it clear it was an urgent matter and “please send someone as soon as possible”.｜我明确说过这事很紧急，“请尽快派人来”。\n[01:06.95]Couldn''t you or someone else have come sooner?｜你或者其他人难道不能早点过来吗？\n[01:09.85]M: I''m sorry, but I''m not in charge of scheduling or logistics.｜男：很抱歉，但我不管排班调度的事。\n[01:13.60]I simply do not know. All I can tell you is I got the call this week and came as soon as I could.｜我不清楚（具体情况）。我只能告诉您，我是这周接到电话后就尽快过来了。\n[01:19.33]W: I see. Well, I''ll have you know my manager is rather indignant that it''s taken you this long to come.｜女：明白了。不过，我得告诉你，我经理对你们拖了这么久才来非常气愤。\n[01:25.86]I understand it might not be your fault, but nevertheless, you should know what the feeling is around here.｜我知道这可能不是你的责任，但你应该知道我们这边的感受如何。\n[01:32.19]M: I understand. And I''m sorry for any inconvenience.｜男：我理解。对造成的任何不便我深表歉意。\n[01:35.50]I will try to resolve your computer problem as swiftly and optimally as I can.｜我会尽全力快速、有效地解决您的电脑问题。\n[01:39.72]What and where is the issue?｜具体是什么故障？在哪里？\n[01:41.75]W: It''s this machine right here.｜女：就是这台机器。\n[01:43.68]It was running slow for a while, I guess, and gradually got worse and worse.｜我想有一段时间它运行有点慢，后来就越来越糟。\n[01:48.54]Last Tuesday, it just stopped working altogether.｜上周二直接彻底瘫痪了。\n[01:51.49]If you switch it on, you will see what I mean.｜你开机看看就知道我说的是什么意思了。\n[01:54.17]M: OK. Do you know if it''s backed up?｜男：好的。你知道它的数据备份过了吗？\n[01:57.64]W: Backed up?｜女：备份？\n[01:58.66]M: I mean do you know if its contents have been copied and saved somewhere else?｜男：我的意思是你知道它里面的内容有没有复制保存到其他地方？\n[02:02.85]W: I don''t know.｜女：我不清楚。\n[02:04.33]M: Well, depending on the ensuing operative scenario, if I need to wipe the system directories clean in order to reconfigure default protocols, then my first intervention should be to intricately retrieve all inventories that I can.｜男：这样，根据后续操作情况，如果为了重置默认协议需要清除系统目录，我的首要操作就是先精细恢复所有能找回的库存数据。\n[02:18.74]Otherwise, all data that was stored on its hard drive will be forever lost.｜否则，存储在硬盘里的所有资料都会永久丢失。\n[02:23.74]W: My manager would know. Let me go get him.｜女：我们经理应该知道。我去叫他。\n[02:27.69]Questions 1 to 4 are based on the conversation you have just heard.｜请根据你刚刚听到的对话回答问题1到4。\n[02:32.24]1. What did the woman do last Tuesday?｜女士上周二做了什么？\n[02:49.11]2.What does the man say he did when he got the call?｜男士说他接到电话后做了什么？\n[03:06.56]3.What is the feeling about the problem around the woman''s workplace?｜女士的办公室里对这个问题是什么感受？\n[03:25.64]4.What does the woman say her manager would know?｜女士说她的经理会知道什么？', NOW(), NOW()
