  @a_cet6_2025_06_1_08, '/audio/exams/listening-cet6-2025-06-1.mp3', 'Conversation Two\n对话二\n\nM: Have you given more thoughts to studying law?\n男：你有进一步考虑过学法律吗？\n\nW: I''ve been thinking about it a lot. Yes.\n女：我确实考虑了很多。是的。\n\nIn fact, this is why I wished to speak to you.\n事实上，这就是我想和你谈谈的原因。\n\nI wanted to hear more about what it''s like.\n我想多了解这个行业的情况。\n\nM: A career in law is a beautiful thing, in my opinion.\n男：在我看来，从事法律方面的工作是一件美好的事情。\n\nMany people will say it''s a boring field, but I disagree.\n很多人会说这是一个枯燥的领域，但我不认同。\n\nThe thing is there are many different branches of law and many different jobs.\n问题是法律有很多分支，也有很多不同的岗位。\n\nW: You are involved with buildings and construction, right?\n女：你从事的是建筑相关的领域，对吧？\n\nM: Correct. I''m a solicitor, specializing in real estate.\n男：没错。我是专攻房地产的律师。\n\nMost of my work involves mediating land disputes.\n我的大部分工作涉及调解土地纠纷。\n\nW: Do you mind giving me an example?\n女：你介意给我举个例子吗？\n\nM: Sure. So in many cases, I am employed to arbitrate between two clashing parties.\n男：当然（可以）。很多时候我被雇来在冲突双方之间进行调解。\n\nLet''s say, for example, there are two landowners who are in a thorny disagreement about something, like the borders of their adjacent plots.\n比如说有两个土地所有者，他们因为某些问题——比如相邻地块的边界——陷入棘手的争执。\n\nSomeone may employ me to break the deadlock and resolve the dispute.\n有人就会雇我来打破僵局并解决纠纷。\n\nOften my work involves negotiating agreements, plain and simple.\n通常我的工作就是促成协议，简单明了。\n\nW: So you are saying that a lot of what you do is fix people''s legal issues, like you try to find a solution that benefits everyone and that prevents a problem from escalating.\n女：所以你的意思是，你的工作主要是解决人们的法律问题，比如说你努力找到一个对各方都有利且避免矛盾升级的方案？\n\nM: Exactly. Well put. You need to remember that courts, like all bureaucracies really, can be very messy, frustrating and expensive.\n男：完全正确。说得很好。你要记住，法院真的就像所有官僚机构一样，（程序）可能非常混乱、令人沮丧且费用高昂。\n\nFor this reason, it''s usually better to resolve problems outside of court whenever possible.\n因此，只要有可能，庭外解决问题通常更好。\n\nW: I see. So besides knowing the law inside out, you need good people skills, right?\n女：我明白了。所以除了精通法律，还需要出色的人际交往能力，对吧？\n\nM: Of course. Any job that involves people requires good interpersonal skills, and any law professional needs to be very eloquent at articulating their arguments.\n男：当然。任何与人打交道的工作都需要良好的沟通技巧，而且任何一位法律从业者都需要能言善辩，能够清楚表达自己的观点。\n\nW: Right. So I''ve been thinking about studying criminal law.\n女：是的。我在考虑学习刑法。\n\nI think it sounds very interesting.\n我觉得刑法听起来很有意思。\n\nM: Mm, yes. I''d say there''s more money in property law, but the stakes are higher in criminal law.\n男：嗯，确实。我想说财产法更赚钱，但刑法牵涉的利害关系更重大。\n\nI can see how you would find it more interesting.\n我能理解你为什么觉得它更有趣。\n\nQuestions 5 to 8 are based on the conversation you have just heard.\n请根据你刚刚听到的对话回答问题5到8。\n\n5.What will many people say about a career in law?\n5. 许多人对从事法律工作有什么看法？\n\n6.What does the man say most of his work involves?\n6. 男士说他的大部分工作涉及什么？\n\n7.Why does the man say it''s usually better to resolve problems outside of court whenever possible?\n7. 为什么男士说只要有可能，庭外解决问题通常更好？\n\n8.What does the man think is required of any law professional?\n8. 男士认为任何一位法律从业者都需要具备什么？\n\nSection B Directions: In this section, you will hear two passages.\nB节 说明：在本节中，你将会听到两篇短文。', 118, 1557.69, 223.50, 341.07, 402.16, 422.16, NULL, NULL, 'cet6-2025-06-1-g02', 'LONG_DIALOGUE', '[03:43.50]Conversation Two｜对话二\n[03:45.50]M: Have you given more thoughts to studying law?｜男：你有进一步考虑过学法律吗？\n[03:48.15]W: I''ve been thinking about it a lot. Yes.｜女：我确实考虑了很多。是的。\n[03:50.95]In fact, this is why I wished to speak to you.｜事实上，这就是我想和你谈谈的原因。\n[03:53.78]I wanted to hear more about what it''s like.｜我想多了解这个行业的情况。\n[03:56.51]M: A career in law is a beautiful thing, in my opinion.｜男：在我看来，从事法律方面的工作是一件美好的事情。\n[03:59.88]Many people will say it''s a boring field, but I disagree.｜很多人会说这是一个枯燥的领域，但我不认同。\n[04:03.89]The thing is there are many different branches of law and many different jobs.｜问题是法律有很多分支，也有很多不同的岗位。\n[04:08.43]W: You are involved with buildings and construction, right?｜女：你从事的是建筑相关的领域，对吧？\n[04:12.10]M: Correct. I''m a solicitor, specializing in real estate.｜男：没错。我是专攻房地产的律师。\n[04:16.10]Most of my work involves mediating land disputes.｜我的大部分工作涉及调解土地纠纷。\n[04:19.28]W: Do you mind giving me an example?｜女：你介意给我举个例子吗？\n[04:21.30]M: Sure. So in many cases, I am employed to arbitrate between two clashing parties.｜男：当然（可以）。很多时候我被雇来在冲突双方之间进行调解。\n[04:28.01]Let''s say, for example, there are two landowners who are in a thorny disagreement about something, like the borders of their adjacent plots.｜比如说有两个土地所有者，他们因为某些问题——比如相邻地块的边界——陷入棘手的争执。\n[04:36.15]Someone may employ me to break the deadlock and resolve the dispute.｜有人就会雇我来打破僵局并解决纠纷。\n[04:40.56]Often my work involves negotiating agreements, plain and simple.｜通常我的工作就是促成协议，简单明了。\n[04:44.70]W: So you are saying that a lot of what you do is fix people''s legal issues, like you try to find a solution that benefits everyone and that prevents a problem from escalating.｜女：所以你的意思是，你的工作主要是解决人们的法律问题，比如说你努力找到一个对各方都有利且避免矛盾升级的方案？\n[04:56.06]M: Exactly. Well put. You need to remember that courts, like all bureaucracies really, can be very messy, frustrating and expensive.｜男：完全正确。说得很好。你要记住，法院真的就像所有官僚机构一样，（程序）可能非常混乱、令人沮丧且费用高昂。\n[05:05.00]For this reason, it''s usually better to resolve problems outside of court whenever possible.｜因此，只要有可能，庭外解决问题通常更好。\n[05:10.30]W: I see. So besides knowing the law inside out, you need good people skills, right?｜女：我明白了。所以除了精通法律，还需要出色的人际交往能力，对吧？\n[05:16.29]M: Of course. Any job that involves people requires good interpersonal skills, and any law professional needs to be very eloquent at articulating their arguments.｜男：当然。任何与人打交道的工作都需要良好的沟通技巧，而且任何一位法律从业者都需要能言善辩，能够清楚表达自己的观点。\n[05:26.08]W: Right. So I''ve been thinking about studying criminal law.｜女：是的。我在考虑学习刑法。\n[05:30.16]I think it sounds very interesting.｜我觉得刑法听起来很有意思。\n[05:32.14]M: Mm, yes. I''d say there''s more money in property law, but the stakes are higher in criminal law.｜男：嗯，确实。我想说财产法更赚钱，但刑法牵涉的利害关系更重大。\n[05:38.59]I can see how you would find it more interesting.｜我能理解你为什么觉得它更有趣。\n[05:41.07]Questions 5 to 8 are based on the conversation you have just heard.｜请根据你刚刚听到的对话回答问题5到8。\n[05:45.77]5.What will many people say about a career in law?｜5. 许多人对从事法律工作有什么看法？\n[06:03.74]6.What does the man say most of his work involves?｜6. 男士说他的大部分工作涉及什么？\n[06:21.01]7.Why does the man say it''s usually better to resolve problems outside of court whenever possible?｜7. 为什么男士说只要有可能，庭外解决问题通常更好？\n[06:42.16]8.What does the man think is required of any law professional?｜8. 男士认为任何一位法律从业者都需要具备什么？\n[07:00.33]Section B Directions: In this section, you will hear two passages.｜B节 说明：在本节中，你将会听到两篇短文。', NOW(), NOW()
