SELECT
  @a_cet6_2025_06_1_15, '/audio/exams/listening-cet6-2025-06-1.mp3', 'Passage Two\n短文二\n\nThere are at least four major problems with work in America today.\n当今美国的工作至少存在四大问题。\n\nFirst, work can be alienating.\n首先，工作可能使人疏离。\n\nWorkers are often not in control of how they work, when they work, what is done with the goods and services they produce, and what is done with the profits made from their work.\n工人通常无法掌控自己的工作方式、工作时间、对他们生产的商品和服务的处置权，以及对他们的劳动所创造的利润的支配权。\n\nSecond, workers are not paid the full value of their labor.\n其次，工人未能获得劳动的全部价值。\n\nReal wages have not kept pace with productivity, driving economic inequality and a decline in labor''s share of income.\n实际工资未能与生产率同步，加剧了经济不平等和劳动者收入份额的下降。\n\nThird, people are time-poor.\n第三，人们陷入时间贫困。\n\nIn the US, full-time employees work an average of 8.72 hours per day despite productivity increases.\n在美国，虽然生产率提升，但是全职员工日均工作8.72小时。\n\nLong working hours contribute to the feeling of time poverty, which has an adverse effect on psychological well-being.\n长时间工作加剧了时间匮乏感，这对心理健康造成负面影响。\n\nFourth, automation puts jobs and wages at risk.\n第四，自动化使工作与薪资陷入危险。\n\nTechnological innovation could in theory liberate people from the 40-hour workweek, but unless changes are made to the structure of work, automation will simply exert downward pressure on wages and further diminish work opportunities.\n理论上技术创新能将人们从40小时工作周中解放出来，但若不改变工作结构，自动化只会对工资造成下行压力，并且进一步减少工作机会。\n\nSo, what can be done to alleviate these problems?\n那么如何缓解这些问题？\n\nThere are competing visions of the best way to arrive at a solution.\n对于达成解决方案的最佳方式，存在几种不同的看法。\n\nOne vision is what''s known as the “post-work” position.\n其中一种被称为“后工作主义”立场。\n\nThe post-work theorists believe that work should not hold a central position in our lives or take up so much of our time.\n后工作理论家认为，工作不应占据我们生活的核心地位或消耗我们过多时间。\n\nThey assert that although doing some work might be necessary, meaning, purpose and social value reside in the communities and relationships built and sustained outside of the workplace.\n他们主张，尽管劳动有其必要性，但人生意义、目标和社会价值实则存在于职场之外构建与维系的社群和人际关系之中。\n\nThus, life should be seen as an end in itself.\n因此，生活本身应该被视为终极目的。\n\nQuestions 12 to 15 are based on the passage you have just heard.\n请根据你刚刚听到的短文回答问题12到15。\n\n12. What do we learn about American workers from the passage?\n12. 关于美国工人，我们从短文中了解到什么？\n\n13.What does the passage say long working hours contribute to?\n13. 短文说长时间工作会造成什么？\n\n14.What does automation do according to the passage?\n14. 根据短文，自动化能做什么？\n\n15.What do post-work theorists advocate?\n15. 后工作理论家主张什么？\n\nSection C Directions: In this section, you will hear three recordings of lectures or talks followed by three or four questions.\nC节 说明：在本节中，你将会听到三篇讲座或讲话，每篇讲座或讲话后面都有三个或四个问题。', 114, 1557.69, 628.17, 742.66, 802.31, 822.31, 725.69, 742.36, 'cet6-2025-06-1-g04', 'PASSAGE', '[10:28.17]Passage Two｜短文二\n[10:29.92]There are at least four major problems with work in America today.｜当今美国的工作至少存在四大问题。\n[10:34.97]First, work can be alienating.｜首先，工作可能使人疏离。\n[10:38.54]Workers are often not in control of how they work, when they work, what is done with the goods and services they produce, and what is done with the profits made from their work.｜工人通常无法掌控自己的工作方式、工作时间、对他们生产的商品和服务的处置权，以及对他们的劳动所创造的利润的支配权。\n[10:49.73]Second, workers are not paid the full value of their labor.｜其次，工人未能获得劳动的全部价值。\n[10:54.24]Real wages have not kept pace with productivity, driving economic inequality and a decline in labor''s share of income.｜实际工资未能与生产率同步，加剧了经济不平等和劳动者收入份额的下降。\n[11:02.70]Third, people are time-poor.｜第三，人们陷入时间贫困。\n[11:05.87]In the US, full-time employees work an average of 8.72 hours per day despite productivity increases.｜在美国，虽然生产率提升，但是全职员工日均工作8.72小时。\n[11:15.30]Long working hours contribute to the feeling of time poverty, which has an adverse effect on psychological well-being.｜长时间工作加剧了时间匮乏感，这对心理健康造成负面影响。\n[11:23.47]Fourth, automation puts jobs and wages at risk.｜第四，自动化使工作与薪资陷入危险。\n[11:29.12]Technological innovation could in theory liberate people from the 40-hour workweek, but unless changes are made to the structure of work, automation will simply exert downward pressure on wages and further diminish work opportunities.｜理论上技术创新能将人们从40小时工作周中解放出来，但若不改变工作结构，自动化只会对工资造成下行压力，并且进一步减少工作机会。\n[11:44.37]So, what can be done to alleviate these problems?｜那么如何缓解这些问题？\n[11:48.44]There are competing visions of the best way to arrive at a solution.｜对于达成解决方案的最佳方式，存在几种不同的看法。\n[11:53.15]One vision is what''s known as the “post-work” position.｜其中一种被称为“后工作主义”立场。\n[11:57.62]The post-work theorists believe that work should not hold a central position in our lives or take up so much of our time.｜后工作理论家认为，工作不应占据我们生活的核心地位或消耗我们过多时间。\n[12:05.69]They assert that although doing some work might be necessary, meaning, purpose and social value reside in the communities and relationships built and sustained outside of the workplace.｜他们主张，尽管劳动有其必要性，但人生意义、目标和社会价值实则存在于职场之外构建与维系的社群和人际关系之中。\n[12:17.62]Thus, life should be seen as an end in itself.｜因此，生活本身应该被视为终极目的。\n[12:22.66]Questions 12 to 15 are based on the passage you have just heard.｜请根据你刚刚听到的短文回答问题12到15。\n[12:27.32]12. What do we learn about American workers from the passage?｜12. 关于美国工人，我们从短文中了解到什么？\n[12:45.09]13.What does the passage say long working hours contribute to?｜13. 短文说长时间工作会造成什么？\n[13:04.58]14.What does automation do according to the passage?｜14. 根据短文，自动化能做什么？\n[13:22.31]15.What do post-work theorists advocate?｜15. 后工作理论家主张什么？\n[13:39.64]Section C Directions: In this section, you will hear three recordings of lectures or talks followed by three or four questions.｜C节 说明：在本节中，你将会听到三篇讲座或讲话，每篇讲座或讲话后面都有三个或四个问题。', NOW(), NOW()
