  @a_cet6_2025_06_2_03, '/audio/exams/listening-cet6-2025-06-2.mp3', 'Conversation One\n对话一\n\nW: We are down to two candidates for one position, and we need to decide by the end of the day in order to finalize this whole procedure.\n女：这个岗位我们筛选出了两位候选人，我们今天内必须决定人选，把整个流程走完。\n\nM: Yes, but it isn''t an easy choice to make. Both applicants are quite strong.\n男：是的，但选起来很难。两位申请人都非常优秀。\n\nW: Let''s get to it then. Both of them went to good universities, and both of them studied business-related subjects.\n女：那我们开始吧。他们上的都是名校，专业都与商科相关。\n\nSo, academically, I''d say they''re pretty much the same. What do you think?\n所以，在学术上，可以说旗鼓相当。你觉得呢？\n\nM: I would agree. Yes.\n男：我同意。是的。\n\nThe only difference worth noting, perhaps, is that it looks like Rachel scored moderately stronger grades throughout high school and university.\n唯一值得一提的区别的或许是瑞秋看起来从高中到大学的成绩都略高于彼得。\n\nBut as I said, only a tiny bit higher than Peter.\n但就像我说的，只比彼得高一点点。\n\nW: That''s true and worth noting. Thank you.\n女：是的，这值得一提。谢谢你。\n\nIn addition, Rachel interviewed very well.\n另外，瑞秋在面试中表现突出。\n\nI thought she came across as bright and alert.\n我感觉她聪明又机警。\n\nM: Yes. She asked some very good questions about the position and the company, which made me think she is very keen about the job.\n男：没错。她对职位和公司提出的一些问题很好，这让我感觉她对这份工作很感兴趣。\n\nW: I thought so too. Now let''s look at Peter''s interview performance.\n女：我也有同感。现在我们再来看看彼得的面试表现。\n\nI thought he also did very well. He came across as respectful and professional. Wouldn''t you say?\n我感觉他的表现也不错。他给人的印象是有礼貌而且专业。不是吗？\n\nCalm and poised; very mature for his age.\n沉稳又从容；就他的年龄而言，很成熟。\n\nM: Exactly. In my notes, I wrote that he seemed composed and in control of his emotions.\n男：完全正确。在我的记录里，我写的是他看起来很镇定，能控制自己的情绪。\n\nI think he definitely looked more mature than Rachel.\n我认为他绝对比瑞秋看起来更成熟。\n\nW: Interesting. So we agree that Rachel appeared inexperienced and less mature than Peter, even though both candidates are the same age and have practically no work experience.\n女：有意思。所以我们都认为，虽然两人同龄且都缺乏工作经验，但瑞秋显得不够老练，也不如彼得成熟。\n\nM: When comparing them side by side, yes, Peter seemed more self-assured, somehow.\n男：如果把他们并排对比，是这样的，不知道为什么，彼得显得更自信一些。\n\nMaybe it was something about their body language.\n可能和他们的肢体语言有关吧。\n\nW: Sure. Maybe he was simply less nervous.\n女：的确。可能他只是没那么紧张。\n\nM: Maybe. Who knows? To be honest, I think I like Rachel better.\n男：也许。谁知道呢？说实话，我觉得我更喜欢瑞秋。\n\nW: Hmm, really? I think I like Peter.\n女：嗯，真的？我觉得我喜欢彼得。\n\nM: Ah, well, if there''s a tie and we can''t come to an agreement, then we''ll take it to John and let him cast the deciding vote.\n男：啊，好吧，如果两位候选人出现平局，我们无法达成一致，那就把它交给约翰，让他来投决定性的一票吧。\n\nQuestions 1 to 4 are based on the conversation you have just heard.\n请根据你刚刚听到的对话回答问题1到4。\n\n1. Why does the man think it is difficult to make the decision?\n1.为什么男士认为很难做决定？\n\n2. What do the speakers say may be worth noting?\n2.对话双方认为什么可能值得注意？\n\n3. According to the man, what might account for Peter appearing somewhat more self-assured than Rachel?\n3.根据男士的说法，可能是什么原因导致彼得看起来比瑞秋更自信一些？\n\n4. What does the man say they will do if they can''t reach an agreement?\n4.男士说，如果无法达成一致，他们会怎么做？', 119, 1567.64, 38.43, 157.06, 197.78, 217.46, 135.76, 138.01, 'cet6-2025-06-2-g01', 'LONG_DIALOGUE', '[00:38.43]Conversation One｜对话一\n[00:40.36]W: We are down to two candidates for one position, and we need to decide by the end of the day in order to finalize this whole procedure.｜女：这个岗位我们筛选出了两位候选人，我们今天内必须决定人选，把整个流程走完。\n[00:49.05]M: Yes, but it isn''t an easy choice to make. Both applicants are quite strong.｜男：是的，但选起来很难。两位申请人都非常优秀。\n[00:54.60]W: Let''s get to it then. Both of them went to good universities, and both of them studied business-related subjects.｜女：那我们开始吧。他们上的都是名校，专业都与商科相关。\n[01:01.63]So, academically, I''d say they''re pretty much the same. What do you think?｜所以，在学术上，可以说旗鼓相当。你觉得呢？\n[01:06.36]M: I would agree. Yes.｜男：我同意。是的。\n[01:07.96]The only difference worth noting, perhaps, is that it looks like Rachel scored moderately stronger grades throughout high school and university.｜唯一值得一提的区别的或许是瑞秋看起来从高中到大学的成绩都略高于彼得。\n[01:15.85]But as I said, only a tiny bit higher than Peter.｜但就像我说的，只比彼得高一点点。\n[01:19.38]W: That''s true and worth noting. Thank you.｜女：是的，这值得一提。谢谢你。\n[01:22.26]In addition, Rachel interviewed very well.｜另外，瑞秋在面试中表现突出。\n[01:25.13]I thought she came across as bright and alert.｜我感觉她聪明又机警。\n[01:27.91]M: Yes. She asked some very good questions about the position and the company, which made me think she is very keen about the job.｜男：没错。她对职位和公司提出的一些问题很好，这让我感觉她对这份工作很感兴趣。\n[01:34.73]W: I thought so too. Now let''s look at Peter''s interview performance.｜女：我也有同感。现在我们再来看看彼得的面试表现。\n[01:39.12]I thought he also did very well. He came across as respectful and professional. Wouldn''t you say?｜我感觉他的表现也不错。他给人的印象是有礼貌而且专业。不是吗？\n[01:45.29]Calm and poised; very mature for his age.｜沉稳又从容；就他的年龄而言，很成熟。\n[01:49.00]M: Exactly. In my notes, I wrote that he seemed composed and in control of his emotions.｜男：完全正确。在我的记录里，我写的是他看起来很镇定，能控制自己的情绪。\n[01:54.90]I think he definitely looked more mature than Rachel.｜我认为他绝对比瑞秋看起来更成熟。\n[01:57.47]W: Interesting. So we agree that Rachel appeared inexperienced and less mature than Peter, even though both candidates are the same age and have practically no work experience.｜女：有意思。所以我们都认为，虽然两人同龄且都缺乏工作经验，但瑞秋显得不够老练，也不如彼得成熟。\n[02:09.92]M: When comparing them side by side, yes, Peter seemed more self-assured, somehow.｜男：如果把他们并排对比，是这样的，不知道为什么，彼得显得更自信一些。\n[02:15.76]Maybe it was something about their body language.｜可能和他们的肢体语言有关吧。\n[02:18.31]W: Sure. Maybe he was simply less nervous.｜女：的确。可能他只是没那么紧张。\n[02:21.39]M: Maybe. Who knows? To be honest, I think I like Rachel better.｜男：也许。谁知道呢？说实话，我觉得我更喜欢瑞秋。\n[02:26.25]W: Hmm, really? I think I like Peter.｜女：嗯，真的？我觉得我喜欢彼得。\n[02:29.23]M: Ah, well, if there''s a tie and we can''t come to an agreement, then we''ll take it to John and let him cast the deciding vote.｜男：啊，好吧，如果两位候选人出现平局，我们无法达成一致，那就把它交给约翰，让他来投决定性的一票吧。\n[02:37.06]Questions 1 to 4 are based on the conversation you have just heard.｜请根据你刚刚听到的对话回答问题1到4。\n[02:42.01]1. Why does the man think it is difficult to make the decision?｜1.为什么男士认为很难做决定？\n[02:59.99]2. What do the speakers say may be worth noting?｜2.对话双方认为什么可能值得注意？\n[03:17.78]3. According to the man, what might account for Peter appearing somewhat more self-assured than Rachel?｜3.根据男士的说法，可能是什么原因导致彼得看起来比瑞秋更自信一些？\n[03:37.76]4. What does the man say they will do if they can''t reach an agreement?｜4.男士说，如果无法达成一致，他们会怎么做？', NOW(), NOW()
