SELECT
  @a_cet6_2025_06_2_07, '/audio/exams/listening-cet6-2025-06-2.mp3', 'Conversation Two\n对话二\n\nM: We''re here with Clémentine Ortega, head designer of the private fashion label L''Orange, to discuss her latest collection.\n男：今天我们邀请到独立时装品牌L''Orange的首席设计师克莱门汀·奥尔特加女士来谈一谈她的最新系列。\n\nMs Ortega, how would you describe this season''s look?\n奥尔特加女士，您如何描述这一季的风格呢？\n\nW: To be honest, my preferred style has always been on the ambiguous side, and I think this collection is even more so.\n女：坦白说，我一直偏好那种不明确的风格，而且我觉得这季更是如此。\n\nI try not to adhere to social norms and expectations.\n我尽量不受社会规范和公众预期的约束。\n\nRather, I always try to incorporate something slightly absurd into my aesthetic.\n相反，我总是试图在我的审美风格中融入一些略微荒诞的元素。\n\nM: The assortment of accessories in this collection has had quite an impact on critics.\n男：本系列中各式各样的配饰对评论家们冲击很大。\n\nThe dazzling cape deployed at the end of the show, for example, bewildered many in the audience.\n比如在秀场末尾展示的那件耀眼披肩，就让观众们很困惑。\n\nWhat was your inspiration for this piece?\n您设计这件作品的灵感是什么？\n\nW: Over the summer, I travelled through rural mountain villages throughout Asia in search of handicrafts to decorate my new studio with.\n女：夏天的时候，我游历了亚洲各地的山区村落寻找一些手工艺品来装饰我的新工作室。\n\nThe embroidery done by the women in a particular village was so exquisite.\n有个村庄里妇女们的刺绣非常精美。\n\nI couldn''t stop thinking about it.\n我念念不忘。\n\nTrying to recreate their designs would have been futile.\n想要重现她们的图案是不可能的。\n\nSo instead, I applied my own eccentric approach.\n所以，我采用了我自有的怪异方法。\n\nUsing glitter, I drew similar, intricate patterns onto the velvet cape.\n我用闪光纸屑在天鹅绒披肩上画上了类似的复杂图案。\n\nThis ended up in the glamorous, luminous look that concluded the show.\n最终得到了秀场最后那件流光溢彩的作品。\n\nM: It was indeed majestic, and yet, dare I say masculine at the same time.\n男：确实很华丽，而且，我敢说，它同时还带有某种阳刚气质。\n\nW: Well, yes. That was intentional.\n女：嗯，是的。那是我有意为之的。\n\nI like to merge styles that are often at opposite ends of the fashion spectrum.\n我喜欢将时尚光谱两端的风格进行融合。\n\nHence the sparkling cape was paired with a traditional power suit you would typically see in a business setting.\n因此，我把那件闪闪发光的披风和一套你通常在商务场合看到的那种传统的商务正装搭配在一起。\n\nIt was sensational if I do say so myself.\n如果让我说的话，那简直是激动人心。\n\nM: Spectacular for sure. A stunning show all around.\n男：的确很令人惊叹。从头到尾都精彩绝伦的（时装）秀。\n\nGoing against stereotypes, the incorporation of indigenous aspects along with your underlying signature touch made this collection a statement of the season.\n打破陈规，将本土元素与您独到风格的融合，让本系列成为这一季的时尚宣言。\n\nYou have proven yourself a formidable young designer, and we can''t wait to see what creations you come up with next.\n您已经证实了自己是一位杰出的年轻设计师，我们也迫不及待想看到您下一季会带来什么样的创作。\n\nQuestions 5 to 8 are based on the conversation you have just heard.\n请根据你刚刚听到的对话回答问题5到8。\n\n5. What are the speakers mainly talking about?\n5.对话双方主要在谈论什么？\n\n6. What does the woman say she always tries to incorporate into her aesthetic?\n6.女士说她总是想把什么融入自己的审美风格中去？\n\n7. What does the woman say she likes to do?\n7.女士说她喜欢做什么？\n\n8. What is the man looking forward to?\n8.男士在期待什么？\n\nSection B Directions: In this section, you will hear two passages.\nB节 说明：在本节中，你将会听到两篇短文。', 123, 1567.64, 236.03, 358.71, 400.23, 416.78, 322.30, 326.83, 'cet6-2025-06-2-g02', 'LONG_DIALOGUE', '[03:56.03]Conversation Two｜对话二\n[03:58.14]M: We''re here with Clémentine Ortega, head designer of the private fashion label L''Orange, to discuss her latest collection.｜男：今天我们邀请到独立时装品牌L''Orange的首席设计师克莱门汀·奥尔特加女士来谈一谈她的最新系列。\n[04:06.36]Ms Ortega, how would you describe this season''s look?｜奥尔特加女士，您如何描述这一季的风格呢？\n[04:10.41]W: To be honest, my preferred style has always been on the ambiguous side, and I think this collection is even more so.｜女：坦白说，我一直偏好那种不明确的风格，而且我觉得这季更是如此。\n[04:18.52]I try not to adhere to social norms and expectations.｜我尽量不受社会规范和公众预期的约束。\n[04:22.66]Rather, I always try to incorporate something slightly absurd into my aesthetic.｜相反，我总是试图在我的审美风格中融入一些略微荒诞的元素。\n[04:28.23]M: The assortment of accessories in this collection has had quite an impact on critics.｜男：本系列中各式各样的配饰对评论家们冲击很大。\n[04:33.65]The dazzling cape deployed at the end of the show, for example, bewildered many in the audience.｜比如在秀场末尾展示的那件耀眼披肩，就让观众们很困惑。\n[04:39.58]What was your inspiration for this piece?｜您设计这件作品的灵感是什么？\n[04:42.41]W: Over the summer, I travelled through rural mountain villages throughout Asia in search of handicrafts to decorate my new studio with.｜女：夏天的时候，我游历了亚洲各地的山区村落寻找一些手工艺品来装饰我的新工作室。\n[04:50.65]The embroidery done by the women in a particular village was so exquisite.｜有个村庄里妇女们的刺绣非常精美。\n[04:55.21]I couldn''t stop thinking about it.｜我念念不忘。\n[04:57.28]Trying to recreate their designs would have been futile.｜想要重现她们的图案是不可能的。\n[05:00.86]So instead, I applied my own eccentric approach.｜所以，我采用了我自有的怪异方法。\n[05:04.74]Using glitter, I drew similar, intricate patterns onto the velvet cape.｜我用闪光纸屑在天鹅绒披肩上画上了类似的复杂图案。\n[05:10.21]This ended up in the glamorous, luminous look that concluded the show.｜最终得到了秀场最后那件流光溢彩的作品。\n[05:14.73]M: It was indeed majestic, and yet, dare I say masculine at the same time.｜男：确实很华丽，而且，我敢说，它同时还带有某种阳刚气质。\n[05:19.93]W: Well, yes. That was intentional.｜女：嗯，是的。那是我有意为之的。\n[05:22.30]I like to merge styles that are often at opposite ends of the fashion spectrum.｜我喜欢将时尚光谱两端的风格进行融合。\n[05:27.13]Hence the sparkling cape was paired with a traditional power suit you would typically see in a business setting.｜因此，我把那件闪闪发光的披风和一套你通常在商务场合看到的那种传统的商务正装搭配在一起。\n[05:34.67]It was sensational if I do say so myself.｜如果让我说的话，那简直是激动人心。\n[05:38.08]M: Spectacular for sure. A stunning show all around.｜男：的确很令人惊叹。从头到尾都精彩绝伦的（时装）秀。\n[05:42.20]Going against stereotypes, the incorporation of indigenous aspects along with your underlying signature touch made this collection a statement of the season.｜打破陈规，将本土元素与您独到风格的融合，让本系列成为这一季的时尚宣言。\n[05:51.61]You have proven yourself a formidable young designer, and we can''t wait to see what creations you come up with next.｜您已经证实了自己是一位杰出的年轻设计师，我们也迫不及待想看到您下一季会带来什么样的创作。\n[05:58.71]Questions 5 to 8 are based on the conversation you have just heard.｜请根据你刚刚听到的对话回答问题5到8。\n[06:03.82]5. What are the speakers mainly talking about?｜5.对话双方主要在谈论什么？\n[06:20.31]6. What does the woman say she always tries to incorporate into her aesthetic?｜6.女士说她总是想把什么融入自己的审美风格中去？\n[06:40.23]7. What does the woman say she likes to do?｜7.女士说她喜欢做什么？\n[06:57.08]8. What is the man looking forward to?｜8.男士在期待什么？\n[07:13.86]Section B Directions: In this section, you will hear two passages.｜B节 说明：在本节中，你将会听到两篇短文。', NOW(), NOW()
