SELECT
  @a_cet6_2025_06_2_09, '/audio/exams/listening-cet6-2025-06-2.mp3', 'Passage One\n短文一\n\nPet dogs can often readily understand a wide range of their owners'' commands and gestures.\n宠物狗通常能很容易理解主人的大量指令和手势。\n\nBut are these abilities inborn or are they exclusively learned through training?\n但这些能力是天生的，还是完全通过训练所得？\n\nTo find out, a new study examined whether stray dogs could understand human gestures.\n为了找到答案，一项新研究考查了流浪狗是否能理解人类的手势。\n\nThe study revealed that 80% of participating dogs successfully followed pointing gestures to a specific location despite having never received prior training.\n研究发现，即使先前从未接受过训练，80%参与研究的狗也能成功通过人类的指向性手势到达特定位置。\n\nThe results suggest that dogs can understand complex gestures by simply watching humans.\n这一发现说明仅通过对人类的观察，狗就能理解复杂的手势。\n\nThis could have implications in reducing conflict between stray dogs and humans.\n这项发现有助于缓解人类与流浪狗之间的冲突。\n\nDogs were domesticated 10,000 to 15,000 years ago.\n狗是在1到1.5万年前被驯化的。\n\nThis means they are probably the oldest domesticated animals on the planet.\n这意味着它们可能是地球上最早的家养动物。\n\nHumans then bred dogs with the most desirable and useful traits so that they could function as companions and workers.\n人类饲养那些具有最讨喜、最有用的特征的狗，让它们充当伙伴和劳力。\n\nThis resulted in domesticated dogs that are highly responsive to human commands and gestures.\n最终造就了对人类指令和手势反应良好的家犬。\n\nHowever, it was not clear whether dogs understand us through training alone, or whether this was an inherent ability.\n然而，依然无法确定狗是通过训练才能理解我们，还是这是一种与生俱来的能力。\n\nWhy does this matter?\n为什么弄清楚这一点那么重要呢？\n\nStray dogs are a common feature in cities around the world.\n流浪狗在世界各地的各个城市之中都很常见。\n\nThey may observe and occasionally interact with people, but such dogs have never been trained and are behaviorally “wild”.\n它们会观察人类并偶尔与人互动，但它们是没有经过训练的，而且行为是“野性的”。\n\nConflicts between stray dogs and humans are a problem.\n流浪狗与人类之间的冲突是个大问题。\n\nUnderstanding how humans shape stray dogs'' behavior may help alleviate this problem.\n理解人类如何影响流浪狗的行为可能有助于缓解这个问题。\n\nAccording to the researchers of the new study, stray dogs are intelligent creatures.\n该项目的研究人员认为，流浪狗是很聪明的动物。\n\nThey closely observe humans and use their understanding of us to make a decision.\n它们会仔细观察人类，并根据它们对我们的理解去做出决定。\n\n“Treating stray dogs with sensitivity and respect and giving them space,” the researchers assert, “can reduce much conflict.”\n研究人员说：“体恤流浪狗，尊重它们并给它们空间，就会减少很多冲突。”\n\nQuestions 9 to 11 are based on the passage you have just heard.\n请根据你刚刚听到的短文回答问题9到11。\n\n9. What does the passage say about 80% of participating dogs in the new study?\n9. 关于参与这项研究的80%的狗，短文说了什么？\n\n10. What may help alleviate the problem caused by stray dogs?\n10.什么可能有助于缓解流浪狗所导致的问题？\n\n11. What do the researchers suggest we do to reduce conflicts between stray dogs and humans?\n11.研究人员建议我们做什么去减少流浪狗与人类之间的冲突？', 125, 1567.64, 462.71, 587.80, 592.49, 611.93, 482.78, 493.84, 'cet6-2025-06-2-g03', 'PASSAGE', '[07:42.71]Passage One｜短文一\n[07:44.63]Pet dogs can often readily understand a wide range of their owners'' commands and gestures.｜宠物狗通常能很容易理解主人的大量指令和手势。\n[07:51.08]But are these abilities inborn or are they exclusively learned through training?｜但这些能力是天生的，还是完全通过训练所得？\n[07:56.51]To find out, a new study examined whether stray dogs could understand human gestures.｜为了找到答案，一项新研究考查了流浪狗是否能理解人类的手势。\n[08:02.78]The study revealed that 80% of participating dogs successfully followed pointing gestures to a specific location despite having never received prior training.｜研究发现，即使先前从未接受过训练，80%参与研究的狗也能成功通过人类的指向性手势到达特定位置。\n[08:14.14]The results suggest that dogs can understand complex gestures by simply watching humans.｜这一发现说明仅通过对人类的观察，狗就能理解复杂的手势。\n[08:21.12]This could have implications in reducing conflict between stray dogs and humans.｜这项发现有助于缓解人类与流浪狗之间的冲突。\n[08:26.88]Dogs were domesticated 10,000 to 15,000 years ago.｜狗是在1到1.5万年前被驯化的。\n[08:32.31]This means they are probably the oldest domesticated animals on the planet.｜这意味着它们可能是地球上最早的家养动物。\n[08:37.50]Humans then bred dogs with the most desirable and useful traits so that they could function as companions and workers.｜人类饲养那些具有最讨喜、最有用的特征的狗，让它们充当伙伴和劳力。\n[08:45.82]This resulted in domesticated dogs that are highly responsive to human commands and gestures.｜最终造就了对人类指令和手势反应良好的家犬。\n[08:52.50]However, it was not clear whether dogs understand us through training alone, or whether this was an inherent ability.｜然而，依然无法确定狗是通过训练才能理解我们，还是这是一种与生俱来的能力。\n[09:01.12]Why does this matter?｜为什么弄清楚这一点那么重要呢？\n[09:03.05]Stray dogs are a common feature in cities around the world.｜流浪狗在世界各地的各个城市之中都很常见。\n[09:06.99]They may observe and occasionally interact with people, but such dogs have never been trained and are behaviorally “wild”.｜它们会观察人类并偶尔与人互动，但它们是没有经过训练的，而且行为是“野性的”。\n[09:16.12]Conflicts between stray dogs and humans are a problem.｜流浪狗与人类之间的冲突是个大问题。\n[09:20.33]Understanding how humans shape stray dogs'' behavior may help alleviate this problem.｜理解人类如何影响流浪狗的行为可能有助于缓解这个问题。\n[09:26.70]According to the researchers of the new study, stray dogs are intelligent creatures.｜该项目的研究人员认为，流浪狗是很聪明的动物。\n[09:32.59]They closely observe humans and use their understanding of us to make a decision.｜它们会仔细观察人类，并根据它们对我们的理解去做出决定。\n[09:38.70]“Treating stray dogs with sensitivity and respect and giving them space,” the researchers assert, “can reduce much conflict.”｜研究人员说：“体恤流浪狗，尊重它们并给它们空间，就会减少很多冲突。”\n[09:47.80]Questions 9 to 11 are based on the passage you have just heard.｜请根据你刚刚听到的短文回答问题9到11。\n[09:52.49]9. What does the passage say about 80% of participating dogs in the new study?｜9. 关于参与这项研究的80%的狗，短文说了什么？\n[10:12.23]10. What may help alleviate the problem caused by stray dogs?｜10.什么可能有助于缓解流浪狗所导致的问题？\n[10:31.60]11. What do the researchers suggest we do to reduce conflicts between stray dogs and humans?｜11.研究人员建议我们做什么去减少流浪狗与人类之间的冲突？', NOW(), NOW()
