SELECT
  @a_cet6_2025_06_2_15, '/audio/exams/listening-cet6-2025-06-2.mp3', 'Passage Two\n短文二\n\nThink your refrigerator is just one big box of evenly cold air? Not so！\n你以为冰箱就是一个冷空气均匀的大盒子吗？事实并非如此！\n\nThe temperature inside the average fridge actually varies from front to back, bottom to top and everywhere in between.\n实际上，普通冰箱内部，从前到后，从上到下，各个区域的温度都有所不同。\n\nBecause of this, food product placement within the appliance is far more important than you probably realize.\n因此，食物在冰箱中的摆放位置比你想象的要重要得多。\n\nThe whole purpose of the modern refrigerator is to slow the growth of bacteria, which thrive in temperatures from 4.4 to 60 ℃.\n现代冰箱的主要目的是减缓细菌的繁殖，而细菌最适宜生长的温度是在4.4℃到60℃之间。\n\nAs a result, refrigerators are typically set at or below that low end to protect foods against bacteria.\n因此，冰箱温度通常会设置在这个下限或更低，来防止食物受到细菌污染。\n\nAlthough it might seem like time spent organizing the fridge will spoil your day, doing so will actually make it more user-friendly, easier to clean and food safety-conscious.\n虽然整理冰箱看起来好像破坏了一天的好时光，但实际上这样做可以让冰箱更方便使用、更容易清洁，而且更有利于食品安全。\n\nThose little bins on the inside of refrigerator doors are convenient, but they don''t maintain a consistent temperature, so definitely refrain from putting perishable foods in there.\n冰箱门内侧的那些小储物格虽然很方便，但温度不稳定，所以千万不要把容易腐烂变质的食物放在那里。\n\nThe top area is not as cold as the bottom of the fridge, so save it for the foods that don''t need extra-chilly temperatures.\n冰箱的上部温度没有底部低，所以可以用来存放不需要特别低温保存的食物。\n\nStore foods that are ready-to-eat or already cooked on the top shelf.\n将可即食的或已经做熟的食品存放在最上层。\n\nThe middle shelf is the most temperature-controlled part of the fridge, so place eggs here.\n冰箱的中层是温度最为稳定的部分，所以把鸡蛋放在这里。\n\nDrinks and prepared foods can also live on the middle shelf if you run out of room up top.\n如果上层放不下了，饮料和熟食也可以放在中层。\n\nThe back of the bottom shelf is the coldest spot in the fridge, so store perishable dairy products here to keep them edible, longer.\n冰箱底层靠后的位置是整个冰箱里最冷的地方，可以把容易变质的奶制品放在那里可以保存更久。\n\nNever store foods with high water content here, because the water within them can and will freeze, effectively ruining them.\n千万不要把含水量高的食物放在那儿，因为里面的水分会结冰，从而毁掉食物。\n\nQuestions 12 to 15 are based on the passage you have just heard.\n请根据你刚刚听到的短文回答问题12到15。\n\n12. Why is food product placement within the fridge very important?\n12.为什么食物在冰箱内的摆放位置很重要？\n\n13. What does the passage say is the whole purpose of the modern refrigerator?\n13.短文中说，现代冰箱的主要目的是什么？\n\n14. Where in the fridge should we store foods already cooked?\n14.我们应该把已经做熟的食品存放在冰箱的哪里？\n\n15. Why should we never store foods with high water content at the back of the bottom shelf?\n15.为什么我们不能把含水量高的食物存放在（冰箱）底层靠后的位置？', 112, 1567.64, 652.00, 763.91, 825.11, 845.11, NULL, NULL, 'cet6-2025-06-2-g04', 'PASSAGE', '[10:52.00]Passage Two｜短文二\n[10:53.73]Think your refrigerator is just one big box of evenly cold air? Not so！｜你以为冰箱就是一个冷空气均匀的大盒子吗？事实并非如此！\n[10:59.72]The temperature inside the average fridge actually varies from front to back, bottom to top and everywhere in between.｜实际上，普通冰箱内部，从前到后，从上到下，各个区域的温度都有所不同。\n[11:07.85]Because of this, food product placement within the appliance is far more important than you probably realize.｜因此，食物在冰箱中的摆放位置比你想象的要重要得多。\n[11:15.59]The whole purpose of the modern refrigerator is to slow the growth of bacteria, which thrive in temperatures from 4.4 to 60 ℃.｜现代冰箱的主要目的是减缓细菌的繁殖，而细菌最适宜生长的温度是在4.4℃到60℃之间。\n[11:26.67]As a result, refrigerators are typically set at or below that low end to protect foods against bacteria.｜因此，冰箱温度通常会设置在这个下限或更低，来防止食物受到细菌污染。\n[11:35.13]Although it might seem like time spent organizing the fridge will spoil your day, doing so will actually make it more user-friendly, easier to clean and food safety-conscious.｜虽然整理冰箱看起来好像破坏了一天的好时光，但实际上这样做可以让冰箱更方便使用、更容易清洁，而且更有利于食品安全。\n[11:48.20]Those little bins on the inside of refrigerator doors are convenient, but they don''t maintain a consistent temperature, so definitely refrain from putting perishable foods in there.｜冰箱门内侧的那些小储物格虽然很方便，但温度不稳定，所以千万不要把容易腐烂变质的食物放在那里。\n[11:59.66]The top area is not as cold as the bottom of the fridge, so save it for the foods that don''t need extra-chilly temperatures.｜冰箱的上部温度没有底部低，所以可以用来存放不需要特别低温保存的食物。\n[12:07.64]Store foods that are ready-to-eat or already cooked on the top shelf.｜将可即食的或已经做熟的食品存放在最上层。\n[12:12.56]The middle shelf is the most temperature-controlled part of the fridge, so place eggs here.｜冰箱的中层是温度最为稳定的部分，所以把鸡蛋放在这里。\n[12:18.89]Drinks and prepared foods can also live on the middle shelf if you run out of room up top.｜如果上层放不下了，饮料和熟食也可以放在中层。\n[12:26.12]The back of the bottom shelf is the coldest spot in the fridge, so store perishable dairy products here to keep them edible, longer.｜冰箱底层靠后的位置是整个冰箱里最冷的地方，可以把容易变质的奶制品放在那里可以保存更久。\n[12:35.28]Never store foods with high water content here, because the water within them can and will freeze, effectively ruining them.｜千万不要把含水量高的食物放在那儿，因为里面的水分会结冰，从而毁掉食物。\n[12:43.91]Questions 12 to 15 are based on the passage you have just heard.｜请根据你刚刚听到的短文回答问题12到15。\n[12:49.29]12. Why is food product placement within the fridge very important?｜12.为什么食物在冰箱内的摆放位置很重要？\n[13:07.18]13. What does the passage say is the whole purpose of the modern refrigerator?｜13.短文中说，现代冰箱的主要目的是什么？\n[13:27.07]14. Where in the fridge should we store foods already cooked?｜14.我们应该把已经做熟的食品存放在冰箱的哪里？\n[13:45.11]15. Why should we never store foods with high water content at the back of the bottom shelf?｜15.为什么我们不能把含水量高的食物存放在（冰箱）底层靠后的位置？', NOW(), NOW()
