event, and we are trying to understand the impact of depression.｜在其中一个课题中，我们聚焦老年人髋部骨折这一常见问题，并且，我们重点探索抑郁症的影响。\n[14:57.32]Often people in hospital with a hip fracture develop depression, and these are the people that then go on to become feeble a lot more quickly than others.｜髋部骨折住院患者往往会出现抑郁症状，这些患者的虚弱速度明显快于其他患者。\n[15:07.56]They get infections; often, these infections lead to death.｜他们发生感染，这些感染常常导致死亡。\n[15:12.06]So we''re trying to slow down that progression to feebleness.｜因此我们正努力延缓这种衰弱进程。\n[15:16.14]So if we can better understand how these factors interact, then we can actually start doing something about it.｜所以，如果能更好地理解这些因素的相互作用机制，我们就能开始着手解决这些问题。\n[15:23.49]The impact that my research will have in Birmingham, first of all, is obviously for older people, because these are the people that are having hip fractures and developing depression.｜我的研究对伯明翰地区的影响首先体现在老年人身上，因为他们患有髋部骨折和抑郁症。\n[15:35.60]And we''re trying to improve their health and their quality of life.｜我们致力于改善他们的健康状况和生活品质。\n[15:39.71]But this isn''t just a problem in Birmingham or even in the UK.｜但这不仅是伯明翰的问题，也不仅是英国的问题。\n[15:44.63]This is a problem globally. People are aging.｜这是一个全球性的问题。人们在变老。\n[15:48.24]There''re a lot more people in the older generation who are living for longer, but not necessarily staying healthy for a large part of their lives.｜越来越多的老年人寿命延长，但他们生命的很大一部分时间里却往往不能保持健康状态。\n[15:57.50]So the last part of their life can often be full of ill health and we''re trying to understand factors that can contribute to the quality of life later on.｜因此，他们的晚年健康状况欠佳，而我们正致力于了解那些影响晚年生活质量的因素。\n[16:07.92]I think the thing that excites me most about my research is that it feels real and relevant.｜我觉得最令我兴奋的是这项研究让人感觉真实且具有相关性。\n[16:14.43]Lots of academics are probably very excited about their research, but it might not be that relevant to those around them.｜虽然很多学者都对自己的研究兴奋不已，但他们的研究却可能与周围人的生活并不相关。\n[16:22.08]Whereas I feel that the work I do is relevant to everyone, because everyone is aging.｜而我认为我所做的研究与每个人都息息相关，因为每个人都会老去。\n[16:27.96]Health is an issue for everyone, regardless of their age.｜健康是所有人都关心的问题，不论年龄几何。\n[16:32.00]And what I''m trying to do is understand the factors that affect health and how we can improve the quality of life and people.｜我所做的就是试图了解影响健康的因素，以及我们该如何改善人们的生活质量。\n[16:40.00]So that''s one of the things that really excites me about it.｜这就是我对这项研究充满热情的原因之一。\n[16:43.70]One of the other things is rather than just taking one perspective—so rather than looking at aging and health just from the perspective of the psychologist—we are now bringing together a lot of different techniques and a lot of different viewpoints to actually look at the sort of different factors affecting health.｜另一件事在于，我们不再只是从单一的角度出发——不再只是从心理学家的角度来看待衰老和健康问题，而是整合了许多技术手段和不同观点来研究影响健康的各种因素。\n[17:03.78]Questions 16 to 18 are based on the recording you have just heard.｜请根据你刚刚听到的录音回答问题16到18。\n[17:09.28]16. What does the speaker say is quite common among older people?｜16. 讲话者说什么在老年人群中很常见？\n[17:27.44]17. What does the speaker think excites her most about her research?｜17. 讲话者认为研究的哪个方面让她最为兴奋？\n[17:46.41]18. How does the speaker approach her research project?｜18. 讲话者是如何开展她的研究项目的？', NOW(), NOW()
