INSERT INTO `listening_audio`
  (`question_id`, `audio_url`, `transcript`, `duration_seconds`, `audio_total_seconds`, `audio_start_seconds`, `audio_end_seconds`, `question_start_seconds`, `question_end_seconds`, `answer_start_seconds`, `answer_end_seconds`, `group_key`, `listening_type`, `lrc_content`, `created_at`, `updated_at`)
SELECT
  @a_cet6_2025_12_1_01, '/audio/exams/listening-cet6-2025-12-1.mp3', 'Conversation One\n对话一\n\nW: Today''s special guest is Lord Blackwell, one of our country''s most experienced and distinguished career diplomats. Welcome!\n女：今天的特邀嘉宾是布莱克韦尔勋爵，他是我国资历最深、最杰出的职业外交官之一。欢迎!\n\nM: It''s my pleasure.\n男：荣幸之至。\n\nW: Our audience will be most interested in learning about a career in the foreign service.\n女：观众们肯定非常想了解外交部门的职业发展。\n\nHowever, before we talk about that, I''d like to ask you about the current developments hitting the news today regarding the Republic of Winopia.\n但在聊这个话题之前，我想先问问您近期关于维诺皮亚共和国的热点新闻有什么最新进展。\n\nWhat can you tell us?\n您能跟我们说一下吗？\n\nM: I''m afraid I don''t know much beyond what we''ve all seen on the news.\n男：恐怕我知道的也只是新闻里报道的那些内容。\n\nIt looks like the government of Winopia seems to be undergoing some sort of crisis of legitimacy, and an interim administration has been transitionally established until a head of state is agreed on.\n看起来维诺皮亚政府似乎在合法性方面出现了危机，在确定国家元首之前，已成立临时政府来进行过渡。\n\nBut my career work has mostly focused around the continental spheres of Europe and the Americas, and thus I''ve never been involved with Winopian relations.\n不过我的工作主要集中在欧洲和美洲大陆地区，因此我从未参与过与维诺皮亚的外交事务。\n\nIt''s for this reason that I don''t know anything on this matter beyond what we can all read in the newspapers.\n正因为如此，关于该国情况，我所知道的也不过是那些我们都可以从报纸上读到的信息。\n\nW: Oh, I see.\n女：哦，我明白了。\n\nM: Nevertheless, be rest assured that our expert envoys at our consulate there will be closely monitoring the situation, and I expect our bilateral relations with that country will not be affected.\n男：不过，请放心，我们驻当地领事馆的特使会密切关注局势，而且我预计我们与该国的双边关系不会受到影响。\n\nW: So how does one get a career in foreign relations?\n女：那人们如何才能在外交关系领域谋得一份事业呢？\n\nM: There are many different paths one can take.\n男：有很多不同的路径可选。\n\nAll diplomats have their own story.\n每位外交官都有自己的故事。\n\nBut in my case, I got a degree in electrical engineering followed by six years'' service in the air force.\n但就我而言，我先取得了电气工程学位，之后在空军服役六年。\n\nThen I went to law school, and upon obtaining a degree in international law, I joined the diplomatic corps where I have been for 22 years.\n随后，我进入了法学院，获得国际法学位后，加入外交使团，到现在已经在外交使团（工作了）22年。\n\nW: What would you say are the key skills one needs for the job?\n女：您认为这份工作需要具备哪些核心技能呢？\n\nM: There are so many.\n男：有很多。\n\nBeing a hard worker and a good student is important.\n勤奋努力、善于学习很重要。\n\nYou never stop learning.\n不断学习。\n\nIn addition, a diplomat needs to be very articulate in their discourse and rhetoric.\n此外，外交官的语言和措辞要清晰明确。\n\nWhether it is defusing attention or enacting policy, people and communication skills are vital.\n无论是平息舆论关注，还是推动政策实施，人际交往能力和沟通能力都至关重要。\n\nQuestions 1 to 4 are based on the conversation you have just heard.\n请根据你刚刚听到的对话回答问题1到4。\n\n1. What do we learn about the man from the conversation?\n1.我们从对话中了解到关于男士的什么信息？\n\n2. What does the man say the government of Winopia is probably undergoing?\n2.男士说维诺皮亚政府可能正在经历些什么？\n\n3. According to the man, how does one get a career in foreign relations?\n3.根据男士的观点，一个人要如何才能在外交领域谋得一份事业？\n\n4. What do the speakers mainly discuss by the end of the conversation?\n4.对话双方在对话结尾处主要讨论了什么内容？', 121, 1543.76, 36.12, 157.40, 161.88, 178.92, 47.76, 52.86, 'cet6-2025-12-1-g01', 'LONG_DIALOGUE', '[00:36.12]Conversation One｜对话一\n[00:37.96]W: Today''s special guest is Lord Blackwell, one of our country''s most experienced and distinguished career diplomats. Welcome!｜女：今天的特邀嘉宾是布莱克韦尔勋爵，他是我国资历最深、最杰出的职业外交官之一。欢迎!\n[00:46.12]M: It''s my pleasure.｜男：荣幸之至。\n[00:47.76]W: Our audience will be most interested in learning about a career in the foreign service.｜女：观众们肯定非常想了解外交部门的职业发展。\n[00:53.16]However, before we talk about that, I''d like to ask you about the current developments hitting the news today regarding the Republic of Winopia.｜但在聊这个话题之前，我想先问问您近期关于维诺皮亚共和国的热点新闻有什么最新进展。\n[01:02.36]What can you tell us?｜您能跟我们说一下吗？\n[01:04.16]M: I''m afraid I don''t know much beyond what we''ve all seen on the news.｜男：恐怕我知道的也只是新闻里报道的那些内容。\n[01:08.04]It looks like the government of Winopia seems to be undergoing some sort of crisis of legitimacy, and an interim administration has been transitionally established until a head of state is agreed on.｜看起来维诺皮亚政府似乎在合法性方面出现了危机，在确定国家元首之前，已成立临时政府来进行过渡。\n[01:20.32]But my career work has mostly focused around the continental spheres of Europe and the Americas, and thus I''ve never been involved with Winopian relations.｜不过我的工作主要集中在欧洲和美洲大陆地区，因此我从未参与过与维诺皮亚的外交事务。\n[01:30.60]It''s for this reason that I don''t know anything on this matter beyond what we can all read in the newspapers.｜正因为如此，关于该国情况，我所知道的也不过是那些我们都可以从报纸上读到的信息。\n[01:36.76]W: Oh, I see.｜女：哦，我明白了。\n[01:38.16]M: Nevertheless, be rest assured that our expert envoys at our consulate there will be closely monitoring the situation, and I expect our bilateral relations with that country will not be affected.｜男：不过，请放心，我们驻当地领事馆的特使会密切关注局势，而且我预计我们与该国的双边关系不会受到影响。\n[01:50.92]W: So how does one get a career in foreign relations?｜女：那人们如何才能在外交关系领域谋得一份事业呢？\n[01:54.76]M: There are many different paths one can take.｜男：有很多不同的路径可选。\n[01:57.52]All diplomats have their own story.｜每位外交官都有自己的故事。\n[01:59.67]But in my case, I got a degree in electrical engineering followed by six years'' service in the air force.｜但就我而言，我先取得了电气工程学位，之后在空军服役六年。\n[02:06.76]Then I went to law school, and upon obtaining a degree in international law, I joined the diplomatic corps where I have been for 22 years.｜随后，我进入了法学院，获得国际法学位后，加入外交使团，到现在已经在外交使团（工作了）22年。\n[02:15.12]W: What would you say are the key skills one needs for the job?｜女：您认为这份工作需要具备哪些核心技能呢？\n[02:19.40]M: There are so many.｜男：有很多。\n[02:21.04]Being a hard worker and a good student is important.｜勤奋努力、善于学习很重要。\n[02:23.96]You never stop learning.｜不断学习。\n[02:25.44]In addition, a diplomat needs to be very articulate in their discourse and rhetoric.｜此外，外交官的语言和措辞要清晰明确。\n[02:30.52]Whether it is defusing attention or enacting policy, people and communication skills are vital.｜无论是平息舆论关注，还是推动政策实施，人际交往能力和沟通能力都至关重要。\n[02:37.40]Questions 1 to 4 are based on the conversation you have just heard.｜请根据你刚刚听到的对话回答问题1到4。\n[02:41.88]1. What do we learn about the man from the conversation?｜1.我们从对话中了解到关于男士的什么信息？\n[02:59.22]2. What does the man say the government of Winopia is probably undergoing?｜2.男士说维诺皮亚政府可能正在经历些什么？\n[03:17.96]3. According to the man, how does one get a career in foreign relations?｜3.根据男士的观点，一个人要如何才能在外交领域谋得一份事业？\n[03:36.86]4. What do the speakers mainly discuss by the end of the conversation?｜4.对话双方在对话结尾处主要讨论了什么内容？', NOW(), NOW()
