delayed bags are only one flight behind their owners and can be delivered within 24 hours.\n大多数延误的行李只比主人晚到一个航班，通常能在24小时内送还给行李主人。\n\nThe other bags are examined by airline employees for clues to their ownership and destination.\n其余的行李会由航空公司工作人员进行检查，寻找能确定行李主人和目的地的线索。\n\nIf the mystery is solved, those bags are returned to their owners within four or five days.\n如果谜团得以解开，这些行李会在4至5天内归还给主人。\n\nBags with no destination code or identification tag are shipped to a central warehouse, and undergo a comprehensive baggage tracing process over the next 90 days.\n而那些没有目的地编码或行李牌的行李，会被运送到一个中央仓库，并在接下来的90天里接受全面的行李追踪流程。\n\nAirlines inventory their mishandled baggage, and many use a database to match the contents with owners'' descriptions.\n航空公司会对处理不当的行李进行清点，许多公司还会使用数据库，将行李内物品与主人的描述进行匹配。\n\nIt takes about three months to go from "missing in action" to "irretrievably lost".\n一件行李从"下落不明"到"无法找回"，大约需要三个月时间。\n\nOnce that happens, the bags are donated to charity, sold at auction, or purchased by a company which sells them to the public.\n一旦被判定为"无法找回"，这些行李会被捐赠给慈善机构、通过拍卖出售，或由某家公司收购后再卖给公众。\n\nSo never pack anything of real value in your checked baggage.\n因此，切勿将任何真正有价值的物品放在托运行李中。\n\nAnd make sure your name is on the bag, along with your phone number, so an agent can contact you.\n同时要确保行李上标注了你的姓名和电话号码，以便工作人员能够联系到你。\n\nQuestions 16 to 18 are based on the recording you have just heard.\n请根据你刚刚听到的录音回答问题16到18。\n\n16. What is the number-one reason a bag ends up lost according to this talk?\n16.根据该讲座，行李丢失的首要原因是什么？\n\n17. What may happen to your baggage even when there are sophisticated automated systems?\n17.即便（机场）配备了先进的自动化系统，你的行李仍可能发生什么情况？\n\n18. What does the speaker advise us to do at the end of the talk?\n18.讲座结尾处，讲话者建议我们怎么做？', 158, 1543.76, 834.42, 992.18, 1035.62, 1053.38, 981.54, 985.56, 'cet6-2025-12-1-g05', 'LECTURE', '[13:54.42]Recording One｜讲座一\n[13:56.50]Every year, of the more than 2.5 billion bags checked onto flights worldwide, 26 million go missing—and of that 26 million, 1 million never make it back to their original owner.｜每年，全球航班中的托运行李超过25亿件，其中丢失的数量为2600万件——而在这2600万件中，有100万件再也没回到原主人手中。\n[14:10.32]Bad weather and flight delays, miscoded destination tags and some people simply forgetting to pick up one of their bags are a few of the reasons.｜恶劣天气、航班延误、目的地标签编码错误，以及有的人仅仅是忘记把行李全部取走而落下一件，这些都是（导致行李丢失的）原因。\n[14:18.92]But the number-one reason a bag ends up lost is that it has no ID tag, and airlines don''t know to whom it belongs.｜但行李丢失的首要原因是行李上没有行李牌（IDtag），航空公司不知道它属于谁。\n[14:27.45]Transferring baggage from check-in to departure gates to arrival gates to baggage claim is a delicate piece of timing.｜将行李从值机柜台转运到出发登机口、再到到达登机口，最后送至行李提取处，这一过程的时间把控极为精细。\n[14:34.76]If the system moves too slowly, the bags won''t make connecting flights.｜如果系统运转太慢，行李就赶不上中转航班。\n[14:39.68]If it''s too fast, the bags may make the connection but the passengers might miss the flight.｜如果运转太快，行李倒是能赶上中转，但乘客是有可能错过航班的。\n[14:45.68]Each airport has its own way of allotting how much time a bag needs to move in transit.｜对于如何分配行李在转运过程中所需的时间，每个机场都有自己的方式。\n[14:51.56]Some airports have sophisticated automated systems, including scanners that read baggage labels, destination-coded vehicles that load and unload the bags without stopping, and sorting machines that route baggage to the appropriate gate.｜有些机场配备了先进的自动化系统，包括可读取行李标签的扫描仪、无须停靠就能装卸行李的目的地编码运输车，以及能将行李分拣至对应登机口的分拣机。\n[15:07.00]Even so, all that technology may not save your baggage tag from being torn off on the conveyor belt, making you the owner of a bag with no name.｜即便如此，这些技术却无法避免行李牌在传送带上被扯掉，而这会让你的行李成为没有姓名标注的行李。\n[15:17.30]Once a bag goes missing and the passenger files a claim, the bag is declared "mishandled" by the carrier.｜一旦行李丢失，且乘客提交了申领申请，航空公司就会将该行李定为"处理不当"。\n[15:23.82]Mishandled refers to bags that have been delayed, lost, stolen or damaged.｜处理不当指的是行李出现延误、丢失、被盗或损坏的情况。\n[15:29.90]Most delayed bags are only one flight behind their owners and can be delivered within 24 hours.｜大多数延误的行李只比主人晚到一个航班，通常能在24小时内送还给行李主人。\n[15:36.26]The other bags are examined by airline employees for clues to their ownership and destination.｜其余的行李会由航空公司工作人员进行检查，寻找能确定行李主人和目的地的线索。\n[15:42.50]If the mystery is solved, those bags are returned to their owners within four or five days.｜如果谜团得以解开，这些行李会在4至5天内归还给主人。\n[15:48.90]Bags with no destination code or identification tag are shipped to a central warehouse, and undergo a comprehensive baggage tracing process over the next 90 days.｜而那些没有目的地编码或行李牌的行李，会被运送到一个中央仓库，并在接下来的90天里接受全面的行李追踪流程。\n[16:00.82]Airlines inventory their mishandled baggage, and many use a database to match the contents with owners'' descriptions.｜航空公司会对处理不当的行李进行清点，许多公司还会使用数据库，将行李内物品与主人的描述进行匹配。\n[16:07.90]It takes about three months to go from "missing in action" to "irretrievably lost".｜一件行李从"下落不明"到"无法找回"，大约需要三个月时间。\n[16:13.18]Once that happens, the bags are donated to charity, sold at auction, or purchased by a company which sells them to the public.｜一旦被判定为"无法找回"，这些行李会被捐赠给慈善机构、通过拍卖出售，或由某家公司收购后再卖给公众。\n[16:21.54]So never pack anything of real value in your checked baggage.｜因此，切勿将任何真正有价值的物品放在托运行李中。\n[16:25.86]And make sure your name is on the bag, along with your phone number, so an agent can contact you.｜同时要确保行李上标注了你的姓名和电话号码，以便工作人员能够联系到你。\n[16:32.18]Questions 16 to 18 are based on the recording you have just heard.｜请根据你刚刚听到的录音回答问题16到18。\n[16:36.78]16. What is the number-one reason a bag ends up lost according to this talk?｜16.根据该讲座，行李丢失的首要原因是什么？\n[16:55.86]17. What may happen to your baggage even when there are sophisticated automated systems?｜17.即便（机场）配备了先进的自动化系统，你的行李仍可能发生什么情况？\n[17:15.62]18. What does the speaker advise us to do at the end of the talk?｜18.讲座结尾处，讲话者建议我们怎么做？', NOW(), NOW()
