  (`question_id`, `audio_url`, `transcript`, `duration_seconds`, `audio_total_seconds`, `audio_start_seconds`, `audio_end_seconds`, `question_start_seconds`, `question_end_seconds`, `answer_start_seconds`, `answer_end_seconds`, `group_key`, `listening_type`, `lrc_content`, `created_at`, `updated_at`)
SELECT
  @a_cet6_2025_12_1_25, '/audio/exams/listening-cet6-2025-12-1.mp3', 'Recording Three\n讲座三\n\nMore and more people travel for a variety of reasons.\n越来越多的人出于各种原因出行。\n\nMany are tourists, but many venture forth on personal or professional business.\n其中许多是游客，但也有不少人是因个人事务或工作出差（而出行）。\n\nWhatever the reason for traveling, a common complaint of travelers is the impersonal accommodations they find.\n无论出行原因是什么，人们常常抱怨的一点就是缺乏人情味的住宿。\n\nAfter spending five consecutive nights in five similar hotels, the business traveler may find it difficult to remember what happened from day to day, or even what towns were visited,\n商务旅行者在连续五晚入住五家相似的酒店后，可能会难以记清每天都发生了什么，甚至记不清去过哪些城镇；\n\nand the tourist may get the mistaken impression that all cities are pretty much the same, at least as far as decoration, food and service are concerned.\n而游客则可能产生一种错觉——所有城市都大同小异，至少在装修、餐饮和服务方面是这样。\n\nTo combat this sense of impersonal sameness, travelers are taking advantage of in-home hospitality or Bed and Breakfast arrangements.\n为了摆脱这种缺乏人情味、千篇一律的感觉，旅行者开始选择家庭接待或住宿加早餐的住宿方式。\n\nB&Bs, I mean, Bed and Breakfast arrangements are private homes which offer lodging and breakfast in a very personalized, friendly setting.\nB&B（即，民宿。下文都会翻译为"民宿"），我的意思是，住宿加早餐模式，指的是环境极具个性化且非常友好的私人住宅，可以为客人提供住宿和早餐。\n\nFor decades, B&Bs have been the classic way to visit Europe, especially the British Isles.\n几十年来，民宿一直是游览欧洲，尤其是不列颠群岛的经典住宿方式。\n\nAnd in fact, they are not really a new idea in America.\n而且事实上，在美国，民宿也并非全新的概念。\n\nThe tradition dates back to colonial times when inns were few and far between, and the weary traveler had to depend on the kindness of strangers for a meal and a bed.\n这一传统可追溯到殖民时期。当时客栈数量稀少，相距很远，疲惫的旅行者不得不依靠陌生人的善意获得食宿。\n\nBut the revival of B&Bs as desirable accommodations is a fairly recent phenomenon.\n但民宿作为受欢迎的住宿方式重新兴起，却是相当新近的现象。\n\nIf the idea of operating a B&B arouses your interest, there are several factors to consider before plunging into this business.\n如果你对经营一家民宿产生了兴趣，在投身这一行业之前，有几个因素需要考虑。\n\nThe first consideration is your property, not only the building itself, but the location.\n首先要考虑到的是你的房产，不仅要考虑到建筑本身，还要考虑到它的地理位置。\n\nIf you live near a famous historical site or in a popular destination, such as New York City or Washington, D.C., your home can be fairly simple, yet still do well as a B&B.\n如果你住在著名历史景点附近，或是住在像纽约、华盛顿特区等热门目的地，即使你的房子（装修）简单，也可以将民宿经营得不错。\n\nOn the other hand, if your home is architecturally unique or has facilities for the traveler, such as a private entrance, private bath or swimming pool,\n另一方面，如果你的房子建筑风格独特，或为旅行者配备了专门的设施（如独立入口、独立浴室或游泳池），\n\npeople may be willing to go some distance to reach you.\n人们可能也愿意远道前来入住。\n\nAnother important factor is the lifestyle of you and your family.\n另一个重要因素是你和家人的生活方式。\n\nYou must take into account whether all members of the family truly enjoy visitors, want to repeatedly discuss local sites and activities, and have the time and energy to handle the additional cooking, cleaning, laundry and the bookkeeping involved.\n你必须考虑到是否所有家庭成员都真的喜欢接待客人，他们是否愿意反复向客人介绍当地的景点和活动，以及他们是否有时间和精力承担额外的烹饪、清洁、洗衣以及记账工作。\n\nThe final consideration is a financial one: potential B&B hosts must be realistic about opportunities for income.\n最后一个需要考虑到的是财务问题：潜在的民宿经营者必须对收入机会有现实的估量。\n\nWhile B&Bs usually have low initial costs, experts estimate it would take at least five rooms rented regularly for the host to earn a living from B&B.\n尽管经营民宿的初始成本通常较低，但专家估计，经营者至少需要保证五间客房常年有客人入住，才能靠民宿维持生计。\n\nQuestions 22 to 25 are based on the recording you have just heard.\n请根据你刚刚听到的录音回答问题22到25。\n\n22. What does the speaker say travelers commonly complain about?\n22.讲话者说旅行者常常抱怨什么？\n\n23. What is said about Bed and Breakfast arrangements?\n23.关于提供住宿和早餐的旅馆，讲座中提到了些什么？\n\n24. What is the first thing you have to consider if you want to start a B&B business?\n24.如果想经营一家民宿，首先需要考虑的是什么？\n\n25. What does the speaker say potential B&B hosts must be realistic about?\n25.说话者说潜在的民宿经营者必须对什么有现实的估量？', 162, 1543.76, 1296.36, 1458.44, 1519.92, 1531.92, 1438.56, 1446.66, 'cet6-2025-12-1-g07', 'LECTURE', '[21:36.36]Recording Three｜讲座三\n[21:38.08]More and more people travel for a variety of reasons.｜越来越多的人出于各种原因出行。\n[21:41.68]Many are tourists, but many venture forth on personal or professional business.｜其中许多是游客，但也有不少人是因个人事务或工作出差（而出行）。\n[21:47.24]Whatever the reason for traveling, a common complaint of travelers is the impersonal accommodations they find.｜无论出行原因是什么，人们常常抱怨的一点就是缺乏人情味的住宿。\n[21:54.24]After spending five consecutive nights in five similar hotels, the business traveler may find it difficult to remember what happened from day to day, or even what towns were visited,｜商务旅行者在连续五晚入住五家相似的酒店后，可能会难以记清每天都发生了什么，甚至记不清去过哪些城镇；\n[22:05.40]and the tourist may get the mistaken impression that all cities are pretty much the same, at least as far as decoration, food and service are concerned.｜而游客则可能产生一种错觉——所有城市都大同小异，至少在装修、餐饮和服务方面是这样。\n[22:16.22]To combat this sense of impersonal sameness, travelers are taking advantage of in-home hospitality or Bed and Breakfast arrangements.｜为了摆脱这种缺乏人情味、千篇一律的感觉，旅行者开始选择家庭接待或住宿加早餐的住宿方式。\n[22:24.82]B&Bs, I mean, Bed and Breakfast arrangements are private homes which offer lodging and breakfast in a very personalized, friendly setting.｜B&B（即，民宿。下文都会翻译为"民宿"），我的意思是，住宿加早餐模式，指的是环境极具个性化且非常友好的私人住宅，可以为客人提供住宿和早餐。\n[22:34.68]For decades, B&Bs have been the classic way to visit Europe, especially the British Isles.｜几十年来，民宿一直是游览欧洲，尤其是不列颠群岛的经典住宿方式。\n[22:39.88]And in fact, they are not really a new idea in America.｜而且事实上，在美国，民宿也并非全新的概念。\n[22:43.68]The tradition dates back to colonial times when inns were few and far between, and the weary traveler had to depend on the kindness of strangers for a meal and a bed.｜这一传统可追溯到殖民时期。当时客栈数量稀少，相距很远，疲惫的旅行者不得不依靠陌生人的善意获得食宿。\n[22:53.68]But the revival of B&Bs as desirable accommodations is a fairly recent phenomenon.｜但民宿作为受欢迎的住宿方式重新兴起，却是相当新近的现象。\n[22:59.96]If the idea of operating a B&B arouses your interest, there are several factors to consider before plunging into this business.｜如果你对经营一家民宿产生了兴趣，在投身这一行业之前，有几个因素需要考虑。\n[23:07.52]The first consideration is your property, not only the building itself, but the location.｜首先要考虑到的是你的房产，不仅要考虑到建筑本身，还要考虑到它的地理位置。\n[23:13.00]If you live near a famous historical site or in a popular destination, such as New York City or Washington, D.C., your home can be fairly simple, yet still do well as a B&B.｜如果你住在著名历史景点附近，或是住在像纽约、华盛顿特区等热门目的地，即使你的房子（装修）简单，也可以将民宿经营得不错。\n[23:25.28]On the other hand, if your home is architecturally unique or has facilities for the traveler, such as a private entrance, private bath or swimming pool,｜另一方面，如果你的房子建筑风格独特，或为旅行者配备了专门的设施（如独立入口、独立浴室或游泳池），\n[23:34.56]people may be willing to go some distance to reach you.｜人们可能也愿意远道前来入住。\n[23:38.40]Another important factor is the lifestyle of you and your family.｜另一个重要因素是你和家人的生活方式。\n[23:43.12]You must take into account whether all members of the family truly enjoy visitors, want to repeatedly discuss local sites and activities, and have the time and energy to handle the additional cooking, cleaning, laundry and the bookkeeping involved.｜你必须考虑到是否所有家庭成员都真的喜欢接待客人，他们是否愿意反复向客人介绍当地的景点和活动，以及他们是否有时间和精力承担额外的烹饪、清洁、洗衣以及记账工作。\n[23:58.56]The final consideration is a financial one: potential B&B hosts must be realistic about opportunities for income.｜最后一个需要考虑到的是财务问题：潜在的民宿经营者必须对收入机会有现实的估量。\n[24:06.96]While B&Bs usually have low initial costs, experts estimate it would take at least five rooms rented regularly for the host to earn a living from B&B.｜尽管经营民宿的初始成本通常较低，但专家估计，经营者至少需要保证五间客房常年有客人入住，才能靠民宿维持生计。\n[24:18.44]Questions 22 to 25 are based on the recording you have just heard.｜请根据你刚刚听到的录音回答问题22到25。\n[24:24.04]22. What does the speaker say travelers commonly complain about?｜22.讲话者说旅行者常常抱怨什么？\n[24:42.46]23. What is said about Bed and Breakfast arrangements?｜23.关于提供住宿和早餐的旅馆，讲座中提到了些什么？\n[25:00.16]24. What is the first thing you have to consider if you want to start a B&B business?｜24.如果想经营一家民宿，首先需要考虑的是什么？\n[25:19.92]25. What does the speaker say potential B&B hosts must be realistic about?｜25.说话者说潜在的民宿经营者必须对什么有现实的估量？', NOW(), NOW()
