  (`question_id`, `audio_url`, `transcript`, `duration_seconds`, `audio_total_seconds`, `audio_start_seconds`, `audio_end_seconds`, `question_start_seconds`, `question_end_seconds`, `answer_start_seconds`, `answer_end_seconds`, `group_key`, `listening_type`, `lrc_content`, `created_at`, `updated_at`)
SELECT
  @a_cet6_2025_12_2_02, '/audio/exams/listening-cet6-2025-12-2.mp3', 'Conversation One\n对话一\n\nW: I must say, I love our canteen!\n女：我得说，我太喜欢我们的餐厅了！\n\nIt''s such a great meeting point!\n它真是个绝佳的聚会地点！\n\nM: Yeah, it really is, both for students and teachers.\n男：是啊，对学生和老师来说都是。\n\nShame about the food.\n可惜食物不怎么样。\n\nW: What do you mean?\n女：你什么意思？\n\nI think the food is fine.\n我觉得食物挺好的啊。\n\nM: I would say the food is just OK, but the prices are absurd.\n男：我觉得食物也就一般，但价格高得离谱，\n\nDon''t you agree?\n你不觉得吗？\n\nW: I don''t, actually.\n女：其实我不这么认为。\n\nI personally think they''re perfectly appropriate.\n我个人觉得价格完全合理。\n\nIf it''s overpriced, why does it get so frantically busy at lunchtimes?\n要是贵得离谱，为什么午餐时间总是挤得水泄不通？\n\nM: Hmm, you make a good point.\n男：嗯，你说得对。\n\nI guess a lot of it is good value, maybe even most of it.\n我想大部分菜品性价比还不错，甚至绝大多数都划算。\n\nHowever, don''t you think 6 bucks for a slice of apple crumble is beyond most students'' budgets?\n但是，你不觉得一份苹果酥要6美元超出了大多数学生的预算吗？\n\nW: Um, yes, desserts are overpriced.\n女：呃，是的，甜点确实定价过高。\n\nI''ll give you that.\n这点我同意。\n\nTo be honest, I''ve forgotten about those, as I never eat them.\n说实话，我忘记了这点，因为我从来不吃。\n\nI never really crave sweet things or any fancy delicacies.\n我对甜食或任何精美佳肴从来没有渴望。\n\nWhat I always go for is their scrambled eggs.\n我每次都点他们的炒蛋。\n\nThey have such a great variety.\n种类特别丰富。\n\nM: Yeah, those are good.\n男：是啊，那些确实不错。\n\nThey also come out really fast.\n而且出餐速度很快。\n\nActually, that''s one of the best things about the canteen—the speed.\n实际上，这就是食堂最大的优点之一——速度快。\n\nIf I fancy something more substantial than a sandwich, but I don''t have much time for lunch, the university canteen is always a good option.\n如果我想吃比三明治更实在的东西，但午餐时间又不充裕，大学餐厅总是不错的选择。\n\nThe kitchen staff work at such a brisk pace.\n厨房员工手脚麻利。\n\nThey really deserve to be complimented for it.\n他们确实应该为此得到表扬。\n\nW: Totally, and it''s such a great environment too.\n女：完全同意，而且环境也特别好。\n\nLike the entire building is beautiful.\n就是说整栋建筑都很漂亮。\n\nM: It is very nice.\n男：确实非常漂亮。\n\nW: The massive glass windows make all the difference.\n女：那些巨大的玻璃窗让一切截然不同。\n\nI think they''re so cool.\n我觉得它们特别酷。\n\nApparently, they did a massive renovation a few years ago.\n据说，他们几年前进行过一次大翻新。\n\nIt cost them a pretty penny.\n这花了一大笔钱。\n\nM: Yeah, I''m not surprised.\n男：嗯，不奇怪。\n\nIt''s a very versatile space, suitable both for eating and relaxing.\n这个空间用途很广，既适合吃饭也适合休息。\n\nW: And for working.\n女：还适合工作。\n\nM: You''re right, working too.\n男：你说得对，也适合工作。\n\nI''ve used my laptop there once or twice.\n我在那儿用过一两次笔记本电脑。\n\nAnd there''s always a group project or meeting going on at the far end.\n而且远处总是有小组项目或会议在进行。\n\nQuestions 1 to 4 are based on the conversation you have just heard.\n请根据你刚刚听到的对话回答问题1到4。\n\n1. What does the woman say about the food at the canteen?\n1.关于餐厅的食物，女士说了什么？\n\n2. How does the woman feel about the canteen''s sweet things or fancy delicacies?\n2.女士感觉餐厅的甜食或精美佳肴如何？\n\n3. What does the man say is one of the best things about the canteen?\n3.男士说餐厅最大的优点之一是什么？\n\n4. What did the canteen undergo a few years ago?\n4.食堂几年前经历了什么？', 117, 1554.89, 36.46, 153.60, 176.06, 195.38, 86.56, 91.42, 'cet6-2025-12-2-g01', 'LONG_DIALOGUE', '[00:36.46]Conversation One｜对话一\n[00:38.90]W: I must say, I love our canteen!｜女：我得说，我太喜欢我们的餐厅了！\n[00:41.30]It''s such a great meeting point!｜它真是个绝佳的聚会地点！\n[00:43.30]M: Yeah, it really is, both for students and teachers.｜男：是啊，对学生和老师来说都是。\n[00:47.06]Shame about the food.｜可惜食物不怎么样。\n[00:48.54]W: What do you mean?｜女：你什么意思？\n[00:49.46]I think the food is fine.｜我觉得食物挺好的啊。\n[00:51.42]M: I would say the food is just OK, but the prices are absurd.｜男：我觉得食物也就一般，但价格高得离谱，\n[00:55.50]Don''t you agree?｜你不觉得吗？\n[00:56.82]W: I don''t, actually.｜女：其实我不这么认为。\n[00:58.26]I personally think they''re perfectly appropriate.｜我个人觉得价格完全合理。\n[01:01.52]If it''s overpriced, why does it get so frantically busy at lunchtimes?｜要是贵得离谱，为什么午餐时间总是挤得水泄不通？\n[01:06.28]M: Hmm, you make a good point.｜男：嗯，你说得对。\n[01:08.76]I guess a lot of it is good value, maybe even most of it.｜