SELECT
  @a_cet6_2025_12_2_07, '/audio/exams/listening-cet6-2025-12-2.mp3', 'Conversation Two\n对话二\n\nW: Hi, Tony, today we''re talking about how managers can get along better with young people at work.\n女：嗨，托尼，今天我们要讨论的是管理者如何在工作场合与年轻人更好地相处。\n\nWe often hear young people today have a poor work ethic.\n我们经常听说现在的年轻人缺乏职业道德。\n\nThat''s not really justified though, is it?\n这是非常不合理的，不是吗？\n\nM: Not really.\n男：确实不合理。\n\nIn reality, young people of this age group are as varied and multifaceted as any other generation.\n实际上，这个年龄段的年轻人和任何其他任何一代一样，是多样且多面的。\n\nW: Yeah, but if you are struggling to work with young people in your workspace, what can you do?\n女：是的，但如果你在工作场所与年轻人一起工作很吃力，你能做些什么呢？\n\nM: Well, it''s essential to connect with them to learn about their values.\n男：嗯，与他们建立联系，了解他们的价值观是很重要的。\n\nIt''s also really important to recognize the way young people want to balance their work life with their personal life.\n认识到年轻人平衡工作与个人生活的方式也很重要。\n\nW: So they generally don''t want to defer happiness in return for career advancement?\n女：所以他们通常不愿意为了职业发展而推迟享受幸福？\n\nM: Absolutely.\n男：完全正确。\n\nThey are not willing to sacrifice their personal lives for their work lives and this leads people to equate that with an unwillingness to work hard.\n他们不愿意为了工作牺牲个人生活，这导致人们将此等同于不愿意努力工作。\n\nW: Right.\n女：对。\n\nBut that couldn''t be further from the truth, could it?\n但这与事实相去甚远，对吗？\n\nM: Young people will work extremely hard during their defined work hours, but they expect to have their time off, like weekends and nights free from work.\n男：年轻人会在规定的工作时间内非常努力地工作，但他们期望有休息时间，比如周末和晚上不工作。\n\nW: So how should managers go about assessing young people''s productivity?\n女：那么管理者应该如何评估年轻人的生产力呢？\n\nM: Generally, young people believe their productivity should not be measured by the number of hours they work, since someone can work for eight hours and accomplish next to nothing of significance for the company.\n男：总的来说，年轻人认为他们的生产力不应以工作时间长短来衡量，因为有些人可能工作八小时，却几乎没有为公司完成任何有意义的事情。\n\nInstead, young people measure their productivity levels by the quality of the work they perform.\n相反，年轻人通过他们完成工作的质量来衡量自己的生产力水平。\n\nW: But we often hear that young people want to feel more than just being a part of a big machine.\n女：但我们经常听说年轻人希望感受到自己不仅仅是大机器的一部分。\n\nSuch a perspective can be hard to discredit, can''t it?\n这种观点很难让人怀疑，对吧？\n\nM: It''s important to legitimize their work.\n男：认可他们的工作很关键。\n\nYoung workers want to work on projects that matter to themselves, the company or the world at large.\n年轻员工希望从事对自己、公司或整个世界有意义的项目。\n\nThey must feel the need to stay working at a company whose values align with their own.\n他们一定是觉得有必要留在一家价值观与自己的价值观一致的公司工作。\n\nW: Thanks for your advice.\n女：谢谢你的建议。\n\nQuestions 5 to 8 are based on the conversation you have just heard.\n请根据你刚刚听到的对话回答问题5到8。\n\n5. According to the woman, what view about today''s young people is not really justified?\n5.根据女士的说法，关于当今年轻人的哪种观点并不合理？\n\n6. What does the man say is important for managers to get along better with young workers?\n6.男士表示，管理者要与年轻员工更好地相处，什么很重要？\n\n7. How do young people measure their productivity levels according to the man?\n7.根据男士的说法，年轻人如何衡量自己的生产力水平？\n\n8. What companies does the man think would appeal to young workers?\n8.男士认为什么样的公司会对年轻员工有吸引力？\n\nSection B\nB节', 116, 1554.89, 231.56, 347.36, 392.50, 411.48, 314.76, 320.34, 'cet6-2025-12-2-g02', 'LONG_DIALOGUE', '[03:51.56]Conversation Two｜对话二\n[03:53.72]W: Hi, Tony, today we''re talking about how managers can get along better with young people at work.｜女：嗨，托尼，今天我们要讨论的是管理者如何在工作场合与年轻人更好地相处。\n[04:00.32]We often hear young people today have a poor work ethic.｜我们经常听说现在的年轻人缺乏职业道德。\n[04:04.12]That''s not really justified though, is it?｜这是非常不合理的，不是吗？\n[04:07.08]M: Not really.｜男：确实不合理。\n[04:08.16]In reality, young people of this age group are as varied and multifaceted as any other generation.｜实际上，这个年龄段的年轻人和任何其他任何一代一样，是多样且多面的。\n[04:14.84]W: Yeah, but if you are struggling to work with young people in your workspace, what can you do?｜女：是的，但如果你在工作场所与年轻人一起工作很吃力，你能做些什么呢？\n[04:20.36]M: Well, it''s essential to connect with them to learn about their values.｜男：嗯，与他们建立联系，了解他们的价值观是很重要的。\n[04:24.32]It''s also really important to recognize the way young people want to balance their work life with their personal life.｜认识到年轻人平衡工作与个人生活的方式也很重要。\n[04:31.40]W: So they generally don''t want to defer happiness in return for career advancement?｜女：所以他们通常不愿意为了职业发展而推迟享受幸福？\n[04:37.24]M: Absolutely.｜男：完全正确。\n[04:38.12]They are not willing to sacrifice their personal lives for their work lives and this leads people to equate that with an unwillingness to work hard.｜他们不愿意为了工作牺牲个人生活，这导致人们将此等同于不愿意努力工作。\n[04:46.00]W: Right.｜女：对。\n[04:46.89]But that couldn''t be further from the truth, could it?｜但这与事实相去甚远，对吗？\n[04:49.84]M: Young people will work extremely hard during their defined work hours, but they expect to have their time off, like weekends and nights free from work.｜男：年轻人会在规定的工作时间内非常努力地工作，但他们期望有休息时间，比如周末和晚上不工作。\n[04:59.07]W: So how should managers go about assessing young people''s productivity?｜女：那么管理者应该如何评估年轻人的生产力呢？\n[05:04.00]M: Generally, young people believe their productivity should not be measured by the number of hours they work, since someone can work for eight hours and accomplish next to nothing of significance for the company.｜男：总的来说，年轻人认为他们的生产力不应以工作时间长短来衡量，因为有些人可能工作八小时，却几乎没有为公司完成任何有意义的事情。\n[05:14.76]Instead, young people measure their productivity levels by the quality of the work they perform.｜相反，年轻人通过他们完成工作的质量来衡量自己的生产力水平。\n[05:20.64]W: But we often hear that young people want to feel more than just being a part of a big machine.｜女：但我们经常听说年轻人希望感受到自己不仅仅是大机器的一部分。\n[05:26.76]Such a perspective can be hard to discredit, can''t it?｜这种观点很难让人怀疑，对吧？\n[05:30.64]M: It''s important to legitimize their work.｜男：认可他们的工作很关键。\n[05:33.36]Young workers want to work on projects that matter to themselves, the company or the world at large.｜年轻员工希望从事对自己、公司或整个世界有意义的项目。\n[05:39.24]They must feel the need to stay working at a company whose values align with their own.｜他们一定是觉得有必要留在一家价值观与自己的价值观一致的公司工作。\n[05:44.52]W: Thanks for your advice.｜女：谢谢你的建议。\n[05:47.36]Questions 5 to 8 are based on the conversation you have just heard.｜请根据你刚刚听到的对话回答问题5到8。\n[05:52.44]5. According to the woman, what view about today''s young people is not really justified?｜5.根据女士的说法，关于当今年轻人的哪种观点并不合理？\n[06:12.88]6. What does the man say is important for managers to get along better with young workers?｜6.男士表示，管理者要与年轻员工更好地相处，什么很重要？\n[06:32.50]7. How do young people measure their productivity levels according to the man?｜7.根据男士的说法，年轻人如何衡量自己的生产力水平？\n[06:51.78]8. What companies does the man think would appeal to young workers?｜8.男士认为什么样的公司会对年轻员工有吸引力？\n[07:10.48]Section B｜B节', NOW(), NOW()
