  @a_cet6_2025_12_2_09, '/audio/exams/listening-cet6-2025-12-2.mp3', 'Passage One\n短文一\n\nMany restaurants are trying to persuade customers to eat more sustainably, moving away from environmentally unfriendly meat towards greener dishes.\n许多餐馆正试图说服顾客吃得更环保，从对环境不友好的肉类转向更绿色的菜肴。\n\nAlthough it sounds counter-intuitive, restaurants which include specific vegetarian sections on their menus may be unintentionally encouraging customers to eat meat, a new study suggests.\n虽然这听起来与预料的相反，但一项新的研究表明，在菜单上设置素食专区的餐馆可能会无意中鼓励顾客吃肉。\n\nBehavioral scientist Linda Bacon, one of the study''s authors, said, "Restaurants can have a positive impact on the environment by encouraging their customers to choose more plant-based food and less meat.\n该研究的作者之一、行为科学家琳达·培根表示："餐馆可以通过鼓励顾客选择更多植物性食品和减少肉类摄入来对环境产生积极影响。\n\nHowever, our findings suggest that while certain restaurant menu designs can encourage some consumers to make pro-environmental food choices, they can have the opposite effect on others."\n然而，我们的研究结果表明，尽管某些餐馆的菜单设计能够促使一些消费者做出有利于环境的食物选择，但它们也可能对另一些消费者产生相反的效果。"\n\nThe study involved 750 people, half of whom frequently ate vegetarian food and half of whom rarely ate it.\n这项研究涉及750名参与者，其中一半人经常吃素食，另一半人很少吃素食。\n\nNo vegetarians were included.\n参与者中不包含素食主意者。\n\nThey were given different menus and asked to choose a meal as if they were eating out with friends.\n他们拿到了不同的菜单，并被要求像和朋友一起外出吃饭一样选择一份餐食。\n\nPlacing vegetarian dishes in a separate section did not have a significant effect on the choices made by infrequent vegetarian food eaters.\n将素食菜肴单独列在一个区域，对很少吃素食的参与者的选择没有显著影响。\n\nBut it did have a notable effect on the frequent eaters, lowering their chance of picking a vegetarian option by 65%.\n但对经常吃素食的参与者有显著影响，使他们选择素食选项的概率降低了65%。\n\nThe researchers also discovered that presenting a vegetarian dish as the chef''s recommendation, or including a more appealing description of a non-meat meal, leads to a greater proportion of infrequent vegetarian eaters choosing a vegetarian option.\n研究人员还发现，将素食菜肴列为厨师推荐，或为非肉类餐食提供更具吸引力的描述，能够促使更多很少吃素食的参与者选择素食选项。\n\nBut again, these altered menu designs backfired with those who ate vegetarian food more frequently, leading them to be less likely to choose a vegetarian dish.\n但同样，这些调整后的菜单设计对经常吃素食的参与者产生了反效果，导致他们选择素食菜肴的可能性降低。\n\nQuestions 9 to 11 are based on the passage you have just heard.\n请根据你刚刚听到的短文回答问题9到11。\n\n9. What does a new study suggest about restaurants including vegetarian sections on their menus?\n关于菜单上含有素食专区的餐馆，一项新研究表明了什么？\n\n10. How was the study carried out on 750 participants?\n10.这项有750名参与者的研究是如何进行的？\n\n11. How do altered menu designs affect frequent eaters of vegetarian food?\n11.调整后的菜单设计对经常吃素食的人有何影响？', 119, 1554.89, 459.96, 578.56, 583.12, 603.08, 471.52, 484.94, 'cet6-2025-12-2-g03', 'PASSAGE', '[07:39.96]Passage One｜短文一\n[07:41.28]Many restaurants are trying to persuade customers to eat more sustainably, moving away from environmentally unfriendly meat towards greener dishes.｜许多餐馆正试图说服顾客吃得更环保，从对环境不友好的肉类转向更绿色的菜肴。\n[07:51.52]Although it sounds counter-intuitive, restaurants which include specific vegetarian sections on their menus may be unintentionally encouraging customers to eat meat, a new study suggests.｜虽然这听起来与预料的相反，但一项新的研究表明，在菜单上设置素食专区的餐馆可能会无意中鼓励顾客吃肉。\n[08:05.24]Behavioral scientist Linda Bacon, one of the study''s authors, said, "Restaurants can have a positive impact on the environment by encouraging their customers to choose more plant-based food and less meat.｜该研究的作者之一、行为科学家琳达·培根表示："餐馆可以通过鼓励顾客选择更多植物性食品和减少肉类摄入来对环境产生积极影响。\n[08:20.28]However, our findings suggest that while certain restaurant menu designs can encourage some consumers to make pro-environmental food choices, they can have the opposite effect on others."｜然而，我们的研究结果表明，尽管某些餐馆的菜单设计能够促使一些消费者做出有利于环境的食物选择，但它们也可能对另一些消费者产生相反的效果。"\n[08:33.14]The study involved 750 people, half of whom frequently ate vegetarian food and half of whom rarely ate it.｜这项研究涉及750名参与者，其中一半人经常吃素食，另一半人很少吃素食。\n[08:41.86]No vegetarians were included.｜参与者中不包含素食主意者。\n[08:45.08]They were given different menus and asked to choose a meal as if they were eating out with friends.｜他们拿到了不同的菜单，并被要求像和朋友一起外出吃饭一样选择一份餐食。\n[08:50.88]Placing vegetarian dishes in a separate section did not have a significant effect on the choices made by infrequent vegetarian food eaters.｜将素食菜肴单独列在一个区域，对很少吃素食的参与者的选择没有显著影响。\n[09:00.12]But it did have a notable effect on the frequent eaters, lowering their chance of picking a vegetarian option by 65%.｜但对经常吃素食的参与者有显著影响，使他们选择素食选项的概率降低了65%。\n[09:09.44]The researchers also discovered that presenting a vegetarian dish as the chef''s recommendation, or including a more appealing description of a non-meat meal, leads to a greater proportion of infrequent vegetarian eaters choosing a vegetarian option.｜研究人员还发现，将素食菜肴列为厨师推荐，或为非肉类餐食提供更具吸引力的描述，能够促使更多很少吃素食的参与者选择素食选项。\n[09:26.68]But again, these altered menu designs backfired with those who ate vegetarian food more frequently, leading them to be less likely to choose a vegetarian dish.｜但同样，这些调整后的菜单设计对经常吃素食的参与者产生了反效果，导致他们选择素食菜肴的可能性降低。\n[09:38.56]Questions 9 to 11 are based on the passage you have just heard.｜请根据你刚刚听到的短文回答问题9到11。\n[09:43.12]9. What does a new study suggest about restaurants including vegetarian sections on their menus?｜关于菜单上含有素食专区的餐馆，一项新研究表明了什么？\n[10:03.38]10. How was the study carried out on 750 participants?｜10.这项有750名参与者的研究是如何进行的？\n[10:22.08]11. How do altered menu designs affect frequent eaters of vegetarian food?｜11.调整后的菜单设计对经常吃素食的人有何影响？', NOW(), NOW()
