  (`question_id`, `audio_url`, `transcript`, `duration_seconds`, `audio_total_seconds`, `audio_start_seconds`, `audio_end_seconds`, `question_start_seconds`, `question_end_seconds`, `answer_start_seconds`, `answer_end_seconds`, `group_key`, `listening_type`, `lrc_content`, `created_at`, `updated_at`)
SELECT
  @a_cet6_2025_12_2_12, '/audio/exams/listening-cet6-2025-12-2.mp3', 'Passage Two\n短文二\n\nNottingham Trent University and the Chinese Academy of Sciences have been trying to find a way to prevent deadly outdoor air pollution from penetrating indoors.\n诺丁汉特伦特大学与中国科学院一直在努力寻找一种方法来防止致命的室外空气污染渗入室内。\n\nThey found that if pollution is frozen to around -18 ℃ in a condensing tube, the particles gather together and fall to the bottom, allowing fresh, clean air to pass through.\n他们发现，如果将污染空气在冷凝管中冷冻至约-18℃，其中的颗粒物会聚集并沉降到底部，从而使新鲜、清洁的空气得以通过。\n\nTheir method was able to remove 99% of pollutants.\n他们的方法能够去除99%的污染物。\n\nIt is hoped that the work could pave the way for simple modification of air conditioning units so that they can also clean polluted indoor air.\n（研究人员）希望这项研究能够为简易改装空调设备铺平道路，使其也能净化受污染的室内空气。\n\nOutdoor air pollution in cities is a global problem, whether it be haze plaguing Calcutta or poor air impacting the health of children in London schools.\n城市室外空气污染是一个全球性问题，无论是困扰加尔各答的雾霾，还是影响伦敦学校儿童健康的恶劣空气。\n\nWhile there are some existing technologies to purify indoor air, they can be inefficient, expensive or produce harmful by-products.\n虽然目前已有一些净化室内空气的技术，但它们往往效率低下、成本高昂或会产生有害副产品。\n\nWhen outdoor air quality is poor, people tend to spend even more time indoors.\n当室外空气质量较差时，人们往往在室内待的时间更长。\n\nBut outdoor pollution also leads to indoor pollution, and people still suffer.\n但室外污染同样会导致室内污染，人们依然会受到危害。\n\nIt is estimated that pollution is linked to over 40,000 early deaths in Britain each year.\n据估计，在英国，每年有超过4万例过早死亡与污染有关。\n\nProfessor Gang Pan of the Chinese Academy of Sciences said, "We have shown in our experiments that simply by circulating polluted air through a small freezing chamber, we can remove most of the fine particles and gas pollutants.\n中国科学院教授潘刚（音译）表示："我们的实验表明，只需让被污染的空气循环通过一个小型冷冻室，就能去除大部分细颗粒物和气体污染物。\n\nOur study makes it possible to add an air cleaner option to household appliances in areas which might experience extremely poor air conditions.\n我们的研究使易发生空气重度污染地区的家用电器上添加空气净化器功能成为可能。\n\nBy controlling indoor air pollution and improving air quality in this way, this work could be greatly beneficial to public health."\n通过这种方式控制室内空气污染并改善空气质量，这项工作对公众健康将大有裨益。"\n\nQuestions 12 to 15 are based on the passage you have just heard.\n请根据你刚刚听到的短文回答问题12到15。\n\n12. What does the passage say about Nottingham Trent University and the Chinese Academy of Sciences?\n12.关于诺丁汉特伦特大学和中国科学院，短文说了什么？\n\n13. What do we learn from the passage about existing technologies to purify indoor air?\n13.关于现有的室内空气净化技术，我们从短文中了解到什么？\n\n14. What do people tend to do when outdoor air quality is poor?\n14.当室外空气质量不好时，人们倾向于做什么？\n\n15. What did Professor Gang Pan of the Chinese Academy of Sciences say about their study?\n15.关于他们的研究，中国科学院的潘刚教授说了什么？', 107, 1554.89, 641.46, 748.92, 753.88, 774.94, 643.42, 653.92, 'cet6-2025-12-2-g04', 'PASSAGE', '[10:41.46]Passage Two｜短文二\n[10:43.42]Nottingham Trent University and the Chinese Academy of Sciences have been trying to find a way to prevent deadly outdoor air pollution from penetrating indoors.｜诺丁汉特伦特大学与中国科学院一直在努力寻找一种方法来防止致命的室外空气污染渗入室内。\n[10:54.22]They found that if pollution is frozen to around -18 ℃ in a condensing tube, the particles gather together and fall to the bottom, allowing fresh, clean air to pass through.｜他们发现，如果将污染空气在冷凝管中冷冻至约-18℃，其中的颗粒物会聚集并沉降到底部，从而使新鲜、清洁的空气得以通过。\n[11:06.40]Their method was able to remove 99% of pollutants.｜他们的方法能够去除99%的污染物。\n[11:10.16]It is hoped that the work could pave the way for simple modification of air conditioning units so that they can also clean polluted indoor air.｜（研究人员）希望这项研究能够为简易改装空调设备铺平道路，使其也能净化受污染的室内空气。\n[11:19.92]Outdoor air pollution in cities is a global problem, whether it be haze plaguing Calcutta or poor air impacting the health of children in London schools.｜城市室外空气污染是一个全球性问题，无论是困扰加尔各答的雾霾，还是影响伦敦学校儿童健康的恶劣空气。\n[11:30.60]While there are some existing technologies to purify indoor air, they can be inefficient, expensive or produce harmful by-products.｜虽然目前已有一些净化室内空气的技术，但它们往往效率低下、成本高昂或会产生有害副产品。\n[11:39.64]When outdoor air quality is poor, people tend to spend even more time indoors.｜当室外空气质量较差时，人们往往在室内待的时间更长。\n[11:44.80]But outdoor pollution also leads to indoor pollution, and people still suffer.｜但室外污染同样会导致室内污染，人们依然会受到危害。\n[11:50.72]It is estimated that pollution is linked to over 40,000 early deaths in Britain each year.｜据估计，在英国，每年有超过4万例过早死亡与污染有关。\n[11:56.88]Professor Gang Pan of the Chinese Academy of Sciences said, "We have shown in our experiments that simply by circulating polluted air through a small freezing chamber, we can remove most of the fine particles and gas pollutants.｜中国科学院教授潘刚（音译）表示："我们的实验表明，只需让被污染的空气循环通过一个小型冷冻室，就能去除大部分细颗粒物和气体污染物。\n[12:10.76]Our study makes it possible to add an air cleaner option to household appliances in areas which might experience extremely poor air conditions.｜我们的研究使易发生空气重度污染地区的家用电器上添加空气净化器功能成为可能。\n[12:20.20]By controlling indoor air pollution and improving air quality in this way, this work could be greatly beneficial to public health."｜通过这种方式控制室内空气污染并改善空气质量，这项工作对公众健康将大有裨益。"\n[12:28.92]Questions 12 to 15 are based on the passage you have just heard.｜请根据你刚刚听到的短文回答问题12到15。\n[12:33.88]12. What does the passage say about Nottingham Trent University and the Chinese Academy of Sciences?｜12.关于诺丁汉特伦特大学和中国科学院，短文说了什么？\n[12:55.24]13. What do we learn from the passage about existing technologies to purify indoor air?｜13.关于现有的室内空气净化技术，我们从短文中了解到什么？\n[13:15.50]14. What do people tend to do when outdoor air quality is poor?｜14.当室外空气质量不好时，人们倾向于做什么？\n[13:34.32]15. What did Professor Gang Pan of the Chinese Academy of Sciences say about their study?｜15.关于他们的研究，中国科学院的潘刚教授说了什么？', NOW(), NOW()
