SELECT
  @a_cet6_2025_12_2_17, '/audio/exams/listening-cet6-2025-12-2.mp3', 'Recording One\n讲座一\n\nResearch recently carried out by my team suggests that fish may be self-aware.\n我的团队最近进行的研究表明，鱼类可能具有自我意识。\n\nA certain species of fish recently passed the well-known mirror test.\n有一种鱼近期通过了著名的镜子测试。\n\nThis is a test that demonstrates self-recognition in animals.\n这是一项证明动物具有自我认知能力的测试。\n\nOnly a few animals, such as humans, apes, dolphins and some birds, can recognize themselves in a mirror.\n只有少数动物，例如人类、猿类、海豚和一些鸟类，能在镜子中认出自己。\n\nAnd only these animals, capable of self-recognition, will attempt to remove marks placed on their skin after noticing them in the reflection.\n也仅有这些具有自我认知能力的动物，在镜中映像中注意到自己身上的记号后，会试图将其去除。\n\nThis ability suggests a level of higher intelligence and awareness.\n这种能力标志着较高水平的智力与意识。\n\nThis is not shown by children until around 18 months.\n人类幼儿直到约18个月大时才会表现出这种能力。\n\nUntil now, no fish has demonstrated the ability.\n迄今为止，尚无鱼类展现出这种能力。\n\nBut our experiments show the fish in question will scrape up against hard surfaces to remove marks placed on its body by our researchers after viewing itself in a mirror.\n但我们的实验表明，实验鱼类在镜中看到自己后，会通过在硬物表面摩擦来去除研究人员在其身体上做的记号。\n\nThe behaviors we observe leave little doubt that this fish behaviorally fulfills all criteria of the mirror test as originally laid out.\n我们观察到的行为基本可以确定，这种鱼类在行为上完全符合镜子测试最初设立的所有标准。\n\nThe fish in our study never attempted to remove the marks when no mirror was present or when the marks were just placed on the mirror.\n当没有镜子或记号只是被留在镜子上时，我们的试验用鱼从未尝试去除标记。\n\nUnmarked fish also did not attempt to remove marks from themselves when interacting with a marked fish on the other side of a window.\n当未被标记的鱼与窗户另一侧带有标记的鱼互动时，也不会尝试去除自身标记。\n\nThese results show either that fish are self-aware or that the mirror test, which is considered to be the gold standard test used to denote higher intelligence, may be flawed.\n这些结果表明：要么鱼类具有自我意识，要么被视为表示高等智力黄金标准的镜子测试本身可能存在缺陷。\n\nWhat is less clear is whether these behaviors should be considered as evidence that fish are self-aware, even though in the past these same behaviors have been interpreted as self-awareness in so many other animals.\n目前尚不明确的是，是否应将这些行为视作鱼类具有自我意识的证据，尽管过去在许多其他动物身上，同样的行为已被解读为自我意识的表现。\n\nDepending on your position, you might reject the interpretation that these behaviors in a fish satisfy passing the test at all.\n根据你的立场，你可能会否定鱼类的这些行为完全符合测试通过标准这一解读。\n\nBut on what objective basis can you do this when the behaviors they show are so functionally similar to those of other species that have passed the test?\n但当它们表现出的行为在功能上与通过测试的其他物种如此相似时，你的否定又是基于什么客观依据呢？\n\nResults from our research raise more questions than answers.\n我们的研究结果提出的疑问多于得出的答案。\n\nWhat if self-awareness develops like an onion, building layer upon layer rather than appearing all at once?\n如果自我意识的发展如同洋葱生长般层层累积，而非突然显现呢？\n\nPerhaps in order to explore self-awareness further, we should stop looking at responses to the mirror as a decisive test.\n或许要进一步探索自我意识，我们应当停止将镜子反应视为决定性测试。\n\nOnly with a richer theory of the self and a larger test battery will we be able to determine all of the various levels of self-awareness, including where exactly fish fit in.\n唯有建立更丰富的自我意识理论体系并采用更全面的测试组合，我们才能确定自我意识的所有不同层次，包括鱼类在其中所处的确切位置。\n\nQuestions 16 to 18 are based on the recording you have just heard.\n请根据你刚刚听到的录音回答问题16到18。\n\n16. What do we learn about the well-known mirror test?\n16.关于著名的镜子测试，我们了解到什么？\n\n17. What does the study by the speaker''s team show about the fish they experimented with?\n17.关于实验用鱼，讲话者团队的研究表明了什么？\n\n18. What does the speaker say about the results of their research?\n18.关于研究结果，讲话者说了什么？', 168, 1554.89, 859.88, 1028.28, 1050.76, 1070.20, 886.24, 895.94, 'cet6-2025-12-2-g05', 'LECTURE', '[14:19.88]Recording One｜讲座一\n[14:21.88]Research recently carried out by my team suggests that fish may be self-aware.｜我的团队最近进行的研究表明，鱼类可能具有自我意识。\n[14:28.24]A certain species of fish recently passed the well-known mirror test.｜有一种鱼近期通过了著名的镜子测试。\n[14:33.00]This is a test that demonstrates self-recognition in animals.｜这是一项证明动物具有自我认知能力的测试。\n[14:38.36]Only a few animals, such as humans, apes, dolphins and some birds, can recognize themselves in a mirror.｜只有少数动物，例如人类、猿类、海豚和一些鸟类，能在镜子中认出自己。\n[14:46.24]And only these animals, capable of self-recognition, will attempt to remove marks placed on their skin after noticing them in the reflection.｜也仅有这些具有自我认知能力的动物，在镜中映像中注意到自己身上的记号后，会试图将其去除。\n[14:56.24]This ability suggests a level of higher intelligence and awareness.｜这种能力标志着较高水平的智力与意识。\n[15:00.94]This is not shown by children until around 18 months.｜人类幼儿直到约18个月大时才会表现出这种能力。\n[15:05.72]Until now, no fish has demonstrated the ability.｜迄今为止，尚无鱼类展现出这种能力。\n[15:09.56]But our experiments show the fish in question will scrape up against hard surfaces to remove marks placed on its body by our researchers after viewing itself in a mirror.｜但我们的实验表明，实验鱼类在镜中看到自己后，会通过在硬物表面摩擦来去除研究人员在其身体上做的记号。\n[15:22.34]The behaviors we observe leave little doubt that this fish behaviorally fulfills all criteria of the mirror test as originally laid out.｜我们观察到的行为基本可以确定，这种鱼类在行为上完全符合镜子测试最初设立的所有标准。\n[15:33.02]The fish in our study never attempted to remove the marks when no mirror was present or when the marks were just placed on the mirror.｜当没有镜子或记号只是被留在镜子上时，我们的试验用鱼从未尝试去除标记。\n[15:41.66]Unmarked fish also did not attempt to remove marks from themselves when interacting with a marked fish on the other side of a window.｜当未被标记的鱼与窗户另一侧带有标记的鱼互动时，也不会尝试去除自身标记。\n[15:50.34]These results show either that fish are self-aware or that the mirror test, which is considered to be the gold standard test used to denote higher intelligence, may be flawed.｜这些结果表明：要么鱼类具有自我意识，要么被视为表示高等智力黄金标准的镜子测试本身可能存在缺陷。\n[16:02.96]What is less clear is whether these behaviors should be considered as evidence that fish are self-aware, even though in the past these same behaviors have been interpreted as self-awareness in so many other animals.｜目前尚不明确的是，是否应将这些行为视作鱼类具有自我意识的证据，尽管过去在许多其他动物身上，同样的行为已被解读为自我意识的表现。\n[16:16.40]Depending on your position, you might reject the interpretation that these behaviors in a fish satisfy passing the test at all.｜根据你的立场，你可能会否定鱼类的这些行为完全符合测试通过标准这一解读。\n[16:24.80]But on what objective basis can you do this when the behaviors they show are so functionally similar to those of other species that have passed the test?｜但当它们表现出的行为在功能上与通过测试的其他物种如此相似时，你的否定又是基于什么客观依据呢？\n[16:34.36]Results from our research raise more questions than answers.｜我们的研究结果提出的疑问多于得出的答案。\n[16:38.64]What if self-awareness develops like an onion, building layer upon layer rather than appearing all at once?｜如果自我意识的发展如同洋葱生长般层层累积，而非突然显现呢？\n[16:46.36]Perhaps in order to explore self-awareness further, we should stop looking at responses to the mirror as a decisive test.｜或许要进一步探索自我意识，我们应当停止将镜子反应视为决定性测试。\n[16:54.32]Only with a richer theory of the self and a larger test battery will we be able to determine all of the various levels of self-awareness, including where exactly fish fit in.｜唯有建立更丰富的自我意识理论体系并采用更全面的测试组合，我们才能确定自我意识的所有不同层次，包括鱼类在其中所处的确切位置。\n[17:08.28]Questions 16 to 18 are based on the recording you have just heard.｜请根据你刚刚听到的录音回答问题16到18。\n[17:13.28]16. What do we learn about the well-known mirror test?｜16.关于著名的镜子测试，我们了解到什么？\n[17:30.76]17. What does the study by the speaker''s team show about the fish they experimented with?｜17.关于实验用鱼，讲话者团队的研究表明了什么？\n[17:50.50]18. What does the speaker say about the results of their research?｜18.关于研究结果，讲话者说了什么？', NOW(), NOW()
