  (`question_id`, `audio_url`, `transcript`, `duration_seconds`, `audio_total_seconds`, `audio_start_seconds`, `audio_end_seconds`, `question_start_seconds`, `question_end_seconds`, `answer_start_seconds`, `answer_end_seconds`, `group_key`, `listening_type`, `lrc_content`, `created_at`, `updated_at`)
SELECT
  @a_cet6_2025_12_2_25, '/audio/exams/listening-cet6-2025-12-2.mp3', 'Recording Three\n讲座三\n\nLet me be honest with you.\n让我坦诚地告诉你们：\n\nIf you''re living your life full of regrets, you''re wasting your time.\n果你活在后悔里，那是在浪费生命。\n\nWhy would you go through life regretting the very decisions that made you who you are today?\n为何用一生去后悔那些塑造了今日之你的决定？\n\nThere are plenty of unfavorable decisions we''ve made, but does that mean we should regret them?\n我们确实做过许多错误的决定，但这意味着我们应当为此后悔吗？\n\nNo!\n不！\n\nI''ve had many moments where I sit and think about all the things I wish I could have done differently.\n我常会坐下来回想那些本可以做得不同的事。\n\nHowever, just because things could be different, it doesn''t necessarily mean they would be better.\n然而，仅仅因为事情可能会有所不同，并不一定意味着它们会更好。\n\nYou don''t have to continually be thinking of all your past decisions and whether or not you made the right one.\n你不需要去不断地思考你过去所做的所有的决定，也不需要思考你的决定是否正确。\n\nYou can''t go back and change anything, so what''s the point in worrying about it?\n你无法回到过去改变任何事情，所以忧虑又有何意义？\n\nEvery single decision you''ve ever made, positive or negative, has made you the person you are today.\n你做过的每个决定，无论是积极的还是消极的，都成就了今天的你。\n\nWe want to go back and change parts of our past, but what would be the benefit of that?\n我们想回到过去，改变一部分过去，但这么做的好处是什么？\n\nWe would have lost the valuable knowledge from the lessons we learned.\n我们会失去从教训中获得的宝贵智慧。\n\nThere are reasons you make the choices you do, and that tells us about who you are.\n你所做的选择都是有原因的，这告诉我们你是谁。\n\nSo when it comes to any decision in life, be unapologetically yourself.\n所以在生活中做任何决定时，请毫无歉意地做你自己。\n\nBecause at the end of the day, it was you who made that decision.\n因为最终做出那个决定的人正是你。\n\nWith less time spent focused on regrets, you''ll finally have time to focus on the more essential things in life.\n花在后悔上的时间少了，你就有时间专注于生活中更重要的事情。\n\nIn any situation, you grow more as a person with every decision you make.\n每种境遇下，每个决定都在促使你成长。\n\nLife is full of lessons to learn, so we can''t let regret stop us from moving forward.\n人生充满需要学习的教训，我们绝不能让悔意阻挡我们前行。\n\nWe don''t know if we''ve made the right or wrong choice until after it''s already been made, so it can be easy to start regretting your decision.\n我们在做出决定之前不知道自己的选择是对还是错，所以很容易开始后悔自己的决定。\n\nBut if the decision has already been made, what''s the purpose of dwelling on it?\n但若已做出决定，那纠结于它又有何用？\n\nThere isn''t one.\n毫无意义。\n\nAll you can do is move forward.\n你唯一能做的是继续前进。\n\nYou can''t let yourself sit there and worry about every past choice.\n你不能让自己坐在那里担心过往的每一个选择。\n\nWe aren''t all perfect.\n我们并不都是完美的。\n\nWhenever you make a decision, there will always be a possibility for regret later, but that''s how life is supposed to be.\n无论什么时候你做了决定，之后总会有后悔的可能，但生活就是这样。\n\nYou will make poor decisions in life—we all do—but it''s what you do with the lessons learned that matters.\n你会在生活中做出糟糕的决定——人人都会——但重要的是你如何运用所学到的教训。\n\nThink about every decision you''ve ever made.\n回想你所做出的每个决定。\n\nWere they always the best?\n它们都是最棒的吗？\n\nOf course not.\n当然不是。\n\nBut look at how far you''ve come since then.\n但请看看做出决定后你已走了多远。\n\nQuestions 22 to 25 are based on the recording you have just heard.\n请根据你刚刚听到的录音回答问题22到25。\n\n22. What should we do with the unfavorable decisions we''ve made?\n22.对于自己做出的错误决定，我们该怎么办？\n\n23. What does the speaker say about every single decision we''ve ever made?\n23.关于我们曾经做出的每个决定，讲话者说了什么？\n\n24. What is life full of  according to the speaker?\n24.根据讲话者的观点，人生充满了什么？\n\n25. What is said to be of real importance when we make poor decisions in life?\n25.讲座中说，当我们在生活中做出糟糕的决定时，真正重要的是什么？', 146, 1554.89, 1324.78, 1471.12, 1532.34, 1544.34, NULL, NULL, 'cet6-2025-12-2-g07', 'LECTURE', '[22:04.78]Recording Three｜讲座三\n[22:07.34]Let me be honest with you.｜让我坦诚地告诉你们：\n[22:09.34]If you''re living your life full of regrets, you''re wasting your time.｜果你活在后悔里，那是在浪费生命。\n[22:13.86]Why would you go through life regretting the very decisions that made you who you are today?｜为何用一生去后悔那些塑造了今日之你的决定？\n[22:19.34]There are plenty of unfavorable decisions we''ve made, but does that mean we should regret them?｜我们确实做过许多错误的决定，但这意味着我们应当为此后悔吗？\n[22:24.94]No!｜不！\n[22:26.30]I''ve had many moments where I sit and think about all the things I wish I could have done differently.｜我常会坐下来回想那些本可以做得不同的事。\n[22:32.14]However, just because things could be different, it doesn''t necessarily mean they would be better.｜然而，仅仅因为事情可能会有所不同，并不一定意味着它们会更好。\n[22:38.38]You don''t have to continually be thinking of all your past decisions and whether or not you made the right one.｜你不需要去不断地思考你过去所做的所有的决定，也不需要思考你的决定是否正确。\n[22:44.94]You can''t go back and change anything, so what''s the point in worrying about it?｜你无法回到过去改变任何事情，所以忧虑又有何意义？\n[22:50.30]Every single decision you''ve ever made, positive or negative, has made you the person you are today.｜你做过的每个决定，无论是积极的还是消极的，都成就了今天的你。\n[22:56.98]We want to go back and change parts of our past, but what would be the benefit of that?｜我们想回到过去，改变一部分过去，但这么做的好处是什么？\n[23:02.32]We would have lost the valuable knowledge from the lessons we learned.｜我们会失去从教训中获得的宝贵智慧。\n[23:07.08]There are reasons you make the choices you do, and that tells us about who you are.｜你所做的选择都是有原因的，这告诉我们你是谁。\n[23:12.52]So when it comes to any decision in life, be unapologetically yourself.｜所以在生活中做任何决定时，请毫无歉意地做你自己。\n[23:17.52]Because at the end of the day, it was you who made that decision.｜因为最终做出那个决定的人正是你。\n[23:21.96]With less time spent focused on regrets, you''ll finally have time to focus on the more essential things in life.｜花在后悔上的时间少了，你就有时间专注于生活中更重要的事情。\n[23:29.52]In any situation, you grow more as a person with every decision you make.｜每种境遇下，每个决定都在促使你成长。\n[23:34.96]Life is full of lessons to learn, so we can''t let regret stop us from moving forward.｜人生充满需要学习的教训，我们绝不能让悔意阻挡我们前行。\n[23:41.20]We don''t know if we''ve made the right or wrong choice until after it''s already been made, so it can be easy to start regretting your decision.｜我们在做出决定之前不知道自己的选择是对还是错，所以很容易开始后悔自己的决定。\n[23:50.40]But if the decision has already been made, what''s the purpose of dwelling on it?｜但若已做出决定，那纠结于它又有何用？\n[23:55.40]There isn''t one.｜毫无意义。\n[23:57.02]All you can do is move forward.｜你唯一能做的是继续前进。\n[23:59.48]You can''t let yourself sit there and worry about every past choice.｜你不能让自己坐在那里担心过往的每一个选择。\n[24:03.36]We aren''t all perfect.｜我们并不都是完美的。\n[24:06.16]Whenever you make a decision, there will always be a possibility for regret later, but that''s how life is supposed to be.｜无论什么时候你做了决定，之后总会有后悔的可能，但生活就是这样。\n[24:13.60]You will make poor decisions in life—we all do—but it''s what you do with the lessons learned that matters.｜你会在生活中做出糟糕的决定——人人都会——但重要的是你如何运用所学到的教训。\n[24:21.52]Think about every decision you''ve ever made.｜回想你所做出的每个决定。\n[24:24.04]Were they always the best?｜它们都是最棒的吗？\n[24:25.60]Of course not.｜当然不是。\n[24:26.84]But look at how far you''ve come since then.｜但请看看做出决定后你已走了多远。\n[24:31.12]Questions 22 to 25 are based on the recording you have just heard.｜请根据你刚刚听到的录音回答问题22到25。\n[24:36.92]22. What should we do with the unfavorable decisions we''ve made?｜22.对于自己做出的错误决定，我们该怎么办？\n[24:55.52]23. What does the speaker say about every single decision we''ve ever made?｜23.关于我们曾经做出的每个决定，讲话者说了什么？\n[25:14.64]24. What is life full of  according to the speaker?｜24.根据讲话者的观点，人生充满了什么？\n[25:32.34]25. What is said to be of real importance when we make poor decisions in life?｜25.讲座中说，当我们在生活中做出糟糕的决定时，真正重要的是什么？', NOW(), NOW()
