fit from your assistance or advice, help them out to gain their respect and trust.\n如果你的帮助或建议能帮到他人，不妨搭把手，以此收获对方的尊重与信任。\n\nM: But it goes without saying that you shouldn''t act like a know-it-all, otherwise you''ll appear arrogant.\n男：但不用说，你不能表现得像一个万事通，否则会让你看起来很是傲慢。\n\nW: Absolutely. Be humble, and you''ll get a lot of time later on to show your genius.\n女：完全同意。保持谦逊，日后一定会有机会展现你的能力。\n\nQuestions 1 to 4 are based on the conversation you have just heard.\n请根据你刚刚听到的对话回答问题1到4。\n\n1. What are the speakers mainly talking about?\n1. 对话中两人主要在谈论什么？\n\n2. What does the woman say is one mistake people make?\n2. 女士说人们常犯的一个错误是什么？\n\n3. What does the woman advise people to do in their work?\n3. 女士建议人们在工作中应该怎么做？\n\n4. Why does the man say one should not act like a know-it-all?\n4. 男士为什么说一个人不应该表现得像个万事通？', 106, 1535.54, 36.69, 142.43, 199.25, 216.81, 130.72, 136.48, 'cet6-2026-06-1-g01', 'LONG_DIALOGUE', '[00:36.69]Conversation One｜对话一\n[00:38.69]M: Welcome to Business Matters.｜男：欢迎来到《商业话题》。\n[00:40.84]Today we have invited career development consultant Lucy Williams to talk about how to get ahead at work. Hi, Lucy.｜今天我们邀请了职业发展顾问露西·威廉斯，请她和大家谈一谈如何在事业上脱颖而出。你好，露西。\n[00:48.50]Many of us never seem to get promoted.｜很多人似乎始终得不到提拔。\n[00:50.99]Why is that? And what can we do about it?｜这是什么原因？我们又该如何应对？\n[00:54.33]W: One mistake people make is to limit communication only to their bosses.｜女：人们常犯的错误是只和上司沟通。\n[00:58.88]It''s important to expand your network and include your co-workers.｜拓展人脉、多和同事往来也十分重要。\n[01:03.04]M: But some of our co-workers are less senior to us.｜男：可有些同事的职级还没有我们的高。\n[01:06.32]Is it really necessary to connect with them?｜真的有必要和他们打交道吗？\n[01:09.16]W: It''s important not to underestimate your colleagues.｜女：千万别小看身边的同事。\n[01:12.21]Sometimes a job title might not clearly demonstrate the influence they may have.｜有时职位头衔未必能清晰地体现出一个人的影响力。\n[01:17.52]M: Now, many of us think that working hard creates a good impression, but this isn''t always true, is it?｜男：现在，不少人觉得埋头苦干就能留下好印象，但事实并不总是如此，对吧？\n[01:23.50]W: That''s right.｜女：没错。\n[01:24.52]We should avoid trying to take on too much work and constantly staying late, just to show that you are committed.｜我们不要为了表现自己尽职尽责，就包揽过多的工作，还经常加班。\n[01:31.38]M: I see. So setting expectations too high at the beginning can make us look bad if we don''t maintain them.｜男：我明白了。一开始把预期定得太高，后续如果无法坚持，反而会让自己难堪。\n[01:38.17]W: Yeah. It''s better to make sure you are putting in quality time instead of just a large quantity of time.｜女：是的。确保高质量的时间投入要比单纯拼工作时长更可取。\n[01:44.71]And these efforts can easily be demonstrated by the results we achieve.｜付出的努力最终都会体现在工作成果上。\n[01:49.22]M: What about helping others at work?｜男：在工作中向别人提供帮助呢？\n[01:51.61]Should you try and go beyond your normal responsibilities and offer to help people with their projects?｜要不要主动分担本职之外的工作，帮同事处理项目？\n[01:57.21]W: Extend your assistance to those who need it, but only as long as your own work will not go unattended.｜女：可以向有需要的人伸出援手，但前提是自己的工作不能耽误。\n[02:04.36]If someone can benefit from your assistance or advice, help them out to gain their respect and trust.｜如果你的帮助或建议能帮到他人，不妨搭把手，以此收获对方的尊重与信任。\n[02:10.72]M: But it goes without saying that you shouldn''t act like a know-it-all, otherwise you''ll appear arrogant.｜男：但不用说，你不能表现得像一个万事通，否则会让你看起来很是傲慢。\n[02:16.78]W: Absolutely. Be humble, and you''ll get a lot of time later on to show your genius.｜女：完全同意。保持谦逊，日后一定会有机会展现你的能力。\n[02:22.43]Questions 1 to 4 are based on the conversation you have just heard.｜请根据你刚刚听到的对话回答问题1到4。\n[02:26.79]1. What are the speakers mainly talking about?｜1. 对话中两人主要在谈论什么？\n[02:43.80]2. What does the woman say is one mistake people make?｜2. 女士说人们常犯的一个错误是什么？\n[03:01.09]3. What does the woman advise people to do in their work?｜3. 女士建议人们在工作中应该怎么做？\n[03:19.25]4. Why does the man say one should not act like a know-it-all?｜4. 男士为什么说一个人不应该表现得像个万事通？', NOW(), NOW()
