  @a_cet6_2026_06_1_07, '/audio/exams/listening-cet6-2026-06-1.mp3', 'Conversation Two\n对话二\n\nW: I think we first need to decide how to divide up the presentation responsibilities.\n女：我认为我们首先需要确定如何分配汇报任务。\n\nFrom what I recall, the presentation consists of five parts, not including introduction and conclusion.\n我记得除去开场白和总结这两块，汇报有五个部分。\n\nThat would mean altogether we need to allocate seven parts between the two of us.\n那就是说我们两个人总共需要分摊七个部分的内容。\n\nM: So, we have the abstract, background research, the project design, the results and the discussion portions.\n男：是啊，有摘要、背景研究、项目设计、研究结果与讨论这几个部分。\n\nAs the abstract section only applies to the article, we needn''t include it in the presentation.\n不过，摘要是依附文章存在的，我们的汇报里可以省略这部分。\n\nHow would you suggest we dole out the rest?\n你建议怎么分剩下的这几部分？\n\nW: How do you feel about handling the background a bit?\n女：你负责背景研究部分怎么样？\n\nIn this way, we can both discuss the part of the project that we devoted most of our time to.\n这样我们俩都可以讲我们投入了大部分时间的项目部分。\n\nM: Hold on a minute.\n男：等等。\n\nYou want me, the one who did the bulk of the task to also do the majority of the presentation?\n你想让我这个完成了大部分工作的人也承担汇报的大部分工作？\n\nThe background research, which was so meticulous, took more than a month.\n背景研究很是烦琐，花了一个多月才做完。\n\nW: Okay, okay. I get it.\n女：好，好，我知道了。\n\nQuit your moaning.\n别抱怨了。\n\nI appreciate the rigorous work ethic you applied to the research, but not the sarcasm that comes up every time I mention it.\n我很欣赏你做研究时认真严谨的态度，可真不喜欢我每次提起这事儿你就冷嘲热讽。\n\nWhat do you think would be a fair arrangement?\n那你觉得怎样安排才算公平呢？\n\nM: I think the best arrangement would be to split the research into two parts, before 1980 and afterward.\n男：我认为最好的安排是把研究按时间分成1980年之前和1980年之后两部分。\n\nI will take the before portion, and you would be assigned the after 1980, leaving the project and results.\n1980年前的部分由我来讲，之后的部分交给你，（这样就）剩下项目介绍和研究结果两部分。\n\nI volunteer to describe the project, but as I struggled a bit with the statistics in the results section, how about you handling that?\n我愿意承担项目介绍部分，但由于我觉得研究结果那部分中的统计数据有点费劲，那部分由你来负责怎么样？\n\nW: That''s agreeable to me.\n女：我同意。\n\nI propose we both handle the discussion section in parts, along with the question and answer afterward, leaving only the introduction and conclusion.\n我提议咱们都处理部分讨论环节，还有后面的问答环节，这样就只剩下开场白和总结了。\n\nM: I will take responsibility for the conclusion and put you in charge of the introduction.\n男：我负责总结部分，开场白交给你。\n\nThis will make it so that we alternate presenting, so as to avoid sounding monotonous to the audience.\n这样，我们交替汇报，也能避免让听众觉得单调。\n\nQuestions 5 to 8 are based on the conversation you have just heard.\n请根据你刚刚听到的对话回答问题5到8。\n\n5. What does the woman say they first need to do?\n5. 女士说他们首先需要做什么？\n\n6. Why does the man refuse to handle the background part?\n6. 男士为什么拒绝负责背景部分？\n\n7. What does the woman urge the man to stop doing?\n7. 女士强烈要求男士不要再做什么？\n\n8. Why does the man suggest he present the conclusion and the woman do the introduction?\n8. 男士为什么提议由他来承担结论部分，让女士负责开场白？\n\nSection B Directions: In this section, you will hear two passages.\nB节 说明：在本节中，你将会听到两篇短文。', 113, 1535.54, 217.11, 330.32, 369.90, 388.45, NULL, NULL, 'cet6-2026-06-1-g02', 'LONG_DIALOGUE', '[03:37.11]Conversation Two｜对话二\n[03:39.59]W: I think we first need to decide how to divide up the presentation responsibilities.｜女：我认为我们首先需要确定如何分配汇报任务。\n[03:44.85]From what I recall, the presentation consists of five parts, not including introduction and conclusion.｜我记得除去开场白和总结这两块，汇报有五个部分。\n[03:52.15]That would mean altogether we need to allocate seven parts between the two of us.｜那就是说我们两个人总共需要分摊七个部分的内容。\n[03:57.12]M: So, we have the abstract, background research, the project design, the results and the discussion portions.｜男：是啊，有摘要、背景研究、项目设计、研究结果与讨论这几个部分。\n[04:04.58]As the abstract section only applies to the article, we needn''t include it in the presentation.｜不过，摘要是依附文章存在的，我们的汇报里可以省略这部分。\n[04:10.15]How would you suggest we dole out the rest?｜你建议怎么分剩下的这几部分？\n[04:13.26]W: How do you feel about handling the background a bit?｜女：你负责背景研究部分怎么样？\n[04:16.09]In this way, we can both discuss the part of the project that we devoted most of our time to.｜这样我们俩都可以讲我们投入了大部分时间的项目部分。\n[04:21.21]M: Hold on a minute.｜男：等等。\n[04:22.67]You want me, the one who did the bulk of the task to also do the majority of the presentation?｜你想让我这个完成了大部分工作的人也承担汇报的大部分工作？\n[04:28.38]The background research, which was so meticulous, took more than a month.｜背景研究很是烦琐，花了一个多月才做完。\n[04:32.55]W: Okay, okay. I get it.｜女：好，好，我知道了。\n[04:34.28]Quit your moaning.｜别抱怨了。\n[04:35.44]I appreciate the rigorous work ethic you applied to the research, but not the sarcasm that comes up every time I mention it.｜我很欣赏你做研究时认真严谨的态度，可真不喜欢我每次提起这事儿你就冷嘲热讽。\n[04:43.02]What do you think would be a fair arrangement?｜那你觉得怎样安排才算公平呢？\n[04:45.36]M: I think the best arrangement would be to split the research into two parts, before 1980 and afterward.｜男：我认为最好的安排是把研究按时间分成1980年之前和1980年之后两部分。\n[04:52.24]I will take the before portion, and you would be assigned the after 1980, leaving the project and results.｜1980年前的部分由我来讲，之后的部分交给你，（这样就）剩下项目介绍和研究结果两部分。\n[04:59.03]I volunteer to describe the project, but as I struggled a bit with the statistics in the results section, how about you handling that?｜我愿意承担项目介绍部分，但由于我觉得研究结果那部分中的统计数据有点费劲，那部分由你来负责怎么样？\n[05:07.24]W: That''s agreeable to me.｜女：我同意。\n[05:08.71]I propose we both handle the discussion section in parts, along with the question and answer afterward, leaving only the introduction and conclusion.｜我提议咱们都处理部分讨论环节，还有后面的问答环节，这样就只剩下开场白和总结了。\n[05:18.07]M: I will take responsibility for the conclusion and put you in charge of the introduction.｜男：我负责总结部分，开场白交给你。\n[05:23.45]This will make it so that we alternate presenting, so as to avoid sounding monotonous to the audience.｜这样，我们交替汇报，也能避免让听众觉得单调。\n[05:30.32]Questions 5 to 8 are based on the conversation you have just heard.｜请根据你刚刚听到的对话回答问题5到8。\n[05:35.28]5. What does the woman say they first need to do?｜5. 女士说他们首先需要做什么？\n[05:52.05]6. Why does the man refuse to handle the background part?｜6. 男士为什么拒绝负责背景部分？\n[06:09.90]7. What does the woman urge the man to stop doing?｜7. 女士强烈要求男士不要再做什么？\n[06:28.75]8. Why does the man suggest he present the conclusion and the woman do the introduction?｜8. 男士为什么提议由他来承担结论部分，让女士负责开场白？\n[06:48.66]Section B Directions: In this section, you will hear two passages.｜B节 说明：在本节中，你将会听到两篇短文。', NOW(), NOW()
