  @a_cet6_2026_06_1_09, '/audio/exams/listening-cet6-2026-06-1.mp3', 'Passage One\n短文一\n\nMakeup can do more than just change your appearance—it can also alter others'' perceptions of you, for better or for worse.\n化妆改变的不只是外在形象——它还会让他人对你的看法变好或变坏。\n\nAccording to new research from the University of Stirling in Scotland, although both men and women perceive women who wear makeup as being of a higher status, men associate makeup with prestigious positive qualities, while women view other women wearing makeup as being dominant and a potential threat.\n苏格兰斯特灵大学的新研究表明：尽管男性和女性都认为化妆的女性社会地位更高，但男性会将化妆和优秀、正面的特质挂钩，而女性则会觉得化妆的女性气场强势，并将其视为潜在的威胁。\n\nThe research showed that men and women both rated the faces with cosmetics as being more attractive, but only women rated made-up faces as being more dominant while only men rated made-up faces as being higher in prestige.\n研究显示，男性和女性都认为化妆后的面容更有吸引力，但只有女性会觉得化了妆的女性气场更强，也只有男性会认为这类女性更有声望。\n\nA follow-up study investigated the root cause behind these differences in perception and found that female-on-female jealousy seemed to be the main cause for the differences in perception.\n一项后续研究探寻了这种认知差异的根源，发现女性之间的嫉妒心理是导致这种认知差异的主要原因。\n\nWomen rating women with makeup said they would be more jealous of them and thought they would be more attractive to men than their non-makeup wearing counterparts.\n在对化了妆的同性进行评价时，女性说她们会心生嫉妒，还认为化妆的女性要比素颜的女性对异性更有吸引力。\n\nCosmetic products are good for more than just giving you a pretty face.\n各类化妆产品的好处不仅仅是让你有一张漂亮的脸。\n\nIt can be particularly useful for women to understand how wearing makeup alters others'' perceptions of them in situations where they are trying to gain others'' trust and admiration.\n女性如果想赢得他人的信任与赞赏，了解妆容如何影响他人的看法会大有裨益。\n\nAt a job interview, knowing whether the hiring committee will consist of men or women might influence a female candidate''s decision about wearing makeup.\n参加求职面试时，了解招聘委员会成员的性别构成可能会影响女性求职者的化妆决定。\n\nWhether the interviewers will view her as attractive, dominant and prestigious can affect the interviewers'' actions and perhaps the outcome of the interview itself.\n面试官是否认为她有吸引力、有主导力且富有威望，会影响面试官的行为，甚至影响面试结果。\n\nQuestions 9 to 11 are based on the passage you have just heard.\n请根据你刚刚听到的短文回答问题9到11。\n\n9. What can makeup do according to new research from the University of Stirling in Scotland?\n9. 苏格兰斯特灵大学的新研究表明，化妆能起到什么作用？\n\n10. How did both men and women rate the faces with cosmetics in the new research?\n10. 在这项新研究中，男性和女性是如何评价化妆后的面容的？\n\n11. Why does a female candidate need to know the gender of the hiring committee members?\n11. 为什么女性求职者需要了解招聘委员会成员的性别？', 111, 1535.54, 436.50, 547.16, 552.33, 571.27, 438.10, 445.87, 'cet6-2026-06-1-g03', 'PASSAGE', '[07:16.50]Passage One｜短文一\n[07:18.10]Makeup can do more than just change your appearance—it can also alter others'' perceptions of you, for better or for worse.｜化妆改变的不只是外在形象——它还会让他人对你的看法变好或变坏。\n[07:26.17]According to new research from the University of Stirling in Scotland, although both men and women perceive women who wear makeup as being of a higher status, men associate makeup with prestigious positive qualities, while women view other women wearing makeup as being dominant and a potential threat.｜苏格兰斯特灵大学的新研究表明：尽管男性和女性都认为化妆的女性社会地位更高，但男性会将化妆和优秀、正面的特质挂钩，而女性则会觉得化妆的女性气场强势，并将其视为潜在的威胁。\n[07:47.22]The research showed that men and women both rated the faces with cosmetics as being more attractive, but only women rated made-up faces as being more dominant while only men rated made-up faces as being higher in prestige.｜研究显示，男性和女性都认为化妆后的面容更有吸引力，但只有女性会觉得化了妆的女性气场更强，也只有男性会认为这类女性更有声望。\n[08:04.51]A follow-up study investigated the root cause behind these differences in perception and found that female-on-female jealousy seemed to be the main cause for the differences in perception.｜一项后续研究探寻了这种认知差异的根源，发现女性之间的嫉妒心理是导致这种认知差异的主要原因。\n[08:17.79]Women rating women with makeup said they would be more jealous of them and thought they would be more attractive to men than their non-makeup wearing counterparts.｜在对化了妆的同性进行评价时，女性说她们会心生嫉妒，还认为化妆的女性要比素颜的女性对异性更有吸引力。\n[08:28.66]Cosmetic products are good for more than just giving you a pretty face.｜各类化妆产品的好处不仅仅是让你有一张漂亮的脸。\n[08:32.92]It can be particularly useful for women to understand how wearing makeup alters others'' perceptions of them in situations where they are trying to gain others'' trust and admiration.｜女性如果想赢得他人的信任与赞赏，了解妆容如何影响他人的看法会大有裨益。\n[08:45.55]At a job interview, knowing whether the hiring committee will consist of men or women might influence a female candidate''s decision about wearing makeup.｜参加求职面试时，了解招聘委员会成员的性别构成可能会影响女性求职者的化妆决定。\n[08:55.63]Whether the interviewers will view her as attractive, dominant and prestigious can affect the interviewers'' actions and perhaps the outcome of the interview itself.｜面试官是否认为她有吸引力、有主导力且富有威望，会影响面试官的行为，甚至影响面试结果。\n[09:07.16]Questions 9 to 11 are based on the passage you have just heard.｜请根据你刚刚听到的短文回答问题9到11。\n[09:12.33]9. What can makeup do according to new research from the University of Stirling in Scotland?｜9. 苏格兰斯特灵大学的新研究表明，化妆能起到什么作用？\n[09:31.57]10. How did both men and women rate the faces with cosmetics in the new research?｜10. 在这项新研究中，男性和女性是如何评价化妆后的面容的？\n[09:51.44]11. Why does a female candidate need to know the gender of the hiring committee members?｜11. 为什么女性求职者需要了解招聘委员会成员的性别？', NOW(), NOW()
