SELECT
  @a_cet6_2026_06_1_12, '/audio/exams/listening-cet6-2026-06-1.mp3', 'Passage Two\n短文二\n\nYou may have seen advertisements trumpeting methods of changing a habit that require absolutely no willpower whatsoever.\n你可能看到过各类广告，鼓吹完全无需意志力就能改变习惯的方法。\n\nBut can you really change a bad habit or create a good one without willpower?\n但你恨得不靠意志力就能改掉坏一个习惯，或者养成一个好习惯吗？\n\nTo answer this question, we first have to ask: “What is willpower?”\n要解答这个问题，我们首先要问：“意志力是什么？”\n\nMost people sadly think of it only as the ability to clench their teeth and resist attractive temptations.\n遗憾的是，大多数人都觉得，意志力只是咬牙抵制诱惑的能力。\n\nIn this view, willpower means self-denial and no fun.\n在这种认知里，意志力等同于自我克制，毫无乐趣可言。\n\nNo wonder people hope to make changes without it.\n也难怪人们都想不靠意志力就发生改变。\n\nI define willpower as using only the thought of your motivators to control your actions.\n我将意志力定义为只靠想着激励自己的因素来控制自身行为。\n\nLet''s say your motivators are “prevent diabetes” and “reach a healthy weight”.\n举个例子，你的动力是“防糖尿病”预和“达到健康体重”。\n\nSo if you are at the all-you-can-eat buffet, you think about your motivator—avoid diabetes through weight loss—and you take small portions and avoid the dessert table.\n那么如果在自助餐厅里，你想到自己的动力——通过减肥来防止糖尿病——你就会只取小份，避开甜品台。\n\nSo, amazingly enough, willpower begins with a thought, a bright idea, some way to improve your life or contribute to others.\n令人惊讶的是，意志力始于一个想法、一个好的念头、一个好的念头、某种改善生活或为他人做贡献的方法。\n\nThis bright idea is your motivator.\n这个好的念头就是你的动力。\n\nDr. Walter Mischel, an expert on willpower skills, uses the expressive term: a burning goal.\n意志力技能专家沃尔特·米切尔博士用了一个富有表现力的术语：一个热切的目标。\n\nWhether you call it a motivator, a burning goal or a bright idea, this idea is the force behind your willpower.\n无论你把它称为动力、热切的目标还是好的想法，它都是意志力背后的力量。\n\nWhat sort of bright ideas, motivators, make for effective willpower?\n什么样的好想法(激励因素)才能促成有效的意志力呢？\n\nIn fact, any goal that you value strongly counts.\n其实，任何你十分珍视的目标都可以。\n\nThe list may include good health, self-respect, a better future for your family, personal mission and being a role model for your child.\n这份清单可能会包含身体健康、自尊自爱、为家人创造更好的未来、个人使命和成为孩子的榜样。\n\nAll these can certainly drive a positive change.\n所有这些目标都能推动我们做出积极的改变。\n\nQuestions 12 to 15 are based on the passage you have just heard.\n请根据你刚刚听到的短文回答问题12到15。\n\n12. What methods do some advertisements trumpet about changing a habit?\n12. 一些广告大肆鼓吹用什么方法来改变习惯？\n\n13. What does the speaker define willpower as?\n13. 讲话者将意志力定义为什么？\n\n14. What may sound amazing enough as regards willpower?\n14. 关于意志力，什么说法听起来可能令人惊讶？\n\n15. What does the speaker say may make for effective willpower?\n15. 讲话者说，什么可能促成有效的意志力？\n\nSection C Directions: In this section, you will hear three recordings of lectures or talks followed by three or four questions.\nC节 说明：在本节中，你将会听到三篇讲座或讲话，每篇讲座或讲话后面都有三个或四个问题。', 107, 1535.54, 611.25, 718.14, 722.67, 741.26, NULL, NULL, 'cet6-2026-06-1-g04', 'PASSAGE', '[10:11.25]Passage Two｜短文二\n[10:13.00]You may have seen advertisements trumpeting methods of changing a habit that require absolutely no willpower whatsoever.｜你可能看到过各类广告，鼓吹完全无需意志力就能改变习惯的方法。\n[10:21.31]But can you really change a bad habit or create a good one without willpower?｜但你恨得不靠意志力就能改掉坏一个习惯，或者养成一个好习惯吗？\n[10:26.58]To answer this question, we first have to ask: “What is willpower?”｜要解答这个问题，我们首先要问：“意志力是什么？”\n[10:30.68]Most people sadly think of it only as the ability to clench their teeth and resist attractive temptations.｜遗憾的是，大多数人都觉得，意志力只是咬牙抵制诱惑的能力。\n[10:38.15]In this view, willpower means self-denial and no fun.｜在这种认知里，意志力等同于自我克制，毫无乐趣可言。\n[10:42.79]No wonder people hope to make changes without it.｜也难怪人们都想不靠意志力就发生改变。\n[10:46.30]I define willpower as using only the thought of your motivators to control your actions.｜我将意志力定义为只靠想着激励自己的因素来控制自身行为。\n[10:52.22]Let''s say your motivators are “prevent diabetes” and “reach a healthy weight”.｜举个例子，你的动力是“防糖尿病”预和“达到健康体重”。\n[10:58.07]So if you are at the all-you-can-eat buffet, you think about your motivator—avoid diabetes through weight loss—and you take small portions and avoid the dessert table.｜那么如果在自助餐厅里，你想到自己的动力——通过减肥来防止糖尿病——你就会只取小份，避开甜品台。\n[11:09.10]So, amazingly enough, willpower begins with a thought, a bright idea, some way to improve your life or contribute to others.｜令人惊讶的是，意志力始于一个想法、一个好的念头、一个好的念头、某种改善生活或为他人做贡献的方法。\n[11:18.21]This bright idea is your motivator.｜这个好的念头就是你的动力。\n[11:20.95]Dr. Walter Mischel, an expert on willpower skills, uses the expressive term: a burning goal.｜意志力技能专家沃尔特·米切尔博士用了一个富有表现力的术语：一个热切的目标。\n[11:28.45]Whether you call it a motivator, a burning goal or a bright idea, this idea is the force behind your willpower.｜无论你把它称为动力、热切的目标还是好的想法，它都是意志力背后的力量。\n[11:35.98]What sort of bright ideas, motivators, make for effective willpower?｜什么样的好想法(激励因素)才能促成有效的意志力呢？\n[11:41.43]In fact, any goal that you value strongly counts.｜其实，任何你十分珍视的目标都可以。\n[11:45.36]The list may include good health, self-respect, a better future for your family, personal mission and being a role model for your child.｜这份清单可能会包含身体健康、自尊自爱、为家人创造更好的未来、个人使命和成为孩子的榜样。\n[11:54.20]All these can certainly drive a positive change.｜所有这些目标都能推动我们做出积极的改变。\n[11:58.14]Questions 12 to 15 are based on the passage you have just heard.｜请根据你刚刚听到的短文回答问题12到15。\n[12:02.67]12. What methods do some advertisements trumpet about changing a habit?｜12. 一些广告大肆鼓吹用什么方法来改变习惯？\n[12:21.56]13. What does the speaker define willpower as?｜13. 讲话者将意志力定义为什么？\n[12:39.99]14. What may sound amazing enough as regards willpower?｜14. 关于意志力，什么说法听起来可能令人惊讶？\n[12:57.94]15. What does the speaker say may make for effective willpower?｜15. 讲话者说，什么可能促成有效的意志力？\n[13:16.66]Section C Directions: In this section, you will hear three recordings of lectures or talks followed by three or four questions.｜C节 说明：在本节中，你将会听到三篇讲座或讲话，每篇讲座或讲话后面都有三个或四个问题。', NOW(), NOW()
