SELECT
  @a_cet6_2026_06_1_17, '/audio/exams/listening-cet6-2026-06-1.mp3', 'Recording One\n录音一\n\nFor many pregnant women, understanding what seafood is safe and healthy, and what should be avoided because of mercury concerns comes with a lot of worrying.\n出于对汞含量的担忧，孕期女性总是忧心忡忡，不知道哪些海产品安全健康，哪些海产品需要避开。\n\nIn part, that''s because the federal government''s advice on the matter, first issued in 2004, has long been criticized as vague.\n这其中有一部分原因是，联邦政府2004年首次发布的相关建议长期以来都被批评为含糊不清。\n\nThat guidance has included advice on how much seafood to eat, and which species pregnant and breast-feeding women should avoid over concerns about mercury contamination.\n这份指导意见包括关于海产品摄入量的建议，也明确了孕期和哺乳期女性出于担心汞污染而需要避免食用的鱼类品种。\n\nBut critics say the government advisory has done more harm than good, scaring many pregnant and breast-feeding women away from eating seafood altogether.\n但批评者表示，这份政府建议弊大于利，吓得许多孕期和哺乳期女性彻底不敢吃海产品了。\n\nThe problem is real.\n这个问题确实确实存在。\n\nAccording to a spokesman for the Food and Drug Administration, or FDA for short, the agency analyzed fish consumption data from more than 1,000 pregnant women in the US and found that 21 percent of them ate no fish whatsoever in the previous month.\n美国食品及药物管理局（FDA）的发言人表示，该局分析了全美一千多名孕妇的鱼类食用数据后发现：21%的孕妇在上个月完全没有吃过鱼。\n\nAnd those who did eat fish consumed far less than recommended by the Dietary Guidelines: Some 50 percent ate less than 2 ounces a week and 75 percent ate less than 4 ounces.\n而那些食用过鱼类的人中，约半数每周吃鱼不足2盎司，75%的人每周食用量低于4盎司，远低于《膳食指南》的推荐标准。\n\nThis week, the FDA issued an update to the advice, listing more than 60 species in a chart that ranks fish as a “best choice”, “good choice” and “choices to avoid”.\n本周，美国食品及药物管理局更新了海产品食用建议，用表格的形式将60多种鱼类划分为“最佳选择”“良好选择”和“应避免的选择”三个等级。\n\nThe goal is to make it easier for mothers-to-be to feel confident about the type of seafood they include in their diets.\n目的在于让准妈妈们能更有把握判断饮食中可以纳入何种海产品。\n\nThe new advice recommends consumers choose a variety of fish to eat.\n新版建议中推荐消费者多样化地食用鱼类。\n\nAnd it comes with an easy-to-understand illustration of what an appropriate portion size should be: 4 ounces for an adult and 2 ounces for children aged 4 to 7.\n同时还提供了通俗易懂的配图，说明适宜食用量：成人4盎司，4至7岁儿童2盎司。\n\nAnd while expectant mothers have long been warned to stay away from shark and four other particular types of fish from the Gulf of Mexico, now there are three new species on the list of what to avoid.\n以往准妈妈们就被警告要避免食用鲨鱼以及来自墨西哥湾的四种鱼类，现在又新增了三种需要避开的鱼类。\n\nBut not everyone is thrilled with the new advice.\n但并非所有人都对这一新建议感到满意。\n\nCritics say the new advice doesn''t always agree with the agency''s own scientific findings.\n有批评者指出，建议内容和该局自身的科学研究结论并不相符。\n\nWhile mercury is of great concern when people are talking about pregnant women and seafood, it''s not the only factor contributing to anxiety.\n虽然汞是人们在讨论孕妇和海产品时非常担心的问题，但它并非导致焦虑的唯一因素。\n\nThe FDA maintains that its final consumption recommendations were based on thorough scientific analysis.\n美国食品及药物管理局表示，最终的食用建议是基于全面的科学分析。\n\nAgency spokesman Cassell says the FDA believes the recommendations will increase confidence, not uncertainty.\n该局发言人卡斯尔称，相信新的建议能够提升大众信心，而非加剧不安。\n\nBut critics disagree.\n但批评者们并不认同。\n\nThey think the FDA''s advice is not based on the evidence in its own detailed report, and so it confuses everyone.\n他们认为最新建议并未基于该局自己详细报告中的研究证据，因此让人们困惑。\n\nQuestions 16 to 18 are based on the recording you have just heard.\n请根据你刚刚听到的录音回答问题16到18。\n\n16. What does the speaker say about the federal government''s advice on seafood safety?\n16. 关于联邦政府的海产品安全建议，讲话者说了什么？\n\n17. What did the Food and Drug Administration do this week?\n17. 美国食品及药物管理局本周做了什么？\n\n18. According to the speaker, what are people concerned about regarding pregnant women and seafood?\n18. 根据讲话者的说法，关于孕妇和海产品，人们担心什么？', 181, 1535.54, 823.60, 1004.39, 1027.99, 1046.58, 902.00, 924.48, 'cet6-2026-06-1-g05', 'LECTURE', '[13:43.60]Recording One｜录音一\n[13:45.57]For many pregnant women, understanding what seafood is safe and healthy, and what should be avoided because of mercury concerns comes with a lot of worrying.｜出于对汞含量的担忧，孕期女性总是忧心忡忡，不知道哪些海产品安全健康，哪些海产品需要避开。\n[13:56.54]In part, that''s because the federal government''s advice on the matter, first issued in 2004, has long been criticized as vague.｜这其中有一部分原因是，联邦政府2004年首次发布的相关建议长期以来都被批评为含糊不清。\n[14:05.98]That guidance has included advice on how much seafood to eat, and which species pregnant and breast-feeding women should avoid over concerns about mercury contamination.｜这份指导意见包括关于海产品摄入量的建议，也明确了孕期和哺乳期女性出于担心汞污染而需要避免食用的鱼类品种。\n[14:17.88]But critics say the government advisory has done more harm than good, scaring many pregnant and breast-feeding women away from eating seafood altogether.｜但批评者表示，这份政府建议弊大于利，吓得许多孕期和哺乳期女性彻底不敢吃海产品了。\n[14:28.03]The problem is real.｜这个问题确实确实存在。\n[14:29.68]According to a spokesman for the Food and Drug Administration, or FDA for short, the agency analyzed fish consumption data from more than 1,000 pregnant women in the US and found that 21 percent of them ate no fish whatsoever in the previous month.｜美国食品及药物管理局（FDA）的发言人表示，该局分析了全美一千多名孕妇的鱼类食用数据后发现：21%的孕妇在上个月完全没有吃过鱼。\n[14:47.89]And those who did eat fish consumed far less than recommended by the Dietary Guidelines: Some 50 percent ate less than 2 ounces a week and 75 percent ate less than 4 ounces.｜而那些食用过鱼类的人中，约半数每周吃鱼不足2盎司，75%的人每周食用量低于4盎司，远低于《膳食指南》的推荐标准。\n[15:02.00]This week, the FDA issued an update to the advice, listing more than 60 species in a chart that ranks fish as a “best choice”, “good choice” and “choices to avoid”.｜本周，美国食品及药物管理局更新了海产品食用建议，用表格的形式将60多种鱼类划分为“最佳选择”“良好选择”和“应避免的选择”三个等级。\n[15:16.07]The goal is to make it easier for mothers-to-be to feel confident about the type of seafood they include in their diets.｜目的在于让准妈妈们能更有把握判断饮食中可以纳入何种海产品。\n[15:24.78]The new advice recommends consumers choose a variety of fish to eat.｜新版建议中推荐消费者多样化地食用鱼类。\n[15:29.49]And it comes with an easy-to-understand illustration of what an appropriate portion size should be: 4 ounces for an adult and 2 ounces for children aged 4 to 7.｜同时还提供了通俗易懂的配图，说明适宜食用量：成人4盎司，4至7岁儿童2盎司。\n[15:41.99]And while expectant mothers have long been warned to stay away from shark and four other particular types of fish from the Gulf of Mexico, now there are three new species on the list of what to avoid.｜以往准妈妈们就被警告要避免食用鲨鱼以及来自墨西哥湾的四种鱼类，现在又新增了三种需要避开的鱼类。\n[15:56.38]But not everyone is thrilled with the new advice.｜但并非所有人都对这一新建议感到满意。\n[15:59.41]Critics say the new advice doesn''t always agree with the agency''s own scientific findings.｜有批评者指出，建议内容和该局自身的科学研究结论并不相符。\n[16:06.73]While mercury is of great concern when people are talking about pregnant women and seafood, it''s not the only factor contributing to anxiety.｜虽然汞是人们在讨论孕妇和海产品时非常担心的问题，但它并非导致焦虑的唯一因素。\n[16:15.55]The FDA maintains that its final consumption recommendations were based on thorough scientific analysis.｜美国食品及药物管理局表示，最终的食用建议是基于全面的科学分析。\n[16:24.00]Agency spokesman Cassell says the FDA believes the recommendations will increase confidence, not uncertainty.｜该局发言人卡斯尔称，相信新的建议能够提升大众信心，而非加剧不安。\n[16:33.30]But critics disagree.｜但批评者们并不认同。\n[16:35.14]They think the FDA''s advice is not based on the evidence in its own detailed report, and so it confuses everyone.｜他们认为最新建议并未基于该局自己详细报告中的研究证据，因此让人们困惑。\n[16:44.39]Questions 16 to 18 are based on the recording you have just heard.｜请根据你刚刚听到的录音回答问题16到18。\n[16:49.51]16. What does the speaker say about the federal government''s advice on seafood safety?｜16. 关于联邦政府的海产品安全建议，讲话者说了什么？\n[17:07.99]17. What did the Food and Drug Administration do this week?｜17. 美国食品及药物管理局本周做了什么？\n[17:26.88]18. According to the speaker, what are people concerned about regarding pregnant women and seafood?｜18. 根据讲话者的说法，关于孕妇和海产品，人们担心什么？', NOW(), NOW()
