明适宜食用量：成人4盎司，4至7岁儿童2盎司。\n[15:41.99]And while expectant mothers have long been warned to stay away from shark and four other particular types of fish from the Gulf of Mexico, now there are three new species on the list of what to avoid.｜以往准妈妈们就被警告要避免食用鲨鱼以及来自墨西哥湾的四种鱼类，现在又新增了三种需要避开的鱼类。\n[15:56.38]But not everyone is thrilled with the new advice.｜但并非所有人都对这一新建议感到满意。\n[15:59.41]Critics say the new advice doesn''t always agree with the agency''s own scientific findings.｜有批评者指出，建议内容和该局自身的科学研究结论并不相符。\n[16:06.73]While mercury is of great concern when people are talking about pregnant women and seafood, it''s not the only factor contributing to anxiety.｜虽然汞是人们在讨论孕妇和海产品时非常担心的问题，但它并非导致焦虑的唯一因素。\n[16:15.55]The FDA maintains that its final consumption recommendations were based on thorough scientific analysis.｜美国食品及药物管理局表示，最终的食用建议是基于全面的科学分析。\n[16:24.00]Agency spokesman Cassell says the FDA believes the recommendations will increase confidence, not uncertainty.｜该局发言人卡斯尔称，相信新的建议能够提升大众信心，而非加剧不安。\n[16:33.30]But critics disagree.｜但批评者们并不认同。\n[16:35.14]They think the FDA''s advice is not based on the evidence in its own detailed report, and so it confuses everyone.｜他们认为最新建议并未基于该局自己详细报告中的研究证据，因此让人们困惑。\n[16:44.39]Questions 16 to 18 are based on the recording you have just heard.｜请根据你刚刚听到的录音回答问题16到18。\n[16:49.51]16. What does the speaker say about the federal government''s advice on seafood safety?｜16. 关于联邦政府的海产品安全建议，讲话者说了什么？\n[17:07.99]17. What did the Food and Drug Administration do this week?｜17. 美国食品及药物管理局本周做了什么？\n[17:26.88]18. According to the speaker, what are people concerned about regarding pregnant women and seafood?｜18. 根据讲话者的说法，关于孕妇和海产品，人们担心什么？', NOW(), NOW()
