INSERT INTO `listening_audio`
  (`question_id`, `audio_url`, `transcript`, `duration_seconds`, `audio_total_seconds`, `audio_start_seconds`, `audio_end_seconds`, `question_start_seconds`, `question_end_seconds`, `answer_start_seconds`, `answer_end_seconds`, `group_key`, `listening_type`, `lrc_content`, `created_at`, `updated_at`)
SELECT
  @a_cet6_2026_06_1_19, '/audio/exams/listening-cet6-2026-06-1.mp3', 'Recording Two\n录音二\n\nI know you''re busy with work, but you also need to take some time off to recharge those batteries.\n我知道大家平时都忙于工作，但也需要抽空休息，让身体充能。\n\nSo should you plan one big vacation for the year or should you take multiple short vacations throughout?\n那么，你是一年休一次长假，还是分多次短期休假呢？\n\nQuantity can sometimes beat quality.\n有时候，数量优于质量。\n\nFirst and foremost, regardless of how you use your vacation days, you need to be using them, and soon.\n首先且最重要的是，无论您如何安排休假时间，都需要开始利用这些假期，并且尽快休假。\n\nThe longer you put off your time off, the worse you''re making things for yourself.\n休假的时间拖得越久，对自身就越不利。\n\nOne nine-year-long study, published in Psychosomatic Medicine, suggests not taking at least one vacation a year may increase your risk of mortality due to heart disease.\n一项历时9年、发表在《心身医学》期刊上的研究表明，如果一年连一次假都不休，患上心脏病进而引发死亡的风险会增加。\n\nSo not only are you killing your joy, you''re possibly killing yourself.\n所以，你不仅在扼杀自己的快乐，还可能正在要自己的命。\n\nGive yourself a break, folks.\n所以，朋友们，一定要给自己放个假。\n\nWhen you should take those breaks, however, depends on a few factors—how many days you have available to use, what activities bring you joy, whether you have a family or not, and other variables come into play.\n至于休假时机，要结合诸多因素判断：可用假期天数、个人喜好的休闲方式、是否有家庭等等。\n\nBecause of that, there''s no perfect formula that works for everyone, but there are still a few things everyone can try to shoot for.\n受以上因素影响，没有什么可以适用于所有人的完美方案，但确实有几条是所有人都可以努力争取一下的。\n\nWe know that in terms of maximizing relaxation, you should aim for vacations that range somewhere between 7 and 11 days long.\n我们了解到，想要最大程度放松身心，单次休假时长控制在7至11天最佳。\n\nThat gives you enough time to let go of your stress at work, completely loosen up and achieve full-on calm.\n这样的时长足够让你释放工作压力、完全放松下来、获得彻底的平静。\n\nThat above-mentioned study also recommends you space out your vacations evenly instead of using up all of your days at once.\n上述研究还建议，要把假期均匀分开，而不是一次性用完。\n\nEight days might sound like a lot for someone who only gets ten days of vacation a year, but if you frame them with weekends, you can manage two evenly spaced eight-day vacations a year.\n对于每年仅享有10天假期的人来说，一次性休假8天听上去好像把假差不多都休完了，但如果把周末考虑进去调休一下，就能规划出两次 8 天的假期。\n\nIf you have 14 days of paid leave, that''s almost three separate eight-day vacations you can use to split your year into thirds.\n如果能有14天带薪假期，那差不多可以拆分出3个为期8天的假期，就可以把一年切分成3段。\n\nAs tempting as it might be to use all your days to take one long summer break, your overall goal should be to achieve the perfect balance between length plus joy and frequency.\n在暑期能休一个长长的假期固然诱人，但休假的核心是在时长、愉悦感和频次之间找到最佳平衡点。\n\nVacation frequency is important, because planning multiple breaks throughout the year means you always have something to look forward to.\n休假频率很重要，因为在一年中安排多次假期意味着你在生活中总会有所期待。\n\nPlanning things and the anticipation that comes with it tend to make us happier.\n做规划以及随之而来的期待，往往会让人心情更加愉悦。\n\nIf you only take one long vacation every year, the excitement builds much more slowly and seems so far off that it can actually lead to feelings of despair.\n如果一年只休一次长假，兴奋感积累缓慢，漫长的等待甚至会让人产生低落情绪。\n\nQuestions 19 to 21 are based on the recording you have just heard.\n请根据你刚刚听到的录音回答问题19到21。\n\n19. What does the speaker say about people not taking any vacation?\n19. 关于那些从不休假的人，讲话者说了什么？\n\n20. What does the nine-year study recommend people do when planning vacations?\n20. 这项历时9年的研究建议人们在规划假期时怎么做？\n\n21. Why is vacation frequency important according to the speaker?\n21. 根据讲话者的说法，休假频率为什么重要？', 153, 1535.54, 1066.45, 1219.41, 1225.00, 1243.10, NULL, NULL, 'cet6-2026-06-1-g06', 'LECTURE', '[17:46.45]Recording Two｜录音二\n[17:48.00]I know you''re busy with work, but you also need to take some time off to recharge those batteries.｜我知道大家平时都忙于工作，但也需要抽空休息，让身体充能。\n[17:54.53]So should you plan one big vacation for the year or should you take multiple short vacations throughout?｜那么，你是一年休一次长假，还是分多次短期休假呢？\n[18:02.42]Quantity can sometimes beat quality.｜有时候，数量优于质量。\n[18:05.26]First and foremost, regardless of how you use your vacation days, you need to be using them, and soon.｜首先且最重要的是，无论您如何安排休假时间，都需要开始利用这些假期，并且尽快休假。\n[18:12.70]The longer you put off your time off, the worse you''re making things for yourself.｜休假的时间拖得越久，对自身就越不利。\n[18:17.59]One nine-year-long study, published in Psychosomatic Medicine, suggests not taking at least one vacation a year may increase your risk of mortality due to heart disease.｜一项历时9年、发表在《心身医学》期刊上的研究表明，如果一年连一次假都不休，患上心脏病进而引发死亡的风险会增加。\n[18:29.10]So not only are you killing your joy, you''re possibly killing yourself.｜所以，你不仅在扼杀自己的快乐，还可能正在要自己的命。\n[18:33.96]Give yourself a break, folks.｜所以，朋友们，一定要给自己放个假。\n[18:36.03]When you should take those breaks, however, depends on a few factors—how many days you have available to use, what activities bring you joy, whether you have a family or not, and other variables come into play.｜至于休假时机，要结合诸多因素判断：可用假期天数、个人喜好的休闲方式、是否有家庭等等。\n[18:50.36]Because of that, there''s no perfect formula that works for everyone, but there are still a few things everyone can try to shoot for.｜受以上因素影响，没有什么可以适用于所有人的完美方案，但确实有几条是所有人都可以努力争取一下的。\n[18:58.89]We know that in terms of maximizing relaxation, you should aim for vacations that range somewhere between 7 and 11 days long.｜我们了解到，想要最大程度放松身心，单次休假时长控制在7至11天最佳。\n[19:07.57]That gives you enough time to let go of your stress at work, completely loosen up and achieve full-on calm.｜这样的时长足够让你释放工作压力、完全放松下来、获得彻底的平静。\n[19:14.29]That above-mentioned study also recommends you space out your vacations evenly instead of using up all of your days at once.｜上述研究还建议，要把假期均匀分开，而不是一次性用完。\n[19:22.81]Eight days might sound like a lot for someone who only gets ten days of vacation a year, but if you frame them with weekends, you can manage two evenly spaced eight-day vacations a year.｜对于每年仅享有10天假期的人来说，一次性休假8天听上去好像把假差不多都休完了，但如果把周末考虑进去调休一下，就能规划出两次 8 天的假期。\n[19:35.08]If you have 14 days of paid leave, that''s almost three separate eight-day vacations you can use to split your year into thirds.｜如果能有14天带薪假期，那差不多可以拆分出3个为期8天的假期，就可以把一年切分成3段。\n[19:43.60]As tempting as it might be to use all your days to take one long summer break, your overall goal should be to achieve the perfect balance between length plus joy and frequency.｜在暑期能休一个长长的假期固然诱人，但休假的核心是在时长、愉悦感和频次之间找到最佳平衡点。\n[19:55.55]Vacation frequency is important, because planning multiple breaks throughout the year means you always have something to look forward to.｜休假频率很重要，因为在一年中安排多次假期意味着你在生活中总会有所期待。\n[20:02.84]Planning things and the anticipation that comes with it tend to make us happier.｜做规划以及随之而来的期待，往往会让人心情更加愉悦。\n[20:08.14]If you only take one long vacation every year, the excitement builds much more slowly and seems so far off that it can actually lead to feelings of despair.｜如果一年只休一次长假，兴奋感积累缓慢，漫长的等待甚至会让人产生低落情绪。\n[20:19.41]Questions 19 to 21 are based on the recording you have just heard.｜请根据你刚刚听到的录音回答问题19到21。\n[20:25.00]19. What does the speaker say about people not taking any vacation?｜19. 关于那些从不休假的人，讲话者说了什么？\n[20:43.40]20. What does the nine-year study recommend people do when planning vacations?｜20. 这项历时9年的研究建议人们在规划假期时怎么做？\n[21:03.00]21. Why is vacation frequency important according to the speaker?｜21. 根据讲话者的说法，休假频率为什么重要？', NOW(), NOW()
