  @a_cet6_2026_06_2_03, '/audio/exams/listening-cet6-2026-06-2.mp3', 'Conversation One\n对话一\n\nW: Hi, Frank, are you working through your lunch hour again?\n女：嗨，弗兰克，你又准备在午餐时间工作吗？\n\nM: No, not at all.\n男：不，完全没有。\n\nIt''s my 10th wedding anniversary next week, and I promised Jane that I would book a city break for us, as I have annual leave to take.\n下周是我和妻子结婚十周年纪念日，由于我有年假要休，我向简承诺要为我们预订一次城市旅行。\n\nAnd it would be nice to celebrate somewhere warm, so I''m trying to book something in Barcelona.\n而且能在一个温暖的地方庆祝一下也挺好的，所以我正试着预订去巴塞罗那的行程。\n\nW: That sounds so romantic.\n女：听起来真浪漫。\n\nI adore Barcelona.\n我非常喜欢巴塞罗那。\n\nIt''s such a fabulous cosmopolitan city.\n它是一座非常棒的国际大都市。\n\nThere''s so much to do there, excellent food and that cathedral that they are still building after about 150 years. Very cool.\n那里有很多事情可做，有美味的食物，还有那座建了大约150年还没完工的大教堂。非常酷。\n\nM: I know. But the anniversary is looming and I''m still scrambling to find accommodation.\n男：我知道。但纪念日快到了，我还在忙着找住处。\n\nEverything is either wildly expensive or already fully booked.\n所有地方要么贵得离谱，要么已经订满了。\n\nI''m starting to feel a bit frantic.\n我开始觉得有点抓狂了。\n\nW: Well, if you are going for a whole week, why don''t you do a couple of nights in somewhere really glamorous and then do the rest of the week a bit further up the coast, where the accommodation is cheaper and that will offset the cost of the expensive place?\n女：嗯，如果你要去一整周，为什么不在一个豪华的地方住上两晚，然后这一周剩下的时间住在离海岸远一点的地方？那里的住宿更便宜，这样就能抵消住在昂贵地方的费用了吧。\n\nM: That might be a good plan.\n男：这或许是个好计划。\n\nIt''s not too expensive to rent a car, so we could still drive into the city.\n租车也不算太贵，所以我们仍然可以开车进城。\n\nYes, there are lots of places outside the city that have pools and are all-inclusive, so we wouldn''t even need to pay for food or drinks.\n是的，城外有很多地方都带游泳池，而且是全包式的，我们甚至不需要支付食物或饮料的费用。\n\nI''ll send a query now about the dates we''re interested in.\n我现在就咨询一下我们感兴趣的日期。\n\nW: That sounds perfect!\n女：听起来很完美！\n\nI''m sure that Jane will be absolutely thrilled to bits.\n我相信简一定会高兴得不得了。\n\nI really do recommend visiting that cathedral.\n我真的推荐去参观那座大教堂。\n\nYou can go all the way up to the top of it, but you need to go up a really steep spiral staircase to get there.\n你可以一直走到它的最顶部，但你需要爬一个非常陡的螺旋楼梯才能到那里。\n\nM: Considering Jane is terrified of heights, I think if I tried to make her do that, I would come back divorced.\n男：考虑到简恐高，我想如果我试图让她爬上去，那么我回来时可能就离婚了。\n\nThanks for the help though.\n不过谢谢你的帮助。\n\nIt was turning into a logistical nightmare.\n这本来快变成一场行程安排的噩梦了。\n\nQuestions 1 to 4 are based on the conversation you have just heard.\n请根据你刚刚听到的对话回答问题1到4。\n\n1. What is the man planning to do?\n1. 男士正在计划去做什么？\n\n2. Why is the man starting to feel a bit frantic?\n2. 为什么男士开始觉得有点抓狂了？\n\n3. What does the woman suggest the man do?\n3. 女士建议男士做什么？\n\n4. What does the man say about his wife Jane?\n4. 关于他的妻子简，男士说了什么？', 109, 1568.77, 36.77, 145.27, 185.19, 202.04, 85.38, 99.56, 'cet6-2026-06-2-g01', 'LONG_DIALOGUE', '[00:36.77]Conversation One｜对话一\n[00:38.47]W: Hi, Frank, are you working through your lunch hour again?｜女：嗨，弗兰克，你又准备在午餐时间工作吗？\n[00:41.95]M: No, not at all.｜男：不，完全没有。\n[00:43.15]It''s my 10th wedding anniversary next week, and I promised Jane that I would book a city break for us, as I have annual leave to take.｜下周是我和妻子结婚十周年纪念日，由于我有年假要休，我向简承诺要为我们预订一次城市旅行。\n[00:51.08]And it would be nice to celebrate somewhere warm, so I''m trying to book something in Barcelona.｜而且能在一个温暖的地方庆祝一下也挺好的，所以我正试着预订去巴塞罗那的行程。\n[00:56.75]W: That sounds so romantic.｜女：听起来真浪漫。\n[00:58.52]I adore Barcelona.｜我非常喜欢巴塞罗那。\n[01:00.09]It''s such a fabulous cosmopolitan city.｜它是一座非常棒的国际大都市。\n[01:02.83]There''s so much to do there, excellent food and that cathedral that they are still building after about 150 years. Very cool.｜那里有很多事情可做，有美味的食物，还有那座建了大约150年还没完工的大教堂。非常酷。\n[01:12.50]M: I know. But the anniversary is looming and I''m still scrambling to find accommodation.｜男：我知道。但纪念日快到了，我还在忙着找住处。\n[01:18.71]Everything is either wildly expensive or already fully booked.｜所有地方要么贵得离谱，要么已经订满了。\n[01:22.91]I''m starting to feel a bit frantic.｜我开始觉得有点抓狂了。\n[01:25.38]W: Well, if you are going for a whole week, why don''t you do a couple of nights in somewhere really glamorous and then do the rest of the week a bit further up the coast, where the accommodation is cheaper and that will offset the cost of the expensive place?｜女：嗯，如果你要去一整周，为什么不在一个豪华的地方住上两晚，然后这一周剩下的时间住在离海岸远一点的地方？那里的住宿更便宜，这样就能抵消住在昂贵地方的费用了吧。\n[01:39.86]M: That might be a good plan.｜男：这或许是个好计划。\n[01:41.89]It''s not too expensive to rent a car, so we could still drive into the city.｜租车也不算太贵，所以我们仍然可以开车进城。\n[01:46.92]Yes, there are lots of places outside the city that have pools and are all-inclusive, so we wouldn''t even need to pay for food or drinks.｜是的，城外有很多地方都带游泳池，而且是全包式的，我们甚至不需要支付食物或饮料的费用。\n[01:55.66]I''ll send a query now about the dates we''re interested in.｜我现在就咨询一下我们感兴趣的日期。\n[01:59.42]W: That sounds perfect!｜女：听起来很完美！\n[02:00.88]I''m sure that Jane will be absolutely thrilled to bits.｜我相信简一定会高兴得不得了。\n[02:04.23]I really do recommend visiting that cathedral.｜我真的推荐去参观那座大教堂。\n[02:07.01]You can go all the way up to the top of it, but you need to go up a really steep spiral staircase to get there.｜你可以一直走到它的最顶部，但你需要爬一个非常陡的螺旋楼梯才能到那里。\n[02:13.95]M: Considering Jane is terrified of heights, I think if I tried to make her do that, I would come back divorced.｜男：考虑到简恐高，我想如果我试图让她爬上去，那么我回来时可能就离婚了。\n[02:20.57]Thanks for the help though.｜不过谢谢你的帮助。\n[02:22.68]It was turning into a logistical nightmare.｜这本来快变成一场行程安排的噩梦了。\n[02:25.27]Questions 1 to 4 are based on the conversation you have just heard.｜请根据你刚刚听到的对话回答问题1到4。\n[02:30.26]1. What is the man planning to do?｜1. 男士正在计划去做什么？\n[02:45.66]2. Why is the man starting to feel a bit frantic?｜2. 为什么男士开始觉得有点抓狂了？\n[03:05.19]3. What does the woman suggest the man do?｜3. 女士建议男士做什么？\n[03:22.34]4. What does the man say about his wife Jane?｜4. 关于他的妻子简，男士说了什么？', NOW(), NOW()
