SELECT
  @a_cet6_2026_06_2_11, '/audio/exams/listening-cet6-2026-06-2.mp3', 'Passage One\n短文一\n\nIn America, at least, “passion” is a word that often comes up on job descriptions and in interviews.\n至少在美国，“激情”这个词经常出现在职位描述上以及面试中。\n\nOn the whole, passionate people are thought of in a positive light and considered likely to achieve their goals.\n总体而言，充满激情的人被正面看待，并且被认为更有可能实现他们的目标。\n\nBut when it comes to predicting achievement, has the importance of passion been overstated?\n但就预测成就而言，激情的重要性是否被夸大了呢？\n\nAccording to a new study from Stanford University, passion may be less important in certain cultures.\n根据斯坦福大学的一项新研究，激情在某些文化中可能没那么重要。\n\nAnd the fact that passion is often seen as a key to achievement may reflect a distinctly Western model of motivation.\n而且，激情常被视为成就的关键这一事实可能反映了一种明显的西方动机模式。\n\nThe chief factor explored in the study was how individualistic a society was.\n该研究探讨的主要因素是社会个人主义的程度。\n\nIn individualistic cultures, the researchers assert people are more motivated by pursuing paths related to their passions, but those in collectivistic cultures are more likely to see themselves as part of a network.\n研究人员断言，在个人主义文化中，人们更有动力去追求与自身激情相关的道路，但那些在集体主义文化中的人更可能将自己视为群体网络的一部分。\n\nThey often place fulfilling obligations to others above focusing on their own interests.\n他们常常把履行对他人的义务置于自己的利益之上。\n\nThe researchers looked at data from nearly 60 countries.\n研究人员分析了来自近60个国家的数据。\n\nThey found that, in science subjects, passion was positively correlated with academic achievements.\n他们发现，在科学科目中，激情与学业成绩呈正相关。\n\nHigher levels of enjoyment and interest also bolstered test scores.\n更高的享受度和兴趣也能提高考试成绩。\n\nBut the strength of this correlation wasn''t the same across cultures.\n但这种关联的强度在文化与文化之间并不相同。\n\nThose in individualistic societies such as the US, Australia and the UK showed a stronger link between passion and achievement.\n在个人主义社会，如美国、澳大利亚和英国，激情与成就之间的联系更强。\n\nThe effect of passion on performance was more subtle for those in more collectivistic societies such as Colombia or Thailand.\n而对于那些生活在哥伦比亚、泰国等集体主义倾向更强的社会中的人来说，激情对表现的影响则更为微妙。\n\nThese findings were mirrored in achievement in both mathematics and reading.\n这些发现在数学和阅读的成绩中都得到了印证。\n\nIt''s clear from the findings that passion isn''t the only thing that motivates people to achieve their goals.\n从这些发现中可以清楚地看出，激情并不是激励人们实现目标的唯一因素。\n\nQuestions 9 to 11 are based on the passage you have just heard.\n请根据你刚刚听到的短文回答问题9到11。\n\n9. What are passionate people considered likely to do in America?\n9. 在美国，充满激情的人被认为可能会做什么？\n\n10. What does a new study from Stanford show about the importance of passion in predicting achievement?\n10. 关于激情在预测成就方面的重要性，斯坦福大学的一项新研究表明了什么？\n\n11. What did the researchers find about the effect of passion on academic achievement for those in more collectivistic societies?\n11. 对于生活在集体主义倾向更强的社会中的人，研究人员发现激情对学业成绩的影响是怎样的？', 120, 1568.77, 444.38, 564.74, 608.33, 629.82, NULL, NULL, 'cet6-2026-06-2-g03', 'PASSAGE', '[07:24.38]Passage One｜短文一\n[07:26.05]In America, at least, “passion” is a word that often comes up on job descriptions and in interviews.｜至少在美国，“激情”这个词经常出现在职位描述上以及面试中。\n[07:34.06]On the whole, passionate people are thought of in a positive light and considered likely to achieve their goals.｜总体而言，充满激情的人被正面看待，并且被认为更有可能实现他们的目标。\n[07:41.55]But when it comes to predicting achievement, has the importance of passion been overstated?｜但就预测成就而言，激情的重要性是否被夸大了呢？\n[07:47.28]According to a new study from Stanford University, passion may be less important in certain cultures.｜根据斯坦福大学的一项新研究，激情在某些文化中可能没那么重要。\n[07:54.33]And the fact that passion is often seen as a key to achievement may reflect a distinctly Western model of motivation.｜而且，激情常被视为成就的关键这一事实可能反映了一种明显的西方动机模式。\n[08:02.89]The chief factor explored in the study was how individualistic a society was.｜该研究探讨的主要因素是社会个人主义的程度。\n[08:09.06]In individualistic cultures, the researchers assert people are more motivated by pursuing paths related to their passions, but those in collectivistic cultures are more likely to see themselves as part of a network.｜研究人员断言，在个人主义文化中，人们更有动力去追求与自身激情相关的道路，但那些在集体主义文化中的人更可能将自己视为群体网络的一部分。\n[08:24.18]They often place fulfilling obligations to others above focusing on their own interests.｜他们常常把履行对他人的义务置于自己的利益之上。\n[08:30.41]The researchers looked at data from nearly 60 countries.｜研究人员分析了来自近60个国家的数据。\n[08:34.77]They found that, in science subjects, passion was positively correlated with academic achievements.｜他们发现，在科学科目中，激情与学业成绩呈正相关。\n[08:41.28]Higher levels of enjoyment and interest also bolstered test scores.｜更高的享受度和兴趣也能提高考试成绩。\n[08:46.84]But the strength of this correlation wasn''t the same across cultures.｜但这种关联的强度在文化与文化之间并不相同。\n[08:51.67]Those in individualistic societies such as the US, Australia and the UK showed a stronger link between passion and achievement.｜在个人主义社会，如美国、澳大利亚和英国，激情与成就之间的联系更强。\n[09:02.17]The effect of passion on performance was more subtle for those in more collectivistic societies such as Colombia or Thailand.｜而对于那些生活在哥伦比亚、泰国等集体主义倾向更强的社会中的人来说，激情对表现的影响则更为微妙。\n[09:11.60]These findings were mirrored in achievement in both mathematics and reading.｜这些发现在数学和阅读的成绩中都得到了印证。\n[09:16.94]It''s clear from the findings that passion isn''t the only thing that motivates people to achieve their goals.｜从这些发现中可以清楚地看出，激情并不是激励人们实现目标的唯一因素。\n[09:24.74]Questions 9 to 11 are based on the passage you have just heard.｜请根据你刚刚听到的短文回答问题9到11。\n[09:29.50]9. What are passionate people considered likely to do in America?｜9. 在美国，充满激情的人被认为可能会做什么？\n[09:47.93]10. What does a new study from Stanford show about the importance of passion in predicting achievement?｜10. 关于激情在预测成就方面的重要性，斯坦福大学的一项新研究表明了什么？\n[10:08.33]11. What did the researchers find about the effect of passion on academic achievement for those in more collectivistic societies?｜11. 对于生活在集体主义倾向更强的社会中的人，研究人员发现激情对学业成绩的影响是怎样的？', NOW(), NOW()
