SELECT
  @a_cet6_2026_06_2_13, '/audio/exams/listening-cet6-2026-06-2.mp3', 'Passage Two\n短文二\n\nWhy does nature create patterns?\n为什么大自然会创造图案？\n\nThe reason patterns often appear in nature is simple—the same basic physical or chemical processes occur in many pattern substances and organisms as they form.\n自然中常常出现图案的原因很简单——许多形成图案的物质和有机体在形成过程中，都发生了相同的物理或化学基本过程。\n\nWhether in plants and animals or rocks, foams and ice crystals, the intricate patterns that happen in nature come down to what''s happening at the level of atoms and molecules.\n无论是植物、动物，还是岩石、泡沫和冰晶，自然界中出现的复杂图案都归结于原子和分子层面发生的情况。\n\nA pattern in nature is any regularly repeated arrangement of shapes or colors.\n自然界中的图案是形状或颜色有规律地重复排列。\n\nSome of the most striking examples include the six-sided arrays of rocks at Giant''s Causeway in the United Kingdom, and the colorful stripes and spots on tropical fish.\n一些最引人注目的例子包括英国巨人堤上的六边形岩石阵列，以及热带鱼身上的彩色条纹和斑点。\n\nPatterns like these begin to form at a small scale when materials undergo processes like drying, freezing, wrinkling, diffusing and reacting.\n当材料经历干燥、冷冻、起皱、扩散和反应等过程时，这些图案开始小规模形成。\n\nThose changes then give rise to complex patterns at a larger scale that people can see.\n随后，这些变化产生了人们可以看到的更大规模的复杂图案。\n\nImagine delicate frozen crystals on a window during winter.\n想象一下冬天窗户上精致的冰晶。\n\nWhat creates that pattern?\n是什么创造了这种图案？\n\nWhen water freezes, its molecules begin clustering together.\n当水结冰时，其分子开始聚集在一起。\n\nWater molecules have a particular bent shape that causes them to stack into clusters as they freeze.\n水分子具有特殊的弯曲形状，这使得它们在结冰时会堆叠成簇。\n\nAs the cluster grows, many outside factors, including humidity and temperature, begin to affect its overall shape.\n随着冰晶簇的生长，湿度、温度等许多外部因素开始影响其整体形状。\n\nIf the water is freezing on a window, for example, random imperfections on the glass surface affect the stacking and create the larger pattern.\n例如，如果水在窗户上结冰，玻璃表面的随机缺陷会影响冰晶簇的堆叠并产生更大的图案。\n\nBut scientists do not always know the purpose of a pattern, or even if there is one.\n但科学家并不总是知道某种图案的意义，甚至不确定它是否具有某种意义。\n\nThe molecular processes involved are simple enough that they might generate a pattern by coincidence.\n所涉及的分子过程非常简单，它们可能只是随机产生了某种图案。\n\nQuestions 12 to 15 are based on the passage you have just heard.\n请根据你刚刚听到的短文回答问题12到15。\n\n12. What does the passage say is a pattern in nature？\n12. 这篇短文说，自然界中的图案是什么？\n\n13. What gives rise to complex patterns at a larger scale?\n13. 什么导致了更大规模的复杂图案的产生？\n\n14. What does the example of frozen crystals on a window show?\n14. 窗户上冰晶的例子说明了什么？\n\n15. What might molecular processes produce according to the passage?\n15. 根据这篇短文，分子过程可能会产生什么？\n\nSection C Directions: In this section, you will hear three recordings of lectures or talks followed by three or four questions.\nC节 说明：在本节中，你将会听到三篇讲座或讲话，每篇讲座或讲话后面都有三个或四个问题。', 116, 1568.77, 630.12, 746.12, 768.80, 786.95, 679.05, 689.48, 'cet6-2026-06-2-g04', 'PASSAGE', '[10:30.12]Passage Two｜短文二\n[10:34.09]Why does nature create patterns?｜为什么大自然会创造图案？\n[10:37.03]The reason patterns often appear in nature is simple—the same basic physical or chemical processes occur in many pattern substances and organisms as they form.｜自然中常常出现图案的原因很简单——许多形成图案的物质和有机体在形成过程中，都发生了相同的物理或化学基本过程。\n[10:48.99]Whether in plants and animals or rocks, foams and ice crystals, the intricate patterns that happen in nature come down to what''s happening at the level of atoms and molecules.｜无论是植物、动物，还是岩石、泡沫和冰晶，自然界中出现的复杂图案都归结于原子和分子层面发生的情况。\n[11:01.21]A pattern in nature is any regularly repeated arrangement of shapes or colors.｜自然界中的图案是形状或颜色有规律地重复排列。\n[11:07.21]Some of the most striking examples include the six-sided arrays of rocks at Giant''s Causeway in the United Kingdom, and the colorful stripes and spots on tropical fish.｜一些最引人注目的例子包括英国巨人堤上的六边形岩石阵列，以及热带鱼身上的彩色条纹和斑点。\n[11:19.05]Patterns like these begin to form at a small scale when materials undergo processes like drying, freezing, wrinkling, diffusing and reacting.｜当材料经历干燥、冷冻、起皱、扩散和反应等过程时，这些图案开始小规模形成。\n[11:29.78]Those changes then give rise to complex patterns at a larger scale that people can see.｜随后，这些变化产生了人们可以看到的更大规模的复杂图案。\n[11:36.36]Imagine delicate frozen crystals on a window during winter.｜想象一下冬天窗户上精致的冰晶。\n[11:41.31]What creates that pattern?｜是什么创造了这种图案？\n[11:43.19]When water freezes, its molecules begin clustering together.｜当水结冰时，其分子开始聚集在一起。\n[11:47.70]Water molecules have a particular bent shape that causes them to stack into clusters as they freeze.｜水分子具有特殊的弯曲形状，这使得它们在结冰时会堆叠成簇。\n[11:54.85]As the cluster grows, many outside factors, including humidity and temperature, begin to affect its overall shape.｜随着冰晶簇的生长，湿度、温度等许多外部因素开始影响其整体形状。\n[12:03.30]If the water is freezing on a window, for example, random imperfections on the glass surface affect the stacking and create the larger pattern.｜例如，如果水在窗户上结冰，玻璃表面的随机缺陷会影响冰晶簇的堆叠并产生更大的图案。\n[12:13.41]But scientists do not always know the purpose of a pattern, or even if there is one.｜但科学家并不总是知道某种图案的意义，甚至不确定它是否具有某种意义。\n[12:19.47]The molecular processes involved are simple enough that they might generate a pattern by coincidence.｜所涉及的分子过程非常简单，它们可能只是随机产生了某种图案。\n[12:26.12]Questions 12 to 15 are based on the passage you have just heard.｜请根据你刚刚听到的短文回答问题12到15。\n[12:30.77]12. What does the passage say is a pattern in nature？｜12. 这篇短文说，自然界中的图案是什么？\n[12:48.80]13. What gives rise to complex patterns at a larger scale?｜13. 什么导致了更大规模的复杂图案的产生？\n[13:07.25]14. What does the example of frozen crystals on a window show?｜14. 窗户上冰晶的例子说明了什么？\n[13:25.03]15. What might molecular processes produce according to the passage?｜15. 根据这篇短文，分子过程可能会产生什么？\n[13:44.35]Section C Directions: In this section, you will hear three recordings of lectures or talks followed by three or four questions.｜C节 说明：在本节中，你将会听到三篇讲座或讲话，每篇讲座或讲话后面都有三个或四个问题。', NOW(), NOW()
