d their children cried or even fell asleep.｜然而，母亲的影响更有效，38%的母亲表示，孩子喜欢她们分享的曲子，而相比之下，30%的父亲在某些情况下表示，他们的孩子（听了他们推荐的音乐后）会哭，甚至睡着。\n[23:47.72]Dr. Egermann claims introducing children to a variety of musical styles is the key to fostering good taste in later life.｜埃格曼博士称，让孩子们接触多样化的音乐风格是培养他们日后良好品位的关键。\n[23:56.48]“By playing children a variety of genres before this critical period, research on familiarisation suggests they will enjoy lots of different types of music as adults,” he added.｜他补充说：“关于熟悉度的研究表明，通过在这个关键时期之前让孩子们接触各种类型的音乐，他们成年后会喜欢许多不同类型的音乐。\n[24:07.72]“The benefits of having a wider taste in music include the ability to manage their emotions more effectively, socialise and bond with others more easily, and to have a better understanding of other cultures as well.”｜拥有更广泛的音乐品位的好处包括：能够更有效地管理自己的情绪，更容易与他人社交和建立联系，以及更好地理解其他文化。”\n[24:21.21]Dr. Egermann advises parents not to push their favourite music too hard on their children, but instead play it as background music while a child is playing.｜埃格曼博士建议，父母不要强行把自己喜欢的音乐灌输给孩子，而是可以在孩子玩耍时将其作为背景音乐来播放。\n[24:31.96]They can also help create positive memories about artists and bands by going to concerts and live music events together.｜父母还可以通过带孩子一起去听音乐会、参加现场音乐活动，来帮助他们创造关于艺术家和乐队的积极记忆。\n[24:39.62]Questions 22 to 25 are based on the recording you have just heard.｜请根据你刚刚听到的录音回答问题22到25。\n[24:45.05]22. What do we learn from researchers'' conclusion at the beginning of the talk?｜22. 我们从讲话开头的研究结论中了解到什么？\n[25:04.19]23. What does Dr. Hauke Egermann say about adolescents?｜23. 关于青少年，豪克·埃格曼博士说了什么？\n[25:23.34]24. What is the key to fostering good taste in later life according to Dr. Hauke Egermann?｜24. 根据豪克·埃格曼博士的说法，培养日后良好品位的关键是什么？\n[25:44.25]25. How can parents help children create positive memories about artists and bands?｜25. 父母可以如何帮助孩子创造关于艺术家和乐队的积极记忆？', NOW(), NOW()
