  (`question_id`, `audio_url`, `transcript`, `duration_seconds`, `audio_total_seconds`, `audio_start_seconds`, `audio_end_seconds`, `question_start_seconds`, `question_end_seconds`, `answer_start_seconds`, `answer_end_seconds`, `group_key`, `listening_type`, `lrc_content`, `created_at`, `updated_at`)
SELECT
  @a_cet6_2026_06_2_25, '/audio/exams/listening-cet6-2026-06-2.mp3', 'Recording Three\n录音三\n\nParents have a small window where they can influence their 8- to 10-year-old children''s music taste, researchers have concluded.\n研究人员得出结论，父母有一个短暂的窗口期可以影响他们8至10岁孩子的音乐品味。\n\nThe 24-month time-frame comes at an age when youngsters are old enough to appreciate poetic lyrics and snappy tunes, but have not yet started to be embarrassed by their mother and father''s preferences.\n这24个月的时间窗口处于这样一个年龄：孩子们已经足够大，能够欣赏富有诗意的歌词和活泼的曲调，但尚未开始对父母（所喜欢的音乐）的品味感到难为情。\n\nDr. Hauke Egermann, a lecturer in music at the University of York, carried out a literature review into more than a dozen studies looking at parental musical influence.\n约克大学的音乐讲师豪克·埃格曼博士对十几项关于父母音乐影响的研究进行了文献综述。\n\n“Children have an ‘openness’ to new music, and this means parents have an important role to play in developing the musical preferences of their kids,” he said.\n他说：“儿童对新音乐有一种‘开放性’，这意味着父母在培养孩子音乐偏好方面可以发挥重要作用。\n\n“However, time is of the essence, as parental influence is most likely to be effective during the critical time period before age 10.\n然而，时间至关重要，因为父母的影响最有可能在10岁之前的关键时期内有效。\n\nDuring adolescence, children tend to gravitate away from their parents'' choices and are more influenced by their peers.”\n在青春期，孩子们往往会偏离父母的选择，而更多地受到同龄人的影响。”\n\nA separate survey of 2,000 British parents by music streaming service Deezer also found that nearly four fifths of parents agreed that their children were far more receptive to their musical suggestions before the age of 10.\n音乐流媒体服务公司Deezer对2 000名英国父母进行的一项独立调查也发现，近五分之四的父母认为他们的孩子在10岁之前更容易接受他们的音乐建议。\n\nIn contrast, just 10% of parents reported positive reactions from their teenage children when they shared their favourite music.\n相比之下，只有10%的父母表示，当他们分享自己喜欢的音乐时，青春期的孩子会有积极的反应。\n\nSome 79% of fathers said they had tried to influence their children''s music, but just 69% of mothers.\n约79%的父亲表示曾试图影响孩子的音乐（品味），而母亲的比例仅为69%。\n\nHowever, mothers were more effective, with 38% reporting that their kids loved the tunes they shared, compared to 30% of dads who in some cases said their children cried or even fell asleep.\n然而，母亲的影响更有效，38%的母亲表示，孩子喜欢她们分享的曲子，而相比之下，30%的父亲在某些情况下表示，他们的孩子（听了他们推荐的音乐后）会哭，甚至睡着。\n\nDr. Egermann claims introducing children to a variety of musical styles is the key to fostering good taste in later life.\n埃格曼博士称，让孩子们接触多样化的音乐风格是培养他们日后良好品位的关键。\n\n“By playing children a variety of genres before this critical period, research on familiarisation suggests they will enjoy lots of different types of music as adults,” he added.\n他补充说：“关于熟悉度的研究表明，通过在这个关键时期之前让孩子们接触各种类型的音乐，他们成年后会喜欢许多不同类型的音乐。\n\n“The benefits of having a wider taste in music include the ability to manage their emotions more effectively, socialise and bond with others more easily, and to have a better understanding of other cultures as well.”\n拥有更广泛的音乐品位的好处包括：能够更有效地管理自己的情绪，更容易与他人社交和建立联系，以及更好地理解其他文化。”\n\nDr. Egermann advises parents not to push their favourite music too hard on their children, but instead play it as background music while a child is playing.\n埃格曼博士建议，父母不要强行把自己喜欢的音乐灌输给孩子，而是可以在孩子玩耍时将其作为背景音乐来播放。\n\nThey can also help create positive memories about artists and bands by going to concerts and live music events together.\n父母还可以通过带孩子一起去听音乐会、参加现场音乐活动，来帮助他们创造关于艺术家和乐队的积极记忆。\n\nQuestions 22 to 25 are based on the recording you have just heard.\n请根据你刚刚听到的录音回答问题22到25。\n\n22. What do we learn from researchers'' conclusion at the beginning of the talk?\n22. 我们从讲话开头的研究结论中了解到什么？\n\n23. What does Dr. Hauke Egermann say about adolescents?\n23. 关于青少年，豪克·埃格曼博士说了什么？\n\n24. What is the key to fostering good taste in later life according to Dr. Hauke Egermann?\n24. 根据豪克·埃格曼博士的说法，培养日后良好品位的关键是什么？\n\n25. How can parents help children create positive memories about artists and bands?\n25. 父母可以如何帮助孩子创造关于艺术家和乐队的积极记忆？', 158, 1568.77, 1322.00, 1479.62, 1544.25, 1556.25, 1461.21, 1479.32, 'cet6-2026-06-2-g07', 'LECTURE', '[22:02.00]Recording Three｜录音三\n[22:03.85]Parents have a small window where they can influence their 8- to 10-year-old children''s music taste, researchers have concluded.｜研究人员得出结论，父母有一个短暂的窗口期可以影响他们8至10岁孩子的音乐品味。\n[22:11.56]The 24-month time-frame comes at an age when youngsters are old enough to appreciate poetic lyrics and snappy tunes, but have not yet started to be embarrassed by their mother and father''s preferences.｜这24个月的时间窗口处于这样一个年龄：孩子们已经足够大，能够欣赏富有诗意的歌词和活泼的曲调，但尚未开始对父母（所喜欢的音乐）的品味感到难为情。\n[22:24.17]Dr. Hauke Egermann, a lecturer in music at the University of York, carried out a literature review into more than a dozen studies looking at parental musical influence.｜约克大学的音乐讲师豪克·埃格曼博士对十几项关于父母音乐影响的研究进行了文献综述。\n[22:35.61]“Children have an ‘openness’ to new music, and this means parents have an important role to play in developing the musical preferences of their kids,” he said.｜他说：“儿童对新音乐有一种‘开放性’，这意味着父母在培养孩子音乐偏好方面可以发挥重要作用。\n[22:45.43]“However, time is of the essence, as parental influence is most likely to be effective during the critical time period before age 10.｜然而，时间至关重要，因为父母的影响最有可能在10岁之前的关键时期内有效。\n[22:54.41]During adolescence, children tend to gravitate away from their parents'' choices and are more influenced by their peers.”｜在青春期，孩子们往往会偏离父母的选择，而更多地受到同龄人的影响。”\n[23:02.46]A separate survey of 2,000 British parents by music streaming service Deezer also found that nearly four fifths of parents agreed that their children were far more receptive to their musical suggestions before the age of 10.｜音乐流媒体服务公司Deezer对2 000名英国父母进行的一项独立调查也发现，近五分之四的父母认为他们的孩子在10岁之前更容易接受他们的音乐建议。\n[23:16.95]In contrast, just 10% of parents reported positive reactions from their teenage children when they shared their favourite music.｜相比之下，只有10%的父母表示，当他们分享自己喜欢的音乐时，青春期的孩子会有积极的反应。\n[23:25.21]Some 79% of fathers said they had tried to influence their children''s music, but just 69% of mothers.｜约79%的父亲表示曾试图影响孩子的音乐（品味），而母亲的比例仅为69%。\n[23:34.01]However, mothers were more effective, with 38% reporting that their kids loved the tunes they shared, compared to 30% of dads who in some cases said their children cried or even fell asleep.｜然而，母亲的影响更有效，38%的母亲表示，孩子喜欢她们分享的曲子，而相比之下，30%的父亲在某些情况下表示，他们的孩子（听了他们推荐的音乐后）会哭，甚至睡着。\n[23:47.72]Dr. Egermann claims introducing children to a variety of musical styles is the key to fostering good taste in later life.｜埃格曼博士称，让孩子们接触多样化的音乐风格是培养他们日后良好品位的关键。\n[23:56.48]“By playing children a variety of genres before this critical period, research on familiarisation suggests they will enjoy lots of different types of music as adults,” he added.｜他补充说：“关于熟悉度的研究表明，通过在这个关键时期之前让孩子们接触各种类型的音乐，他们成年后会喜欢许多不同类型的音乐。\n[24:07.72]“The benefits of having a wider taste in music include the ability to manage their emotions more effectively, socialise and bond with others more easily, and to have a better understanding of other cultures as well.”｜拥有更广泛的音乐品位的好处包括：能够更有效地管理自己的情绪，更容易与他人社交和建立联系，以及更好地理解其他文化。”\n[24:21.21]Dr. Egermann advises parents not to push their favourite music too hard on their children, but instead play it as background music while a child is playing.｜埃格曼博士建议，父母不要强行把自己喜欢的音乐灌输给孩子，而是可以在孩子玩耍时将其作为背景音乐来播放。\n[24:31.96]They can also help create positive memories about artists and bands by going to concerts and live music events together.｜父母还可以通过带孩子一起去听音乐会、参加现场音乐活动，来帮助他们创造关于艺术家和乐队的积极记忆。\n[24:39.62]Questions 22 to 25 are based on the recording you have just heard.｜请根据你刚刚听到的录音回答问题22到25。\n[24:45.05]22. What do we learn from researchers'' conclusion at the beginning of the talk?｜22. 我们从讲话开头的研究结论中了解到什么？\n[25:04.19]23. What does Dr. Hauke Egermann say about adolescents?｜23. 关于青少年，豪克·埃格曼博士说了什么？\n[25:23.34]24. What is the key to fostering good taste in later life according to Dr. Hauke Egermann?｜24. 根据豪克·埃格曼博士的说法，培养日后良好品位的关键是什么？\n[25:44.25]25. How can parents help children create positive memories about artists and bands?｜25. 父母可以如何帮助孩子创造关于艺术家和乐队的积极记忆？', NOW(), NOW()
